   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42890</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">4G/5G Mobile Technologies</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In the mid-session quiz, students will take an individual quiz on UTSOnline. You will not have access to Internet or UTSOnline resources during the test. Please come to the test well prepared and on time. Solutions for the quiz questions will be discussed in class following the quiz.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Mid-Session Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The mid-term (Assessment Task 1)  will be held in class time as shown in the weekly program.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The mid-term (Assessment Task 1)  will be held in class time as shown in the weekly program.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To allow students to demonstrate their knowledge of the concepts learnt in the subject, apply their skills to solve problems and self-assess their progress in the subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task is based on analysis of measurements obtained from an operational Telstra LTE network. It is designed to provide students with an overview of LTE physical layer procedures and performance measurements. Students will evaluate measurements results recorded from a live LTE network using a commercial measurement tool (NEMO Handy by Anite). Matlab will be used for measurement analysis. Project work will be done by students outside class hours.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class in Week 11</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Practising engineers are expected to analyse live measurements taken from an operational network to check and validate the performance of a 4G network. By evaluating measurements from a Telstra LTE network, students learn to apply industry tools and techniques to demonstrate their subject knowledge, problem solving and research skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of the final exam is to test the overall understanding of the subject contents and address Objectives 1, 2 and 3 of the subject. The final will be held on the dates shown in the UTS exam timetable and students will take two individual quizzes ( Part 1 and Part 2) on UTSOnline. You will not have access to Internet or UTSOnline resources during the final exam.The intent of the final exam is to allow students to demonstrate their knowledge of 4G/5G mobile networks operation, standards and problem solving which they have learnt in the subject. This is an open book exam.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The intent of the final exam is to allow students to demonstrate their knowledge of 4G/5G mobile networks operation, standards and problem solving which they have learnt in the subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task involves students working working in a group and presenting an extensive research of the topic to their peers in the classroom. Further details are available on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Research Topic</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
