   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41051</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Accelerating Your Prototyping and Commercialisation Strategies</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A Design Portfolio depicts an individual’s curated learning journey or roadmap of their individual and team experience of leading for innovation during early-stage prototyping. Each individual in a team will develop a unique perspective on their journey and will submit an individual portfolio. The Design Portfolio is an ePortfolio in the format of student’s own choice. Students can use the Learning Management System (LMS) ePortfolio tool or develop their own using other platforms (e.g. Weebly, WordPress). The Design Portfolio should begin with an introduction to themselves, their team, and their team project(s) and the intended target audience for the prototype. The Design Portfolio should include a summary of the top strengths and blind spots listed in the student’s Fingerprint for Success assessment, the student’s reflection on their F4S assessment and the student’s learning contract. The ePortfolio should be written from the student’s individual perspective and be original work describing making process throughout the prototyping process as seen through the inclusion of artefacts and reflections. The ePortfolio should end with a summary that synthesises the individual’s development and achievement of the subject learning outcomes and their personal learning goals throughout the subject journey. Students demonstrate their achievement using a collection of artefacts together with reflections that meet the Performance Standard Criteria to Pass, below.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">100</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">First iteration of the Design Portfolio is submitted.  The team presentation on the final version of the prototyping is submitted electronically by 11:59 pm in the final week of class and presented in class on the following day. Final version of the Design Portfolio including the student’s Reflection on the Design Thinking Process is submitted electronically by 11:59 pm in the final week of class and presented in class on the following day.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">First iteration of the Design Portfolio is submitted.  The team presentation on the final version of the prototyping is submitted electronically by 11:59 pm in the final week of class and presented in class on the following day. Final version of the Design Portfolio including the student’s Reflection on the Design Thinking Process is submitted electronically by 11:59 pm in the final week of class and presented in class on the following day.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To clearly communicate a learning contract including learning goals that explain what progress was made toward the final individual Design Portfolio. For the Design Portfolio to depict a curated individual learning journey or road map demonstrating the student’s understanding and attainment of each of the subject leaning objectives, their personal learning objectives, and how this understanding has shaped them throughout the prototyping process.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
