   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42722</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Additive Manufacturing for Medical Innovations</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The student will be assessed individually based on completion of three key practical activities including: Design in Solidworks; Materialise; and successful production by 3D printing of designed file.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Practical Activities</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submission of CAD file, demonstrator assessment of Materialise competencies and successful production of 3D print.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assess if the student can apply acquired competencies in CAD (Solidworks), design optimization (Materialise) and production by 3Dprinting combined with intellectual context of 3D printing in the medical field in a practical manner.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The student is required to write report of no more than 3500 words describing and demonstrating how to apply 3D printing in solving an existing and/or future clinical needs or treatment. This should include background, market analysis and prototype design of the proposed construct, ethical implications and explanation into the “science” behind the design and/or tissue construct.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">3D Printing Studio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">No more than 3500 words. Pages unlimited including figures.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assess if the students can apply acquired competencies in CAD, 3D printing and apply in designing a solution using 3D printing for a medical application.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The student group is required to make a 10 mins presentation with 5 mins question time with every student in the group participating in the presentation. The group is required to show initial CAD design, revision and final CAD product, market analysis, medical problem addressing and scientific explanation on the usage/process of their design.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10 mins presentation with 5 mins question time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assess if the student can articulate their ideas, design and concept and deliver it in a presentation to a wider audience to address a gap/limitation in current medical industry that can be solved by 3D printing.</Data></Cell>
