   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32513</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Advanced Data Analytics Algorithms</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual assessment. This task involves reading and understanding some data mining and data analytics literature. You will read and critique a data analytics research paper. This assignment is to be done individually.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Understanding the Literature</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The task requires submission of a report of 10 pages in an 11 or 12 point font.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 5              UTS Online submission deadline: 11:59 28 Aug 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Online submission deadline: 11:59 28 Aug 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Please note: Weighting of Assessment Criteria is approximate. Please see your subject guide for mark allocation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The goal of this assignment is to develop your skills in a practical data mining project related to your workplace. If you’re not working or there isn’t a suitable problem in your workplace, then you are free to choose a workplace you’re interested in. The main thing is to make it as practical and useful as you can. You can choose to either work with a dataset using scikit-learn (Python), Rattle (R) or WEKA (Java). If you have trouble finding a suitable dataset, speak with me and we can find one. The goal will be to derive a business problem then solve it using data analytics. You can do this assignment by yourself or in pairs. You will need to submit a report of around 20–30 pages describing the problem and your solution.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Practical Workplace-Related Data Analytics Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A report of around 20-30 pages in an 11 or 12 point font.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">9</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 9              UTS Online submission deadline: 11:59pm 25 Sep 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Online submission deadline: 11:59pm 25 Sep 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Please note: Weighting of Assessment Criteria is approximate. Please see your subject guide for mark allocation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The goal of this assignment is to develop your skills in proposing and selling a data analytics project. Ideally, the project could be related to the industry you work in, but if you want to choose a different domain, that’s fine. The project should be something that could be done within one year. Note: Students don’t need to actually do the project as part of this assignment: they're just proposing a project. The main thing is to choose a project that you’re interested in and passionate about!</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Pitch and Plan for Solving a Domain Problem</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 11              UTS Online submission deadline: 11:59pm 9 Oct 2019</Data></Cell>
