   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42091</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Advanced Energy Conversion Systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students complete a major project report in stages throughout the teaching session. There are four control methods for electrical machines covered in this subject:  Brushless DC control method Field-oriented control method Direct torque control method Model predictive control method  Students work on a project throughout the semester and undertake modelling and simulation using each of these four methods and prepare a final report that includes chapters that cover students’ work with each of these methods. Students’ modelling and simulation using each of the control methods must be written up as four separate Progress Reports and submitted on the interim due dates shown. These four Progress Reports will be worth 10% each, and feedback will be provided on students’ work that they can then use to improve their work before preparing the Final Report. In the Final Report, students should incorporate their revised progress reports, and add an introduction and further analysis. In particular, students should reflect on their reports to discuss important factors to consider in the design of advanced control methods for energy conversion systems, and to analyse the role of these different control methods in future smart grids against various criteria such as performance, efficiency, cost-effectiveness, and suitability for different smart grid technologies.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">80</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">4000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">See timetable</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">See timetable</Data></Cell>
