   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48371</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Advanced Engineering Computing</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Writing assignments allows students to reflect their understanding of the theory and possible applications, in order to demonstrate their level of competency. The assignments require students to solve problems routinely encountered by strructural engineers by using the numerical techniques taught in the lectures. -Assignments – Dr Erkmen – 10%. The assignments require students to solve engineering problems by using the numerical techniques taught by Dr. Erkmen</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To be advised in the lecture</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To be advised in the lecture</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To give students the opportunity to practice problem solving. The assessment task gives students the opportunity to practice various approaches related to engineering problems and to evaluate them. Students will classify, formulate, and solve various problems, and differentiate the different types of solutions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">-Quiz on Matlab – A/Prof Khabbaz -25% The quiz requires students to complete tasks by using Matlab to achieve final solutions to civil engineering problems whilst developing models and solving technical problems.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Matlab Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To be advised in the lecture.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To be advised in the lecture.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The quiz requires students to complete tasks by using Matlab to achieve final solutions to civil engineering problems whilst developing models and solving technical problems.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is an authentic assessment task as the projects will reflect the real world problems that an engineer might face in industry. There will be groups of students assigned for one project. Each project will be posted at the beginning of the session. Students will be able to use any software they want or have access to solve the assigned project. Students will be asked to validate their solution using Matlab by adopting at least one of the techniques that is covered in the lecture notes (by simplifying the problem if necessary). There will be four rounds of presentations/discussions related to the projects:  The first round of presentations will be on what the students have thought of running the project and how they planned it. The second round will be on the discussions of the results obtained and how they have been validated. In the third round the students will teach the techniques to the rest of the class. The fourth round will be on reflection on what they have learned from the project and from each other.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">65</Data></Cell>
