   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32509</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Advanced Interaction Design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To develop students' sensitivities and perceptions about how people experience their use of interactive technologies in their everyday lives, and the ability to articulate how various factors influence people's user experiences arising during-and-through their use of interactive technologies.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">User Experience Journal Entries</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Journal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each journal entry will use the template provided, and should be between 2-4 pages long.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Journal 1 (at the beginning of tutorial 4) and Journal 2 (at the beginning of tutorial 7).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Journal 1 (at the beginning of tutorial 4) and Journal 2 (at the beginning of tutorial 7).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assess students' understanding of different aspects of user experience. This includes both the conceptual and practical aspects of user experience when people use interactive technologies in their everyday lives.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will work individually and in groups of 4-5 to develop the interaction design for a system that supports good user experience. The project and the problem have been designed to provide opportunities to practise a human-centred design methodology in user experience design by combining user research, design ideation, prototyping methods and evaluation activities. Through this, students will develop personas, user stories, ideation, prototypes of the systems and evaluation of these prototypes in real life situations to refine the design of the system. Exercises during tutorials will provide students with opportunities to familiarise themselves with the various user experience techniques and tools used in this assignment. Work conducted during tutorials will also provide opportunities for students to familiarise themselves with the specific requirements of the assignment and more importantly, receive guidance and formative feedback on their understanding of the skills and evolving thinking about design.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design Assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Prototyping and User Experience Evaluation Report (25%) due at the beginning of Week 10 tutorial. Design-in-Action video of the evaluated design (25%) due on Friday 23 October by 23:59hr.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Prototyping and User Experience Evaluation Report (25%) due at the beginning of Week 10 tutorial. Design-in-Action video of the evaluated design (25%) due on Friday 23 October by 23:59hr.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The marking criteria will be included with the assignment. Students will be asked to assess the contribution of their peers to the group project. This peer assessment will be used to determine whether all group members receive the same mark for the assignment. If discrepancies in contribution are noted, individual marks will be scaled in accordance with the peer feedback.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To provide students with opportunities to practise a Human-Centred Design methodology to focus on designing to support User Experience through combining user research, design and evaluation activities including theory, exploratory and experimental studies, prototyping and evaluation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is an individual assessment. In Part 1, students will submit a document that provides evidence on how they have used online forums in a timely manner to support their own learning and also to contribute positively to supporting peer learning. In Part 2, students will create a Personal Portfolio which consists of a carefully chosen compilation of work samples the student has personally created during this subject. The portfolio is a valuable resource that students can use to demonstrate their work, their skills and their proficiency with various tools work to prospective employers. As such, it should be organised, accessible and purposeful without overwhelming the reader. Students should choose work samples that reflect and demonstrate the development of their skills in using various tools to support designing for UX. They could be be related to sketches, personas, scenarios, user journeys, as well as stories and the re-creations of these stories through pictures and videos, and so on. Further details about the content selection for this assessment can be found in the Assignment 3 description document.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection Document and Personal Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">26/10/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday 26 October 2020              To Canvas (Turnitin) by 12.00 afternoon.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The marking criteria will be included with the assignment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To evaluate students' capacity to reflect upon their own understanding and proficiency of the range of skills and tools used in user experience design.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To Canvas (Turnitin) by 12.00 afternoon.</Data></Cell>
