   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">31242</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Advanced Internet Programming</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Throughout the session, students are expected to participate in laboratory exercises, conduct independent study, engage other professionals and support other learners. Students might achieve these goals by, for example, asking and answering questions online, giving presentations, attending user group meetings, writing blog posts, learning new tools or experimenting with emerging technologies. Students will create a portfolio of evidence that demonstrates their understanding of the subject learning objectives and an ongoing commitment to learning and engagement. A template for the portfolio will be made available on UTS Online/Canvas. The template will include a list of behaviours as well as guidelines for providing evidence that demonstrates this commitment. While there will be a small number of mandatory tasks, students will have freedom to design their learning in ways that they feel will most enhance their learning. Graded and written feedback on partial progress will be provided prior to the census date.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio of Reflection and Analysis</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">60</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week range</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 1 to Week 12              Students must add to their skills portfolio by Friday 11:59pm each week. Graded and written feedback on partial progress will be provided prior to the census date. Further feedback and advice on how to improve the quality of work will be provided though in-class activities and at the student's request during class time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students must add to their skills portfolio by Friday 11:59pm each week. Graded and written feedback on partial progress will be provided prior to the census date. Further feedback and advice on how to improve the quality of work will be provided though in-class activities and at the student's request during class time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will design and implement a medium sized web application incorporating multiple data sources, transaction integrity, data and application security.  This project will be carried out in groups.  The deliverables will include a working application that MUST be demonstrated in the labs, in addition to electronic submission of source code, documentation, revision control logs. Submission details will be specified in the assignment handout.  Detailed feedback with advice for improvement and to understand the learning objectives achieved will be provided verbally during the demonstration and electronically after submission.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Advanced Internet Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class in Week 12              System functionality demonstrations are due in the Week 12 laboratory session. Students will have the opportunity to improve their code as a result of peer feedback for their final code submission by 2 November 2020, 11:59pm (i.e., Monday of Assessment Week 1).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">System functionality demonstrations are due in the Week 12 laboratory session. Students will have the opportunity to improve their code as a result of peer feedback for their final code submission by 2 November 2020, 11:59pm (i.e., Monday of Assessment Week 1).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will independently research a Java EE technology (chosen from a list provided in the assignment handout or approved by the tutor). Students will write a short report that provides an analysis of the context, development, advanced features and possible improvements of the technology. In addition, students will submit sample code that demonstrates advanced features and/or implementation details. A high standard is expected: the report and code will need to show expert insight and technical creativity. Submission details are specified in the assignment handout.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
