   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48663</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Advanced Manufacturing</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The numerical control (NC) in machining is an important task in the advanced manufacturing; some refer to the numerical control in manufacturing as the 3rd phase of the industrial revolution. In this assessment, the students to work on 3 tasks: The principles of the NC with mathematical modelling, The writing of G-Code instruction to control a CNC milling machine in 3D tool movement and the application of the CAD/CAM in G-Code generation. Another CAD/CAM application is present in this project-based assessment, the 3D printing. Student need to build their models using a polymer filament 3D printer. A comparison study of the accuracy and tolerances to analysed and reported. The students’ codes to be machined on a CNC milling machine and the students’ parts to be assess.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">G-Coding, CNC, CAD/CAM and Additive Manufacturing</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">03/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 3 May 2020              Submit your laboratory report in pdf format to 'Assignments' in 48663 on UTSOnline.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit your laboratory report in pdf format to 'Assignments' in 48663 on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Experimental validation of students' knowledge.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The metrology is the measurement and comparison to standards science. This assessment task is to measuring the part quality characteristics and comparing them with design specifications. The students to practice the experimentally investigation of the control of tolerances in mechanical parts, methods of measurement, selection of measurement instrument and the application of statistics to the measurement process.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering metrology and measurements</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">19/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 19 April 2020              Submit your laboratory report in pdf format to 'Assignments' in 48663 on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit your laboratory report in pdf format to 'Assignments' in 48663 on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab-based work.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment task number 3 is a calculation based homework assignment consists of questions based on topics covered in weeks 4 and 5. Students will perform the application of the statistical process control theories on a set on real-life data mathematical questions, including industry data and lab direct measurements.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Statistical Process Control (SPC)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 10 May 2020              Submit your laboratory report in pdf format to 'Assignments' in 48663 on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">validation of students' knowledge</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit your laboratory report in pdf format to 'Assignments' in 48663 on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is an extended project mode task. The student will required to match the gained practical experiences through the session with practical application. Students work in groups to practice the team and resources management, CAD/CAM, manufacturing, metrology and robotic assembly process.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Robotics and DFX Applications</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">07/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 7 June 2020              Submit your laboratory report in pdf format to 'Assignments' in 48663 on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit your laboratory report in pdf format to 'Assignments' in 48663 on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Experimental validation of students' knowledge.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment task number 5 is a calculation-based homework assignment consisting of two questions:  The process planning: Tool life and production rate. The analysis of Flexible manufacturing cell utilization rate.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">CIM and CAPP</Data></Cell>
