   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42092</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Advanced Power Electronics</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Analysis and solution of problems related to power electronics. Students will complete 5 online quizzes. The quizzes are mainly related to the online lecture videos and tutorials. They are designed to assess students’ understanding of the subject on a regular basis.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Problem solving quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20 minutes per quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To test knowledge of in-depth understanding of theory and application individual components of power electronics circuits as preparation for the project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students work in groups of two to complete assigned laboratory tasks. The assessment consists of four lab tasks. Labs are to be completed in groups but each group member must prepare an individual report for each lab (4 lab reports in total). Pre-lab work is reading, hand-analysis and computer simulation. Post-lab work to analyse results and write a report (including, text, figures and measurement results). Each of the four lab reports is worth equal weighting towards the assessment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10-15 pages for each lab report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To develop skills in modelling and practical applications of power electronics as preparation for the project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group project with students working in a group of 2 to design, simulate, test and practically demonstrate a working model of a converter meeting set of criteria (power density, cost, efficiency, and transient behaviour). Students must deliver a Progress Report and a Final Report at the times mentioned in the due dates. For these milestones, students must submit one report per group. The report must follow the IEEE article format. After submission of the Final Report, students must deliver a group presentation. An individual viva-voce will be conducted to assess individual understanding of the project topic.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
