   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41026</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Advanced Software Development</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment task will require a team of 4-6 students to analyse the selected project problem; and produce, submit and present a group report containing individual modules or work related to  Software requirements &amp; development plan; Software architecture &amp; design; DevOps pipeline setup; and Software prototype  The individual student contributions or parts will be collated in a group deliverable for submission and assessment (group submission but individual assessment). The deliverables of this assessment task are called “Release 0” and also include a compulsory group report, DevOps pipeline and software prototype presentation (no PowerPoint slides) during the scheduled assignment assessment or review session (showcase), and individual contribution logbooks - as per Subject Weekly Schedule. Any individual student who failed to appear, defend their work and present in these compulsory assignment assessment and review sessions (Showcase) will receive zero (0) as a final individual mark. The additional information about the software project and assessment tasks will be provided in the project brief. This task will be submitted as a group but will be assessed individual as per assigned individual module as agreed with the tutor.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Release 0</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is a technical report, thus there is no compulsory minimum and maximum word limit. For a general guidance, the recommended word limit for this assignment is maximum 5000 words excluding diagrams, bibliography, logbooks and appendices. Word limit will be regarded as recommended rather than compulsory, and no student will be disadvantaged by being under or over the recommended word limit.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday August 19, 2019 by 09:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday August 19, 2019 by 09:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstrate the ability to analyse, plan, architect and design a software development project and setup the DevOps environment before commencing the actual development in small releases and iterations.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment task will require a team of 4-6 students to produce, submit and present a final combined group report (comprises of individual contributions), working software application (comprises of individually implemented and tested software features or modules) and individual contribution logbooks for software Release 1. Based on the plan, software requirements, architecture and design (based on Assessment Items 1) for Release 1, each individual student in the group shall  Implement the assigned feature or module of the software application; Provide the updated plan, requirement, architecture and design of the assigned software application feature or module for release 1; Provide automated software unit and acceptance testing with executed tests and defect log; and Integrate automated testing with DevOps pipeline   The individual student contributions or parts will be collated in a group final deliverable for submission and assessment (group submission but individual assessment). The deliverables of this assessment task are called “Release 1”. The deliverables of this assessment task also include a compulsory oral/visual presentation (no PowerPoint slides) of the individually implemented working software application during the scheduled assignment assessment or review session (showcase), individual contribution logbooks and working software code implemented - as per Subject Weekly Schedule. Any individual student who failed to appear and present in these compulsory assignment assessment and review sessions (Showcase) will receive zero (0) as a final individual mark. The additional information about the software project case study and assessment tasks will be provided in the project brief. Note: Please note that each release will have at least 3 iterations or as advised by the teaching staff. Each iteration will be of 1 week duration. Marking of release 1 will be done progressively during the weekly Release 1 tracking sessions in the scheduled workshop and also in the final showcase. Each team is required to present work-in-progress software to their product owner (tutor) during the in-workshop weekly stand-up meetings, get feedback and marks for the software component or feature developed as per plan. You must attend all the weekly in-workshop stand-up meetings to earn marks for work-in-progress software. Each weekly tracking session is worth 3 marks.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Release 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday 16 September, 2019 by 09:00 AM.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday 16 September, 2019 by 09:00 AM.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstrate the ability to implement a software application using the professional software development practices, DevOps and automated testing tools.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment task will require a team of 4-6 students to produce, submit and present a final combined group report (comprises of individual contributions), working software application (comprises of individually implemented and tested software features or modules) and individual contribution logbooks for software Release 2. Based on the plan, software requirements, architecture and design (based on Assessment Items 1 &amp; 2) for Release 2, each individual student in the group shall  Implement updated assigned feature or module of the software application; Provide the updated plan, requirement, architecture and design of the assigned software application feature or module for release 2; Provide automated software unit and acceptance testing with executed tests and defect log; and Enable branching development (dev branch and prod branch) with DevOps pipeline  The individual student contributions or parts will be collated in a group final deliverable for submission and assessment (group submission but individual assessment). The deliverables of this assessment task are called “Release 2”. The deliverables of this assessment task also include a compulsory oral/visual presentation (no PowerPoint slides) of the individually implemented working software application during the scheduled assignment assessment or review session (showcase), individual contribution logbooks and working software code implemented - as per Subject Weekly Schedule. Any individual student who failed to appear and present in these compulsory assignment assessment and review sessions (Showcase) will receive zero (0) as a final individual mark. The additional information about the software project case study and assessment tasks will be provided in the project brief. Note: Please note that each release will have at least 3 iterations or as advised by the teaching staff. Each iteration will be of 1 week duration. Marking of release 2 will be done progressively during the weekly Release 2 tracking sessions in the scheduled workshop and also in the final showcase. Each team is required to present work-in-progress software to their product owner (tutor) during the in-workshop weekly stand-up meetings, get feedback and marks for the software component or feature developed as per plan. You must attend all the weekly in-workshop stand-up meetings to earn marks for work-in-progress software/ project tracking. Each weekly tracking session is worth 3 marks.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Release 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday 18 October, 2019 by 09:00 AM.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstrate the ability to implement an advanced software application using the professional software development practices, DevOps and automated testing tools.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday 18 October, 2019 by 09:00 AM.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">It includes 6 in-workshop UTSOnline quizzes of about maximum 10 minutes each (complete during the scheduled workshop session in the last 20 minutes of the workshop). The quizzes shall measure the degree that the theory, as taught by the subject and practised by the individual in each of the phases of the project, is understood by each individual.</Data></Cell>
