   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32536</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Advanced Software Modelling</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The mid-session test will examine the material presented in the class thus far covering objectives 1-3. The specific topics for the test will also be discussed in the class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Mid-session Test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The project work assignment is a group work assignment, which will give hands-on experience in developing an object-oriented model using UML. Objectives 3-5 and 7.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The deadline for the assignment is 6 p.m. in Week 14 i.e. June 5th. The report is to be handed in to the lecturer in charge by the above mentioned deadline. Reports can be collected after marking from the Student Centre.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The marks for the assignment report will be allocated as follows: · 40% for the analysis and design document - mostly UML or BPMN diagrams  · 40% for an explanation of the diagrams as documented plus some brief discussion of the process of deriving them  · 20% for a discussion of 'lessons learned' i.e. a critique of the modelling language used (bad and good features)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">3-hour closed book examination, covering all the material in the subject</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
