   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49254</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Advanced Soil Mechanics and Foundation Design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will classify, formulate, and solve various problems, and differentiate the different types of solutions. A number of assignments for each topic are prepared. Assignment questions will be uploaded on UTSOnline and students should solve the question and provide the detailed calculations for the design. Every single step of the calculation and utilised formulations with proper reference to notes and available literature should be provided.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments (Summative)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To give students the opportunity to practice problem solving. The assessment task gives students the opportunity to practice various approaches related to foundation design and analysis of unsaturated and saturated soil behaviour and to evaluate them.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A group of 3 to 4 students will work on a major research project with case studies. A different topic will be given to each group. Students should write a report with details covering Executive Summary, Introduction/background, Aims of the project , Modelling dimensions and geometry, Summary of the materials properties and extra assumptions used , calculations steps, outputs , discussion of results and list of references. Students should refer to UTSOnline for Instructions for major project report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group research project report (Summative)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To engage with research and to encourage students to be research oriented and life long learners. To develope research skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students can solve these quizzes available on UTSOnline and submit the detailed solution and the answer online. These are individual quizzes to support student preparation for the main assignments and tasks.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Online Quiz (Formative)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To allow students to demonstrate what they have learnt, to establish what more they should learn and give them the opportunity to have formative and feed forward assessment of their performance.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The open book final exam covers all topics. Students can bring their notes and books. Students can use a programmable calculator.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Examination (Summative)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
