   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42991</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Advanced Water and Wastewater Treatment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1 relates to the topic of stakeholder engagement with respect to desalination, water and wastewater reuse. The student should document/review current understandings/knowledge towards the public acceptance of using seawater desalination and wastewater reuse for drinking based on previous and recent studies/literature. Additional details are given on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Community engagement strategy for wastewater reuse and desalination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual written report (8-12 pages)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59pm, Sunday 26th April 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59pm, Sunday 26th April 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will understand the socio-technical aspect of water and wastewater treatment technology. This will develop and assess the capability of students to apply their understanding and knowledge of engaging the community in selecting suitable water resources and technology in terms of community needs and perceptions and the strategies in engaging the stakeholders.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 2 will include schematic diagrams, calculations, and discussions on the design of an advanced wastewater treatment process. The purpose of the task is to consider the factors that influence the amount of energy used in the wastewater treatment plants. The objective of the design exercise is to work through the steps required to evaluate the total and specific power requirements.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design of an advanced wastewater treatment process</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual written report (8-12 pages)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM, Sunday 24th May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM, Sunday 24th May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will understand the engineering design process of a membrane bioreactor and compare the design parameters with a conventional treatment plant. Furthermore, this will develop and assess the capability of students to apply their knowledge to the design of an advanced water/wastewater treatment plant for wastewater reuse.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will understand the engineering design process of a seawater desalination plant and apply their knowledge to the design of an advanced desalination process. ROSA program will be utilised to help in the design.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design of an advanced seawater desalination plant</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual written report (8-12 pages)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM, Sunday 14th June 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of the task is to consider the design factors of a seawater desalination plant. Furthermore, this will develop and assess the capability of students to apply their knowledge to the design of an advanced desalination process.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM, Sunday 14th June 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Open book exam. All topics covered in the lectures and assignments are assessed.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 hours + 10 minutes reading time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam Period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam Period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assess the competency of students in stakeholder engagement strategy, design, operation, optimisation of conventional and advanced water and wastewater treatment, computer-based design tools, life cycle analysis of water treatment and desalination plants.</Data></Cell>
