   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49322</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Airconditioning</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to attend the laboratory session they enrolled before the session started. They will be guided to conduct experiments on an air conditioning test rig in CB11.B4.109. Following the experiments, students will be required to work on a laboratory report in a team. Each team should have 2-5 members and is required to submit one report. Students must refer to all the documents for laboratories as published on UTSCanvas.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 10 May 2020              Submit your laboratory report in pdf format to 'Assignments' in 49322 on UTSCanvas. Only one submission from one of your team members is required.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit your laboratory report in pdf format to 'Assignments' in 49322 on UTSCanvas. Only one submission from one of your team members is required.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1: Air conditioning processes. Questions involving calculations and analysis Assignment 2: Psychrometric and Cooling towers. Questions involving calculations and analysis Assignment 3: Compressors and refrigeration cycle. Questions involving calculations and analysis Assignment 4: Duct and pipe design. Questions involving calculations and analysis</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">All the assignments should be submitted electronically through the subject page of UTSCanvas. Assignment 1 due 29 March 2020; Assignment 2 due 19 April 2020; Assignment 3 due 17 May 2020; Assignment 4 due 27 May 2020.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">All the assignments should be submitted electronically through the subject page of UTSCanvas. Assignment 1 due 29 March 2020; Assignment 2 due 19 April 2020; Assignment 3 due 17 May 2020; Assignment 4 due 27 May 2020.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">These assignments are aimed to help students to enhance and demonstrate their understanding of and analysis skills for air conditioning processes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Throughout the semester you will work on a semester-long project associated with the topics that you are learning in this class. You will be provided with feedback on each portion and expected to update each portion for the final submission. This semester project will be treated like a research project in that you are expected to develop and submit an abstract of what you plan to do, then after working on your project, you will submit your findings in the form of a journal article and a recorded presentation. These will be peer-reviewed by your peers and the instructor. Please keep in mind ideas of what you may be interested in doing for this project as we go through the material in this course. Students are expected to complete the project using eQuest and Camel in teams and to submit an electronic. An oral presentation to be delivered at week 9.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">31/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 31 May 2020              The final report should be submitted electronically through the subject page of UTSCanvas.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The aim of the project is to enhance students’ learning of Building HVAC and Energy Simulation and the Environmental Impact, through the using of software package for load estimation in the design of air condition systems.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The final report should be submitted electronically through the subject page of UTSCanvas.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students should revise the subject with not only the learning guidance, lecture notes, class examples and assignment questions, but also the laboratory and project reports. It will cover the contents in the whole subject. It's non-descriptive, so only based on calculations. On average, each question takes 30 minutes to answer. Open book exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination (open book)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 hours plus 10 minutes reading time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
