   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41889</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Application Development in the iOS Environment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The project will require students to demonstrate their understanding and skills in programming including:  Data types Loops and conditionals Strings, arrays, and dictionaries Testing and debugging Using version control  Program functionality will be evaluated by an automated testing suite, and code style will be reviewed manually.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual Programming Project 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">200-300 lines of code</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">03/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 3 April 2020              Feedback for programming tasks (Assessment Tasks 1, 2 and 3) is generally given within 2 weeks of the due date.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Feedback for programming tasks (Assessment Tasks 1, 2 and 3) is generally given within 2 weeks of the due date.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Details of the assessment criteria will be made available in the project specification.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The project will require the students to demonstrate their understanding and skills in programming including:  Data types Loops and conditionals Strings and arrays Classes and OOP Dynamic memory allocation and deletion Testing and debugging Using version control</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The project will require students to demonstrate their understanding and skill in building a practical iPhone/iPad application, specifically:  Cocoa Touch UI frameworks Apple Human Interface Guidelines  Students will evaluate their peers' functionality, visual appeal, and &quot;fun factor&quot;. Markers will rate usability and code style.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual Programming Project 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">300 – 400 lines of code</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 15 May 2020See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Details of the assessment criteria will be made available in the project specification.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The project will require the students to demonstrate their understanding and skill in building a practical iPhone/iPad application solution from given customer requirements.  Designing the solution. Building a GUI program. Using the various GUI components. Testing and debugging.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This group project requires students to explore and understand specific iOS frameworks using available online resources, develop working code examples, and explain how those frameworks solve specific problems. Student groups will describe their product in a final presentation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">About 5 min video presentation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 5 June 2020See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Details of the assessment criteria will be made available in the project specification.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This group project requires students to explore and understand specific iOS frameworks using available online resources, develop working code examples that utilise the iOS frameworks.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
