   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49136</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Application of Timber in Engineering Structures</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">On-line Assessment Task Students are required to solve design problems for tension, compression and flexural member and a bolted connection. The task is based on a spread sheet format. Students can see immediate qualitative feedback on their performance on the spread sheet and can attempt the task as many times as they like before the due date.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">24/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday 24 April 2020              All tasks are made available online and for submission of the tasks, students only need to upload their task online.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">All tasks are made available online and for submission of the tasks, students only need to upload their task online.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will need to design a timber structural element based on AS1720.1. The assessment is designed to help students understand the fundamental behaviour of timber (A5), problem solving (B1) and be able to design timber elements (B2). The assessment tasks provide immediate feedback and therefore allows students to evaluate and revise their models/calculations (C1, C3).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is a group exercise. Each group is required to work on a detailed design of a commercial building using the EXPAN design guides. Design components include –  Floor options Columns and beams Roof Connections  Students should submit a Detailed Report which should highlight design assumptions, alternative solutions, detailed drawing and list of key features and discussions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design Assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">60</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">08/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday 8 June 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Presentation Students need to present the outcomes of their Detailed Design Assignment (Assessment Task 2) to the class and to a panel of assessors (typically 3 academics/practicing engineers). Each group is allowed 20 minutes to present alternative solutions, final design, key features and discussion on their choice of final design. This will be followed by discussion/review by the class and panel of assessors.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation of detail design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20 minutes presentation + 10 mins Q&amp;A</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">22/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday 22 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assess the competency of students in following areas – Demonstrate understanding of project brief and outcomes (C1, E1) Working effectively as a design team (E2, E3) Be able to justify design alternatives (B1, B3, B5)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final quiz will be an open book quiz and covers all the materials relevant to the subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 hours</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday 5 June 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assessment will assess the following - understanding of fundamental material properties and natural characteristics of wood (A5) understanding of the design principles for a commercial timber building and its components (A5, B1, B2, C1, C2, C3) problem solving skills (B1, B3)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Review of all material</Data></Cell>
