   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48024</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Applications Programming</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The task is to code a well-designed solution to a small specification. The output of this task is a Java program of one or more classes. Submit your solution to PLATE at https://plate.it.uts.edu.au.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Labs</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each weekly lab on average should take about 2 hours for the typical student.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Not applicable</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Not applicableSee Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">All labs are marked for correctness only. The early labs are marked by PLATE, and the GUI labs are marked by a combination of PLATE, student peer marking, and the Subject Coordinator. The minimum essential requirement for a pass in any one lab is to pass more than half of the assigned tasks. If, due to extenuating circumstances, you are unable to attend the peer marking session, please contact your tutor or the subject coordinator before the assessment task is due to discuss an alternative solution. Absence from the peer marking session without approval is subject to a penalty of 50 per cent of the marks for the assignment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The labs, both assessed and non-assessed, provide practice in programming.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The task is to develop a well-designed OO system that uses lists. The output of this task is a Java solution of one or more classes. You submit Java code for marking by PLATE at https://plate.it.uts.edu.au.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Programming assignment 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">04/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Monday 4 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assignment is marked on correctness by PLATE, based on the match to the model solution’s IO trace. The minimum essential requirement for a pass in this assessment is to complete the tasks worth half the mark.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This programming assignment provides practise and tests for the topics of system design and lists.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The task is to develop a well-designed OO GUI system that uses the MVC framework. The output of this task is a Java program of one or more classes. You submit Java code for marking. This is marked by a combination of automated PLATE marking, peer marking and marking by the subject coordinator. Submit your solution to PLATE at https://plate.it.uts.edu.au.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Programming assignment 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">01/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Monday 1 June 2020See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assignment is marked on correctness. The minimum essential requirement for a pass is to complete tasks worth more than half the marks.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This programming assignment provides practise and tests for the topics of system design, GUIs and MVC.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Answer 40 multiple-choice questions. The exam is open book.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Examination</Data></Cell>
