   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41087</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Applications Studio B</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students create an Individual Learning Contract (ILC), and then have it agreed to by their academic mentor(s). The ILC will be created in Trello, with a structured format and length requirements as noted in the template that will be provided. Students are expected to choose challenging activities that allow them to develop deeper technical expertise in their chosen branch of data engineering. The ILC should describe the following:  Activities that will enable the student to gain the knowledge and skills that will enhance the student’s contribution to the Team and Product/Prototype. Activities that will enable the student to gain extra knowledge and skills that they nominate, and do not necessarily address the Product/Prototype. The knowledge and/or skill that they have chosen to teach to their peers.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual Learning Contract Agreement</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">27/03/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 27 March 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Creation of an Individual Learning Contract allows students to identify and document their learning direction, and set goals for the session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students must submit evidence of their individual work completed throughout the session that demonstrates how they have met the goals articulated in the Individual Learning Contract (ILC). Students' work will be assessed against what was agreed in the ILC. The length and format of the submission will depend upon what activities were chosen in the ILC. Part of this includes teaching the class activity that was agreed in the Individual Learning Contract.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual Learning Contract Finalisation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 5 June 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In finalising the Individual Learning Contract, students demonstrate that they have achieved the goals set near the start of the session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Teams create a written proposal for their Product/Prototype, and have it agreed to by their Product Owner(s) and academic mentor(s). The proposal should include agreed deliverables and a timeline for the work to be carried out. The length of the proposal should be sufficient to fully describe the proposed Product, deliverables and timeline. A template with suggested section headings will be provided as guidance. Teams set up a WiKi on UTSOnline that they will use throughout the session for delivery of the Product outcomes. This assessment task (the proposal) forms the first item to be posted on the WiKi.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Team Product/Prototype Proposal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">03/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 3 April 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Creating a Product/Prototype Proposal allows teams of students to define a scope for their studio work for the current session, and to negotiate the scope and outcomes with the Product Owner(s) and academic mentor(s).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There are three parts to this task:  The working Product or Prototype, which must be demonstrated in class. A presentation delivered in class that describes what was produced, including a demonstration. The length of the presentation will typically be between 10-20 minutes depending upon the number of students in the team. A set of WiKi pages that document the Product/Prototype produced. The number of WiKi pages will depend upon the complexity of the Product/Prototype and the number of students in the team. There must be a history of regular contributions from the proposal stage to delivery, that shows the team's progress over time.  All students must be present in class for the final presentation/demonstration, and all students must have contributed to the WiKi throughout the session. The WiKi should document the process followed, and contributions by individual team members.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Team Product/Prototype Delivery</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12/06/2020</Data></Cell>
