   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49098</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Applied Financial Management</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The Online Problem Sets represent self-directed online resource utilisation within a digital platform. Students are required to engage with the subject material and demonstrate mastery of technical and theoretical knowledge weekly by testing their understanding. Marks will be awarded on the level of mastery achieved prior to the commencement of each week. There will be 10 weekly Online Problem Sets undertaken during the seminar testing each student's skills developed and knowledge constructed of the subject content. These problem sets act as a feedback loop for students to gauge their progression and understanding of the material presented and highlights which learning objectives students need to improve weekly.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Online Problem Sets</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week range</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week  to Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Online Problem Sets focus on applied financial concepts and models to which students must apply analytical skills and understanding of finance influences on business. They consist of a combination of multiple choice, numerical and case study questions. The aim of the Online Problem Sets is to help students develop study habits and address the learning objectives of each week.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment is based on collaborative work among group members for the creation of a financial model for your business. Your group is required to produce a financial model (using the guidelines available in UTSOnline) of your business. It is based on the work that has been, and is being, undertaken in the seminar, online material on UTS and other information which must be researched and /or resourcefully created. For the group assignment, students will be assessed as a team, which means each group member will normally receive the same mark. No complaints about group operation will be considered after the assignment has been submitted. Please see the assignment section of UTSOnline for full details.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">End of Week 10 (Sunday at 11:55 pm)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">End of Week 10 (Sunday at 11:55 pm)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to prepare a financial model for a particular firm in order to analyse the current and future performance using various models and techniques.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Communicating in a face to face environment is an important skill for student’s business career. Presentations are based on and reflecting industry experience and real-world contemporary issues. Each group is required to produce a 15-minute presentation with audio. The presentation is to be delivered in PowerPoint or an alternative digital visual presentation method (e.g., Presi, Keynote etc.) and contain the associated audio of the presentation content (the soundtrack). Students are required to submit their analysis and valuation of the case study online. Students will work in teams and will submit a joint presentation and will allocate the effort across the members of the group. Students are encouraged to come to an agreement on the allocation and procedures for disagreement should anyone not contribute. All group members must contribute to the production of the presentation, and speak on the presentation soundtrack. Assessment marks will be allocated according to both coherent analysis and presentation style. In addition to communicating in a face to face environment, students are required to develop their online communication skills by recording a screencast. The screencast is to explain an aspect of contemporary financial topics both accurately and creatively. Please see the assignments section of UTSOnline for full details.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Online Video Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">End of Week 11</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students have to present the analysis and valuation of their case study in the seminar in order to draw conclusions about the feasibility of expansion/ replacement investment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">End of Week 11</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment develops and assesses collaboration and critical thinking skills among students. Students are required to peer review each other in the presentation assessment. Each group will peer review and provide constructive feedback on two presentations. Failure to participate by any member in peer reviews will result in zero (0) marks for this component of assessment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Peer Review</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to review the presentation of two other groups and assess them in order to give them constructive feedback.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
