   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49118</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Applied Geotechnics</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment 1 is associated with individual problem solving questions. Where feasible, assignments are designed to encourage students to work with a wide range of data inputs and apply conventional and innovative design approaches. This assessment includes two sets of authentic assignments. They require detailed solutions to the given technical problems, preparation of small written reports and completion of a self-learning module. All assignment questions are published on UTSOnline. (Set #1: Assignments 1 to 3)  Assignment 1: Soil mechanics problems Assignment 2: Shallow foundations and retaining wall design Assignment 3: Dewatering systems and design of cofferdams (Set #2: Assignments 4 to 6) Assignment 4: Design of reinforced soil walls Assignment 5: Landfill design and stability Assignment 6: Railway track analysis</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Set #1: Assignments 1 to 3) due date: 25/8/19 by 11:59 pm, submit on UTS-Online &#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;- * Assignment 1: Soil mechanics problems  * Assignment 2: Shallow foundations and retaining wall design  *Assignment 3: Dewatering systems and design of cofferdams  (Set #2: Assignments 4 to 6) due date: 6/10/19 by 11:59 pm, submit on UTS-Online &#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;- * Assignment 4: Design of reinforced soil walls  * Assignment 5: Landfill design and stability  * Assignment 6: Railway track analysis</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Set #1: Assignments 1 to 3) due date: 25/8/19 by 11:59 pm, submit on UTS-Online &#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;- * Assignment 1: Soil mechanics problems  * Assignment 2: Shallow foundations and retaining wall design  *Assignment 3: Dewatering systems and design of cofferdams  (Set #2: Assignments 4 to 6) due date: 6/10/19 by 11:59 pm, submit on UTS-Online &#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;&#45;- * Assignment 4: Design of reinforced soil walls  * Assignment 5: Landfill design and stability  * Assignment 6: Railway track analysis</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Strengthen design skills and problem solving techniques; identify students’ issues in analysis and design, apply corrective measures and give students appropriate feedback. Students will classify, formulate, and solve various problems, and differentiate the different types of solutions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is a group assignment. Each group consists of 3 students.Each group should select one topic from the list and provide a project report (MS-Word) as well as a presentation file (MS-PowerPoint). Students should work as a team, to collect current articles, integrate the related information, compare existing methods, recommend approaches based on their suitability and find at least one appropriate case study associated with their topic. It will be an opportunity for students to practice real world engineering problems and promote their critical thinking and research skills. Different research projects are allocated to each group of students to practice disciplinary research skills. Students will form themselves in small groups, providing a collaborative learning experience. Students can directly connect the defined research projects to one or some of the subject topics; hence, they will be able to understand deeply the issues involved in the subject through research based learning. In main sections please explain the past, the present and the future situations of your research topic if warranted. Design and construction aspects of the selected method can be explained. Some illustrative examples would also be useful. Please provide at least one relevant case study with appropriate details and discussion.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Research Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The presentation file should include at least 45 slides. The length of project report should be at least 30 pages including the title page, table of contents, introduction, background, all main sections, conclusions and the list of references.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">* Project:  Week 11 -13/10/2019 by 11:59 pm (Submit on UTS-Online)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">* Project:  Week 11 -13/10/2019 by 11:59 pm (Submit on UTS-Online)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To engage with research and to encourage students to be research oriented and lifelong learners. To develop research and team work skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment 3 is associated with in class quizzes. Students undertake three open book quizzes in this subject to assess and further develop their understanding of key concepts in applied geotechnics, problem solving skills, engineering decision making and innovative thoughts. Past exam questions with solutions are posted on UTSOnline. Students are expected to review the notes, past exam papers and lecture slides before attending the quiz. Quiz 1: (time allowed: 20-30 minutes) on soil mechanics, shallow foundations and retaining wall design Quiz 2: (time allowed: 20-30 minutes) on dewatering systems, design of cofferdams, design of reinforced soil walls Quiz 3: (time allowed: 20-30 minutes) on landfill design and stability and railway track</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
