   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41165</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Biomaterials and Biomechanics Studio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">For this assessment task, students will be expected to prepare a report detailing the anatomy of the musculoskeletal joint in the healthy and pathological state, epidemiology of the disease, discuss the current treatment strategies, and their efficacy. Students will be expected to present a plan (or preliminary data) for mathematical and computational modelling (in Strand7). The report (and the presentation) should at least have the following items  Title of project: This should be a clear description of your project. Project motivation: Musculoskeletal disorder you are addressing Background and context of the project: Background and context of the project. Aims and objectives: Main objectives of your project. Literature review: This section is a review of the literature, which should outline the most important works that have already been carried out related to your selected project. Research methodology: This section is a broad outline of the methodology (mathematical modelling and Strand7 modelling) you plan to use. Research plan and timelines: This section should summarise the steps and timelines. References: This section is a list of all the references that have been referred to in this report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project plan (Report and Presentation)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentations in Week 5 (19 and 20 August), Report due on 20 August 11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentations in Week 5 (19 and 20 August), Report due on 20 August 11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report and Presentation carry 25% of the final mark</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstration of team’s and individual’s ability on the clinical understanding of chosen musculoskeletal disorder, efficacy of the existing treatment approaches (surgical and non-surgical) using data extracted from the literature. Demonstration of team’s and individual’s ability to develop a feasible plan for mathematical and computational modelling of the musculoskeletal disorder. Demonstration of the team’s ability to write a scientific report (1500 words). Demonstration of the individual’s ability to communicate effectively with peers and general audiences, and answer questions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Groups will be expected to submit a 2500-word final project report detailing their work on a specific musculoskeletal disorder in hip, knee, spine, shoulder, skull or any other musculoskeletal joint. For this assessment task, groups will be expected to prepare their final report (in a journal manuscript format) detailing the clinical question being addressed, research hypothesis, mathematical and computational models developed, results obtained and their interpretation in the clinical context. The report (and the presentation) should at least have the following items  Title of project: This should be a clear description of your project. Abstract: 250-word summary of the entire project (research question, methods, results, and conclusions) Background and context of the project: Background and context of the project. Research Hypothesis: Main objectives of your project. Methods and Materials: This section is a broad outline of the methodology (mathematical modelling and Strand7 modelling) you plan to use. Results: Mathematical modelling and computational modelling results Discussions and conclusion: Discuss your results in the light of clinical data and previous work References: This section is a list of all the references that have been referred to in this report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Project Report (and Presentation)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentations in Week 12 (14 and 15 October), Report due on 15 October 2019 11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentations in Week 12 (14 and 15 October), Report due on 15 October 2019 11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report and Presentation carry 50% of the final mark.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstration of team’s and individual’s ability on the clinical understanding of the chosen musculoskeletal disorder, efficacy of the existing treatment approaches (surgical and non-surgical) using data extracted from the literature. Demonstration of team’s and individual’s ability to develop a realistic mathematical and computational model of the musculoskeletal disorder. Demonstration of the team’s ability to write a scientific report (2500 words). Demonstration of the individual’s ability to communicate effectively with peers and general audiences, and answer questions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Groups are expected to submit their final Strand7 model and solution files for assessment. The model files will be assessed for complexity and errors in pre-processing, solve time errors, and post-processing.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Strand7 Model and Solution files</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
