   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42060</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Biomedical Industry Frameworks</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group of 5 students. The idea Imagine you are a start-up company. You have identified a need/problem in the health or medical technology market that you believe you have the skills to solve. The problem that you are addressing may result in an entirely new product being designed, or an incremental improvement to an existing device already on the market. Approach Recommendation on how to approach this assignment:  Brainstorm or research health issues that exist that are not currently dealt with in an optimal way. You may want to take an existing product and consider broadening its use to a particular market segment when you are doing this (eg 3rd world, remote locations, in-home care, aged care, etc.) Select one issue and its specific market segment to focus on for the assignment. Generate ideas of how you can solve the issue using technology (note – you will not have to conduct any technical design for this assignment. Only high-level technology considerations will be required). Select an initial technology direction / product solution for the problem (very high level only).  What is required  What is the problem you are solving? 1/2 mark Who is the patient population this problem is associated with (describe who typically has this problem, the specific issue you will address, how solving this problem will have a positive impact on them) 1 mark Who will use the device (who is the customer, who is the user?) 1/2 mark Where will the device be used? What is the target market – location/territory. 1/2 mark What is the market size (population size of who suffers from this problem or who will benefit from your device) 1/2 mark Brief overview of how you will address the issue (product solution) - very high level idea only – what is the technology and how does it work. 1 mark Brief overview of how the user will interact with the device. 1 mark  Presentation Provide all of this information in a presentation to the class. The whole group must contribute in some way (not everyone needs to speak). Powerpoint / props / other presentation material are allowed and encouraged. No written submission is required for this assessment – marks are based on information provided in the presentation only.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Pitch</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Time limit = 4 minutes (+ 1-minute Q&amp;A)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">31/03/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Tuesday 31 March 2020              Week 4 - Due in class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 4 - Due in class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students to pitch their topic for the project – provides the opportunity to consider the customer needs first rather than the technology solution. Pitching a new MedTech idea, concisely. Defining a MedTech market need, customer, and conducting initial market research.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design for User - Case Study – Glooko: Getting the need right  Initially, who did Dalal believe was the customer and who was believed to be the end user? 2 marks In the end, who were the actual end customers and who were actual the end users? 2 marks How might this be different in a different market such as Australia or the UK? 2 marks  A1 &amp; 2 &amp; 3 – initially – both customer and user were American diabetes patients. In the end, the customer was the insurer or provider, and the end user was the diabetes patient. It could be different in a different market, as the market dynamics are different, and consumers may expect / be willing to pay for this product, hence the customer and end user may actually be the diabetes patient in both cases.   Using the information provided in the case study, design a smart phone user-interface(s) that reports on the information that BOTH Dalal and Mrs Madra need available to them. Aim to make the look/feel of the interface as simple, easy to use and intuitive as possible, with only the essential information provided. You may design one interface for both users, or two separate interfaces – this is up to you. 8 marks  Mrs Madra needs to inject the proper amount of insulin, and Mr Dalal needs to monitor his diet and overall health to try to avoid becoming a person with diabetes   What is the overarching user needs statement for the Glooko product? 2 marks What are 3 lower level user requirements for the Glooko product? 2 marks Write 2 technical requirements to fulfil each of your 3 user requirements in question 6. 2 marks  5/6/7 - (5) to compare and analyse my diabetes data, simply, accurately, and easily, on one interface, with automatically loaded data. (or similar) 6 &amp; 7 – depend on student’s response.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design for User Case Study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">08/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday 8 May 2020              Week 8</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 8</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Provides specific case study of “design for user” in medical device technology. Understanding design for the user, and how it may be considered within new medical technology developments.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">What is required  What is the problem you are solving? 5 marks Overview of your product / technology 4 marks Overview of the design/development process you will undertake 3 marks Overview of regulatory process – which territories, agencies, types of submissions, key information required for submissions 3 marks Overview of key risks of the device and how you plan to overcome them 3 marks What are the key usability considerations for the product? 4 marks Any gaps or outstanding considerations you still need to address 3 marks  Presentation Provide all of this information in a presentation to the class. The whole group must contribute in some way (not everyone needs to speak). Powerpoint / props / other presentation material are allowed and encouraged.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Time limit = 8 minutes (+ Q&amp;A)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">26/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Tuesday 26 May 2020              Week 11 - In-class presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Provides a complete end-to-end MedTech device development portfolio, from conception of the idea to implementation to market. Group presentation of group work and findings. To provide an overview of the end-to-end process required to deliver a new MedTech device to market.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 11 - In-class presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Formatting  1 submission required per individual – include team name &amp; student number on cover sheet. 15-page limit, including FMEA (plus references &amp; cover sheet). 12-point font, double line spacing. Diagrams or illustrations are encouraged where appropriate to convey the information.  What is required  What is the problem you are solving? 2 marks Who is the target population, what is the market size? 2 marks Describe your product / technology solution and HOW it addresses the problem 2 marks Outline of the design/development process you will undertake 4 marks Outline the regulatory process – which territories, agencies, types of submissions, key information required for submissions 5 marks Overview of key risks of the device and how you plan to overcome them (include an FMEA identifying 10 different risks/failure modes of the product, using the template provided) 10 marks What are the key usability considerations for the product? 5 marks Do you believe there will be IP generated? 5 marks Are there any strong ethical considerations for this project? 5 marks Any gaps or outstanding considerations you still need to address 5 marks Referencing – reference list and in-text referencing required (refer to UTS Harvard reference guide on UTS Library website). 5 marks</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15 page limit, including FMEA (plus references &amp; cover sheet).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday 5 June 2020              Online submission</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Online submission</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Provides a complete end-to-end MedTech device development portfolio, from conception of idea to implementation to market. Individual report is based on group-project topic. To provide an overview of the end-to-end process required to deliver a new MedTech device to market.</Data></Cell>
