    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Provides a complete end-to-end MedTech device development portfolio, from conception of the idea to implementation to market. Group presentation of group work and findings. To provide an overview of the end-to-end process required to deliver a new MedTech device to market.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 11 - In class presentation. 26th May</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Formatting  1 submission required per individual – include team name &amp; student number on cover sheet. 15 page limit, including FMEA (plus references &amp; cover sheet). 12 point font, double line spacing. Diagrams or illustrations are encouraged where appropriate to convey the information.  What is required  What is the problem you are solving? 2 marks Who is the target population, what is the market size? 2 marks Describe your product / technology solution and HOW it addresses the problem 2 marks Outline of the design/development process you will undertake 4 marks Outline the regulatory process – which territories, agencies, types of submissions, key information required for submissions 5 marks  Overview of key risks of the device and how you plan to overcome them (include an FMEA identifying 10 different risks/failure modes of the product, using the template provided) 10 marks   What are the key usability considerations for the product? 5 marks   Do you believe there will be IP generated? 5 marks   Are there any strong ethical considerations for this project? 5 marks   Any gaps or outstanding considerations you still need to address 5 marks   Referencing – reference list and in-text referencing required (refer to UTS Harvard reference guide on UTS Library website). 5 marks</Data></Cell>
