    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Part A due 11:59pm Sunday 19 April. Part B due 11:59pm Sunday 31 May 2020.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Part A due 11:59pm Sunday 19 April. Part B due 11:59pm Sunday 31 May 2020.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment assesses your ability to take notes on LabArchives during your lab activity in the SuperLab between Week 2 and 6 (part A) and between Week 7 and 11 (part B).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">One 10 minute presentation with 5 minutes of question/discussion time. Students will be given an opportunity to present and share their engineering solution to their peers. The theme will have to incorporate elements of biomedical polymers and its application. In your presentation you will include:  literature review; hypothesis and aims; results; discussion and conclusions, students' contribution.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15 minutes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              In class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment develops your ability to present your project that you will work on as a group from week 2 until week 11. During these weeks you will &quot;engineer&quot; and test new tissues using biomedical polymers, cells and 3D bioprinters. Each group will be required to present their project developed in the SuperLab in a professional presentation manner for the class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment develops your ability to summarise your lab activities from week 2 until week 11 that you will present as a group in week 12 (Group Presentation). In your report you will include:  literature review; hypothesis and aims; results; discussion and conclusions, highlighting the student's specific contribution to the project.</Data></Cell>
