   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41164</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Biomedical and Assistive Devices Studio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">(A) Write a valid Project system specification that helps in build and test the system. It should include requirements analysis, the functional specification describes what has to be implemented, the Systems architecture that describes how the functions will be realized using a chosen prototypical systems development, and testing procedure based on functional specification. The group can choose any mothed that includes IEEE SRS or others but needs to involve drawing or graphically designed, Functional design, Functional specifications and Non-functional specifications. (B) Write a valid Project literature review. This Project literature review should include at least the following parts:  Title of project: This should be a clear description of your project. Project motivation: what a problem that project will help to solve and what the functional and economic results (if any) Background and context of the project: This section should explain the background and context of the project. Aims and objectives: This section should spell out three objectives for your project. Literature review: This section is a review of the literature which should outline the most important works that have already been carried out in relation to your selected project. Research methodology: This section is a broad outline of the methodology you plan to use. Resources required: This section outlines the resources required for the project. Research plan and timetable: This section should summarise the steps and approximate timing. References: This section is a list of all the references that have been referred to in this report. Appendix A: the journal book of the team. The project should have a journal that includes weekly one-page documents (extra pages allowed) that designed to keep your client informed on: what happened during the last week; your thoughts and recommendations on those events; and your current short-term plan.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project stage 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Minimum 2500 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">4</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 4              week starting 30 March 2020, it is due at the start of the Lab time. Please submit online.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">week starting 30 March 2020, it is due at the start of the Lab time. Please submit online.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project system specification 10% Assessment: Project literature review 10%</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstrate the ability to get proper sources, familiarity with the knowledge, analysis of existing research, and writing functional specification and functional requirements to implement the project. Demonstrate the ability of academic writing and project management.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report the design and the design justification decisions. Demonstration working project in early stages. Presentation  The presentation duration is 10 minutes for presentation and five minutes for questions. Maximum marks allocated for presentation: 15% Marks will be awarded based on the content not duration. The presentation will be marked as a team as well as on an individual basis. Each team member responsibility is to have knowledge that covers the whole project. The presentation questions, each team member may be asked several questions about the whole project (not just her/his task) that have been learned in the doing the project and then used in the implementation. Each team member is expected to know exactly how the project implementation works and be able to justify the design choices which have been made. If the team member fails to answer the questions with the appropriate substance then she/he will be awarded zero for the entire Assessment task 2: Project stage 2. All enrolled students must be available to make the presentation. All students must stay in the classroom until all the presentations are over. Students who miss the presentation need to make alternative arrangements by emailing the subject coordinator. The marks will be considered individually marked, each group must go ahead with their presentation even if some of their group members are absent.  General guidelines Each team should present a demonstration of teamwork and individual ability of project design and early functional implantations, and demonstration of the ability to the early stage of the project working. The presentation should provide information about the project title, the motivations behind the project, high-level information about the project, the design approach, the part of early-stage working, and the teamwork and individual task. The team may be considered:  Session (semester) planning, when tasks are to be completed, who does what, recognition of major issues Criteria for successful completion Others like presentation style and professionalism.  The individual members can use the items below to reflect on their levels of contribution to the project:  The ability to work with other team members. The ability to motivate other team members. The ability to overcome difficulties. The ability to generate ideas. Attendance and timekeeping. Taking a fair share of the work.  Report The Report length is from 2500 to 4000 words plus an additional extra pages for the references and the appendices. The report mark is 20%, it will be rewarded based on the team and as well as an individual. General guidelines Each team should take care of the report style and report technical content. Each team needs to submit one report that may be having the following sections:  Introduction Context and overview of the project and its motivations. Project Management: A project plan for what had been done and what required for the rest of the semester. Design and Specification: Each project component (unit, block, or task) can be defined using some formal method from systems/software engineering and plan, together with ‘plain’ English to aid explanation. The implementations of early stages. The test specification and the test results with descriptions particularly how it works. Each team member task and work contribution with a link to the design, implementation, test, and documentation. Conclusion: Summarise your findings Appendix A: the journal book of the team, each team member task/ time. Appendix B onwards: design, figures, graphs, diagrams, drawing, code, components list, etc.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project stage 2 (Report and Presentation)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">35</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7              week starting 27 April 2020 at Lab time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">week starting 27 April 2020 at Lab time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstration of team work and individual ability of project design and early functional implantations. Demonstration of ability to early stage of the project working.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There are several different kinds of projects for students to select. After selecting a project, the students are asked to design a functional project that may be including: a. Design of various required algorithms. b. Design and implement of hardware and software. c. Test of system performance of the real time. d. Perform an oral presentation for the demonstration of project work. e. Write a report Presentation  The presentation duration is 15 minutes for presentation and five minutes for questions. Maximum marks allocated for presentation: 25%. The marks will be awarded on the content, not duration. The presentation will be marked as a team as well as on an individual basis. Each team member's responsibility is to have knowledge that covers the whole project. During the presentation questions, each team member may be asked several questions based on the whole project (not just her/his task) that have been learned in the doing the project and then used in the implementation. Each team member is expected to know exactly how the project implementation works and be able to justify the design choices. If the team member fails to answer the questions with the appropriate substance, then she/he will be awarded zero for the entire Assessment task 3: Project stage 3. All enrolled students must be available to make the presentation. All students must stay in the classroom until all the presentations are over. Students who miss the presentation need to make alternative arrangements by emailing the subject coordinator. As the team will be considered individually marked, each group must go ahead with their presentation even if some of their group members are absent.  General guidelines The demonstration is for the entire system in operation, ready for acceptance by the client (the subject staff). Each team should present a demonstration of teamwork and individual ability of project design and functional implantations, and demonstration of the project work. The presentation should provide information about the project title, the motivations behind such a project, high-level information for the project, the design approach, functional working, and the teamwork and individual task. The team may be considered:  Implementations, the critical design choices, and the changes since the previous presentation. Present a satisfactory contribution to the development of the project (both in terms of performing assigned tasks and contribution to the team). The completion of system design and implementation that meets the requirements of the project. Others like presentation style and professionalism.  The individual members can use the items below to reflect on their levels of contribution to the project:  Reflect on her/his learning about:   Group work Technical and teamwork interaction challenges What the different approach that may be considered to do the project of her/his part.   The ability to motivate other team members. The ability to generate ideas. Attendance and timekeeping. Taking a fair share of the work.  Report The Report length is from 2500 to 4000 words plus additional extra pages for the references and the appendices. The report mark is 20%, awarded based on the team as well as the individual. General guidelines Each team should take care of the report style and report technical content. Each team needs to submit just one report that may be having the following sections:  Introduction Context and overview of the project and its motivations. Project Management: A project plan for what had been done during the whole project progress. Design and Specification: Each project component (unit, block, or task) can be defined using some formal method from systems/software engineering and plan, together with ‘plain’ English to aid explanation. Changes to the project implementation since the previous Assignment The implementations and critical design choice for the final stages. The completion of system design and implementation that meets the requirements of the project. The test specification and the test results with descriptions particularly how it works. Analysis of test report and discussion of results of the test report also defend any shortcomings of the system and future development Conclusion: Summarize the project and results. Appendices:  Appendix A: the journal book of the team. It also needs to include:  Each team member task/ time, each team member task and work contribution with a link to the design, implementation, test, and documentation. Each team member technical and teamwork interaction challenges. Each team member reflects on what different approach that may be considered to do the project of his part.  Appendix B onwards: design, figures, graphs, diagrams, drawing, code, components list, etc.</Data></Cell>
