   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49131</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Bridge Design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are supposed to individually provide a demands diagram and prioritise the requirements. They also have to produce engineering drawings for the proposed bridges and justify selection of proposed bridge types in a brief report. This will be an individual assignment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Concept Design of a Bridge, i.e. Selecting Loads and Structural System</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">09/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6.00pm Thursday 9 April 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment relates to topics covered in lectures 1-2 and involves two different conceptual bridge designs for the client.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are supposed to individually perform computer modelling and analysis in order to design the reinforced concrete deck with some prestressing where appropriate. In addition, they have to calculate design tensile forces in the cables and find the maximum axial and lateral load on the pylon. This will be an individual assignment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Analysis and Design of a Bridge</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">14/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6.00pm Thursday 14 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment relates to topics covered in lectures 3-5 and involves designing a typical bridge. The actual type of bridge will be specified in the project brief such as a cable stayed bridge across a river with concrete deck.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment relates to topics covered in lecture 9 and involves different hydrologic and hydraulic aspects of bridge design such as finding the rainfall intensity, the average recurrence interval and the maximum flow rate. This will be an individual assignment worth 10% of the overall mark.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Hydrologic and Hydraulic Aspects of Bridge Design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">04/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6.00pm Thursday 4 June 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment relates to topics covered in lecture 9 and involves different hydrologic and hydraulic aspects of bridge design such as finding the rainfall intensity, the average recurrence interval and the maximum flow rate. This will be an individual assignment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task consists of four online quizzes which each quiz worth 2.5% of the overall mark. Each individual quiz includes different aspects of bridge design covered in the lectures.</Data></Cell>
