   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">31245</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Business Process and IT Strategy</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Online discussion and analysis of relevant articles/real-world examples during tutorials. These topics will explore key topics supporting/complementing the subject matter. Students are required to participate in online discussion board forum and review/ analyze the required articles.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Topic review and discussion</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week range</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 3 to Week 11              Part A (Online participation) - See discussion board for activities and deadline. Post open for discussion will be announced via UTSonline. Part B (Tutorial class activities): See the tutorials schedule available online. Submission at the end of your weekly tutorial class.  For more information see further information and assessment-1 outline available online.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Part A (Online participation) - See discussion board for activities and deadline. Post open for discussion will be announced via UTSonline. Part B (Tutorial class activities): See the tutorials schedule available online. Submission at the end of your weekly tutorial class.  For more information see further information and assessment-1 outline available online.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To demonstrate an in-depth understanding of the concept of IT strategy and business processes based on scholarly articles and real-world case studies.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Apply knowledge, theories, and insights gained during lectures and tutorials to a chosen case study. This is a group assessment. Students will be asked to prepare a report and present their understanding.  Students will work in a project group to develop a business and IT strategic plan in response to a proposal request. Based on the provided scenario and additional research, the groups will be required to formulate/present a report for a business. This report will include an analysis of the company using Information Systems Strategy Triangle (business strategy, organisational strategy, and IT strategy), social business strategy, and information resources strategy. Full details will be available at the subject site (UTSOnline) in week 2.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study review, discussion and presentation (team work)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Min 2000 Words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Wednesday 20 May 2020              Week 10. Online submission via Turnitin. For more information see assessment-2 outline available online.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 10. Online submission via Turnitin. For more information see assessment-2 outline available online.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To apply knowledge and theories gained during lectures and tutorials to develop an optimal strategic business &amp; IT plan.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment includes in-class/tutorial quiz. Quiz questions contain multiple choice questions, fill in the blanks, matching words, true/ false and/or a real–world case study with a set of questions about the topics covered in the lectures.</Data></Cell>
