   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">31269</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Business Requirements Modelling</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment item includes 10 individual closed-book short quizzes conducted in seminars and professional engagement in the workshop tasks in class each week. Short quizzes are held for 12 minutes each, mostly at the start of the seminar session. Questions in the quiz are of a short answer format and each quiz will contain a maximum of 3 questions. Each quiz is worth 1.5% and assessed in weeks 3 to 12. The quizzes will measure the degree that the theory, as taught in the subject and practiced by the individual in subject assignments, seminars and workshops, is understood by each individual student. 0.5% is allocated for professional engagement each week in the workshop classes. Professional engagement involves engaging in discussion and argument, asking insightful questions, and working in teams to achieve outcomes. The mark for this task is cumulative, and is based on the quality of a student’s spoken and written participation in weekly individual, small group and whole class workshop and homework/online activities. Additionally, in-class informal mini-presentations and group activities will also contribute to this task. Each week, immediate formative feedback will be provided by the lecturer straight after the completion of weekly quiz. Quiz marks will be uploaded to UTSOnline gradebook each week. This will allow students to track their progress in the subject regularly.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Short Quizzes and Professional Engagement</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There is no word limit.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Short Quizzes will be conducted on UTS Online each week on Monday from 10  to 10:15 a.m. and assessed in weeks 3 to 12.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Short Quizzes will be conducted on UTS Online each week on Monday from 10  to 10:15 a.m. and assessed in weeks 3 to 12.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment will require a group of maximum 6 students to assess the Case Study and for the group to produce a report containing Business Process Model, Data Model and Data Dictionary. Students will work on this case study each week in class in the workshop (and seminar) and also outside the class to produce drafts of their diagrams/models. Each week, students will be required to bring their work in progress to workshop sessions so as to get face to face formative feedback from their tutors before the formal submission deadline. This will enable the students to identify and correct any issues before formal submission, and consequently improve their learning and performance in the assignment. Additional information about the Case Study and detailed assessment criteria and other details will be provided in the assignment specification.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Requirements Analysis Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The recommended word limit for this assignment is maximum 1000 words excluding diagrams, bibliography and appendices. Word limit will be regarded as recommended rather than compulsory, and no student will be disadvantaged by being under or over the recommended word limit.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday 04/05/2020 at 8 a.m.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday 04/05/2020 at 8 a.m.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment will require a group of maximum 6 students to assess the same case study as Assignment 1 (Requirements Analysis Report) and produce a report containing several UML diagrams, functional requirements using user stories and use cases, and non-functional requirements as parts of software requirement specifications. Students will work on this case study each week in class in the workshop (and seminar) and also outside the class to produce drafts of their diagrams/models. Each week, students will be required to bring their work in progress to workshop sessions so as to get face to face formative feedback from their tutors before the formal submission deadline. This will enable the students to identify and correct any issues before formal submission, and consequently improve their learning and performance in the assignment. Additional information about the case study and detailed assessment criteria and other details will be provided in the assignment specification.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">OO Requirements Analysis and Specification Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">18</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The recommended word limit for this assignment is maximum 3000 words excluding diagrams, bibliography and appendices. Word limit will be regarded as recommended rather than compulsory, and no student will be disadvantaged by being under or over the recommended word limit.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday 08/06/2020 at 8 a.m.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday 08/06/2020 at 8 a.m.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The open-book final exam will test your understanding of all the topics and models taught in the subject. It will include a short case study and most exam questions will be based on this case study requiring students to draw various models. There may also be some quiz-style short-answer questions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The exam will be 2 hours in duration.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
