   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48016</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Capstone Project Part A</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are registered through the intranet. An email is automatically sent to the supervisor. The supervisor then needs to “agree and accept” or “decline” the students request.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Registration</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The Registration form is the Faculty’s way of linking you, your project, an academic supervisor, and the allocated project number</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Writing a report to plan their study allows students to reflect their understanding of the theory and possible applications in order to demonstrate their level of competency in the following: Understanding context and needs  Give a brief qualitative description of your topic, as well as a precise statement of the project Identify what contributions the project can make to the engineering community in terms of scholarship, novel design, validation and verification of a method or model Describe why you think you are suitable to undertake the project by giving a brief description of your track record, in the area of the topic  Refining the project  Describe the specific objectives and the value of the project Describe the viability of the project. Identify the key technical assumptions  Planning the project  Identify other non-technical assumptions such as economic, social, cultural, etc on which the project is based and to what extend you will be able to address them State different stages and methodologies of the project. State possible software requirements and reasons State any equipment and facilities available and that you intend to use State what, if any, data that you will need to obtain or generate Give at least 3 references you have identified academically accessible, appropriate and relevant to the project Provide a realistic timeline for your project completion Identify a broad range of foreseeable risks associated with the undertaking of the project Provide the list of references used in preparing the proposal Identify learning needs and how these will be assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Proposal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10-15 pages</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">4</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 4</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The Proposal is intended to be a detailed planning document for the capstone project. Its purpose is to discuss the project with the supervisor, identify approximate timelines and meeting dates. The proposal provides the basis of a contractual agreement between the student and her/his supervisor regarding project objectives.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The progress report should include  Goals which you set for the session Comment on progress in relation to the goals, work plans and achievements Problems or issues which affected your progress and the identified strategies to overcome them A comprehensive review of the literature related to your project area which places the work in a broader body of knowledge. Comment on the involvement of external or industry supervisor. Details of any changes to the proposal and updated version of the proposal.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Progress Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">70</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10-20 pages</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 2 of Assesment period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The Progress Report is intended to describe in adequate detail the progress made during the first session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 of Assesment period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
