   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">31016</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Career Management for IT Professionals</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Resume: 20% (Marking time 15m) Students submit a Resume via turnitin. The letter is in response to a job ad that the students find online. They are encouraged to do this in response to graduate positions in their relevant field. Cover Letter: 20% (Marking time 15m) Students submit a Cover letter via Turnitin. The letter is in response to a job ad that the students find online. They are encouraged to do this in response to graduate positions in their relevant field.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Job applications</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Length of all components in this assessment may be found on UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">As per program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">As per program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To prepare students for real-world job applications.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will prepare an application for a job within the IT sector. They will conduct a group interview conducted by someone within the IT industry. 15% interview performance Interviewers from industry conduct group interviews and mark each student on a marking matrix. 10% interview reflection Students submit a max. 2-page reflection on their interview performance and areas of improvement. This also encourages the students to reflect on teamwork and personality content covered in class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Interview</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">As per program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">As per program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To prepare students for a group interview.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will learn how to work within a team and using a specific methodology, scrum. 15% Trello Review Students will be taught Trello in the first class. Trello is a simple and free task management system widely used in industry. Students will be allocated into groups and will be given guidelines on using the system to manage their assignment submissions. Students will be given 10mins in each class to conduct a standup meeting and update each other on their assignment process. At the end of the session, the groups Trello board will be marked according to a marking matrix. 10% Reflection Students submit a max 2-page reflection on their Trello usage and the weekly standups.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Planning Board</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">As per program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">For students to become technically proficient in an industry-standard project management software and methodology.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">As per program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
