   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49255</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Catchment Modelling</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are asked to design a conceptual model of water flow through a catchment and to write a report describing and justifying the generic processes and flow paths included in their model.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1-Conceptual Catchment Model</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10-15 pages</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday (midnight) two weeks after the week in which Block 1 was held.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday (midnight) two weeks after the week in which Block 1 was held.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are asked to analyse the calibration of a catchment model through comparison of recorded and predicted data, and to suggest suitable approaches to improve the calibration. Outcomes of this analysis are to be presented as a report to a boss.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 2-Model Calibration</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10 page report presented to a line manager.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday (midnight) two weeks after the week in which Block 2 was held.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday (midnight) two weeks after the week in which Block 2 was held.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students have to predict the runoff hydrograph from a catchment using alternative process models. These alternative predictions are to be compared and a report prepared presenting the two hydrographs and reasons for any differences (if any) between the two alternative process models.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 3-Hydrograph Generation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5 - 10 page report exclusive of calculations that are to be included as appendices to the report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday (midnight) two weeks after the week in which Block 3 was held.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday (midnight) two weeks after the week in which Block 3 was held.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Examination</Data></Cell>
