   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48530</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Circuit Analysis and Design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Labs 1, 2 and 6 are Groupwork design tasks, each with a laboratory to test your design. You must work as a team and submit a single report, for which you will both be given the same mark. Lab 1: After confirming your understanding of the step response of first order circuits, as a team of two, you will apply that theory to the design of a flashing light circuit for a given specification. Lab 2: As a team of two, decide how you will achieve optimum power transfer in a wireless power transfer circuit, and test your theory in the lab session. Lab 6: As a team of two, determine parameters to achieve an active filter of given specification, and test your theory in the lab session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Groupwork Laboratory Assignments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">18</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab 1: 27/03/2020, 18:00. Lab 2: 3/04/2020, 18:00. Lab 6: 22/05/2020, 18:00.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab 1: 27/03/2020, 18:00. Lab 2: 3/04/2020, 18:00. Lab 6: 22/05/2020, 18:00.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assess students' achievement of their groupwork design projects and their testing in the laboratory.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There will be 2 Quizzes, each marked out of 6%.  The quizzes will be Restricted open book – see Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Tutorial Quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 1 at the start of tutorials in Week 7 (which commences 27/04/2020). Quiz 2 at the start of tutorials in Week 10 (which commences 18/05/2020).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 1 at the start of tutorials in Week 7 (which commences 27/04/2020). Quiz 2 at the start of tutorials in Week 10 (which commences 18/05/2020).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To encourage students to spread the learning load evenly throughout the session, to provide timely feedback on their understanding.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Labs 3, 4 and 5 are labs with testing undertaken as a team but with each individual team member writing and submitting their own report. Lab 3 examines steady-state sinusoidal single-phase circuits. Lab 4 examines sinusoidal three-phase circuits, including unbalanced circuits. Lab 5 examines the passive, series RLC, band-pass filter.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual Laboratory Assignments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">18</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab 3 Assignment due 10/04/2020, 18:00. Lab 4 Assignment due 17/04/2020, 18:00. Lab 5 Assignment due 15/05/2020, 18:00.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assess students' understanding of the material covered in the laboratory sessions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab 3 Assignment due 10/04/2020, 18:00. Lab 4 Assignment due 17/04/2020, 18:00. Lab 5 Assignment due 15/05/2020, 18:00.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">For a given product specification, students must design a circuit, broken into subcircuits, purchase the components, build and test the circuit, and write a report. Individual students will be assessed on their design and test of their own subcomponent (6%) and the team will receive a group mark (6%) for the overall testing and documentation on the whole circuit as a product.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5/06/2020, 18:00 See also Further information.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5/06/2020, 18:00 See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assess students' ability to work as a team to draw from and extend the knowledge they have gained in the Subject to design a circuit to meet a product specification.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The final exam will test your understanding of the subject contents, including Second order circuits, Sinusoidal steady-state analysis (phasors), Sinusoidal steady-state power calculation, balanced three-phase circuits, Laplace transformation and its use in circuit analysis, Convolution, Bode Plots, Frequency selective circuits, Active filter circuits, Fourier series, and Two-ports circuits. Please note that knowledge from prerequisite subjects, as revised in early chapters of the textbook, may be required. Restricted open book Exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 hours plus 10 minutes reading time</Data></Cell>
