   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">31247</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Collaborative Business Processes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are to:  Select a topic from the list provided by the instructors Review of the literature on the topic Critically evaluate the research Include case studies</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Literature Review</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Literature review</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Max 4000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments are due Sunday night before class on the weeks specified in the calendar.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments are due Sunday night before class on the weeks specified in the calendar.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To understand the problem domain, tools and limitations clearly and deeply before generating ideas or solutions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment #2- Part 1 a) Formulate Problem Collaboratively  The students will formulate collaboratively a single problem.  In order to formulate the problem, the students make use of at least two primary sources of inputs.  Literature search carried out earlier informs the formulation of the problem. The selection of problems must be supported by evidence from evolving practice and academic and professional literature.  Importantly, the students will divide themselves into sub-groups, where one group would act as stakeholders and specify the problem, while other group would act as consultant. The groups would swap and take turns to develop the problem.     (b) Co-design Criteria for Evaluation The students will also co-design evaluation criteria for project work.  Assignment #2- Part 2 Based on the problem formulated, the students will: (a) Evaluate Alternatives (b) Develop a Solution (on paper)  Assignment #2- Part 3 (a) Proposal Development After developing solution, the students develop a proposal. (b) Presentation Finally, the student groups will also present and defend their problem formulation and solution in class and respond to questions raised by their lecturer and peers. The report(s) will have individual sections marked out. The marks for the reportcomp take into account the following components:  Overall final artefacts produced Quality of collaboration Individual contributions  Quality of collaboration and extent of individual contributions will be demonstrated, and in turn assessed, based on various artefacts including comments in discussion boards, video recordings, written reports, peer and observer evaluations of interactions as well as instructor spot evaluations and inspections. Rubric for this will be provided on the UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Collaborative Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report: maximum 8000 words; Presentation: @ (each person 4 mins) (+ PPT slides).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments are due Sunday night before class on the weeks specified in the calendar.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments are due Sunday night before class on the weeks specified in the calendar.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To demonstrate the application of tools taught by collaboratively formulating problem, providing solution, and developing a proposal based on that.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each group member will be marked individually based on their performance on the evaluation, reflection tasks against a codesigned criteria sheet. Assignment #3- Part 1 The student groups will be matched with each other, so some sections of the student performance would be observed by another group, who record the sessions and provide their feedback and commentary as part of evaluation. The students would also evaluate the projects summatively at the end using the evaluation criteria they had designed as a class. Assignment #3- Part 2 The students are encouraged to keep a Journal describing, and reflecting on, thier personal experience in a Collaboratory process that they undertook during your project work. Using this, the students will use reflection strategies to enhance students’ personal contributions to the workplace. In this reflective task, the students ask themselves questions such as what went well, what did not go well, how they could improve these in the future etc. It is understood that the reflection would be subjective.The marking will be for the quality of questions they ask themselves and how they describe, rather than actual content of the answer.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Collaborative Project, Evaluation and Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Generally, assignments are due Sunday night before class on the weeks specified in the calendar; however, for this assignment, submission request may be split and self-reflection can be submitted after the last class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To reflect on the effect of whole experience associated with peer review and evaluation of work of peers to oneself.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Generally, assignments are due Sunday night before class on the weeks specified in the calendar; however, for this assignment, submission request may be split and self-reflection can be submitted after the last class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Answer a few multiple choice and structured questions based on the lecture resources and tools offered in the class. Quiz would also be employed as pre-requisite to launching into project. It is important that the student is prepared to learn these early. Two quizzes would be employed. Best grade would be chosen. They have two attempts to get it right.</Data></Cell>
