   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49202</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Communication Protocols</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A 55 minute online quiz will be held on the dates specified in the program. You must be present to obtain a mark for the quiz. Late arrivals may be refused entry to the quiz room. In the tutorial immediately following the quiz, there may be an opportunity to retake the quiz collaboratively with access to notes and ressources. Your quiz mark for the final assessment will be composed of a weighted combination of your individual quiz score and collaborative quiz score.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Review Quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 1 : 13:00 on 26/03/2020;  Quiz 2 : 13:00 on 09/04/2020;  Quiz 3 : 13:00 on 30/04/2020.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 1 : 13:00 on 26/03/2020;  Quiz 2 : 13:00 on 09/04/2020;  Quiz 3 : 13:00 on 30/04/2020.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Regular quizzes are held each block to give students feedback on the progress in understanding key concepts and procedures. The quiz questions are of a similar style and level of difficulty as the external online exam required for certification for the Alcatel-Lucent Networking Routing Specialist 1 program.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will retrieve an obfuscated Mininet lab exam script via Git, which they will execute in their virtual machine image. Using this script, you will need to complete a series of tasks on the emulated network, including (but not limited to) traffic analysis, route analysis, port scans, and various types of performance testing. Performance metrics may include measurements such as latency, jitter, packet loss and throughput. You will be expected to describe exactly how you performed each test that you used and provide a technically accurate interpretation of the results. The task will be a restricted open-book exam.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory Test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">TBD - we will discuss this in class as this is the first time we will run the lab exam. It will either be at the end of the Friday of Block 3 OR one or two weeks after, but a final decision will be made in consultation with students. Multiple scheduling options may be offered to accommodate all students.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">TBD - we will discuss this in class as this is the first time we will run the lab exam. It will either be at the end of the Friday of Block 3 OR one or two weeks after, but a final decision will be made in consultation with students. Multiple scheduling options may be offered to accommodate all students.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Completeness (50%) - Did you complete all parts of the lab examination? Did you miss any important faults or significant deviations between the expected and actual network behaviour? Have you adequately interpreted each of your observations? Accuracy (50%) - How accurate and precise were your measurements and observations? Did you correctly calculate any required efficiencies, overheads, throughputs, latencies or other metrics? Did you correctly apply appropriate statistical methods (e.g. calculation of means, standard deviations etc.)?</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab activities allow students to link theory and practice using industry standard tools and techniques. Students will capture packets using the 'wireshark' software, and analyse the composition, flow and timing of packets and frames in a very similar way to what a professional telecommunication engineer would do in configuring and troubleshooting a real-world network. In the lab exam, students will demonstrate their capabilities to analyse traffic, identify faults and measure network performance in a simulated network environment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This will be an online exam, 2 hours in length. You will permitted to bring one double-sided A4 page of handwritten (i.e. not typed), original (i.e. not photocopied or reproduced in any form) notes into the exam. This sheet may contain anything you like, as long as it is handwritten and original</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">08/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">01:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1.00pm Friday 8 May 2020              The exam runs from 13:00 to 15:30.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This provides an opportunity for students to demonstrate their individual understanding of key concepts and procedures as would be used in an industrial setting</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The exam runs from 13:00 to 15:30.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Take the online IP addressing test during the class time as specified in the program. You must achieve a minimum mark of 80% in this test to be considered as a 'pass'. You have up to 3 attempts to pass this test. Your highest successful test result of the three attempts will be used in the calculation of the result for this assessment task. If you score less than 80%, you will fail the task and receive a mark of 0.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">IP Addressing Test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">IP Test attempt 1 : 12:00 on 26/03/2020;  IP Test attempt  2 : 12:00 on 09/04/2020;  IP Test attempt  3 : 12:00 on 30/04/2020.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">IP Test attempt 1 : 12:00 on 26/03/2020;  IP Test attempt  2 : 12:00 on 09/04/2020;  IP Test attempt  3 : 12:00 on 30/04/2020.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assure that all sudents passing the subject have a minimum level of understanding of critically important concepts such as IP addressing, subnetting and supernetting. The style of questions and level of difficulty are similar to the computer based exam for the Alcatel-Lucent Networking Routing Specialist 1 industry certification (which also has a minimum pass rate of 80%)</Data></Cell>
