   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">31265</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Communication for IT Professionals</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is an individual assessment task that builds your skills in finding, evaluating and referencing information sources. You will investigate and evaluate information to become familiar with the context of the future team project, critically evaluating the information and sources to synthesise your research into a written summary. You will write a summary of the research that you have conducted so far, ensuring that information sources found and used are reliable and relevant, and are referenced correctly in your summary. The information collected will be collated in a digital collage by your team to get a better understanding of the ethical, social, cultural, economic and environmental issues surrounding your design interest area.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual Background Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">500 words excluding references</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">23/08/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 23 August 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To develop report writing skills based on finding, evaluating and referencing information relevant to the team project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Use the information collated in Task 1a and the team meeting to identify alternative solutions to the chosen problem. Next, justify the selection of one solution which best meets the needs of the community. Finally, use the template on UTSOnline to write up your proposal. The proposal will:   clearly outline the problem  explain what your team will design and implement.  The proposal is a planning document that helps make decisions about the necessary work to develop the design solution. Social, ethical, cultural and budgetary considerations must be taken into account.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">EWB Challenge Team Proposal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">4000 words (excluding title page, table of contents, reference list, appendices)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">13/09/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 13 September 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To propose a design solution that reflects social, environmental and ethical impacts.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Write a report that summarises your design solution. Your team will communicate, document and justify your design solution for the EWB Challenge in a written report using the template. This report will explain your decision making, problem solving, project design, and development through collaborative teamwork and project management. The role of each individual in writing this report needs to be recorded.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">EWB Challenge Team Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5000 words (excluding title page, executive summary, table of contents, reference list and appendices)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">18/10/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 18 October 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To communicate to a professional standard a design solution.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Your EWB Challenge project team must give an online presentation to the members of your tutorial class about your design solution. All team members are expected to speak as part of a coordinated oral presentation by your team. Visual aids in the form of a slideshow or similar are required to support your team’s presentation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">EWB Challenge Team Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20-minute presentation, at least 3-minute presentation per team member</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              In tutorial classes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In tutorial classes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To professionally present a design solution to an audience of your peers.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Use the narrative reflection you created as a group in week 5 and adapt it to your learning story at the culmination of the subject. This is presented through a diagram and through an oral presentation which is recorded online. In addition, provide a reflection which looks back on the group learning contract created in week 4 and assess how this worked out in practice.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Narrative reflections</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">500 words</Data></Cell>
