   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32003</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Computer Game Design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is a group assignment. Design and construct a board game in a randomly assigned group. This assessment evaluates students' abilities to brainstorm and negotiate ideas with diverse group members and then effectively playtest and enhance your designs in an iterative cycle. The grade is divided between the overall quality of the game (as playtested by other students in the class) as well as the documentation that each group member keeps about the design and playtest process. Details will be provided in the assignment specification sheet.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design &amp; Build a Board Game</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">14/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Tuesday 14 April 2020              Released - Week 1.  Hardware Submission and Peer Review Playtests - Week 5 Lab  Soft Copy Submission - Start of Week 6 (Tuesday 14th April, before 11:59pm)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Released - Week 1.  Hardware Submission and Peer Review Playtests - Week 5 Lab  Soft Copy Submission - Start of Week 6 (Tuesday 14th April, before 11:59pm)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is an individual, online, open-book quiz to test knowledge on the Unity game engine after completing the relevant tutorial material.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Unity Fundamentals Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 15 May 2020              Quiz to be completed in students' own time on Canvas before the end of Week 9 (Friday 15th May before 11:59pm)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz to be completed in students' own time on Canvas before the end of Week 9 (Friday 15th May before 11:59pm)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is an individual assignment. Present a critique report on a digital game based on the concepts taught in class. Students should choose an existing and accessible digital game to critique. The report should critique the design of the chosen game in terms of the concepts discussed during the lectures, including formal elements, dramatic elements, and dynamic systems. More information about this assessment will be made available through UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Game Critique</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">01/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 1 May 2020              Released - Week 3.  Report due on Canvas by the end of Week 7 (Friday 1st May, before 11:59pm).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Released - Week 3.  Report due on Canvas by the end of Week 7 (Friday 1st May, before 11:59pm).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is a group assignment. Design a digital game as a group using a modern game engine. This is a chance for students to reinforce what they learned in the board game assessment and go further with more complexity in their game design, scoping their designs to be within the skill set of their group, and overcoming software development challenges in a digital game engine. Again, the grade will be divided between the overall quality of the game and the documentation that is kept throughout the iterative design process. Details will be provided in a separate assignment specification sheet.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design &amp; Build a Digital Game</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 5 June 2020              Released - Week 6.  Peer review playtests - Week 12 Labs.  Soft Copy Submission - End of Week 12 (Friday 5th June, before 11:59pm).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Released - Week 6.  Peer review playtests - Week 12 Labs.  Soft Copy Submission - End of Week 12 (Friday 5th June, before 11:59pm).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is a group assignment. Design a digital game as a group using a modern game engine and submit a group report. Details will be provided in a separate assignment specification sheet.</Data></Cell>
