   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32501</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Computer Graphics</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This quiz is in an open-book / open internet format and is to be completed during the lab of the specified week. The quiz will be completed on UTSOnline and students will be provided with a code in the lab to access the quiz. This is an individual assessment and students are expected to complete the quiz without communicating with other students.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 6              at home online test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">at home online test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task assesses student knowledge on the content presented within the first half of the session, including ray tracing vs raster, coordinate systems, camera views, vector and matrix mathematics, lighting, and shading.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This quiz is in an open-book / open internet format and is to be completed during the lab of the specified week. The quiz will be completed on UTSOnline and students will be provided with a code in the lab to access the quiz. This is an individual assessment and students are expected to complete the quiz without communicating with other students.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              at home online test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">at home online test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task assesses student knowledge on the content presented within the first half of the session, including the OpenGL pipeline, 3D modeling representations, texturing methods, and shaders.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment is linked to the the “Group Graphics Project - Code and Application Quality” assessment task. Groups are required to present their project to the rest of the class, with each group member talking about the the contributions that they made to the project. Each group will have 10 minutes, including time to present and time for the lecturer and peers to ask questions. Students will be assessed on the degree of their contribution to the project and on the depth of their knowledge on their contribution areas. More detailed specifications of this assessment will be released on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Graphics Project - Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12 In-class presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task assess individual contributions to the group project and the extent of each individual’s knowledge via a presentation and open dialogue with the lecturer. It is also a chance for students to see what other groups have worked on and gain inspiration through collegial discourse.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12 In-class presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will work in groups of 3-5 members to produce a substantial and authentic offline 3D web application prototype. Groups will have the choice of working on one of small number of specified application, though groups may propose their own application designs in discussion with the lecturer, if they wish. The aim here is to produce an application that would have real-world value and that can be added to future employment portfolios. These applications will utilize knowledge learnt during the lectures and labs but will also require group members to broaden their knowledge through self-learning of relevant topics. The group will be assessed as a whole on the quality and technical difficulty of the application from a user experience perspective as well as a coding and solution design perspective. Group members are expected to contribute evenly to the project and this is assessed via the “Group Graphics Project - Presentation” assessment task.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Graphics Project - Code and Application Quality</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">19/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 19 June 2020              Submission of all code should be done through UTSOnline before the given date.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submission of all code should be done through UTSOnline before the given date.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task assess students’ grasp of the practical knowledge and skills presented throughout the session, requires students to collaborate closely with a small group of their peers, and encourages students to broaden their understanding via self-learning in order to produce an authentic 3D web application.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
