   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48389</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Computer Modelling and Design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is an excel based learning exercise and requires students to model and analyse a number of structures using microstran. Students need to download the excel spread sheet from UTSOnline and each student will get a unique set of parameters for the problems based on their student number. Students can get immediate feedback on their solutuion from the spreadsheet and the problems can be attempted multiple times. Completed spread sheet should be uploaded to UTSOnline before the due date. Whilst students can upload multiple attempts on UTSOnine, only the final submission will be taken into account for grading purpose.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">eTask - Computer methods of structural analysis</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">03-April-2020, 17:00</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">03-April-2020, 17:00</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">For students to test their understanding of introductory concepts of computer modelling of structural frameworks and the use of structural analysis software.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is a supervised, hands-on, restricted open book test, which takes place in the computer laboratory. Students are required to calculate loads and stresses in structures and model and analyse 2D load bearing trusses and frames using commercial software. Individual feedback sheet for the quiz will be emailed to students within approximately 2 weeks from the quiz date.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">35</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1.5 hrs approx. - details will be posted on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">28-April-2020, 13:00-15:00</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">28-April-2020, 13:00-15:00</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1) Computer methods of structural analysis: Ability to prepare computer models of plane frames and trusses, to analyse them and to correctly interpret the computer output. 2) Structural Loads on Buildings: Ability to establish Permanent and Imposed actions on buildings in accordance with AS/NZ1170.0:2002.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is a supervised, hands-on, restricted open-book test, which takes place in the computer laboratory. Students are required to model and analyse 2D and 3D load bearing trusses and frames using commercial software. Individual feedback sheet for the quiz will be emailed to students within approximately 2 weeks from the quiz date.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">02-Jun-2020, 13:00-14:00</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To test student competency in computerised methods of structural analysis: Ability to prepare computer models of 2D and 3D trusses, frames and grillages and to take advantage of symmetry conditions. Ability to analyse structures subjected to applied static loads, temperature effects and foundation settlement. Ability to identify and rectify errors in computer models and to correctly interpret the output. Ability to understand the theory and algorithms used in developing frame analysis software and to apply them using spreadsheet software to analyse simple plane trusses.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">02-Jun-2020, 13:00-14:00</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are given a structural design problem where students work in a group (typically 4 or 5 students per group) to arrive at a design solution. There is no single correct solution to this design problem. The assignment will require the students to (i) workout applicable loads on the structure (based on AS1170), (ii) model the structure using a commercial software (Microstran), (iii) analyse the model, (iv) interpret the model output and use the output in design of structural members and system, and (v) undertake optimisation of design solution. Students should work on this task as a group throughout the session and there will be opportunities for students to receive feedback on their work during in-class review sessions. Details of the assignment and requirements will be posted on UTSOnline during week 0.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design Assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">35</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">29-May-2020, 17:00</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">29-May-2020, 17:00</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The output of the final design should be presented in the form of an engineering drawing and a scaled physical model. The drawing should be prepared using AutoCAD with proper dimensions and at a suitable scale. Sufficient details should be included in the drawing so that it is self-explanatory. Refer to UTSOnline for the Design Assignment requirements and details.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design Assignment: For students to test their understanding of calculating structural load based on AS1170, to correctly model structures using microstran and design the structure based on the model outputs.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task is based on the online e-Task system. Students are required to solve a number of problems (typically two) For students to test their understanding of earthquake actions on buildings in accordance with AS1170.4:2007 and to correctly interpret the code provisions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 15              Approximately Week 15 – Refer to the weekly class schedule</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Approximately Week 15 – Refer to the weekly class schedule</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The output of the final design should be presented in the form of an engineering drawing. The drawing should be prepared using AutoCAD with proper dimensions and at a suitable scale. Sufficient details should be included in the drawing so that it is self-explanatory.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design Assignment: For students to test their understanding of calculating structural load based on AS1170, to correctly model structures using microstran and design the structure based on the model outputs.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is a supervised, hands-on, restricted open-book test, which takes place in the computer laboratory. Students are required to model and analyse 2D and 3D load bearing trusses and frames using commercial software.</Data></Cell>
