   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41078</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Computing Science Studio 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Find 10 articles, and evaluate, summarise and code 4 articles on 1 topic chosen from a provided list. References and coding will be made available to all students of the subject. You must find relevant, high-quality articles on the topic, from diverse sources and with a variety of research perspectives. You will need to reference the articles correctly and then critically evaluate the 4 you have chosen, based on key criteria and with reference to the topic you are discussing.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Research and evaluation assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1000-2000 words: made up of 250-500 words per evaluation for 4 evaluations. Bibliography and reference lists are excluded, but all other words are included.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">24/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5.00pm Friday 24 April 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task introduces students to the fundamental skills of searching and evaluating the existing scientific literature, understanding and exploring the context of existing research, and synthesising this knowledge to inform future research.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">You can choose below two ways to conduct your replication work:  Choose one paper from the provided set of replicable papers. Replicate a result it reports by using the stated method and software provided by the research article. Add additional controls, measures and processes where appropriate. Your research supervisor will provide you a replicable task with given method, datasets or other input. Alternatively, you may need to obtain software and datasets used by the original author, or recreate them based on the description in the paper. The focus will be on perceptive elucidation and clarification of the original article, providing supporting (or falsifying) data, as well as designing additions and alterations to the original study design. You should only include the Aim, Method and Results sections of the paper.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Replication</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1000-1500 words – the emphasis here is on the accuracy of the replication, and the report itself can be short. Bibliography and reference lists are excluded, but all other words are included.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5.00pm Friday 5 June 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task develops skills in undertaking scientific research. The students will independently replicate existing results, providing a more structured environment that “green-fields” research, but still actively contributing to the scientific endeavour through verifying or falsifying existing work.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">You can choose below two ways to write the report: (1) Choose an article to redevelop and rewrite, incorporating their literature and their data. Rewrite it focusing on developing areas that are missing from the discussion. Add additional literature, controls and measures where appropriate. Alternatively, (2) your supervisor would advise you how to write a report based on his requirements to write methodology, and discussion etc.  In this assignment, you will present an article in a format appropriate for publication, including all details necessary for replication, as well as all updating and extending the literature review. All text should be your own (although some method description text and results text may be from assignment 2). Although references and methods from the original article should be thoroughly explored, no text whatsoever should be re-used except with proper referencing. This assignment will be partnered to an associated oral presentation in Week 12.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Write a report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">3000-4000 words, but mediated by the need to rewrite the paper thoroughly and with adequate coverage (ie. can be longer if necessary). Bibliography and reference lists are excluded, but all other words are included. The replication data you produced in assignment 2 can be used in this assignment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5.00pm Monday 15 June 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task focuses on presenting evidence and results in a scientific manner appropriate to Computer Science research.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment is the highest weighted. You should participate in all peer-review opportunities to provide feedback to your peers. Participate in in-class group exercises and in-class/online discussions. The assessment includes the below three elements. There are in total, 2 peer reviews, 2 self-reflection reports and 1 presentation.  Peer Review: You will provide peer reviews for other students work in assignment 2 and 3.  Self-reflection: You will conduct self-reflections for your assignment 2 and 3.  Presentation: You will present your work to the class in week 11 or 12. You can present individually or in group (if you are working on a same topic). However, you will be individually assessed.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Review process: Peer review, self-reflection &amp; presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">At least 500 words per Peer Review Report At least 500 words per Self-reflection Report 5 mins for each Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">19/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday 19 June 2020              Marked throughout the teaching session up until completion of the assessment period. Assessment Task 4 - Peer-review of Reports Assessment 4 - Self-Reflection of ReportsSee also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Marked throughout the teaching session up until completion of the assessment period. Assessment Task 4 - Peer-review of Reports Assessment 4 - Self-Reflection of Reports</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reviewing and engaging with the broader scientific community is one of the fundamental tasks any researcher must engage in. This task gives the students opportunities to engage in constructive peer-review in an academic setting.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
