   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41079</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Computing Science Studio 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Conduct literature review in the selected topic (either your own topic or the one provided by mentors during Week 1 and Week 2). Literature review should be concise, comprehensive and sources critically evaluated. You must find relevant, high-quality articles on the topic, from diverse sources and with a variety of research perspectives. You will need to reference the articles correctly and then critically evaluate them, based on key criteria and with reference to the topic you are discussing. (approximate word count: 1,000 words) Based on the literature review formulate research problem and prepare project proposal (including research questions and objectives) (approximate word count: 1,000 words) Prepare appropriate project plan that will enable you to effectively manage work in the group. Make sure that clear work breakdown structure is created, tasks are assigned to individuals and adequate amount of time is allocated to each task. Workloads should be designed in a way that each team member does similar amount of work. (approximate word count: 500-1,000 words) Propose appropriate methodology to answer stated research question and solve the proposed problem (approximate word count: 500-1,000 words)  Students individually will be required to work on the proposal and then meet and agree on one proposal they submit. Evidence of their individual work will be appendix to this report. The assessment should be submitted via UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project proposal, project plan, and project methodology</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">3,000-4,000 words: appendix. tables, text on figures, captions, bibliography and reference lists are excluded, but all other words are included.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">14 April 2020; 11.59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">14 April 2020; 11.59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task allows students to master their skills of searching and evaluating the existing scientific literature, understanding and exploring the context of existing research, and synthesising this knowledge to inform future research. This task also develops skills in preparing and writing research project proposal, selecting appropriate methodology and preparing feasible plan of work.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">You will be asked to review project proposal prepared but other group. For a given project proposal prepare critical analysis that will clearly state advantages and shortcomings of reviewed proposal – this will be done in a form of structured report. The assessment should be submitted via UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report of project proposals</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1,000 words (on avarege): tables, text on figures, captions, bibliography and reference lists are excluded, but all other words are included.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5 May 2020; 11.59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5 May 2020; 11.59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task allows students to further improve their critical analysis skills and ability to prepare proper research review.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Review your project proposal (Assessment Task 1) in the context of the feedback you have received from Task 1 and from your mentors and peer-reviews. Include in your report revised list of research questions and objectives (approximate word count: 1,000 words per review). Design of research – prepare detailed plan of your experiments or research; what and how will be done. Make sure that the designed experiments will help you to answer the stated research question from Assessment Task 1 (approximate word count: 1,000 words per review). Conduct the experiment and present your results analysis – you need to prepare and conduct your planned experiments. The results you obtain need to be presented in a way that is easy to understand and that they help you, later on, with your discussion. Presented analysis should provide answer to the research question presented in your project proposal (Assessment Task 1) (approximate word count: 1,000 words per review). Verify and validate of research outcomes – you need to assess the validity of your results. Make sure that what you present is significant and correct (approximate word count: 750 words per review). Discussion and conclusions – you are expected to discuss and summarise your research study. Also identify the potential future directions for your study (approximate word count: 750 words per review).  Students individually will be required to work on the verification and validation of research outcomes, discussion and conclusions and then meet and agree on final version they submit. Evidence of their individual work will be appendix to this report. The assessment should be submitted via UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Research paper</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">3000-4000 words: tables, text on figures, captions, bibliography and reference lists are excluded, but all other words are included.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
