   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48353</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Concrete Design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There are 3 assignments in this task. All assignments are quantitative requiring design calculations and design decisions. Students will analyse and design to Limit State Design philosophy of the current Australian Standard (AS3600-2009) in accordance with current accepted design practice. Assignment 1 (Basic Concepts &amp; RC Beams) Assignment 2 (RC Slabs) Assignment 3 (RC Columns) Assignment questions will be uploaded to UTSOnline and students should solve the question and provide the detailed calculations for the design. Each step of the calculation and utilised formulations with proper reference to notes and available literature should be provided.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design Assignments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design/drawing/plan/sketch</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1: 07/04/2020, 11:59pm; Assignment 2: 28/04/2020, 11:59pm; Assignment 3: 19/05/2020, 11:59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1: 07/04/2020, 11:59pm; Assignment 2: 28/04/2020, 11:59pm; Assignment 3: 19/05/2020, 11:59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There will be one mid-session quiz covering RC Beams and one-way slabs. This quiz will assess aspects of concrete material properties and behaviour of concrete structures that are reflected in code requirements for design. The quiz may include theoretical, numerical and design-based questions and will be held during class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Mid-session quiz held in class on 01/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Mid-session quiz held in class on 01/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There will be one Design Project (Residential, Commercial and Industrial) in this task. This project is quantitative requiring team working skills, calculations and design decisions. Students will work in groups of 5 and will analyse and design to Limit State Design philosophy of the current Australian Standard (AS3600-2009) in accordance with current accepted design practice. All groups should provide the detailed calculations for the design and drawings in a proper report. Each step of the calculation and utilised formulations with proper reference to notes and available literature should be provided.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design/drawing/plan/sketch</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design Project: 05/06/2020 in the lecture class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design Project: 05/06/2020 in the lecture class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The exam may comprise one (1) theoretical question and three (3) design calculations. The exam covers all topics as follows:  RC columns Two-way and flat slabs Development length Prestressed concrete  The exam will be restricted open book. You are allowed to use the Lecture Notes, Handouts, AS3600-2009 and AS/NZ 1170 in the exam.</Data></Cell>
