   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49116</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Contaminated Site and Waste Remediation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Undertake electronic Quizzes within UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Knowledge quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">n/a</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The quizzes are available from the start of session and need to be completed by the due dates.  See UTSOnline for details</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The quizzes are available from the start of session and need to be completed by the due dates.  See UTSOnline for details</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task allows students to evaluate their understanding of both subject structure, technical knowledge and professional knowledge and skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task involves the creation of a project proposal, which details the technical challenges that will be encountered during the design project (Task 3).  In particular, it will identify a conceptual model for the site contamination and how to handle predictive modeling of contaminant transport. The conceptual model will capture what is known or inferred about the contaminants (sources, releases, release mechanisms), site conditions (geology, hydrogeology) contaminant fate and transport (exposure pathways, potential receptors, and risks).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project proposal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Typically the report varies from 10-20 pages however it the quality of the responses not the pages which are assessed. Please use provided exemplars and assessment weighting as a guide.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">09/12/2018</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:45 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.45pm Sunday 9 December 2018              Submission through the Task 2 dropbox in UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submission through the Task 2 dropbox in UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assessment framework is based around the structural complexity of the approach used to analyse and solve the problem. This framework and examination of student exemplars will form an in-class activity.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To encourage students to structure the problem and allow feedback on their approach to ​problem-solving before undertaking the detailed work/calculations required for the full design report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will create a Project Design report which will be a standalone report incorporating relevant aspects of the project proposal, any updated information and the detailed working/modelling. A well developed conceptual model and predictive modeling sections with conclusions are expected. See UTSOnline for the report structure.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Typically the report varies from 20-30 pages however it is the quality of the responses not the pages which are assessed. Please use provided exemplars and assessment weighting as a guide.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">18/01/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:45 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.45pm Friday 18 January 2019              Submission through The Task3 dropbox in UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assessment framework is based around the structural complexity of the approach used to analyse and solve the problem. This framework and examination of student exemplars will form an in-class activity.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To produce a professional style written Design Report by building on the project proposal (Task 2) in order to give a full design experience.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submission through The Task3 dropbox in UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task involves creating a multimedia presentation about the way that the Project Design (Task 3) was undertaken. See UTSOnline for more details</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Peer review</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Multimedia presentation is limited to 5 minutes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10/02/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:45 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.45pm Sunday 10 February 2019              Task 4 should be uploaded to the students UTS YouTube account. A file with the URL should be uploaded to the task 4 Dropbox in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 4 should be uploaded to the students UTS YouTube account. A file with the URL should be uploaded to the task 4 Dropbox in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To determine skills in effectively preparing and presenting a reflection upon the professional engineering experience undertaken in Assessment Task 2 and 3.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task involves creating a multimedia presentation of the challenges and decisions that were made in undertaking the Project Design (Task 3). See UTSOnline for more details</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5 minutes only</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10/02/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:45 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.45pm Sunday 10 February 2019              Task 4 should be uploaded to the students UTS YouTube account. A file with the URL should be uploaded to the task 4 dropbox in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 4 should be uploaded to the students UTS YouTube account. A file with the URL should be uploaded to the task 4 dropbox in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task develops skills in effectively using multimedia to communicate. It complements the written outcomes delivered in Task 3.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task involves producing a document which shows your reflection upon how the design problem and the activities undertaken allowed you to demonstrate your capabability to apply established engineering methods to complex engineering problem solving. The structure of the reflection report is provided in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Historically this has been 4-10 pages</Data></Cell>
