   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48580</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Control Studio B</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to prepare a presentation that clearly describes the project that they will carry out in this subject and identify some possible advanced control system solutions that they will explore. This presentation should consist of:  Project name Project nature: academic, industrial or research Project challenges Project requirements Rationale for feasible solutions Task distribution among team members Expected outcome</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project requirements and solution design rationale</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10 minute presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment is due in end of Week 10 of the session. There is no word limit for the report. Submit a Group Report in a zipped folder containing all files (doc/tex, pdf,..) and MATLAB codes, movie/animation files to UTSOnline or email the tutor.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment is due in end of Week 10 of the session. There is no word limit for the report. Submit a Group Report in a zipped folder containing all files (doc/tex, pdf,..) and MATLAB codes, movie/animation files to UTSOnline or email the tutor.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To demonstrate the ability to understand and explain control systems requirements and propose a feasible solution design.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will demonstrate in the lab the project progress based on a first advanced control design and implementation. Particularly, students must individually be able to cover the following points:  Describe how the mathematical model of the system to be controlled was obtained. Justify the first controller selected for your system and how it was tuned. Show a clear understanding of the simulated response of the autonomous system  Explain how the controller was practically implemented. Moreover, analyse the obtained autonomous behaviour and compare it with the one obtained in simulation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Interim project demonstration</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstration</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10 minute presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab report is due at the end of week 12, there is no word limit.  Submit a Group Report in a zipped folder containing all files (doc/tex, pdf,..) and MATLAB codes, movie/animation files to UTSOnline or email the tutor.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab report is due at the end of week 12, there is no word limit.  Submit a Group Report in a zipped folder containing all files (doc/tex, pdf,..) and MATLAB codes, movie/animation files to UTSOnline or email the tutor.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To demonstrate knowledge of state feedback control of multivariable systems, including modelling, analysis, control design and computational simulation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to justify the final scope of the project as well as the solutions to be implemented. Each student should individually be able to demonstrate and explain the following points:  Final requirements Methods, tools and resources used to achieve the objectives Justification of the final proposed solution using control engineering concepts Evaluation and validation of the proposed solutions  Final practical testing of the developed autonomous control system.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final project demonstration</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15 minute presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">n/a</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class in       in the laboratory in the first lab session right after StuVac 1.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To demonstrate practical skills in implementation of advanced control strategies, including the design process and performance evaluation of real-world dynamic systems under control.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">in the laboratory in the first lab session right after StuVac 1.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Student are required to justify the final scope of the project as well as the solutions to be implemented. This report should consist of:  Project name Project nature: academic, industrial or research Final requirements Methods, tools and resources used to achieve the objectives Final proposed engineering solutions Evaluation and validation of the proposed solutions Conclusions and future work  The report will be submitted via Turnitin. The report should include figures, tables and references as appropriate.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final project report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10,000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period              Centrally-conducted.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Centrally-conducted.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To demonstrate understanding of the challenges and requirements of autonomous advanced control systems design. Moreover, the methods, tools and resources to achieving their objectives are also evaluated in this report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will complete a total of three assignments during the session. These assignments are designed to link with project work. Students will be expected to adapt various issues and problems raised in these assignments to improve the performance of their project work. Students are required to derive system models for control purposes. Moreover, control system design techniques will be applied for simulated systems. Thus, these assignments will cover: Multivariable (not necessarily linear) system modelling and simulation State-feedback and observer design Optimal control and filtering design Control design for nonlinear systems Assignments will be submitted via Turnitin. Each assignment should include figures, tables and references as appropriate.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5000 words for each assignment</Data></Cell>
