   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49329</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Control of Mechatronic Systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The students need to answer a number of questions related to the modeling of control system, and control system stability, controllability, and observability analysis. The student needs to clearly write down their answers together with necessary MATLAB code to support their answers. See the assignment document on Canvas for more details.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">13/08/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">09:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">9.00am Tuesday 13 August 2019              Week 4</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 4</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Modelling and analysis of mechatronic systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The students need to answer a number of questions related to the state feedback control, optimal control, observer design, nonlinear system stability etc. The student needs to clearly write down their answers together with necessary MATLAB code to support their answers. See the assignment document on Canvas for more details.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">03/09/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">09:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">9.00am Tuesday 3 September 2019              Week 7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Feedback control of linear and nonlinear mechatronic systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">For this group task, each group of students will be allocated one project. They need to complete the modeling of the control system, implement the control algorithm, analyze the results obtained. They also need to write a report detailing the project requirement, the methodology adopted, the algorithms implemented, and the results they obtained. See the project document on Canvas for more details.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">08/10/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">09:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">9.00am Tuesday 8 October 2019              Week 11</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 11</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is a restricted open book exam assessing the students' understanding of the different modeling, analysis, and control methodologies for linear and nonlinear control systems. See the sample exam questions on Canvas for more details. Students are allowed to bring 5 A4 pages handwritten notes and any calculators to the exam.</Data></Cell>
