   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42036</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Cyber Security for Mobile Platforms</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The students will be assigned tasks using Android Studio to perform security methods for mobile platform.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 6              In lab</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In lab</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The labs will provide the opportunity for students to demonstrate their ability to develop cybersecurity methods for mobile platforms.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The students will have a quiz on Week 7. This quiz may include both short answer and multiple choices types. The students will answer questions related to knowledge learned from Week 1 to Week 5 and submit to the lecturer at the end of class. Results and feedbacks for the quiz are given in Week 9.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7              In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The quiz will assess the student’s knowledge about the theoretical and some practical aspects of the subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will be divided into groups to do their projects together. There will be 3-5 students in a group, and they will cooperate and collaborate to complete their assigned projects. The projects will be performed based on knowledge and skills the students learn in the lectures and labs. The projects will be carried out in workshops. The students will submit the reports to the lecturer by the end of Week 11, and they are required to present their achieved results during the allocated time in Week 12. The students will be assessed on the basis of achieved results, reports for research projects, collaboration and presentation skills in the project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Projects</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The technical report will be less than 20 pages. The presentation will last for 30 minutes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The last day (Sunday) of Week 11 for the report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The students will work on workshop-based projects, where they will apply skills learnt in classes, labs, as well as their own research in Cybersecurity for Mobile Platform. Furthermore, the project presentation will assess the presentation and reporting skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The last day (Sunday) of Week 11 for the report.</Data></Cell>
