   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32146</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Data Visualisation and Visual Analytics</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment requests each student to read and review selected recent conference or journal article, which proposes a new visualisation approach. After reviewing the article, each student should be able to summarize the key concepts and essential techniques adopted in this approach for achieving the visual representation and navigation of large information spaces. Students also have to describe the advantages and weaknesses of the approach, in terms of efficiency of space utilization, satisfaction of aesthetics rules, computational cost, human cognition cost, efficiency of navigation scheme as well as the real-time response time (if it is an interactive visualisation). Each student is required to submit a Review Report and give a Class Talk of 5 minutes to present the review.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Technique Review</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">24/09/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">08:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">8.00pm Thursday 24 September 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment requests each student to either design a visualisation to satisfy a list of specific user requirements, or implement a particular visualisation technique based on a given list of technical issues that are described in the assignment specification. In the designing stage, students are required to select an appropriate visual metaphor, design a set of optimised graphical properties and attributes for the representation of data, and design a particular navigation scheme that includes the viewing scheme and interaction scheme. In the implementation stage, students are required to use one or more programming languages, such as Java or C++, to create a particular visualisation prototype based on a list of given technical requirements described in the assignment specification.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design: Data Visualization</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">08/10/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">08:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">8.00pm Thursday 8 October 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is a group assignment where students are required to design a process (or a lifecycle) of visual data analysis to maximize the satisfaction of a particular user's requirements. In the design, students are required to select an appropriate framework of data analytics, in which one or more visualization and interaction techniques may be involved to enhance the data analytics (or visual data mining) process through acceleration of cognition (or interactive algorithm adjustment). Provide your arguments on why your proposed framework is optimized. In this assignment, students are required to work in a group of two to complete the assignment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design: Visual Data Analytics</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
