   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32606</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Database</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In this lab test, students will be required to successfully translate the given question statements in English into SQL queries that run on a computer. The queries are single table queries. Each query will be marked as correct or incorrect. The database to be used in this lab exam will be provided.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">SQL Lab Test 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7              Please be advised there may be changes to these dates due to unforeseen circumstances. If so, students will be informed via email. SQL TEST 1 will be conducted in your scheduled tutorial time. Make sure you sit in the tutorial you were allocated to. Please bring your laptops just in case your lab computer does not work.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Please be advised there may be changes to these dates due to unforeseen circumstances. If so, students will be informed via email. SQL TEST 1 will be conducted in your scheduled tutorial time. Make sure you sit in the tutorial you were allocated to. Please bring your laptops just in case your lab computer does not work.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Test basic SQL skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In this lab test, students will be required to successfully translate the given question statements in English into SQL queries that run on a computer. The queries are multi-table queries (i.e. these queries involve joining operation(s)). Each query will be marked as correct or incorrect. The database to be used in this lab exam will be provided.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">SQL Lab Test 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">8</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 8              SQL Test 2 will be held during the lab time. If there is any change you will be informed via email. Summative feedback will be given during lecture time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">SQL Test 2 will be held during the lab time. If there is any change you will be informed via email. Summative feedback will be given during lecture time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Test advanced SQL skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Two questions about Database Acid Properties &amp; Data Integrity.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Credit test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design/drawing/plan/sketch</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
