    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment item will be held during the lecture time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Test advanced entity relationship design skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will create a database of their own choosing, which should be a simplified version of a database used in a real-world software system, subject to minimum necessary conditions, such as minimum number of tables, and minimum number of relationship types, that will be specified in a separate document.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">HD Assignment/MiniDatabaseProject</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 10              The soft copy of your assignment along with the code which you have used to build your database must be submitted in a USB your code needs to be tested if populates tables and data. This USB must be submitted before the lecture. You will submit your USB drive with the code before your presentation starts in the lecture time. HD assignment pre-approval Individual Feedback will be given before you submit your work via 3 consultations you schedule with your academic staff member.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The soft copy of your assignment along with the code which you have used to build your database must be submitted in a USB your code needs to be tested if populates tables and data. This USB must be submitted before the lecture. You will submit your USB drive with the code before your presentation starts in the lecture time. HD assignment pre-approval Individual Feedback will be given before you submit your work via 3 consultations you schedule with your academic staff member.</Data></Cell>
