   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">31061</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Database Principles</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In this lab test, students will be required to successfully translate the given question statements in English into SQL queries that run on a computer. The queries are single table queries. Each query will be marked as correct or incorrect. The database to be used in this lab exam will be provided.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">SQL Lab Test 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7              Held during in your scheduled lab time. Please be advised, there may be changes to these dates due to unforeseen circumstances. If so students will be informed via email. Please sit in your scheduled lab time, as there are only 30 computers in each lab. It is advised that students should bring their laptop just in case your lab computer fails to operate Postgress Sql.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Held during in your scheduled lab time. Please be advised, there may be changes to these dates due to unforeseen circumstances. If so students will be informed via email. Please sit in your scheduled lab time, as there are only 30 computers in each lab. It is advised that students should bring their laptop just in case your lab computer fails to operate Postgress Sql.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To test SQL skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In this lab test, students will be required to successfully translate the given question statements in English into SQL queries that run on a computer. The queries are multi-table queries (i.e. these queries involve joining operation(s)). Each query will be marked as correct or incorrect. The database to be used in this lab exam will be provided.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">SQL Lab Test 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">8</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 8              Held during the scheduled lab time. If there is any change you will be informed via email. Summative feedback given during the lecture time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Held during the scheduled lab time. If there is any change you will be informed via email. Summative feedback given during the lecture time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To test SQL skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will answer two questions. One is about data integrity and the other is about the ACID properties of a database transaction. The time to answer these questions is 60 minutes. The exam will require essay-style answers to demonstrate your understanding. Each answer must be no more than one page long.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Class Written Exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
