    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Test advanced entity relationship design skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will create a database of their own choosing, which should be a simplified version of a database used in a real-world software system, subject to minimum necessary conditions, such as the minimum number of tables, and the minimum number of relationship types, that will be specified in a separate document. Students who want to attempt this item need to submit by hand to the lecturer who is in charge of this item (Dr Srinivas Madhisetty) a brief document summarizing their chosen database project for approval. Upon his approval, students will design and implement their databases. Students also need to write SQL queries against their databases to support the major functions in the software systems that use the databases. Soft copy of your HD assignment is given on a USB drive, before the lecture.</Data></Cell>
