   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49127</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Decentralised Environmental Systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to undertake research on methods of decentralised water treatment systems that are used in a modern setting. They are then required to undertake technical, social and economic analyses of a chosen system and compare it with other systems available in the commercial market.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Research &amp; analytical report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Essay</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15 pages</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">28/08/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12.59pm Friday 28 August 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment criteria sheet will be distributed and discussed in Block 1 session in class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assess students' ability to understand and evaluate current POU/POE systems.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to design decentralised treatment systems to specified criteria. This is an open-ended design assessment. Students can assume the data; however, it should be noted clearly, justifiable and well-referenced.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15 pages</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">16/10/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 16 October 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assessment outline and criteria will be distributed in class in Block 2.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To demonstrate the ability to apply knowledge related to designing decentralised water/wastewater treatment systems.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to undertake a site visit to understand elements of a sustainable development that incorporates decentralised water and/or wastewater treatment and other systems. Students are required to work collaboratively. A site visit report that describes what was observed, and a critical analysis of the systems is to be submitted.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Site visit report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10 pages</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">02/10/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 2 October 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The aim of this task is for students to undertake a site visit and critically analyse the systems in place based on current industry standards.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The class assignments will consist of a number of short-answer questions both quantitative and qualitative. There will be 2 class assignments during blocks and feedback will be given to students in class and also in their marked class assignments within the first two weeks. Assignment marks will be posted on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
