   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42028</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Deep Learning and Convolutional Neural Network</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Implement a simple kNN classifier for digit classification Implement a Linear classifier using SVM for digit classification Implement a Linear classifier using Neural Network for digit classification Compare the three implementations in terms of classification accuracy and top choices.   Write a short report on the implementation, linking the concepts and methods learned in class and also provide comparative study.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">No particular length limit. Generally, the report should be about 5 pages maximum.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 10 April 2020              Submission via Canvas</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submission via Canvas</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To ensure that the student has a firm understanding of the basics. This will facilitate the learning of advanced topics. To allow students to self-assess whether/how the subject suits their learning objectives (this task will be done before the census date). To guide students to start the course project and Task 2.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Customize AlexNet/GoogleNet/ResNet and reduce/increase the layers. Train and test on image classification. Implement a custom CNN architecture for object detection and localization. Train and test the custom architecture on a given dataset for detection of multiple Objects, using Faster RCNN or Yolo object detection methods.   Training, validation and testing datasets will be provided. Write a short report on the implementation, linking the concepts and methods learned in the class and also provide comparative study.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">No particular length limit. Generally, the report should be about 10 pages maximum.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">29/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 29 May 2020              Submission via Canvas</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submission via Canvas</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To ensure that the student has a firm understanding of CNNs and Object Detections algorithms. This will facilitate the learning of advanced topics for research and also assist in completing the project. To allow students to self-assess whether/how the subject suits their learning objectives. To guide students to start the course project (see Task 3).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Any one of the following problems, or any combination:  Design/Implement an image classification algorithm. Design/develop an object detection system for detecting specific objects in a video and localizing them. Develop a clear problem statement that is within the capabilities of CNNs and design and capture a dataset of significant size that addresses this problem. Compare a series of algorithms against each other to determine optimum performance, and then suggest new approaches that improve performance. Develop a user interface that allows the operational use of an algorithm to achieve a real-world solution.   A list of potential projects will be provided as a guide and to stimulate discussion, but students are required to independently develop their project topics to have appropriate scope and focus. Completing this project involves reviewing, mastering and applying a large part of the scope covered by this subject, but also doing additional independent research and extending and innovating from the previously mastered techniques. The project plan should definitely include use of some of the techniques mastered in the two previous assignments, but ideally should also include extra techniques mastered independently. Write a report covering the:   Problem, solution, and approach taken Implementation steps Prepare a basic interface for demonstration (in the final week), and Report the accuracy of the system on validation and test datasets.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">No particular length limit. Generally, the report should be 20 pages maximum.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 5 June 2020              Demonstration is due in the lab/tutorial class in Week 14. Report submission via Canvas.</Data></Cell>
