   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49928</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design Optimisation for Manufacturing</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task involves the modelling and graphical optimisation of two problems, one linear programming problem, and one nonlinear programming problem. The student is required to derive the mathematical models of the optimisation problems, and use graphs to demonstrate the location of the solutions, and submit these as an individual report. See the assignment document on Canvas for more details.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1: Modelling of optimisation problems and graphical optimisation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 3, 14 August, 11:59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 3, 14 August, 11:59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">For this group task, each group of students will be allocated one project about linear programming. They need to complete the modelling of the optimisation problem, implement the optimisation algorithms, analyze the results obtained. They also need to write a report detailing the project requirement, the methodology adopted, the algorithms implemented, and the results they obtained. See the project document on Canvas for more details.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project 1: Linear programming and its applications</Data></Cell>
