   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42907</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design for Durability</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">As part of a team, students are asked to undertake a detailed design and construction planning project from the durability and service life design viewpoint. The overall weighting of the assessment mark will comprise 30% for group work + 20% for individual student work in the project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Major Design For Durability Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each group will submit a 5000 words (maximum) Durability Plan report for assessment. The author(s) of each section of the report must be identified in the report. Each student will be required to submit a one-page diary of self and group members’ contribution to the Durability Plan report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Team formation &amp; team leader by week 2; Presentation will be made during week 3-10; The Durability Plan report must be submitted via Turnitin UTSOnline by the Team Leader the end of the teaching semester of week 12; Individual diary (1-page) shall be submitted by all students via Turnitin UTSOnline at the same time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Team formation &amp; team leader by week 2; Presentation will be made during week 3-10; The Durability Plan report must be submitted via Turnitin UTSOnline by the Team Leader the end of the teaching semester of week 12; Individual diary (1-page) shall be submitted by all students via Turnitin UTSOnline at the same time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">As part of a team, students are invited to undertake a detailed design and construction planning project from the durability and service life design viewpoint. Students will present the group’s work and findings to the class. One member of each group is expected to present one part of this work. Individual students’ assessment will be made from a diary of the student’s contribution to the final report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There will be 10 questions. Students are to provide precise answers demonstrating their understanding of the subjects discussed during week 1 to week 5.</Data></Cell>
