   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48436</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Digital Forensics</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Content of Weeks 1 to 6. This is an individual assessment. This is a closed book quiz. This will be a UTSOnline Quiz with feedback at the end of the quiz.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7              In Class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In Class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment involves Group Research on a chosen Forensics topic. A topic is chosen from:  Document Metadata Memory Forensics Hidden Data on Hard Disk Windows/Linux Artifacts Social Media Security  This is a group based assessment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 11              On-line submission by the beginning of class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">On-line submission by the beginning of class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assignment is designed for students to demonstrate their skill in researching digital forensic topics in a real world environment. Students will practice their skills in collecting evidence from a digital device for later analysis by a forensic specialist.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are given an image file acquired from a suspect's laptop and asked to assess if allegations of failing to comply with company policies regarding the use of company time or intellectual property are proven. Topics are taken from the weekly labs. Students will work in small groups, but are assessed individually.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Skills tests</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstration</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Skills Based Assessments (SBAs) are designed for students to demonstrate their skill in locating forensic evidence on a digital device.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This exam is a restricted open-book exam. Students may bring one double-sided A4 sheet with handwritten notes. Calculators will not be allowed. This is an individual assessment.</Data></Cell>
