    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit to UTSOnline by 1 October 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit to UTSOnline by 1 October 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Criteria: Single answers (Quantitative and qualitative) and methodology/approach to problem-solving.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Short answer questions on local and global environmental issues and solutions</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment task 3a: Ecological Engineering, Environmental flow (10%) Assessment task 3b: Two class assignments on ecology and sustainable solutions to environmental issues. The questions are semi-open ended questions. The students work on group of 3-4; Answers are put on UTSOnline after 2 weeks and students can discuss on their approach as opposed to answers provided in UTSOnline; Assignment 3B questions will be sent to distance mode students during block 1 or 2 and 3</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Ecologically sustainable management</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">26</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit assessment task 3a by 8 October to UTSOnline. Assignment 3b consists of two parts- class assingnment 1 and class assignment 2.. The students will be provided with the questions on 3 September (class assignment 1) and on 1 October (class assignment 2). For block mode students both class assignments should be done during the class and submitted in groups.  For distance mode both the class assignment questions will be sent by email and students should submit by email (class assignment 1 by 6 September and class assignment 2 by 4 October)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Criteria: Single answers (Quantitative and qualitative) and methodology/approach to problem-solving.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Short supplementary assignments on Ecology and solutions to environmental problems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit assessment task 3a by 8 October to UTSOnline. Assignment 3b consists of two parts- class assingnment 1 and class assignment 2.. The students will be provided with the questions on 3 September (class assignment 1) and on 1 October (class assignment 2). For block mode students both class assignments should be done during the class and submitted in groups.  For distance mode both the class assignment questions will be sent by email and students should submit by email (class assignment 1 by 6 September and class assignment 2 by 4 October)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The exam will consist of a number of short-answer questions both quantitative and qualitative. This will be an open book exam, and as such you can bring your lecture notes and books for your reference during the exam.</Data></Cell>
