   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48531</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Electromechanical Automation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Four 2-hour laboratories: EM energy Conversion, Stepper, BLDCM, and PLC. Students can perform authentic tasks in teams in the practical sessions. They should follow lab supervisor's instructions and uphold safety guidelines given on the 1st page of the Lab note. A lab report is an individual work, to be submitted within one week from the lab date via UTSOnline. Lab average mark is the average of the best three out of four lab marks. Note that the default lab average weighting is 30% for assessment plan A. The lab average weighting is 40% for assessment plans B and C. Note: Please sign the cover page and have it signed by your lab supervisor, submit this signed page together with your report. You may like to keep a pdf copy for yourself.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory Work</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab duration is 2 hours each for 4 labs.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students' teamwork and collaboration are encouraged. If you do a face-to-face lab, then please submit your individual report. Otherwise, for online labs, a report can be a group work of maximally 5 students. All lab reports should be submitted online, and are due in one working week time after the lab date.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students' teamwork and collaboration are encouraged. If you do a face-to-face lab, then please submit your individual report. Otherwise, for online labs, a report can be a group work of maximally 5 students. All lab reports should be submitted online, and are due in one working week time after the lab date.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Criteria 1: Correct lab prework to show the ability to apply electromagnetic fundamentals, basic concepts of electromechanical energy conversion and power electronics in practical work. Punctual lab attendance and abidance to safety regulations, Criteria 2: Correct use of lab equipment, Familiarity with electric machines and instrumentation. Overall quality of lab reports, submitted before a due date.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Development of practical skills in measuring, parameter calculation, experimental observation, and validation of theoretical calculations.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Closed book quiz. Quiz weighting is 20% for assessment plans A and B. The quiz weighting is 0% for assessment plan C, i.e., students can choose not to sit the quiz but instead submit an assignment report on a relevant topic. The assignment topic can be chosen among those of advanced automation systems or practice-based projects as provided on UTS online, or of students' own choice in relevance to electromechanical automation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1 hour plus 5 minutes reading time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">On-line, open-book, subject to requirements resulting from the COVID-19 impact.  The midsession quiz will be ONLINE, it will be OPEN-BOOK in the MCQ format. It will take place in the week following StuVac Week 1.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">On-line, open-book, subject to requirements resulting from the COVID-19 impact.  The midsession quiz will be ONLINE, it will be OPEN-BOOK in the MCQ format. It will take place in the week following StuVac Week 1.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Comprehension of the basic concepts of electric and magnetic fields, electric machines and automation systems. Correct problem-solving answers to show the ability to demonstrate knowledge of fundamentals of fields, circuits, devices, modelling and control through formal written exams.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assurance of knowledge of fundamentals of electromagnetic fields, circuits, devices, and modelling and control of electromechanical systems; and development of problem-solving skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are to write a technical report addressing a topic chosen from \\Course_Documents-48531\EMA_Assignment or \\Assignments of the subject online; or a topic of students' own choice that is relevant to Automation and Control, Modelling &amp; Simulation, Research oriented to Automation Science and Engineering using electromechanical actuators. Topics include current industrial and domestic automation systems (such as warehouse, railway, mining, construction, UAV, or home robotics), an automation project involving design, simulation or implementation, The assignment can be done in groups (maximum 3 students) or individually. There is no word limit for the report. Note that the assignment weighting is 20% for assessment plans A and C. For plan B, this assessment component weighs 0%, i.e. an assignment report can be assessed alternatively to a midsession quiz.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task duration is 10 weeks.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task will be due at 11:59 pm on the Thursday of Week 10.  Students' teamwork and collaboration are encouraged.  Subject to requirements resulting from the COVID-19 impact, an assignment report can be a group work of maximally 5 students to be submitted online.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstration of comprehensive knowledge of electromechanical actuation with applications to various automation systems. Students are encouraged to explore modern automation systems from the electromachanical drive, sensing and control perspectives. Overall quality of written report presentation (spelling, grammar, structure, cover sheet, table of contents, references and clarity) and of oral seminar presentation (articulation of automation knowledge, question handling and time management) to show technical comprehension on electromechanical automation processes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Development of technical knowledge of electromechanical automation processes and introduction to advances in automation systems.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task will be due at 11:59 pm on the Thursday of Week 10.  Students' teamwork and collaboration are encouraged.  Subject to requirements resulting from the COVID-19 impact, an assignment report can be a group work of maximally 5 students to be submitted online.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">open book two-hour exam. Note that the default weighting for a final exam is 30% for assessment plan A. For assessment plans B and C, the final exam weighting is 40%. A macro in Excel spreadsheet will choose the best overall mark for the subject out of all three assessment plans. The subject's overall mark is the maximum of the marks by plan A, B and C.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 hours plus 10 minutes reading time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period              Note that this exam will also be conducted ONLINE and open-book in the MCQ format.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Note that this exam will also be conducted ONLINE and open-book in the MCQ format.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Criteria 1: Correct problem-solving answers and correct reasoning to show the ability to demonstrate knowledge of fundamentals of fields, circuits, devices, modelling and control through formal written exams.  Criteria 2: Correct answers and correct explanations to reflect experience and knowledge of practical automation processes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Development of problem-solving skills and technical knowledge of electromechanical automation systems including their closed-loop control design and performance analysis. Assurance of fundamental knowledge of electromechanical energy conversion. &#160;</Data></Cell>
