    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period              Assessment Week 2 Session B</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment Week 2 Session B</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In assessing your performance in this subject, we will be looking for evidence that:      You are able to efficiently carry out an accurate analysis of the requirements of embedded systems which are similar to those dealt with in this subject.     You have understood the concepts used in embedded software design and are able to apply them to the design of practical systems such as simple embedded systems.     You can distinguish between the different methods of implementing a real-time embedded system and know their limitations and how to apply them correctly.     You have understood the methods of hardware interfacing and are able to apply them to practical embedded systems such as those covered in this subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To analyse a set of specifications, design, simulate, test and practically demonstrate a simple embedded system. Skill in maintaining a record of an engineering design, reflecting on laboratory experiences, recording test results, and documenting software designs.</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48451</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Embedded Systems Studio A</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Hands-on tasks – three to be completed throughout the semester To become competent in designing digital circuits using VHDL and implementation using Xilinx programmable logic device. Technical expertise is exhibited and assessed through these 3 assignments. There will be three assignments: Assignment 1 10% Introductory VHDL No Demonstration required ( individual assignment). Assignment 2 12% VHDL application 1 Demonstration required. Assignment 3 12% VHDL application 2 Demonstration required. Both Assignment 2 and Assignment 3 are group work. Each student is expected to know exactly how the assignment implementation works and be able to justify the design choices which have made. Assessment briefs will be posted in UTSOnline on the dates available in content by week section. Each of them has its own objectives and marking criteria..</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">34</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">During the whole semester</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment Task 1: Draft Learning Contract due 13 August 2020 at 7:30pm (end of studio class)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment Task 1: Draft Learning Contract due 13 August 2020 at 7:30pm (end of studio class)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">It will be published with each assessment requirements</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To gain practical experience in hardware design. These three assignments will include design, simulation, implement and demonstrate (for A2, and A3) by writing HDL code that implements an application specific Digital system in hardware ( FPGA or CPLD).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Two in-class quizzes throughout the semester To test overall knowledge of basic digital techniques and their application to the design of state machines used in control units, Digital hardware design process and Programmable Logic, VHDL, Computing technologies, and architectures</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Class quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">66</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each quiz will take up to two hours.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment Task 2: Midway project presentation due 3 September 2020 in class and midway project report due 5pm 4 September 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment Task 2: Midway project presentation due 3 September 2020 in class and midway project report due 5pm 4 September 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each quiz will have its own criteria that can be found in the quiz paper</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Test the students' knowledge of digital systems, RTL and VHDL language as well as knowledge of a particular PLD and FPGA coding.To test overall understanding.</Data></Cell>
