   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32557</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Enabling Enterprise Information Systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment will include two parts: (i) a set of case study questions and (ii) short questions. The case studies questions will be related to IS environments, concerned with enterprise information systems issues. Students will need to carefully read each case study and answer each question in details. Short-answer questions will be related to the subject's concepts, and assess students understanding of the teaching materials. Further information about this assement will be provided in the class and also on UTS Online</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Information System review and evaluation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A template will be provided on UTS Online for students to download and complete.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">17/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5.00pm Friday 17 April 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this assessment is to examine students' ability to analyze real world case studies and problems, and to assess case study questions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task will include two in-class quizes. Each quiz will have 15 marks and will include thirty questions from a number of given subject topics. Quiz questions will be distributed in the class and students will have a given time to answer questions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to the assignment template</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 6 and Week 11, Check Canvas for details</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 6 and Week 11, Check Canvas for details</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment is to design a prototype of an information service or services to support business systems in contemporary collaborative and complex business environment. Students must identify services that provide value to stakeholders in complex business and social environments. Groups start by identifying the vision for a system of interest to them and then design a service that addresses this vision, and how it will provide value to stakeholders. The design is approached and evaluated from a number of perspectives especially the service integration into business activity, process workflow, social networking and knowledge sharing, and user design perspectives.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design Exercise (group)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design/drawing/plan/sketch</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to the assignment guideline on UTS Online</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5.00pm Friday 5 June 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessed throughout the semester. Students' class participation includes questions and answering in the class as well as active group participation in case studies and class activities. 1 mark will be granted for an active participation in each teaching week, with a total of 10 marks for the whole semester.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Class participation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Not applicable</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Not applicable              Active participation reflects ongoing weekly engagement in group/table activities as well as class discussions. Students need to demonstrate continuous attempts to contribute to in-class discussions</Data></Cell>
