   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48230</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Communication</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">a) You will record an audio learning narrative identifying your key learning goals for this subject and your time at university. b) Look back and reflect on your learning narrative from Week 3 and reflect on your learning journey in this subject in a written reflection and oral presentation video which is recorded and submitted online.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Learning Narratives</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">a) 3-minute audio recording b) 500-word written reflection and 3-5 min video</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">a) 11:59 pm, Sunday Week 3; b) 11:59 pm, Sunday Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">a) 11:59 pm, Sunday Week 3; b) 11:59 pm, Sunday Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is an individual assessment designed to encourage you to reflect in different ways on your individual learning goals for this subject and professional engineering skills and capabilities to be developed in this subject and your course.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is an individual assessment task that builds your skills in finding, evaluating and referencing information sources. You will investigate and evaluate information to become familiar with the context of the future team project, critically evaluating the information and sources to synthesis your research into a written summary. You will write a summary of the research that you have conducted so far, ensuring that information sources found and used are reliable and relevant, and are referenced correctly in your summary. Teams will be formed in the Week 4 tutorial based on your design interest area, and this individual assessment task will contribute background research to the team project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual Background Research Summary</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">500 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">4</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 4              11.59 pm Sunday</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59 pm Sunday</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To create an effective team design solution, it is essential that each team member is familiar with the social, environmental, economic and cultural context of the community for which your team will create a design solution. This individual assessment task will allow you to develop your research skills and information literacy (finding, evaluating and referencing information), and acquire knowledge relevant to the team project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Your team will build on the information collated in Task 2a to identify alternative design solutions to the chosen EWB Challenge Design Problem. Justify the selection of one design solution that is most appropriate for the community, to be further developed by your team. The team proposal documents this design solution, clearly outlining the problem and what your team intends to design and implement. The proposal is a planning document that helps to make decisions about the necessary work to develop the design solution. Social, cultural, environmental and cost considerations must be taken into account.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">EWB Challenge Team Proposal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2000 words (excluding title page, table of contents, reference list, appendices)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">8</Data></Cell>
