   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48250</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Economics and Finance</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will analyse two countries and their international involvement with a focus on monetary policy, trading partners and regulations.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Macro economic report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Maximum 5 page report submitted via turnitin. The report should compare and contrast relations between two countries.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Sunday 5 April 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To create an understanding of the macroeconomic environment with a focus on the engineering sectors.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will present on the application of management accounting principles and concepts from the perspective of a public company. Prepare a presentation on behalf of a public engineering company.  10% 5 min 1-on-1 presentation (Max 10 slides) A 5min one-on-one presentation, maximum 5 minutes and 10 slides. 20% An additional 15 Slides. Discuss key strategic decisions that were taken by the company in relation to regulatory change.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Management Accounting Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Sunday 10 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To apply an understanding of management accounting concepts as they relate to a company. This will also develop the students' presentation abilities.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will be presented with a real-world scenario and asked to apply financial accounting techniques to answer the lab quiz questions. Complete a number of accounting tasks during a 70-minute lab task. Students will apply basic accounting techniques to a real-world scenario.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Financial Accounting Lab Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
