    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">completeness - minimum requirement of six entries as per instructions quality - entries are assessed according to the published rubric timeliness - entries must be submitted according to your schedule as determined on the spreadsheet on UTSOnline. Any entries submitted late will incur a marks penalty originality - must be student's own work</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To provide a framework for developing and documenting graduate attributes and competencies during internship</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">When you reach the end of your internship, you must finalise the placement by submitting the Evaluation Form on CareerHub. Once submitted, the system will automatically generate an email to your supervisor with a link for them to fill out the Host Organisation Evaluation Form. These forms must be submitted within two weeks after the internship finish date. It is your responsibility to ensure that both forms &#45;- yours and your host organisation &#45;- are submitted in a timely manner. You cannot pass 48110 EE1 unless both you and your employer submit the Evaluation Forms.</Data></Cell>
