   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42013</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Graduate Project 12cp (Part 1 of 2) (2x6cp)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students present progress on their project in a three (3) minute timeframe with no more than one PowerPoint slide.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">3-minute project presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">You will practice oral communication skills by presenting progress on your project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project progress report (as this is the first part of a two-session 12 cp project) as determined by the outcomes of the project and those negotiated through a learning contract.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Progress report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">85</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Typically of the order of 40 pages + appendices and any other evidence required by the supervisor</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment criteria are determined as part of the learning contract.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This component provides students the opportunity to select and develop particular graduate attributes relevant to their development needs to a level consistent with master's program outcomes. In this first part of the 12 cp project, this assessment task can either be a Literature Review or Review of Methods, Technologies etc. as negotiated between the student and the supervisor.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In this subject students undertake a significant research or industry project under the supervision of an academic member from FEIT. Task 1 will typically be a Final proposal.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Project Proposal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10 pages plus appendices (typically) Individual learning contracts may specify differently.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment criteria are determined as part of the learning contract.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This component provides students with the opportunity to provide evidence of their ability to contribute to and complete a significant research or professionally oriented project related to their discipline major.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to identify graduate attributes that they wish to demonstrate in this subject. As part of their learning contract a student and their academic supervisor will agree on what evidence of that development (attribute and level) will be submitted. The evidence should come from the student’s involvement in the project and concurrent experiences. The contract will include assessment criteria.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Interim report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40 pages (plus evidence in agreed format) Individual learning contracts may specify differently.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment criteria are determined as part of the learning contract.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This component provides students the opportunity to select and develop particular graduate attributes relevant to their development needs to a level consistent with Masters program outcomes. In this first part of 12 cp project, this assessment task can either be a Literature Review of Review of Methods, Technologies etc. as negotiated between the student and the supervisor.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
