   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42014</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Graduate Project 12cp (Part 2 of 2) (2x6cp)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to produce a report that effectively communicates the project aims, methodology and outcomes at a level appropriate for a professional engineer.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">100</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Project report (This should encompass the work and related outcomes completed in both parts of a two-session 12 cp project including conclusions and recommendations and as determined by the outcomes of the project.). The number of pages in the report will depend to an extent on the nature of the work undertaken. Your supervisor will be able to offer relevant advice. As a guide you could expect to write a maximum of 100 pages for your report (not including appendices).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30/10/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday 30 October 2020              Friday of the first week of final assessment period.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday of the first week of final assessment period.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment criteria are determined in negotiation with the academic supervisor. A marking guide is provided on Canvas.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This component provides students the opportunity to select and develop particular graduate attributes relevant to their development needs to a level consistent with master's program outcomes; these are as negotiated between the student and the supervisor.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The learning objectives and expected graduate attribute outcomes will be determined and agreed to in the individual learning contract. (note that there will be some non-negotiable objectives and graduate attributes for this task)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Research Plan</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Approximately 10 pages</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday 1st week of final assessment period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday 1st week of final assessment period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This component provides students with the opportunity to assess their status of progress and submit a research plan that will assist in completing the project to meet the set criteria and submit it on time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to identify graduate attributes that they wish to demonstrate in this subject. As part of their learning contract a student and their academic supervisor will agree on what evidence of that development (attribute and level) will be submitted. The evidence should come from the student’s involvement in the project and concurrent experiences. The contract will include assessment criteria.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Interim report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40 pages or more (plus evidence in agreed format) Individual learning contracts may specify differently.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment criteria are determined as part of the learning contract.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This component provides students the opportunity to select and develop particular graduate attributes relevant to their development needs to a level consistent with Masters program outcomes. In this second part of 12 cp project, this assessment task can either be an updated Literature Review or Review of Methods, Technologies etc., report on deliverables wrt project outcomes; these are as negotiated between the student and the supervisor.</Data></Cell>
