   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48321</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Mechanics</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment tasks will be posted on UTSOnline. Assignment 1 is a short report on a structure of the student's choice (contributes 10% to final mark). Assignment 2 is a set of problems to solve on 'trusses and pin-jointed frames'. Assignment 3 is a set of problems to solve on 'internal actions'. Assignments 2 and 3 consist of a series of past exam questions to solve (each contributes 20% to final mark).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Three Assignments (Summative)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Varies with each assignment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments are to be submitted by the due date.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments are to be submitted by the due date.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To provide students with practice in problem solving and applying concepts to real or model structures.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The topic and tentative scheduling for each Quiz is shown in the subject program on UTSOnline. Each Quiz will commence at the beginning of the relevant lecture or tutorial session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Four Topic Quizzes (Formative)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 hour process consisting of first an individual quiz, then a collaborative quiz, then a review session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">n/a</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class in       as indicated in the program.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">as indicated in the program.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To allow students to demonstrate what they have learnt, to determine what they don’t know yet, and to learn it collaboratively with their peers. In addition each collaborative quiz will be followed by a review session where all questions, alternative answers and common misconceptions will be discussed.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The Stage 1 exam will be conducted under the same conditions as formal, centrally conducted exams. The questions in this exam paper will consist of multiple-choice questions that cover every topic in the subject. The questions will be set at or just above the level required to satisfactorily demonstrate the associated learning outcomes. The Pass mark for this exam is 75%. Students who receive greater than or equal to 75% in the Stage 1 exam are only required to answer the first two questions in the Stage 2 exam. These questions will be marked holistically using the criteria based on the UTS grade descriptors. Students who receive less than 75% in the Stage 1 exam are required to answer the whole of the Stage 2 paper. GRADE DESCRIPTORS 85 to 100% - work of outstanding quality on all objectives. This grade may also be give to recognise particlular originality or creativity. 75 up to 85% - work of superior qulaity on all objectives, demonstrating a sound grasp of content. 65 up to 75% - work of good quality showing more than satisfactory achievement on all objectives, or work of superior quality on most of the objectives 50 up to 65% - work showing a satisfactory achievement on the overall objectives.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Exam (Summative)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Stage 1 exam will be held in class time. Stage 2 exam will be held in normal centrally conducted exam period.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To allow students to demonstrate their knowledge of the concepts of mechanics and their skills in applying them to solve problems at the level appropriate to begin the subsequent subject, Mechanics of Solids. Stage 1 - The threshold exam is intended to provide assurance that students who passed 48321 have demonstrated satisfactory knowledge in all subject topics. To assist students in their learning an exam review will be held in StuVac, where all questions, alternative answers and common misconceptions will be discussed. The intent is to help students identify and address gaps in their learning before sitting the Stage 2 exam. The temporal separation between the Stage I and Stage 2 exams is to allow students time for this revision and review to occur.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Stage 1 exam will be held in class time. Stage 2 exam will be held in normal centrally conducted exam period.</Data></Cell>
