   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41035</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Practice Preparation 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The Reflection on Peer Review Activity 1 provides students with the opportunity to assess themselves and their peers in relation to the commitments they made in their Peer Review Group Charter. Students are expected to notice how others provide feedback and reflect upon their own ability to provide feedback.  Review peers’ draft learning journals and prepare feedback for peers on their work prior to the Week 5 tutorial. In the Week 5 tutorial, based on your obligations under your Peer Review Group Charter, provide verbal feedback to peers on their work and receive feedback from peers on your own work. Notice other students’ and your own strengths and challenges with both giving and receiving feedback. (Late penalty clause c provides that students who do not complete this component of the assessment on the specified date receive a mark of zero for this assessment). Submit a written reflection on your individual fulfillment of your Peer Review Group Charter following Ullmann’s (2017) Levels of Reflection.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection on Peer Review Activity 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Written reflection minimum 500 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">21/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">09:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">9.00am Tuesday 21 April 2020              Due date for tutorials scheduled on Friday is Wednesday 29 April</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Due date for tutorials scheduled on Friday is Wednesday 29 April</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will develop their capacities to both give and receive effective feedback, and to conduct critical self-review. Feedback on this task will guide students in what is needed for success in assessment task 2.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A reflective learning journal that communicates professional attributes and reflects on professional responsibilities. The reflective learning journal includes the following elements: 1. A succinct and engaging Professional Biography that includes information about the student’s major/field of practice, what has influenced their choice to study that major, and what they have to offer potential employers. Students should include a professional photograph of themselves, and a competitive resume. 2. No fewer than four journal entries (minimum 500 words each) demonstrating capacity for reflective learning. All journal entries must include at least some of the ‘deeper’ levels of reflection identified by Ullmann (2017), including reference to the required reading. Where appropriate, journal entries should include photographs taken by the student to illustrate situations or events that have been recounted. Topics of the journal entries are advised to students in the Canvas Assignments folder. 3. A summative reflection on the subject as a whole and how the student has met the Subject Learning Objectives (does not need to include all of Ullmann’s levels of reflection, nor refer to required reading).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflective learning journal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Journal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">90</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Minimum 2,000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">13/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">09:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">9.00am Wednesday 13 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The Reflective Learning Journal communicates to a reader how the student has fulfilled the subject learning objectives (SLOs). Students are expected to curate the artefacts of their inquiry into how to obtain a job, the capabilities they need in order to contribute to a workplace, and how to learn in a workplace. It is anticipated that their learning journals will include a resume, a succinct professional biography, and at least four pieces of reflective writing.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Your group should prepare (and practise), an 8 minute group oral presentation that will be presented during the last tutorial session to your colleagues. Your presentation should:  briefly describe the engineer and workplace your group visited share what you discovered, with similarities and differences from your individual expectations.  All students of each group must participate in this presentation. A copy of the marking sheet for this assessment task is given in the relevent section on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
