   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41045</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Practice Preparation 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 1: EPP2 Student Portfolio (Individual) Students will be required to complete a variety of portfolio entries as part of the in-class activities and submit online each week.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Developing Professional Practice</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20/09/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 20 September 2020              (end of Stuvac)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">(end of Stuvac)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 1: Content, written communication</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">You will be engaged in a variety of pre-class, in-class and post-class activities based on the topics under investigation across the six sessions. You will be assessed on your engagement with the materials, insight into your learning, pre-class preparation, communication skills and your ability to collaborate with and provide feedback to your peers.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 2: Learning Proposal (Individual) This task is your opportunity to consider your past workplace experience and make decisions about your future learning needs. Using the template provided on UTSOnline, students are to identify competencies, attribute, or skills in which some, or further, experience and learning is required. The template highlights the actions you will take on your internship and the types of artefacts you will collect as evidence of your future claims of competency. Students to submit a softcopy to Turnitin through UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Preparing for the Workplace</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">16/08/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 16 August 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 2: Content, written communication, presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The objective of this task is to assist in setting your learning goals and help you make decisions about the types of activities you need to plan for in order to maximise your learning and success for your senior internship. Learning goals and activities will be developed in accordance with the Engineers Australia Competency Standard – Stage 2 – Professional Engineer.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 3: Case Study Report (Group and individual) Based on a case study, student groups will analyse and critique events. Group discussions will be based on a set of focus questions. Stakeholder needs, ethical considerations, social responsibility and the role of creativity and leadership will be explored. Students will individually prepare a written report based on their group discussions. Students to submit a softcopy to Turnitin through UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Practice in Context</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2000 words (excluding headings and reference list)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30/08/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 30 August 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 3: Content, written communication, presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Your objective for this task is to demonstrate an understanding of the social context in which engineering is practiced. As a member of a small group, you will identify the issues described in a case study based on a past student's internship experience. Through the development of this task, you will analyse the relationships between leadership (followership), ethics and social responsibility. Students will consider the role of teamwork and mentoring within the context.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 4: Short video presentation In class you will be given a question relating to your past engineering workplace. You will make a short video recording your answer (as in a job interview). You will be given time to prepare, rehearse and work with a partner to film each others' response. Your film will be uploaded to your Portfolio and you will be required to review the effectiveness of your performance. Students must bring a video recording device to class to complete this task (tablet or phone). Activity will be followed by tutor feedback and peer review.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Workplace Cultures for Engineers</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">3 minutes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06/09/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 6 September 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 4: content, presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Your objective for this task is to consider your first internship or engineering work placement in terms of the workplace culture you experienced. Through this task you will draw conclusions as to what aspects of workplace culture are important to you and why. Your ability to reflect on your past experience and communicate your ideas effectively will be critical to this task.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
