   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48141</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Practice Preview 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 1.1 Reflective journal (Individual) Students are to complete a reflective ePortfolio entry as an in-class exercise during Tutorial 2 based on the experiences and learning from a group interaction or problem encountered. Students awarded 7.5/10 for the first entry will be deemed to have demonstrated insight into their learning according to the four stages of Kolb’s learning cycle and no further journal entries will be required. If a second entry is necessary, it will be submitted according a negotiated timeline and incorporate feedback from the tutor. Task 1.2 EPP2 Student Portfolio (Individual) Students will be required to complete a variety of portfolio entries as part of the in-class activities and submit online each week.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Developing Professional Practice</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 1.1 Reflective Journal submitted through ePortfolio no later than Monday 9 April at 5.00pm;             Task 1.2 Student portfolio submitted online in Tutorial 6; Task 1.3 Participation In class and ongoing over six sessions</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 1.1 Reflective Journal submitted through ePortfolio no later than Monday 9 April at 5.00pm;             Task 1.2 Student portfolio submitted online in Tutorial 6; Task 1.3 Participation In class and ongoing over six sessions</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 1.1  Content, Written Communication, Presentation. Task 1.2  Content, Written Communication</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">You will be engaged in a variety of pre-class, in-class and post-class activities based on the topics under investigation across the six sessions. You will be assessed on your engagement with the materials, insight into your learning, pre-class preparation, communication skills and your ability to collaborate with and provide feedback to your peers.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 2.1 Learning Proposal (Individual) Part 1: This task is your opportunity to consider your past workplace experience and make decisions about your future learning needs. Using the template provided on UTSOnline, students are to identify four Elements of Competence in which some, or further, experience and learning is required by you. The development of your learning proposal will involve the review of your past experience and identify gaps in your competence develop. The template highlights the actions you will take on your internship and the types of artefacts you will collect as evidence of your future claims of competency. Part 2: You are required to set four very specific and clear learning goals. These goals should relate directly to the AE Competency Standard – Stage 2 and the workplace but may include something outside the workplace which supports you in attaining a competency. For example: Complete a public speaking course. Part 3: The final step is to complete an overall competency ranking and make judgments about your performance against the 16 elements of competence using the descriptors provided by Engineers Australia. Students to submit a softcopy to Turnitin through UTSOnline. Task 2.2 Resume (Optional: no marks, Career Hub access only) This task recognises that students are at different stages in securing their second internship. Some students may have organised a placement while others may have not begun the process. For this reason, students are encouraged to make a decision as to whether they need to submit a resume for Career Hub approval and therefore gain access to current internship opportunities. If you choose to proceed, you are to develop a resume that reflects later-stage development appropriate to your current level of study and industry experience. To be competitive, emphasis should be placed on professional presentation, currency, technical and non-technical information and effective communication of your experience. Students to submit a softcopy to Turnitin through UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Preparing for the Workplace</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 2.1 Learning Proposal submitted to UTSOnline no later than Friday 20 April at 5.00pm.   Task 2.2 Resume (optional) submitted to UTSOnline no later than Wednesday 18 April at 5.00pm.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 2.1 Learning Proposal submitted to UTSOnline no later than Friday 20 April at 5.00pm.   Task 2.2 Resume (optional) submitted to UTSOnline no later than Wednesday 18 April at 5.00pm.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 2.1  Content, Written Communication, Presentation Task 2.2  Written Communication, Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The objective of this task is to assist in setting your learning goals and help you make decisions about the types of activities you need to plan for in order to maximise your learning and success for your senior internship. Learning goals and activities will be developed in accordance with the Engineers Australia Competency Standard – Stage 2 – Professional Engineer.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 3.1 Case Study Report (Group and individual) Based on a case study, student groups will analyse and critique events. Group discussions will be based on a set of focus questions. Stakeholder needs, ethical considerations, social responsibilty and the role of creativity and leadership will be explored. Students will individually prepare a written report based on their group discussions. Guidelines for the format of this report can be found in the EPP2 Student Workbook and Learning Guide. Students to submit a softcopy to Turnitin through UTSOnline. Task 3.2 Presentation (Group) Within the context of the case study, student will work in groups to develop a visual representation (mind map, flow chart or model etc.) illustrating the processes that lead to positive leadership and innovation in the engineering workplace. Students will prepare and present their work in class. Please also refer to Learning Guide.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Practice in Context</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2000 words (excluding headings and reference list)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 3.1 Case Study submitted to UTSOnline no later than Monday 21 May at 5.00pm Task 3.2 Group Presentation completed and submitted in Tutorial 5 week beginning 7 May.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 3.1  Content, Written Communication, Presentation. Task 3.2  Content, Oral Communication, Group Work</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Your objective for this task is to demonstrate an understanding of the social context in which engineering is practiced. As a member of a small group, you will identify the issues described in a case study based on a past student's internship experience. Through the development of this task, you will analyse the relationships between leadership (followership), ethics and social responsibility. Students will consider the role of teamwork and mentoring within the context. Students will work in groups to formulate their ideas and communicate findings in oral and written form.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 3.1 Case Study submitted to UTSOnline no later than Monday 21 May at 5.00pm Task 3.2 Group Presentation completed and submitted in Tutorial 5 week beginning 7 May.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 4 Short video presentation (Individual) In class you will be given a question relating to your past engineering workplace. You will make a short 2 minute video recording your answer (as in a job interview). You will be given time to prepare, rehearse and work with a partner to film each other’s response. Your film will be uploaded to your Portfolio and you will be required to review the effectiveness of your performance. Students must bring a video recording device to class to complete this task (tablet or phone). Activity will be followed by tutor feedback and peer review.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Workplace Cultures for Engineers</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 minutes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 4 Short video presentation submitted to UTSOnline in class during Tutorial 6 week beginning 14 May.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 4 Short video presentation submitted to UTSOnline in class during Tutorial 6 week beginning 14 May.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 4.1  Content, Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Your objective for this task is to consider your first internship or engineering work placement in terms of the workplace culture you experienced. Through this task you will draw conclusions as to what aspects of workplace culture are important to you and why. Your ability to reflect on your past experience and communicate your ideas effectively will be critical to this task.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to Learning Guide Attend one EPR2 seminar. Your attendance will be recorded – make certain this is done</Data></Cell>
