   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41038</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Practice Reflection 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task has 3 parts. Students choose 3 of the following topics to write 3 reflections in relation to their internship:  Ethical conduct and professional accountability (3.1) Effective communication in professional and lay domains (3.2) Creative, innovative and pro-active demeanour (3.3) Professional use and management of information (3.4) Management of self, and professional conduct (3.5) Leadership and Teamwork (3.6) Another topic relevant to your current or future study plan  1a) Three pieces of reflective writing are drafted using the information provided in the week 1 lecture, and the further explanation provided in the Learning Guide. The reflections should be around 500 words each. 1b) The reflections are submitted to the students Peer Review Group on UTSOnline using the Group Journal function. Group members review their peers’ reflections using the Peer Review Sheet (available on UTSOnline). Students use the Peer Review Sheet as a guide. 1c) Students write a paragraph summarising the feedback received from their peers in tutorial 1 and include any decisions they have made about changes they intend to make. The paragraph should be around 250 words.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Review of peers’ draft reflections</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Approximately 1500 words for the draft reflections and 2c) a paragraph summarising the feedback received from peers.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">23/08/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 23 August 2020              Task 1a: Submit by 11:59 am on Sunday, 9 Aug Task 1b: Submit by 5.00 pm on Friday, 14 August; Task 1c: Submit by 11.59 on Sunday 23 August</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 1a: Submit by 11:59 am on Sunday, 9 Aug Task 1b: Submit by 5.00 pm on Friday, 14 August; Task 1c: Submit by 11.59 on Sunday 23 August</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To give feedback on the three draft reflections, and to get feedback from peers on their internship and the writing of their reflections.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">3 reflections based on critical events from their internship</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Completed Reflections</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1500 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">27/09/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 27 September 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflections should:  recount/describe experience react to and evaluate that experience including identifying feelings, and/or reflecting upon personal beliefs recognizing and analysing difficulties relate the experience to academic, professional, or broader literature related to the topic referencing this literature in accordance with the UTS Harvard conventions, evidencing literate engagement with the topics explain what lessons have been learned (retrospective outcomes), and what the student’s future intentions are (prospective outcomes) in relation to each topic.  Language use communicates meaning clearly with a professional/formal degree of accuracy indicative of careful editing.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students begin to establish their identity as professional engineers which develops the confidence and the resilience necessary to succeed in their future studies.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In online seminar groups, students will deliver a 3-slide presentation describing:  where the internship took place and the students’ role in the company; the students’ hopes and expectations on joining the company; what the student actually experienced when he/she joined.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Three-slide presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5-8 minutes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment completed after seminar</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assess students’ ability to verbally establish a professional identity and to discuss aspects of interest about their professional experience.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment completed after seminar</Data></Cell>
