   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41048</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Practice Reflection 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students produce a curated graduate employment e-portfolio that is succinct, has high impact, and demonstrates belonging and commitment to the professional engineering community.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Curated graduate employment e-portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">13/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">09:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">9.00am Monday 13 April 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students communicate succinctly in e-portfolio format their professional capabilities and attributes to potential employers and the wider professional engineering community as a demonstration of belonging, commitment to and ability to contribute to the professional engineering community.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The Reflection on Peer Review Activity 1 provides students with the opportunity to assess themselves and their peers in relation to the commitments they made in their Peer Review Group Charter. Students are expected to notice how others provide feedback and reflect upon their own ability to provide feedback.  In workshop 1, based on your obligations under your Peer Review Group Charter, provide verbal feedback to peers on their work and receive feedback from peers on your own work. Notice other students’ and your own struggles with both giving and receiving feedback. (Late penalty clause c provides that students who do not complete this component of the assessment on the specified date receive a mark of zero for this assessment).  Submit a written reflection on your individual fulfillment of your Peer Review Group Charter following Ullmann’s (2017) Levels of Reflection.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection on Peer Review Activity 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Written reflection 400-700 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">09:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">9.00am Monday 6 April 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will develop their capacities to both give and receive effective feedback, and to conduct critical self-review.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Complete one of the following tasks:  Task A: Engineering Professional Development Resource:  i) identify an area or dimension of your degree studies that contrasted with what you learned during internship; ii) prepare a professional development resource (e.g. a case study) together with a rationale/exegesis for the resource that explains how the resource enhances the current engineering student experience in the content area; iii) present the resource at the event specified in the Subject Outline Program, and engage with feedback about its value and effectiveness (see Teaching and learning strategies section above); iv) write a short reflection (minimum 400 words) upon the experience of soliciting and receiving this feedback from peers and academic staff/industry representatives and what you learned from this. This task should be submitted as a final report containing: i)background/rationale for the resource; ii)the resource; and iii)reflection on the presentation of the resource to peers and academic staff/industry representatives.  Task B: Scoping Report for Chartered Engineer Status  i) research what is required for Engineers Australia (EA) Chartered Engineer status; ii) reflecting on your experience during your internships, prepare a short report that demonstrates your capability to meet at least two of the EA stage 2 competencies at functional level or above; iii) prepare a presentation of the information contained in the report and present this at the event specified in the Subject Outline Program, and engage with feedback about its value and effectiveness (see Teaching and learning strategies section above); iv) write a short reflection (minimum 400 words) upon the experience of soliciting and receiving this feedback from peers and industry and what you learned from this. This task should be submitted as a final report containing: i) a brief background summary of the Chartered process and the benefits of chartered status; ii) competency claims against a minimum of two EA stage 2 competencies; and iii) reflection on the presentation of the background and competency claims to peers and academic staff/industry representatives.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Personal commitment to and capability to fulfill obligations to the engineering profession</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">09:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">9.00am Monday 11 May 2020              Video yourself giving a 3-5 minute presentation and upload in the Assessment folder; Report approximately 1,000 words long</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
