   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48142</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Practice Review 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit your Draft Internship Report by the due date with, as a minimum, the sections required for the Draft Internship Report as defined in the 48142 EPR2 “Learning Guide” completed to a high standard. Then, participate in the Peer Review session and provide meaningful feedback to your peer by the due date. More information about this assessment task is available in the 48142 EPR2 “Learning Guide” and on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Peer Review of Draft Internship Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit your Draft Report by 11:59pm on Sunday 30th August. Complete the Peer Review process by 11:59pm on Wednesday 2nd September.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit your Draft Report by 11:59pm on Sunday 30th August. Complete the Peer Review process by 11:59pm on Wednesday 2nd September.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To provide an opportunity to have a sample of work from your Internship Report reviewed by a peer prior to submission of your completed Internship Report for formal assessment, in order to:  develop your capacity to both give and receive effective feedback, and to conduct critical self-review get feedback about your interpretation of the report criteria better develop your understanding of the report criteria by assessing a peer’s work against them learn from the experiences of your peer.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Write an internship report that:  Briefly summarises where you worked and what you did during all your internships. Reflects on your experience and summarises what you have learned in relation to the objectives of the Professional Engineering Practice Program and the criteria defined in the 48142 “Learning Guide”. Demonstrates that you have developed technical competence, a foundation both for socially responsible and sustainable practice and for ethical practice, leadership/followership capabilities, communication capabilities and teamwork capabilities. Identifies your current competencies in relation to the Engineers Australia Stage 2 National Competency Standards Chooses Elements of Competence from at least 3 different Competency Units (see EA Stage 2 Competency Standards) as the basis for at least 3 Engineering Competency Claims (refer to 48142 EPR2 “Learning Guide” for more information) that could be used in support of an application for CPEng with Engineers Australia Includes an updated CV.  More detailed instructions are in the 48142 EPR2 “Learning Guide” and resources are available in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Internship Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">60</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Approximately 5000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit your Internship Report by 9:00am on Monday 21st September 2020.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit your Internship Report by 9:00am on Monday 21st September 2020.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment criteria are available in the assessment rubric attached to the task in UTSOnline. There is a video in UTSOnline that explains how to view this.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To reflect on experience, learn from this and prepare for subsequent experience</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Deliver an 8 to 10-minute video presentation to demonstrate your suitability as a prospective candidate for a position in an organisation of your choice. This video presentation must include:  A brief introduction of yourself and your degree; A clear description of the role and responsibilities within the organisation you are applying for; A brief history of your previous experience (from both internships); Demonstration of the following competencies (through examples and evidence):   a. Socially responsible and sustainable engineering practice; b. Ethical practice; c. Leadership and/or followership capability; d. Other relevant competencies and / or technical proficiencies you have developed.   A clear correlation between your competencies and the role you are applying for; A brief discussion of attributes / competencies you want to improve (and how you plan to do this); A brief vision for your future contribution to the organisation.  More information about this assessment task is available in the 48142 EPR2 “Learning Guide” available in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Video Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit your Presentation Video by 11:59pm on Wednesday 14th October 2020.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">An assessment rubric is attached to the task in UTSOnline. There is video available on UTSOnline that shows how this can be viewed.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Prepare a presentation showcasing your experience and capabilities, pitching you for a target job of your selection.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit your Presentation Video by 11:59pm on Wednesday 14th October 2020.</Data></Cell>
