   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41036</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Professional Experience 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">If you are not already working full time, you will need to find a job that is suitable for an engineering internship (Suitable internships are ones that meet the FEIT Placement Requirements. You can read this on the FEIT Professional Practice Program Forum on UTSonline). You can search for a job through the faculty's careers management system (CareerHub). To find internships already deemed suitable by the faculty, you need to search for ‘FEIT Approved’ in the search function on CareerHub. Alternatively, you can find one independently ensuring the position meets the FEIT Placement Requirements. To be counted as an internship towards your Diploma in Professional Engineering Practice, your job must satisfy the following criteria:  The placement objective is to enrich student learning by engaging students in:   Meaningful and relevant work related to the student’s field of study or major (Eg. Civil, Mechanical, Mechatronics, Electrical, ICT, Biomedical, Software, etc.). Basic, repetitive labouring work such as bricklaying, digging, wiring, etc. should not be a significant part of a student’s role. Provide the student with practical opportunities to apply theories learnt at University. Introduce the student to professional workplace cultures and expectations. The placement aim is best achieved when students are integrated into organisations as an employee with a qualified mentor and can contribute to engineering activities over a significant time-period.   Duration/hours: The student should be engaged by organisations on a temporary or fixed-term basis and complete the below hours determined by their course.   The Bachelor with Diploma in Professional Engineering Practice requires two 6-month full-time placements totaling 1680 hours. The first internship requires a minimum of 770 hours and must not exceed 910 hours (excluding any leave taken). See further information below.   Qualified supervisor:   The supervisor must be a qualified Engineering professional or equivalent.  Please note:  All students must work between 21 and 42 hours per week. Internships must be one continuous period of employment with one employer. It is not normally possible to “string together” two or more periods of employment to make up the required number of hours. Any further work agreed to beyond the students’ course required hours is an agreement between the student and the host organisation and should be dealt with in compliance with Fair Work Ombudsman (www.fairwork.gov.au) International pupils on a student visa are permitted to work full-time hours when the position is a compulsory component of their course. Once International students have reached their required placement hours for their course requirements, they are not permitted to continue fulltime work. In the instance of host organisations offering student visa holders a position at the end of their placement, student visa holders must comply with their regular visa working hours of 20 hours per week.  Before commencing your job, we recommend that you obtain a written contract detailing the conditions of your employment (see section Further information below). We strongly advise you to communicate the objectives of your internship program with your employer, and to review these objectives throughout your internship. When you have found an internship, you must register the internship by submitting relevant documentation in the FEIT Placement Workflow on CareerHub under dashboard at least one week before your internship start date. If you have not had your internship approved by the faculty before your start date, any hours you complete will not be counted. For overseas internships, forms are required to be submitted at least one month before your departure date. It is your responsibility to ensure that both yours and your employer’s forms are submitted in a timely manner.</Data></Cell>
