    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students must secure an internship before undertaking this subject</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">You must inform the University at least one week before starting your internship (at least one month before departure for overseas internships). This is achieved by submitting your Placement Summary Form in CareerHub. Your internship starting date cannot be before the date that you officially passed the relevant prerequisite subject (i.e. the date that results are officially released by the University indicating satisfactory completion of 41035 Engineering Practice Preparation 1). You must have passed 41035 EPP1 in order to have your Placement Summary Form approved. Only after your Placement Summary Form has been approved will you be enrolled in 41036 Engineering Professional Experience 1 and the concurrent subject 40137 Work Integrated Learning 1. If you lodge your form late the hours you completed before submitting your form will not be counted. If you lodge your form close to the census date for the session, you may not be enrolled in that session.</Data></Cell>
