   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48260</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Project Management</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">You will work in groups of 5 to 9 people to develop a detailed project management plan for a given project. Your plan should include (but is not limited to): Activities, Network Diagram, Risk Management Plan, Resource Plan, Microsoft Project (or equivalent) generated Program, Detailed Financial Estimates, etc.. Details of the project will be made available in week 1. Feedback will be in the form of grading against criteria listed on the project marking guide. Comments may be added by the marker as needed. For the group assessment components in this subject, students will be assessed as a team, where each member of the team will normally receive the same mark. If you have trouble with the operation of your group, ask the tutor for advice (preferably ask as a group). If some of the group feel that other member(s) are not contributing, the tutor should be informed and a group meeting held to produce a solution. In extreme cases, a group member may be asked by the subject co-ordinator to withdraw from the subject, do extra work or accept a lower mark. Marks will be based on your group project mark and your individual contribution to the group.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Project (&amp; sub-tasks)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Assignment Final Report soft copy only needs to be submitted to Turnitin through UTSOnline (i.e. no hard copy required). Submission of soft copy is due before your presentation session. Group Presentation session times will be notified through an Announcement in UTSOnline - see Notes in Week 11 of the Programme.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Assignment Final Report soft copy only needs to be submitted to Turnitin through UTSOnline (i.e. no hard copy required). Submission of soft copy is due before your presentation session. Group Presentation session times will be notified through an Announcement in UTSOnline - see Notes in Week 11 of the Programme.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To organize and work as a team to define, produce and present outcomes, and to monitor the Project Management process.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each group will be required to do a pitch of their solution to a panel which may include the subject coordinator / lecturer and other academic staff. The assessment of your presentation will be based on the presentation marking guide provided to you on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
