   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42908</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Project Preparation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to OPELA official Website</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Online Post-Enrolment Language Assessment (OPELA)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15/03/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 15 March 2020              Online Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Online Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students complete the online post-enrolment language assessment to ascertain their level of Academic English literacy.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students define a research question, secure an academic supervisor and complete a registration form online provided by FEIT.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Kick-off</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">As per the registration form provided.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">01/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Wednesday 1 April 2020              Completed on Project MatchSee also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Completed on Project Match</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To define a research question and secure an academic supervisor.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students prepare a literature review of their chosen project topic area which is located within the domain of their course/major. The literature review will show evidence of learning from external sources, such as Library research methods programs. The literature review clearly identifies a research question that will be addressed through the follow-on research project proposal. Refer to Canvas for further details and comprehensive Assessment Guide. This task is marked by the subject teaching staff. This forms the initial literature review for your Engineering Graduate Project. This assessment will be assessed for English language proficiency. You may be directed to further language support after the completion of this subject if your language is below the required standard.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Literature Review</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Literature review</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2000-2500 words including a reference list Needs to include 15 high quality references</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">17/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 17 May 2020              Submit soft copy to Turnitin</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To review and critically evaluate academic literature in the chosen topic of study.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit soft copy to Turnitin</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A project proposal will be prepared, critically identifying a research question, series of hypotheses, details/plan on activities the student will undertake, and the evidence that will be provided to verify the student has achieved the required levels of attainment of FEIT Graduate Attributes and AQF level 9 descriptors. The plan will be used as a basis for work to be undertaken in a project subject in a following session, typically 42003 Engineering Graduate Project. Refer to Canvas for further details and comprehensive Assessment Guide.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual Project Proposal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">60</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10-11 pages excluding cover sheet and references.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">07/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 7 June 2020              Submit soft copy to Turnitin</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit soft copy to Turnitin</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To develop a professional project proposal for the research project to be undertaken.</Data></Cell>
