   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41029</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Research Preparation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students complete a problem analysis of their research interests relating to contemporary engineering challenges Student start to define their research questions with critical thinking supported by videos and suggested readings. A template is given in UTSOnline. This is marked by the subject teaching staff.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Problem Analysis Brief</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">3 - 5 pages.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 5 April 2020              Submitted softcopy to UTSonline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submitted softcopy to UTSonline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To clarify aims of research and associated risks and stakeholder concerns.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students prepare a project management plan for their proposed research. This plan includes a work-flow in terms of a Gantt chart which shows a logical sequence of their research activities. A communication plan which demonstrates communication channels with stakeholders, e.g supervisors, involved in the proposed research is also required. The student applies project management knowledge and skills to make a professional project management plan for their capstone project. A template is given in UTSonline. This is marked by the subject teaching staff.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Management Plan</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5 - 7 pages</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">03/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 3 May 2020              Submitted softcopy to UTSonline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submitted softcopy to UTSonline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This plan demonstrates student’s capability of managing and completing the proposed project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Student synthesises and refines tasks 1 and 2 to make a professional research proposal. The proposal will include:  problem definition (revised) methodology project management plan (revised)  In addition, a progress statement will be included about achieved and expected value of the particular research project. A template is given on UTSOnline. This is marked by the Capstone supervisor.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Research Proposal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">70</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Typically 15 pages</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">07/06/2020</Data></Cell>
