   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32570</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Enterprise Architecture Practice</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment task will require a group of 4-6 students to select one topic related to enterprise software architecture, conduct research, develop architecture prototype and write a report based on their findings. The deliverables of this assessment task also includes individual contribution logbooks attached in the report appendix. The group is expected to review at least 20 references relevant to the topic. The additional information about the report structure and detailed marking scheme will be provided in the assignment brief. The assignment brief will be made available via UTSOnline. Students may choose to work in a lab or from home.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Research Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Approximately twenty (20) A4 pages (single space, excluding references and appendix)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30/08/2020, 11.59pmSee also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30/08/2020, 11.59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this task is to demonstrate your ability to effectively describe the enterprise architecture both as a design and practice, its value and application to technical and business environments of different organisations and industry verticals.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">It includes 4 pre-workshop quizzes/tests (complete before the scheduled workshop session) and 4 in-workshop individual quizzes (of about maximum 20 minutes each, held as the first part of the workshop session). The quizzes shall measure the degree that the theory, as taught by the subject and practised by the individual in each of the phases of the project, is understood by each individual. No quiz submissions are allowed after the deadline. No makeup quizzes are allowed. Attendance at all workshop sessions is required.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There is no word limit.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Ongoing</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this task is to enable students to demonstrate that they can correctly describe the enterprise architecture theoretical and practical concepts, as taught by the subject and practiced by the individuals, and provide feedback to teaching staff about what is learnt or what is not.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment task will require a team of 4-6 students to develop a report comprising of an (software intensive) enterprise architecture for a case study. This also involves identifying, selecting and planning the implementation of projects arising from the enterprise architecture. The deliverables of this assessment task also includes individual contribution logbooks. The additional information will also be provided in the assignment brief.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Architecture Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There is no word limit.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">18/10/2020, 11.59pmSee also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this task is to demonstrate that you can effectively apply the enterprise architecture theoretical and practical concepts to successfully deliver an industry strength architecture project as a team or company.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">18/10/2020, 11.59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment task is related to assignment 3. This assessment task includes an oral/visual presentation of the enterprise architecture report developed in assignment 3. Each team member must participate in the presentation for individual contribution assessment. A zero mark will be given to an individual for assignment 4 who fails to participate in the report presentation for individual assessment. Each group presentation is expected to last no more than 15 minutes and subsequently allow 5 minutes for questions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There is no word limit.</Data></Cell>
