   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32569</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Enterprise Business Requirements</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will develop a complete set of use cases and models for a software system handed out in a case study document. They will be working with a group of 4 students. This assignment includes activities such as requirements elicitation through interviewing a customer, writing use cases, requirements analysis and modelling.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1: Software Requirements Specification writing (Group)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The details of the deliverable will be given in the assignment sheet.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Wednesday 15 April 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Learning is demonstrated through students' effective oral and written communications with a customer through role playing exercises to elicit software requirements for a given case study. Students will work in a small team to elicit, model and analyse customer requirements and write use cases. Students will also learn to negotiate with the customer and prioritise customer's needs and goals.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will work in the same team as Assignment 1 to write a complete Software Requirements Specification (SRS) from the use cases developed in Asssignment 1. They will have their final meeting with the Customer to elicit the remaining requirements and explore quality requirments.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 2: Writing Software Requirements Specification</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The details of the deliverable will be given in the assignemnt sheet.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">08/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 8 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To develop skills in writing complete Software Requirements Specification documentation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will work in their group and will be given an already written Software Requirements Specifications document to conduct a formal review and inspection and produce an inspection report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 3: Software Requirements Inspection (Group)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The details of the deliverable will be given in the assignment sheet.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">22/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 22 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will work in a small team to learn how to conduct a formal validation and inspection of an already developed Software Requirements Specification document in order to find defects in the document that may lead to erroneous software.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Class participation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are expected to attend and actively participate in the exercises set for 10 tutorial classes. Students will receive 1 mark for each tutorial session for satisfactory participation assesed by the tutor.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To give students ongoing practice for tasks that they need to carry out for assignements 1, 2 and 3.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The exam will be an open-book examination and will consist of multiple-choice questions derived from all the material covered in the lectures, tutorials and assignments.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Two hours</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The final examination will assess students overall understanding of the Requirements Engineering disciplinary fundamentals, ability to critique systems for standard software specification quality attributes, and understanding of constrains, ambiguities and uncertainties in requirements.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
