   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49125</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Environmental Risk Assessment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises where students are asked (1) to use statistical tools to estimate probability and uncertainty, and (2) to use a real case for preliminary risk assessment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">19/08/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday 19 August 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment is to test students' knowledge in risk assessment tools, risk ranking and risk assessment approaches, in a real world context.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises where students use relevant scientific tools to assess environmental risk from real world examples.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">35</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">14/10/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday 14 October 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assignment will be assessed by problem statement (20%), problem formulation (40%), and problem solving (40%). Feedback will be provided within 2-3 weeks of submission deadline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment is to examine students' capability of applying environmental risk assessment principles/standards to solve real world problems, using a range of tools.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is a restricted open book examination. The exam will test students’ grasp of knowledge in environmental risk assessment, e.g. the concept of hazards and risks and their assessment; understanding and application of risk assessment tools e.g. statistics and risk models; communication and presentation of ideas and solutions in addressing complex risk problems. The exam is an extension of assignments and in-class exercises.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 hours and 10 minutes reading</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will be required to apply risk assessment knowledge and tools, together with engineering standards in addressing real world problems (e.g. potential hazards).</Data></Cell>
