   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49115</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Facade Engineering</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1 (Design)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design/drawing/plan/sketch</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">07/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6.00pm Thursday 7 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment relates to topics covered in lectures 1-3 and involves structural modelling of existing installation, and wind loading assessment. This assignment intends to convey to students an understanding of the application of the Wind Loading Code, and the structural models used for various types of glazing systems. This will be a Group assignment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 2 (Design)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design/drawing/plan/sketch</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">28/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6.00pm Thursday 28 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Aluminium and Glass detailed design. This assignment intends to convey to students an understanding of the detailed structural design of glass and aluminium.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 3 (Design Strategies)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design/drawing/plan/sketch</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">04/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6.00pm Thursday 4 June 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Develop a strategic approach to how the risks arising from a design/documentation/installation process are to be addressed. The assignment intends to identify the critical decision making processes required to achieve the successful delivery of the design.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 4 (Procurement &amp; Waterproofing)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design/drawing/plan/sketch</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">04/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6.00pm Thursday 4 June 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Develop a procurement strategy, outline specification, and waterproofing assessment and details for the building described in Assignment 2. The assignment intends to identify how a procurement strategy is conveyed to the construction team, and the issues relating to the waterproofing of a specific area of the construction.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exam covering the entire subject content</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A centrally conducted formal examination covering the entire subject content. The exam will be mostly have a multiple choice and short answer type format.</Data></Cell>
