   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49047</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Finite Element Analysis</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There will be five take home assignments. They are related to problem solving and modeling using the designated software. The questions will be posted at UTSOnline. Students will generally be given 2 weeks to submit the assignments.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment #1 due: 07/08/2019 Assignment #2 due: 21/08/2019 Assignment #3 due: 04/09/2019 Assignment #4 due: 18/09/2019 Assignment #5 due: 02/10/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment #1 due: 07/08/2019 Assignment #2 due: 21/08/2019 Assignment #3 due: 04/09/2019 Assignment #4 due: 18/09/2019 Assignment #5 due: 02/10/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To provide students with practice in problem solving and applying concepts to real or model structures.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The final exam consists of 5 or 6 problem solving type questions. This is an open book exam. The problems are based on the theory taught in the subject. The type of questions reflect the real word scenarios. The two styles of questions are as follows: 1. Multiple choice questions 2. Calculation questions For multiple choice questions, students will be expected to solve for the correct answer. List and describe short answer questions will involve selecting the most appropriate answer and justifying the reason for selecting the answer. For calculation questions, students will need to apply formulae and interpret, interpolate and extrapolate tabulated and graphical data to solve for unknown values.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To give the students the opportunity to practice problem solving. The assessment task gives students the opportunity to practice various approaches related to the Finite Element Methodology. Students will classify, formulate and solve various problems and differentiate types of solutions.</Data></Cell>
