   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49117</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Floodplain Risk Management</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students complete a literature review and write a discussion paper on one of the following  how flood risk is managed in NSW the role of analytical method in defining flood risk and their limitations</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">As a guide your assignment should be approximately 10 pages long including any diagrams. The entire assignment must be submitted as a single report in Word or PDF format.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12/09/2018, midnight</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12/09/2018, midnight</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Marking critieria and marks allocation are provided in the assignment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Undertake an assignment from a choice of three covering: 1) Floodplain management policy, including the development of the policy and the rationale. 2) Floodplain management procedures - how floodplain management is implemented. 3) Role of mathematical modelling in floodplain management.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students assess the role of land use planning in reducing flood risk. Students analyse the flood risk in a town where flood risk information is provided and determine appropriate environmental planning instruments to reduce the overall flood risk in the town.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">As a guide your assignment should be approximately 10 pages long including any diagrams. The entire assignment must be submitted as a single report in Word or PDF format.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10/10/2018, midnight</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10/10/2018, midnight</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Marking critieria and marks allocation are provided in the assignment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Undertake an assignment from a choice of two covering: 1) Role of the SES and its policy and procedures, including emergency planning. 2) Development of Floodplain management options, including a selection of a mix of mitigation measures.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students assess a land development and its related existing flood risk. Students determine based on the flood risk of the town how to stage development considering the provision of flood free public infrastructure and cash flows.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 3</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Complete tables and worksheets, accompanying maps, DCP and LEP. The entire assignment must be submitted as a single report in Word or PDF format.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10/10/2018, midnight</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Marking critieria and marks allocation are provided in the assignment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Complete the assignment by assigning appropriate land uses for the different parts of a town compatible with its flood risk including development of a development control plan.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10/10/2018, midnight</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students assess the continuing flood risk of a town. Students devise based on the flood risk of the town an evacuation management plan and how it is resourced.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 4</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">As a guide your assignment should be approximately 10 pages long including any diagrams. The entire assignment must be submitted as a single report in Word or PDF format.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">24/10/2018, midnight</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">24/10/2018, midnight</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Marking critieria and marks allocation are provided in the assignment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Complete the assignment based on the role of smart housing and provision of critical infrastructure in reducing floor risk.</Data></Cell>
