   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41101</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Fundamentals of Biomedical Engineering</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are given a set of open problems about the challenges that face the health care system and how to integrate its different components, i.e., private and public hospitals, GPs, private health providers, health insurance, etc. They will need to conduct a review of existing approaches in Australia and overseas, and then come up with a recommendation that is both practical and economically sound. Students may also investigate the process of introducing a new medical device to the market.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Health innovation and economics</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To be familiar with health innovation and economics.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will be involved in processing, visualization and analysis of various types of signals. The task will also involve implementation of classification algorithms, such as support vector machines and neural networks. Each group is expected to give a presentation and submit a detailed report about the implementation of the assignment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Medical/assistive devices</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To be familiar with medical and assistive devices.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students need to model and compute the attenuation of wireless signal propagation through human body. Students may need to use suitable tools or software for wireless signal propagation simulation. Each group is expected to give a presentation and submit a detailed report about the implementation of the assignment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Wireless in biomedicine</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To be familiar with wireless applications in biomedicine.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each group is expected to give a presentation and submit a detailed report about the implementation of RNAi for the treatment of different types of diseases. This will include studying the therapeutic approaches related to genetic manipulation and the application of RNA interference (RNAi), developing an understanding of the existing therapeutic approaches, and the obtained results.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Genomics &amp; Bioinformatics</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To be familiar with genomics and bioinformatics.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students need to acquire, process and analyse physiological data. Students will be using the bio-radio portable device to acquire signals and process them in Matlab. They will need to enhance the signal quality through applying appropriate filters and then analyse the signals in both time and frequency domains..</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Matlab and Laboratory assessments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
