   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41162</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Fundamentals of Biomedical Engineering Studio A</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Depending on the project that each group has selected, the task will involve one of the following:  Evaluate a basic model of tissue-wireless signal interaction using Matlab and HFSS-ANSYS (electronics). Acquire and visualize muscle activities using Matlab Process biomedical signals using LabVIEW. Build, test and evaluate the design of a mini PCR unit Present your project findings in a professional manner using appropriate slides and information suiting the project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation: Molecular Diagnostics or Biomedical Assistive Devices</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">35</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each group is expected to give a 15-minute presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 6. 15th April. In class presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 6. 15th April. In class presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To develop a prototype or solution to the project(s) in either Molecular Diagnostics or Biomedical Assistive Devices.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Based on the chosen project, students need to demonstrate one of the following:  Analysis and classification of biomedical signals, including processing, visualization and analysis of various types of signals. The task will also involve implementation of classification algorithms, such as support vector machines and neural networks. Implementation of a simple bio-mechatronics system. This could involve the utilization of muscle activities (obtained using electromyogram) to control a particular device. Understand the fundamental concepts of RNA sequencing. Develop solutions to the current problems in sequencing technologies.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation: Biomedical Signals and Devices or Sequencing Technologies</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">35</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each group is expected to give a 15-minute presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12. 3rd June. In class presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12. 3rd June. In class presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To develop and present your solutions in either Biomedical Signals and Devices or Sequencing Technologies.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The Journal will comprise of artefacts and reflections and will be reviewed regularly during the teaching period and formative feedback will be provided by your mentor and tutors. Students will collect artefacts of their project development and implementation and reflect on how these illustrate their achievement of the subject learning objectives. This individual journal will be kept to both document progress and reflect on developing capabilities. A final reflection summary will be included in the portfolio. Artefacts might include:  Exploration of the problem Discussions with stakeholders Articulating a unique and concise design problem Idea generation and developing many solutions Prototypes developed Testing of prototype for refinement if applicable  Each artefact needs to be accompanied by an explanation and a reflection of what learning you achieved. Achievement of each learning objective must be substantiated with a minimum of 2 artefacts, each with a reflective statement. A summative reflective statement is also included as a way for you to summarise what you have learnt and how these skills might transfer to your career opportunities.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Journal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Journal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">07/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Sunday 7 June 2020              Online submission</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To record and document your participation and contribution to the selected projects.</Data></Cell>
