   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42038</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Fundamentals of Database and Software Development</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are expected to analyse a sub-system of a relatively complex IS to identify data requirements and, eventually, to design a database which meets these requirements. Given an informal description of a system, students are asked to (i) provide a conceptual model focusing on the key data underlying the target IS, (ii) eliciting database requirements for such a system and (iii) design a database that meets those requirements. Additionally, students design/identify some innovation, additional value or feature to integrate within the pre-existent system. They present the system extension at a business level and, finally, they design an extension for the existing database accordingly.  The project is group (30%) and individually (70%) assessed.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project 1 – Database design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7              7 September @ 11:59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">7 September @ 11:59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Given a system presented at the time, students elicit requirements from a data perspective and design a database accordingly.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are expected to provide a conceptualisation of the target system which is similar to the one proposed in the previous tasks but that addresses a software perspective. Therefore, requirements are understood as software requirements or functionalities. The target architecture design is composed of an abstracted description of software modules, which provide key functionalities, and their interactions. The architecture is expected to meet the software requirements previously identified. The project is group (30%) and individually (70%) assessed.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project 2 – Software design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              19 October @ 11:59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">19 October @ 11:59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Able to specify key functionalities and the interactions of a sub-system of a relatively complex IS presented at the time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students conclude their experience by completing a reflective assessment item which consists of an essay organised in multiple points. Each part of the essay requires non-obvious reflections that will be assessed against the criteria reported in the table below. Apart from the experience in the subject, issues to reflect on depend on trends at the time of delivery. In generic terms, they normally address the relationship between technology and society with a focus on IS &amp; IS professionals. This is an individual assessment task.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflective Essay – Information and Software in modern society</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">03/11/2020</Data></Cell>
