   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42080</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Fundamentals of Information Systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">4 quizzes will be conducted with each worth 10 marks (Total 40 marks). Each quiz will test students’ learning skills for each module taught in the subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Module Quiz (4)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Maximum 30 minutes with approximately 20 questions in each quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To test the knowledge of fundamental concepts covered each week. This provides regular checks as to where students are behind and provide them guidance to appropriate contents for each module taught.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Forum Contribution. This assessment will initiate group interactions and develop critical problem-solving capacity. Discussion topics from each module will be posted on the forum and the students are required to post their solutions and comment on postings from colleagues. Marks would be given based on participation and quality of content.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Online discussion</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students demonstrate their ability to apply the concepts learnt to a problem presented.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will form a group of 2 to 3. A contemporary Business IS/IT challenge will be given to each group. The group must work together to develop a report. The report must elaborate the challenge on hand highlighting key issues with it. They must research current industry practices and theory to find several potential solutions to the issue. They must then conduct a comprehensive analysis to recommend the best solution. Finding are then presented in the class as a group. The key parts of the task:  Report [Due end of Semester] (Group and individually assessed) Presentation [Due in final workshop] (Group assessed in the class)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">4000 words maximum</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment is to test students’ ability to characterise a real-life business IS/IT challenge, research the current practices, and to devise an appropriate solution for the challenge.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
