   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32555</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Fundamentals of Software Development</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In every tutorial/laboratory each week students are required to do tutorial exercises and laboratory task. Each student will complete these tasks during two hour laboratory time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Tutorial/Laboratory Work</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">At the end of the tutorial/laboratory each week.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">At the end of the tutorial/laboratory each week.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Correct use of UML Object Oriented Analysis and Design Techniques. Correct Java Code.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment of student’s participation in tutorial exercises and laboratory tasks.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A case study is released in the second week of semester and following are produced from this specification. Students transform this text into (i) use case descriptions (ii) create three UML diagrams: a use case model, a class diagram and sequence diagrams (iii) write code in Java for three goals (iv)write code to connect to database (v) write code to design user interface.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Software Models and Java Programming</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Part 1 (Use case model) and Part 2 (Use case descriptions) due in Week 5 (7th April) ; Part 3 (Class Diagram) and Part 4 (Sequence Diagrams) due in Week 8(5th May); Part 5 (Screen Design), Part 6 (Connection to Database ), and Part 7 (Java code) due in Week 12(2nd June).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Part 1 (Use case model) and Part 2 (Use case descriptions) due in Week 5 (7th April) ; Part 3 (Class Diagram) and Part 4 (Sequence Diagrams) due in Week 8(5th May); Part 5 (Screen Design), Part 6 (Connection to Database ), and Part 7 (Java code) due in Week 12(2nd June).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Correct use of UML Object Oriented Analysis and Design Techniques. Correct Java Code.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment of student’s drawing of software modelling skills and Java programming skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Exam.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Multiple Choice Examination</Data></Cell>
