   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42075</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Game Design Studio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There are 3 separate quizzes scheduled throughout the semester. Each quiz is worth 5%. These will be completed during the regularly scheduled lecture time and will last approximately 30 minutes. Questions will cover the material covered in the lectures and as part of assigned reading. The written quiz will mostly be in the form of short-answer questions. No outside material is allowed.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Short Quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class in Week 4, Week 8 and Week 11.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class in Week 4, Week 8 and Week 11.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Measure progress and understanding of the subject material</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">You will work on a major game project as a team. The work will be divided into 4 Sprints. Each Sprint is worth 15%.  For each Sprint, you will be required to set tasks to be completed by the end of the Sprint, estimate the amount of time you expect the tasks to take, record the tasks as they are completed and submit a Sprint report. Also, you must write a group and an individual reflection following the Recount-React-Analyse pattern. Sprint report templates with samples will be provided via UTSOnline. Intermediate deliverables: Sprint reports and demos of work in-progress. Final deliverables: Presentation and report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Team Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">60</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              All code, assets and documents submitted through UTSOnline by Friday midnight (11:59PM) of Week 6, Week 8, Week 10 and Week 12. For this assessment, 50% of the grade will be determined by the group's overall performance and the 50% will be determined by each member's contribution.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">All code, assets and documents submitted through UTSOnline by Friday midnight (11:59PM) of Week 6, Week 8, Week 10 and Week 12. For this assessment, 50% of the grade will be determined by the group's overall performance and the 50% will be determined by each member's contribution.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Putting theoretical skills to practice</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There are 4 separate deliverables for this assessment: 1- Build an Arcade Game from the 80s (from Scratch) and document the process (includes reflection) (5%); 2- Build an Arcade Game from the 90s (from Scratch) in teams using SCRUM (includes reflection) (5%); 3 – Build a Game to Client Specifications (Part 1). Design a Simple Game, Write User Stories and Find a Team that Builds your Game (5%); 4 – Build a Game to Client Specifications (Part 2). Implement a Game Following the User Stories written by another team (10%).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab Exercises</Data></Cell>
