   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42056</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Games Research Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A report (roughly 1000 words) should be submitted that identifies a chosen project topic, the motivation for undertaking this specific project, the expected outcomes of the project, and a learning contract that determines how success within the project is determined and how marks will be allocated.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Proposal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">4</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 4              Submission via UTSOnline/Canvas using the provided proposal template. (Deadline: Friday midnight of Week 4)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submission via UTSOnline/Canvas using the provided proposal template. (Deadline: Friday midnight of Week 4)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assessment task provides students with an early milestone to ensure that they have made suitable progress in identifying a project through consultation with their supervisor. By this stage, students and supervisors should have established the project direction and learning contracts such that students are aware of the expectations of them for the session before the Census Date.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There are three components to this task:  Project Deliverables – the exact deliverable(s) of the project (a prototype, a design, a literature review, etc.) are determined by the learning contract established early in the semester with the supervisor and marked accordingly. Project Report – the report will be in the format of an IEEE or ACM double-column publication (maximum of 8 pages) and will contain a title, abstract, a refined discussion of the project objectives and motivation, a description of the work done and the deliverable, an analysis of the deliverable of the project, and a discussion of potential future work. In the case where the deliverable is a literature review or a research report itself, the Project Deliverable and Project Report can be combined into a larger document.  Self-Reflection – A written reflection and self-evaluation of the student’s own performance, knowledge gained, and potential areas of self-improvement.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Deliverables</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">85</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              Project Report to be submitted via UTSOnline/Canvas using the supplied ACM double-column research paper format. The reflection part of this assessment should be incorporated into the Discussion, Future Work, and Conclusion parts of this report. (Deadline: Friday midnight of Week 12)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Report to be submitted via UTSOnline/Canvas using the supplied ACM double-column research paper format. The reflection part of this assessment should be incorporated into the Discussion, Future Work, and Conclusion parts of this report. (Deadline: Friday midnight of Week 12)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment is the culmination of the work done throughout the session. It is a final summative evaluation of the project overall, including both the success of the project and the student’s growth in knowledge and skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
