   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49257</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Geographic Information Systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Computer Laboratory Exercises: For each laboratory class, students will be given a GIS problem they will need to solve, applying their newly learnt skills. You will submit your work and any answer sheets electronically by the given due date. There will be eight practical exercises, of which Lab 2 (worth 5%) and two further labs (worth 7.5%) will be assessed. These two exercises will be chosen at random.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Practicals</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">During the lab class as students finish their work or at a later date (as stated in the lab exercise) for students who required to work beyond the class hour. The solutions of the lab exercises will be demonstrated during lab classes or lectures.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">During the lab class as students finish their work or at a later date (as stated in the lab exercise) for students who required to work beyond the class hour. The solutions of the lab exercises will be demonstrated during lab classes or lectures.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Correctness of solution, comprehensiveness and interpretation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To practice real world problems and promote students' critical thinking. To encourage a deep approach to learning. To improve students' hands on skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is an individual assignment. Students will be required to write an essay on a given question based on their own research.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual Assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Essay</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">07/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Tuesday 7 April 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation/structure, appropriateness/sufficient detail of content, referencing.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To make a sound link between learning, applications of the topics and each student’s own discipline or field of interest To assess and further develop students’ research and writing skills</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is an open book online quiz done in students' own time. The quiz will be open for one week and students will have one hour to complete the quiz once started. It covers most topics taught up to and including Lecture 5.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Online Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Sunday 10 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Correctness and comprehension.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To encourage students to review the main concepts of the topics and integrate the knowledge gained throughout the first half of the session. To assess students' learning.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In groups of 4-5, students will collaborate on a project for a given site. The project will include stakeholder analysis, the mapping of the project site using GPS and handheld GIS, the acquisition of additional data as required and a purpose-directed spatial/environmental data analysis using GIS. Students will need to deliver a project report about their work and give a brief oral and a poster presentation. All group members will have to actively participate in either of the presentations. Each member of a group will receive the same mark for both components of the assignment (see Groupwork, below). Groupwork For the group assignment students will be assessed as a team, which means each group member will normally receive the same mark. If you have trouble with the operation of your group, ask your tutor for advice (preferably ask as a group). If some of the group feel that other members are not contributing, the tutor should be informed and a group meeting held to produce a solution. In extreme cases, a group member may be asked by the tutor to withdraw from the Subject, do extra work or accept a lower mark. No complaints about group operation will be considered after the assignment has been submitted.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Wednesday 20 May 2020              Report: 20th May 2020. Oral and Poster Presentation: 21st May 2020.  Note: There is a field trip on Thursday 30th April 2020.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report: 20th May 2020. Oral and Poster Presentation: 21st May 2020.  Note: There is a field trip on Thursday 30th April 2020.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Correctness, comprehesiveness and completeness of information acquisition and management, user identification and analysis, models and spatial analysis; appropriate presentation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To improve students' capability to identify information required for conducting common environmental engineering projects. To evaluate various alternative solution procedures and employ appropriate techniques and present the results in a professional approach. To develop the research capabilities of students. To promote students' team work skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is an open book test during the last lecture. This test will cover the application of most topics and examine your understanding of the impact and the potential of GIS for environmental engineering projects, and will evaluate your project design skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Test</Data></Cell>
