   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48360</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Geotechnical Engineering</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will classify, formulate and solve various problems, and differentiate the different types of solutions. Assignment tasks will be posted on UTSOnline. Marked assignments can be collected in the tutorial classes, two weeks after submission.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Geotechnical Engineering assignments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Varies with each assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">* Assignments  Set 1: Week 7, Sunday 3/05/20, Time: 23:59 * Assignments  Set 2: Week 11, Sunday, 13/05/20 Time: 23:59See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">* Assignments  Set 1: Week 7, Sunday 3/05/20, Time: 23:59 * Assignments  Set 2: Week 11, Sunday, 13/05/20 Time: 23:59</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To strengthen design skills and problem solving techniques; identify students’ issues in analysis and design, apply corrective measures</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The main aim of the group project is to develop design skills for solving Geotechnical Engineering problems. The description of the group project will be provided to all students. All projects require an oral presentation and a written report, which includes the methods used in the design and the necessary calculations. Marks will be awarded based on the written report, the presentation and the adequacy of the design work and correctness of calculations.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Major design project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12, Sunday 07/06/20, Time: 23:59.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12, Sunday 07/06/20, Time: 23:59.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Work in a team to evaluate, design and summarise a real life geotechnical project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Three open book quizzes will be held during the teaching session. The aims of these quizzes are to keep students up to date with the concepts and methods covered in lectures, practice problem solving techniques, provide a convenient means for students to assess their understanding of fundamental rules and ability to deal with small design and practical problems.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Class quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 1 - Date: Week 4, Tuesday, 31/03/20, Time: 10am – 11am (Tut1) and 12pm - 1pm (Tut2);  Quiz 2 - Date: Week 8, Tuesday, 05/05/20, Time: 12pm - 11am (Tut1) and 12pm - 1pm (Tut2);  Quiz 3 - Date: Week 11, Tuesday, 26/05/20, Time: 12pm - 11am (Tut1) and 12pm - 1pm (Tut2).See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To strengthen design skills and problem solving techniques; identify students’ issues in analysis and design, apply corrective measures</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 1 - Date: Week 4, Tuesday, 31/03/20, Time: 10am – 11am (Tut1) and 12pm - 1pm (Tut2);  Quiz 2 - Date: Week 8, Tuesday, 05/05/20, Time: 12pm - 11am (Tut1) and 12pm - 1pm (Tut2);  Quiz 3 - Date: Week 11, Tuesday, 26/05/20, Time: 12pm - 11am (Tut1) and 12pm - 1pm (Tut2).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This exam lasts for about 2 hours and normally consists of 5 to 7 questions on different topics. The final exam is an open book and students can bring calculators (including programmable) and any written material in the examination venue.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final exam</Data></Cell>
