   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32531</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Global Information Systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report on the trends in globalisation. It will be greatly beneficial for students to be present during the lectures to understand what is going on and to write their Report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual Assignment Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The Report should be not more than 3000 words.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">01/09/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5.00pm Tuesday 1 September 2020              Must be submitted through Turnitin. Hard copies are not accepted.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Must be submitted through Turnitin. Hard copies are not accepted.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The report will help students gain a deeper understanding of Global Information System issues, both theoretically and practically through a critical examination of literature published in books, refereed journals, conference proceedings etc, published after 2012. A minimum of 20 seperate articles and/or books should be accessed as a basis for the report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 2 Report (20%) is a group work, wherein students are expected to work on a substantial problem related to global information systems and global business. Creation of a project report and presentation of project will be in a group. All presentations will take place towards the end of the semester, and students are expected to be present and participate in formal presentation of the project. Presentation (10%) will be assessed individually. Hardcopies of the project reports will NOT be returned. You will be given a separate sheet with the marker's comments. Soft copies of both report and presentation are required. For group assessments in this Subject, students will be assessed as a team, where each member of the team will receive the same mark for the assignment. If you have trouble with the operation of your group, ask the Subject coordinator for advice (preferably ask as a group). If some of the groups feel that other members are not contributing, the Lecturer should be informed and a group meeting held to produce a solution. In extreme cases a group member may be asked by the lecturer to do extra work or accept a lower mark. No complaints about group operation will be considered after the assignment has been handed in to the lecturer.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Assignment Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The Report should be not more than 3000 words.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">29/09/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5.00pm Tuesday 29 September 2020              Must be submitted through Turnitin. Hard copies are not accepted.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Must be submitted through Turnitin. Hard copies are not accepted.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20% Group Report 10% Individual Presentation Please note - Weightings are approximate. Please see subject guide for mark allocation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The report helps to gain a general understanding of global information systems and how organisations attempt to leverage business performance and even deliver new business directions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Based on topics covered in the class, reading material provided and research expected of the students.</Data></Cell>
