   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42012</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Green Technologies: Water-Waste-Energy Nexus</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to select one favourable green technology based on current Sustainable Design Features in Faculty of Engineering and IT Building (CB11). They need to illustrate the understanding of targeted technology using a real case study. The content consists of: 1) the initial cause of problem; 2) why use this technology; 3) how this technology can help, including the concept of the technology, the engineering design of process and operation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Green Technology Case Study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">maximum 8 pages for each assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Due date: 28 Aug. 2020 by 11:59 pm through Turnitin</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Due date: 28 Aug. 2020 by 11:59 pm through Turnitin</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of the assignment is to cultivate students' cognitive ability, as well as improve their research skills. Through this task, students will gain better in-depth knowledge about green technology and motivate their enthusiasm for learning through self-study.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Closed-book and supervised tests. Cover topics from Week 1 to Week 4</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">90 minutes + 5 minutes reading time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Close-book Quiz – Examination date: 29 Aug. 2019 (Week 6)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Close-book Quiz – Examination date: 29 Aug. 2019 (Week 6)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assess students' knowledge of green technologies (the need, fundamental science and engineering principles) and green technologies for water and wastewater treatment and management.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are divided into groups and are required to organise and participate in a field trip to either water/wastewater treatment plant or waste treatment plant or landfill site. After the visit, students are requested to present their finding and evaluations in front of class. Peer feedback for presentation will be given by subject Coordinator as well as other groups. They also need to answer questions raised from other groups. Most treatment plants would accept students in groups, so please organise yourselves into groups. Prior to the visit, students need to undertake research and get information about the plant visited as well as prepare a list of questions you would ask the field inspector and/or operator. Please note, the field trip report and presentation need to be an group effort. The report will be marked and written feedback will be given.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report and Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group written report (maximum 20 pages for each assignment)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation on 14 Oct. 2020 (Week 11) and report is due on 16 Oct. 2020 (by 11:59 pm through Turnitin).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of the task is to provide students with a real-life situation to better understand present technological advances in sustainable engineering as well as acquire Australian industry experience. Through this task, students will experience the true art of green technology. They will also gain competence in the recognition and evaluation of green technology based on technical, environmental, economic and socio-cultural criteria.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation on 14 Oct. 2020 (Week 11) and report is due on 16 Oct. 2020 (by 11:59 pm through Turnitin).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Questions include a mix of multiple choice questions, short essay questions and calculation questions. University guidelines will be strictly followed for all exams. The final exam is an open book exam.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Formal Final Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 hours + 10 minutes reading time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assess what students know about green technologies for waste management and energy recovery, as well as the assessment and evaluation of green technologies. The final examination will incorporate both theoretical and practical questions where students will be expected to demonstrate the knowledge which they have learnt in this subject and problem solving skills to provide the correct answers.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
