   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41167</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Health Innovation Studio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There are several different kinds of projects for students to select. After selecting a project, the students are asked to design a functional solution, write a report and pitch their solution.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Health Innovation project - Early solution</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In Weeks 2, 3, 4 and 5 you will partake in a weekly observation of the work done in each session, with marks given in class based on the student’s effort each week (20%); Week 5 Health Innovation project report due on 22/8/2019 at 23:59 in turnitin via UTSOnline (50%); Week 6 Health Innovation project pitching in class (30%).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In Weeks 2, 3, 4 and 5 you will partake in a weekly observation of the work done in each session, with marks given in class based on the student’s effort each week (20%); Week 5 Health Innovation project report due on 22/8/2019 at 23:59 in turnitin via UTSOnline (50%); Week 6 Health Innovation project pitching in class (30%).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstration of team and individual ability of design/implementation of an innovative health solution and demonstration of the ability to communicate effectively with peers and general audiences.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection entries on top 5 moments during the semester</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflective ability assessment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">An average of 200-word entry per top five moments over 10 weeks, plus other additional media as appropriate.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">01/10/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Tuesday 1 October 2019              in turnitin via UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">in turnitin via UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstration of ability to communicate effectively with peers and reflect on their learning.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to learn to use a tool (e.g. Jira) in order to record team process activities, and, to provide evidence of team and project level decisions. Their work in the tool will be assessed by their participation in the tools, as evidenced by usage and comments.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Process assessment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">08/10/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Tuesday 8 October 2019              in agreed tool. Show in class. However, participation is expected at least once a week from Weeks 7 – 11 (except STUVAC).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this task is to learn to make and record process decisions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">in agreed tool. Show in class. However, participation is expected at least once a week from Weeks 7 – 11 (except STUVAC).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Requirements for the team’s project are developed over the semester. Also developed our assessments and tests against the requirements. At the end of the semester judgement is made by the team and by their mentor/client as to how well they have achieved the requirements.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Product design and assessment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">08/10/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Tuesday 8 October 2019              in class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">in class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this task is to learn how to build solutions satisfying customer requirements and assess against those requirements.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The student needs to pitch the solution to the customer in the form of a 3-minute video/5-minute presentation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Pitch of the solution to the customer</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
