   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41166</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Healthomics and Molecular Diagnostics Studio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Weekly short presentations for the studio or short presentation of a potential solution for a given problem associated with the subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Pitch #1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/04/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12.00pm Friday 5 April 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To develop the skill of researching problems/background information and partially to measure the development of presentation skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to do a presentation or pitch on their current progress. This will be graded, and the facilitators will provide feedback.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Pitch #2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">24/05/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12.00pm Friday 24 May 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task ensures students are meeting their set milestones and deliverables for the project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20-25 minute presentation to demonstrate knowledge of any of these:  Understanding of sequencing technologies, their limitations, and their use in solving biological problems. Predicting how high-throughput sequencing will influence health care, human ethics and other aspect of society. The student can also choose to present the result of the laboratory work in a frame of a scientific presentation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final seminar</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20-25 minutes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">07/06/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12.00pm Friday 7 June 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To be familiar with the engineering background and problems associated with diagonostic technologies (PCR machine) and show progress in presentation skills and communicating ideas.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The student will reflect one of the aspects of diagnostic technologies by demonstrating their skill in written communication:  describing one specific stakeholder by highlighting key engineering problems associated with it discussing its limitations, and predicting future improvements contemplating how PCR is changing society (i.e. health care, research, data storage, privacy, ethics, investment) project report that describe the process and result of the design work.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Written report, essay format max 5 pages</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">16/06/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 16 June 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To be familiar with the engineering background and problems associated with diagnostic technologies (PCR machine) and articulate the final design as a written report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
