    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A professionally written laboratory report is required for the lab experiments on Heat Exchangers. It should contain Table of Contents, Introduction, Methodology, Results and Discussion, Conclusion, and References. Sample calculations of at least one test are required. Lab report is a group work, and must be submitted in teams of 3-5 students only. More details can be found at UTS Online/Course Documents/ Lab Document.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There will be no physical Lab. We will upload the video of the Heat Exchanger Lab with step by step setting up the lab and collection of the data if the university is open for filming. Reading data will be provided between Week 6 and week 9. Report due Week 11 (05/06/2020 at 11:59pm)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There will be no physical Lab. We will upload the video of the Heat Exchanger Lab with step by step setting up the lab and collection of the data if the university is open for filming. Reading data will be provided between Week 6 and week 9. Report due Week 11 (05/06/2020 at 11:59pm)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The final examination will cover the contents in the whole subject:   The final examination will cover the contents in the whole subject. Duration: 2 hrs + 10 mins reading time  Open-book (any materials of print, typed, or written type can be used) There will be four questions.  Programmable calculators are allowed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Exam</Data></Cell>
