   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Human-centred Design Methods</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">For this quiz, students will work together in small groups of 3. Students are quizzed on their understanding of the subject matter, the way the subject itself is set up, and their responsibilities as ethical and people-focused researchers.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz on subject</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1 hour</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06/08/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Thursday 6 August 2020              During tutorial</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">During tutorial</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstrated knowledge of the subject through preparation and teamwork</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To provide students with an awareness of human-centred research methods as taught in this subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assignment requires students to independently study and develop a research proposal, followed by contacting potential participants and performing in-depth interviews. Afterwards, students are encouraged to learn substantial methods for the analysis of data and its reporting. Tutorials and class meetings give students the opportunity to receive guidance and feedback on their progress.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Poster on interviews</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">One A1-sized printed poster, with A4- appendices including all transcripts and all thematic analysis details.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">03/09/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">01:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1.00pm Thursday 3 September 2020              Submission is through Turnitin in Canvas before 1pm on Thursday 3 September.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submission is through Turnitin in Canvas before 1pm on Thursday 3 September.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To provide students with the opportunity to put into practice and further develop skills in human-centred research. This includes literature research, developing relevant questions, performing interviews, qualitative data analysis, and communication of findings.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assignment requires students to independently study and develop a research proposal, followed by contacting potential participants and performing in-depth interviews. Afterwards, students are encouraged to learn substantial methods for the analysis of data and its reporting. Compared to assessment task 2, this task puts more emphasis on the quality of writing a paper and dissemination of findings in an academic way. Due to the visual and physical nature of most cultural probes, a video deliverable enables students to communicate their work effectively. Tutorials and class meetings give students the opportunity to receive guidance and feedback on their progress.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Short paper and video on probes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Paper: No more than 4 pages, using the provided template, with appendices. Video: not exceeding 90 seconds.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">22/10/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">01:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1.00pm Thursday 22 October 2020              Submission is through Turnitin in Canvas before 1pm on Thursday 22 October.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To provide students with the opportunity to put into practice and further develop skills in human-centred research. Following the direction set out in task 2, this task approaches similar research questions with another qualitative research tool, namely cultural probes. Students will learn its application and analysis, and communication of findings.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submission is through Turnitin in Canvas before 1pm on Thursday 22 October.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will select one or more of the papers from the provided reading list, read it, analyse it and then present their findings in class time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Short presentation (10 minutes plus 5 for questions). Short document (no more than 1000 words, summarising and critiquing the paper).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Student paper presentations will be distributed throughout Block 2, 3 and 4. The accompanying document will be submitted at the time of the presentation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Student paper presentations will be distributed throughout Block 2, 3 and 4. The accompanying document will be submitted at the time of the presentation.</Data></Cell>
