    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To provide students with the opportunity to put into practice and further develop skills in human-centred research. This includes literature research, developing relevant questions, performing interviews, qualitative data analysis, and communication of findings.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assignment requires students to independently study and develop a research proposal, followed by contacting potential participants and performing in-depth interviews. Afterwards, students are encouraged to learn substantial methods for the analysis of data and its reporting. Compared to assessment task 2, this task puts more emphasis on the quality of writing a paper and dissemination of findings in an academic way. Due to the visual and physical nature of most cultural probes, a video deliverable enables students to communicate their work effectively. Tutorials and class meetings give students the opportunity to receive guidance and feedback on their progress.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Short paper and video on probes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Paper: No more than 4 pages, using the provided template, with appendices. Video: not exceeding 90 seconds.</Data></Cell>
