   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48362</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Hydraulics and Hydrology</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students undertake practice based assignments, similar to what engineers undertake in practice. Students will use computer modelling to undertake detailed calculation to support their proposed design. One assignment will be hydrology based and the other hydraulics.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">60</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Written reports vary with the assignment tasks but not more than 10 pages.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Hydrology assn 26 Sept Hydraulics assn 10 October</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Hydrology assn 26 Sept Hydraulics assn 10 October</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To demonstrate an understanding of hydraulic and hydrology modelling and usefully communicate subject knowledge through the preparation of written reports.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The examination is open-book examination comprising 4-5 questions. All question should be answered. The questions will be a mix of theoretical and calculation type questions. The exam duration is 2 hours with 10 min reading time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Exam</Data></Cell>
