    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41193</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">IS Data Visualisation Studio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students work in groups to identify a real-world problem, identify different stakeholders and analyse their respective decision-making environments using design thinking practices.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Problem definition and stakeholder analysis</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group report: maximum 1500 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students become familiar with the purpose of problem definition and stakeholder analysis.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students work in groups to identify and ethically harvest data and apply contemporary data quality and data integration methodologies.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Data preparation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group report: maximum 2000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students practice ethical data harvesting and ensuring data quality.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In this task, students are expected to demonstrate the main features of their data exploration prototype. All group members are expected to actively contribute to their prototype demo and will be asked on-the-spot questions about different features of the prototype, including brief statement of the problem, the underlying data structures, data quality and integration practices and visual ethics, multidimensional model and data exploration features.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Visual data exploration prototype - presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15 mins per group</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students demonstrate their visual data exploration prototype.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students work in groups to design multidimensional models suitable for non-technical stakeholders as well as implement a prototype using a commercial data visualisation software.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Visual data exploration prototype - report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group report: maximum 2500 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students develop capability in designing a visual data exploration prototype.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Following group presentations, each student reflects on the lessons learned from their own group project and the in-class presentations given by other groups. The reflection focuses on the central question: “If given an opportunity to do this project again, what would I do differently?” The reflection is expected to cover the whole life-cycle of the project, starting from the analysis of stakeholder problems, problem-driven (rather than data-driven) visual data exploration needs of different stakeholders, identification and ethical harvesting of relevant data, data quality, integration, data modeling for the identified stakeholders, design and implementation of a data exploration environment all the way to project presentations and lessons learned.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Prototyping project reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To reflect on the project in the form of key lessons learned.</Data></Cell>
