   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32563</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">IT Professional and Society</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1. Discussion (10%): Students are expected to participate in class discussions on IT professional and ethical issues. You may refer to lectures, books, journals, websites or personal experiences in discussions. Try to back up your contributions with arguments and evidence with relevant references, links, etc. Participations will be audited by teaching staff. Discussion topics will be provided in lectures and tutorials. You should use coherent arguments bearing in mind the advice given in lectures and on this site for making professional and ethical arguments.  ask intelligent answers or suggest ideas to others ask and answer questions, agree, disagree or try to bring the discussion back to the topic discussions should relate to the topic use coherent arguments make comments of personal nature that are respecting others.  2. Reflective essay (15%): 3-5 pages (excluding the title, TOC and reference pages).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Participation in online discussion</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstration</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">17/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6.00pm Friday 17 April 2020              Week 6</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 6</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group (10%) and Individual (10%) marks. In Assignments 2 and 3, your group (5-6 in a group) will research the topic thoroughly, presenting your main findings (Assignment 2 Project presentation) to your fellow students and writing up your findings in a standard report format also (Assignment 3 Project written Report). Project presentation: You and your group will be given 20 minutes to present the main findings of your project and to answer any questions from the audience. You must submit a group nomination form in Week 4-5. Your presentation time/date will be allocated in Week 6. Full details of assignment 2 will be available on the Canvas subject site.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week range</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 8 to Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project written report: Your group will research the selected topic thorougly, writing up your findings in a standard report format and also presenting (Assignment 2 presentation) your main findings to your fellow students. You will need to discuss any ethical implications, social, cultural impact issues and/or legal issues connected with your topic. Questions you need to answer and justify your answers from the evidence accumulated in the research of your topic. The group report must be submitted on time. This assignment (total 35%) consists of: 30% Project report marks - Group (10%) and Individual (20%) marks. 5% Individual contribution marks (in week 12 tutorial). Full details will be available on the Canvas subject site.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">35</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group report: maximum 20 pages excluding title pages, TOC, references and appendix.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6.00pm Friday 5 June 2020              Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In assignment 4, you will produce a reflection on what you have learned during the semester. Write your learning experiences from all lectures, tutorials and assessments. When reflecting on what you have learned you should consider the questions below:  what you already knew: what was your position on ethics at the start? what you expected to learn what you learnt from lectures, tutorials, other students’ assignment 2 project presentations and Online Discussion Board what difference do you imagine it will make to your future life, if any? Speculate on what IT ethics may be in the future.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflective Essay</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The reflection must form a coherent, structured work, maximum 10 pages Times New Roman 11pt, 1.5 spacing, number all pages (excluding the title, table of contents and appendix pages). You may show references (Harvard style) to websites, books and journals but it is your ability to discuss the subject matter and how you have developed that knowledge which matters. Details will be available on the subject site.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6.00pm Friday 12 June 2020              Week 13</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 13</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
