   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42011</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Industrial Water Pollution Control Engineering</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to undertake a site visit to an industrial site to understand elements of a wastewater treatment system. A site visit report that describes what was observed, and a critical analysis of the systems is to be submitted.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Field Visit Based Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10 pages</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">09/01/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Thursday 9 January 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The aim of this task is for students to undertake a site visit and critically analyse the systems in place based on current industry standards.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There will be class assignments during the blocks. The class assignments will consist of a number of short-answer questions both quantitative and qualitative. Feedback will be given to students in class and also in their marked class assignments within the first two weeks. Assignment marks will be posted on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Class assignments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Variable.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">These assessment tasks will occur during the block classes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">These assessment tasks will occur during the block classes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assess knowledged learned in the class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to design a treatment system for an industrial plant.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15 pages</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30/01/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Thursday 30 January 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to demonstrate that they have learnt, understood and apply knowledge related to designing a treatment system for a specific industry.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This will be an open book exam, and as such you can bring your lecture notes and books for your reference during the exam. The exam will consist of a number of short-answer questions both quantitative and qualitative.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The duration of the examination is 2 hours and 10 minutes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
