   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">31489</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Industry Study 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will develop a business case for addressing a business problem. Students will identify and describe a problem to be solved, something to be designed or something to be developed. There should also be a description of how this specific project fits into the organization's overall context, the objectives of the project and its expected benefits. There should be sufficient information for the organization and the university mentor to assess the merits of the intended project, the likely effort for its completion and the likelihood of successful completion.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Research background: Research problem</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Approximately 2-3 A4 pages (1000-1500 Words) excluding references and appendix.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:55 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.55pm Wednesday 15 April 2020See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The problem and its context are clearly described. The significance of the problem to the organization is clearly described. A feasible method to achieve achieve an outcome is clearly described. The expected benefits of the outcome are clearly described.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students identify a problem to be investigated, a problem to be solved, something to be designed or something to be developed, and then develop a proposal for the investigation, design or development. An essential element of the problem is that it must involve some unknown or novel elements.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will extend the assignment 1 report (problem description, literature review) to include a suitable method with which to complete the project, a description of how the project was carried out, the findings or results, some analysis of the findings and a conclusion. Since the project could be an investigation or a design or a development or solving a problem the description of the method should be a plan of how the main work of the project will be done and how the validity and integrity of the results will be assured. Since few projects happen as they were planned, a description of what actually happened should also reflect on what can be done in similar future projects to assure better outcomes. The findings or project outcomes should be analysed to draw some conclusions about the project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final report: Research problem investigation and results</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">80</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Approximately 10-12 A4 pages (5000-6000 Words) excluding references and appendix.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">22/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:55 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.55pm Monday 22 June 2020See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Review of existing knowledge of the problem and potential solutions. Implementation of proposed and described method. Outcomes are analysed to produce findings that are then synthesized to form conclusions. Conclusions and recommendations are described.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students perform their proposed investigation or design or develop their proposed solution to problem with due attention to rigour and validity.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In this assessment task you should argue your case, or compare and contrast theory and practice, deduce generalisations from your case study, etc. You should state your conclusions and recommendations. As well you should state whether you met your objectives and how well your methodology worked. Finally lessons learnt should be discussed.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Approximately 20 pages (7000-8000 words)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Not applicable</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Not applicable              20th January 2015</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The final report must address all the objectives reflecting the student’s understanding, critical thinking and development of methodologies and practices suitable for their chosen topic of study.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20th January 2015</Data></Cell>
