   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">31490</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Industry Study 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will identify and describe a problem to be solved, something to be designed or something to be developed. There should also be a description of how this specific project fits into the organization's overall context, the objectives of the project and its expected benefits. There should be sufficient information for the organization and the university mentor to assess the merits of the intended project, the likely effort for its completion and the likelihood of successful completion.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project proposal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Between 1000 and 2500 words (about 2 to 5 pages).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 6</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The problem and its context are clearly described. The expected benefits of the project are identified. The proposed work is feasible.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students identify a problem to be investigated, a problem to be solved, something to be designed or something to be developed then develop a proposal for the investigation, design or development. An essential element of the problem is that it must involve some unknown or novel elements.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will extend the assignment 1 report by including a review of existing knowledge, and a description of their proposed research, design or development method. Students will perform the research, design or development and record the results of doing so. Students need to discuss and link findings from both the theory (literature review) and practice (organisational review). Students need to make final conclusions with future investigation options. Students need to incorporate feedback received from both sponsor organisation and academic mentors. Additional information and assessment criteria details will be provided in the assignment 2 handout.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Investigation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">80</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Approximately fifteen (15) A4 pages (5000-6000 words)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">TBA</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">TBA</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Review of existing knowledge identifies obstacles to progress. Feasible investigation method is proposed. The proposed investigation is performed. Investigation results are analysed and synthesized to form conclusions. The conclusions are evaluated against the project's intended benefits.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students perform their proposed investigation or design or develop their proposed solution to problem.</Data></Cell>
