   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41181</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Information Security and Management</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Student teams must prepare a report of approximately 2500 words and must include:  description of the targeted IT environment; a detailed analysis of the corporate environment; and plan for approaching the identification of security threats.  Group assessed 20%, individually assessed 20%.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Planning Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2500 words.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment is for students to demonstrate their ability to plan an investigation of security management issues in corporate organisations. Students are required to work as a team and use IT security planning and project management principles to plan an IT security investigation and management project. They will be required to follow prescribed procedures to evaluate the risk levels, potential impact of threats and vulnerabilities, and cost‐benefit analysis of control methods. Student teams will be tested on their ability to analyse the security objectives of businesses and requirements and propose justified contingency plans to manage security risks.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to submit a case investigation report of approximately 2000 words along with exhibits to support findings and a bibliography. This report should consist of:  an overview of the IT security management case; list of risks, threats and possible countermeasures; analysis of findings; review and reflection on the findings and propose justified recommendations.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case Investigation Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2000 words.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment is for students to conduct investigation of serious security management issues in corporate organisations. Students will be required to apply prescribed management and audit procedures as well as analysis of roles, duties and privileges. They will be required to prepare a security management report based on the findings of their investigation and by using knowledge of IT security policies, risk assessment and risk management processes. Students are also required to identify personnel security, training, security education needs, and associated legal and ethical awareness.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Open book exam.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Two hours.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This open book examination will assess students’ appliance of security analysis and security management methods to minimize the risks and procedures to security audit. Students must demonstrate an ability to relate, analyse and respond to questions around IT security management and audit under examination conditions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
