   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32560</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Information Systems Architecture Design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Preparation and participation throughout the course. Students are expected to attend all sessions and actively participate in them. Participation may be evaluated by participation in discussions (online and in-class), performance in class exercises, and delivery of required outcomes from those activities. Much of these activities will revolve around case studies that will be used to explore key topics supporting/complementing the subject matter. Students are required to read/review each case study in class. They will then be required to complete the form “Analysis and Debate Preparation Form” available at UTSOnline, submit it to lecturer, and participate in the discussion that follows. In summary, participation means: Written submission of the weekly discussion questions / hands-on sessions. Active involvement in in-class discussions. Active and regular involvement in online discussions. Case study review and discussion related to the topic will covered each week. The discussion/debate of each case study will contribute equally to the total mark (10%). Students will receive oral feedback during the class session and final marks in week 12. The full specification and requirements will be available on UTSOnline in week 1.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Class Exercise Preparation and Performance</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Throughout the term in each class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Throughout the term in each class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual assessment and preparation for class sessions and level of performance in class exercises.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment has two components: in-depth topic analysis and prototype development. In-depth topic analysis: You work on this assignment as a group (as approved by your lecturer). The number of group members will be decided in class. Your lecturer will assign your group to one of the topic areas after receiving your topic preferences. Each student in the group will be assessed on their individual contributions and peer assessment. For in-depth analysis each group needs to: (Task 1) Perform a literature analysis for the topic you have been assigned. (Task 2) Outline ‘current practice’ in the topic area. (Task 3) Compare the literature analysis (Task 1) with current practice (Task 2). Does current practice match theory? Is the ‘real world’ ahead or behind what the research tells us? (Task 4) Describe each component of your prototype and how they work together to form an enterprise Information System architecture. Prototype development: The second section of the assignment requires each group to develop a cloud-based prototype infrastructure that satisfies enterprise requirements by supporting individual business activities and broader business processes, within the same topic area as the in-depth analysis described above. Each group needs to identify a specific organization to support, and develop a prototype cloud-based infrastructure to support them. Each group needs to describe the proposed components of their prototype in detail. Project proposals are used to structure the project on an individually negotiated basis. The weight for this assignment is as follows: 1. Report -15% of the total marks. 2. Prototype -20% of the total marks. Further details can be found in the assignment description on UTSOnline. Advice and support about the choice of cloud services and other tools will be provided in class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In-Depth Topic Analysis and Prototype Development</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">35</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 11 before class time. For late submission please see faculty procedure and advice section.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 11 before class time. For late submission please see faculty procedure and advice section.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To develop skills in in-depth topic analysis from exisiting academic literatures and current practices and to develop a cloud based infrastructure for facilitating agility for a specific business organization.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each group is required to give a short presentation to outline of your proposed framework in a given case study. Students will be required to present their answers and prototype in class. Use of innovative presentation technologies as well as excellent group coordination and communication skills are critical in this assessment. The level of practicality of the proposed solution as well as its clarity are amongst key assessment criteria.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 11 during class hours and leftover presentations if any will be in Week 12 during class hours.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5% for group presentation, 10% for individual presentation. Announcement to be made in class and UTSOnline by the subject coordinator.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The focus of evaluating the oral presentations is to assess your learning from a particular case study, to demonstrate your skill in clearly understanding a case study problem and your ability to propose and present good solutions to a top management team.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 11 during class hours and leftover presentations if any will be in Week 12 during class hours.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment has two parts (Part I and II) which includes two in-class quizzes. Each part is worth 20 marks. Quiz questions contain multiple choice questions, fill in the blanks, true/ false and case study with a set of questions or a descriptive type questions about the subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quizzes</Data></Cell>
