   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32703</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Information Technology Strategy</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Inquisitive and critical questioning of the lecture contents/issues, and contribute work-based experience on the same issue</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Class contributions</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">16/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Saturday 16 May 2020              At the end of the course</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">At the end of the course</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">You are to conduct in Project Part 1 a critical evaluation of your company’s business-IT strategic alignment practices to identify and analyze any strategic or alignment gaps. This will form the basis for the development, in Project Part 2, of your proposed (enhanced or new) business-aligned IT strategy to close the identified strategic issues or gaps. You are required to interview your company executives to understand, and incorporate into your assignment report, their perspectives of your company business and IT’s contributions to the business in order to make your assignment work- (and business-) relevant. Please document the transcripts of the executive interviews (as research data base) in the appendix of your assignment report (not included in the word count limits stated below). Project Part 1 tasks: The report (3000 words) required for Project Part 1 should demonstrate your ability in applying the concepts, methods and frameworks taught in class and from the extant literature to investigate critical IT-related strategic issues in your company business including (but not limited to) the following: 1. Analyze and evaluate how your firm’s Value Chain(s) create customer value and capture value and critically examine the role of IT (including internet and social media, if used) in the value creation process; identify your firm’s core processes and core competencies, and explicate IT role therein; why are they core? Are they distinctive? Why? Strengths and weaknesses? 2. Analyze and evaluate the use (or potential use) of enterprise architecture and IT governance in your firm’s strategic planning process and in maximizing (a) business-IT strategic alignment; (b) customer value creation and (c) organizational agility; how? Why? Strengths and weaknesses? 3. Use the King-Teo framework (or equivalent) to assess the degree (of integration) by which business and IT collaborate in developing your firm’s strategies and strategic plans; explain social dynamics observed together with the interview data; are they effective? Why? How does the prevailing collaboration relationship impact the quality of existing IT strategy formulation and execution? 4. Use the Luftman’s Strategic Alignment Maturity Model to assess your firm’s current maturity level – use (as many executives &amp; staff as you can access) business and IT executives’ evaluations of all six dimensions as the basis of your assessment. Strengths / weaknesses? 5. Integrate the above analyses to provide a holistic evaluative view of your firm’s current state of IT strategy – planning and execution – in support of business and customer value creation. What are the major strategic issues or gaps? Why?</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Part 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">28/03/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">09:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">9.00am Saturday 28 March 2020              Project Part 1 of your assignment is due by email soft copy at 6:00 pm on Thursday 27 March.  Use of plagiarism detection software: Assessment taks submitted via electronic upload will be subject to similarity detection software. Where routinely used, students will be given the opportunity to review their own work prior to submission.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Part 1 of your assignment is due by email soft copy at 6:00 pm on Thursday 27 March.  Use of plagiarism detection software: Assessment taks submitted via electronic upload will be subject to similarity detection software. Where routinely used, students will be given the opportunity to review their own work prior to submission.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Part 2 Objective: From the insightful strategic analysis of Project Part 1, the student is required in Project Part 2 to: develop the proposed (enhanced or new) business-aligned IT strategy to close the identified strategic issues or gaps using Strategy Map and other models and frameworks taught in class.  The student is required to engage and interview their organization's executive leaders to gain their insights on their firm’s new or evolving strategies and business models to make this a practice-based assignment. Interview data should be documented in an appendix of the assignment report (not included in the word-count limits).  Project Part 2 tasks: The report (4000 words) for Project Part 2 must detail the approaches and rationales of developing your proposed new or enhanced business-aligned IT strategy for your firm, based on your findings in Project Part 1 above and to close off the IT strategic gaps identified. It should include (but not limited to) the following aspects:   Develop the business-aligned IT strategy in the context of and as part of the development of the firm’s Strategy Map using the Norton-Kaplan framework, clearly delineating the causal relationships (alignments) between elements of the four perspectives, particularly the Information Capital. Clearly articulate, with sound business and/or conceptual justifications, how the strategy map has addressed all relevant strategic alignment issues identified in Part 1. Articulate the correspondingly enhanced Value Chain, cross-referenced to the core processes identified in the Strategy Map, and the associated IT systems (including use of e-business and/or social media, etc.) required to enhancing its business and customer value creation capabilities as “promised” by the business-aligned IT strategy. Develop and describe (a) the enterprise architecture to represent the envisioned “future state” of the enterprise as articulated by the strategy map, and (b) the attendant IT governance framework require to coordinate the planning and execution of the IT strategy (in the form of, e.g. business/IT program plan and management). Explain what is needed to be done to make the architecture and framework work effectively for the firm. Develop and justify the requisite sourcing strategy to implement the new strategy espoused by the Strategy Map. Propose a new approach (or possible organizational model) for maximizing business-IT collaboration and alignment, including approach to future strategy developments. To demonstrate your sound understanding of your company’s business, your proposed business-aligned IT strategy and associated plan must articulate how they contribute to your company’s competitive advantage (which includes the expected strategic outcomes such as new business capabilities/revenue growth and/or productivity improvement and the corresponding requisite capital investments). Use the Kaplan-Norton method to document the implementation plan (including the investments required). This requires close engagement with business and IT executives. Make sure you make specific references to the sources of ideas and suggestions used in preparing your report. You must make use of the theories and best practices published in the relevant literature to explain/justify your proposed strategies and implementation plans.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Part 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">45</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">16/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6.00pm Saturday 16 May 2020              Both the (fully completed Project Part 1 and Project Part 2 combined together) Assignment Report and the Power-point Slides must be submitted: softcopy by email to dilek.ck@uts.edu.au by 6pm on Friday 18 May.  Use of plagiarism detection software: Assessment taks submitted via electronic upload will be subject to similarity detection software. Where routinely used, students will be given the opportunity to review their own work prior to submission.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Both the (fully completed Project Part 1 and Project Part 2 combined together) Assignment Report and the Power-point Slides must be submitted: softcopy by email to dilek.ck@uts.edu.au by 6pm on Friday 18 May.  Use of plagiarism detection software: Assessment taks submitted via electronic upload will be subject to similarity detection software. Where routinely used, students will be given the opportunity to review their own work prior to submission.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation Task: Each student is required to present their organization’s strategic alignment analysis of current state of strategic use IT in support of value creation in business (per Project Part 1 outcomes) and the proposed new business-aligned strategy using Strategy Map and the requisite Implementation Plan together with the enabling enterprise architecture and governance framework (per Project Part 2 outcomes). Each presentation must be coherent, cogent (with rationales), succinct and finish within the allotted time (to be determined depending on the total number of enrolled students).</Data></Cell>
