   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41090</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Information and Signals</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There are 5 quizzes and each lasts for 30 mins. Each multi-choice quiz will be given in-class by accessing the tab Assignment in the UTSOnline subject folder. Each quiz will test your knowledge of the fundamental concepts in the online lecture that you watch before coming to class and related exercises. Solutions for the quiz questions will be discussed in class following the quiz.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In-class quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">4-6 questions in 30 mins</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Before seminar/lectures in class each week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Before seminar/lectures in class each week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this assignment is to give students feedback on their understanding of key concepts from the online lectures.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">You will form a group of 2-3 students. Your group will choose a research topic from the list of topics in the tab Project of the UTSOnline subject folder (each topic has 4-5 examples of research papers or technical reports). The group will then need to complete the following tasks with help and feedback from the lecturer during consultation hours, online forum, and dedicated in-class slots:  T1: Write a literature review on the group’s research topic using provided papers and other papers from international/national conference/journal venues that you will find yourself or from discussion with the lecturer (1-2 pages) T2: Write a detailed report on the method, approach, and findings of one paper of your choice (1-2 pages) T3: Simulate to replicate the result/findings from the above paper (simulations code and 1-2 pages report) T4: Write your own evaluation/comments on the findings of the paper (0.5-1 page) T5: Propose future investigation or research problems from the paper (0.5-1 page)  The above guides are for the students about how the report should be written/structured. However, there is no limit in terms of length/pages for each section or the whole report. Each group is required to submit a final report of the project. The report should contain the project title, names of group members, a table that details contributions of each member, and 5 sections for the above 5 tasks (a template is available on UTSOnline). The report will be assessed as a group effort. However, if a student fails to document his/her contribution to his/her group project (when required), the project mark for this student will be discounted.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Collaborative research project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">8 weeks</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Please check on UTSOnline Assignment Dropbox</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Please check on UTSOnline Assignment Dropbox</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this assignment is to expose students to state-of-the-art research activities in information theory and signal processing through literature review, simulating/replicating others’ research findings and developing students’ critical thinking skills to compare and evaluate different existing information and signal processing systems. Additionally, the collaboration, communications skills to work in a team are also developed.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Specific tasks and experiments are presented in the Lab guide book for each lab. The 3 books can be found in the Assignment tab of the UTSOnline subject folder. Before each lab, you are required to read the guide book and carry some pre-lab tasks that will be assessed in your lab report. Any work involved with Matlab is COMPULSORY. You need to complete the Matlab pre-work (if any) before attending the lab. Your Matlab work will be attached to the lab report. The lab is either pass/fail which means you either receive the full allocation mark or 0%. If you have made a serious attempt of the assignment but it is unsatisfactory, you will be offered feedback and an opportunity for re-submission without penalty.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab reports</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">See program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Please check on UTSOnline Assignment Dropbox</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this assignment is to equip students with hands-on experience on using contemporary tools, equipment that are currently used in the related industries. Over the 3 labs, students will do experiments with equipment like digital storage oscilloscope (Agilent DSO-X 2004A with Wave Gen), Arbitrary Waveform Generator (Agilent 33210A with Option 002),TIMS trainer, and software tools like Matlab, LabView.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Please check on UTSOnline Assignment Dropbox</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The exam is 2-hour and open book. All content learnt from online lectures, notes, and tutorial workshops 1 to 9. Requires application of technical concept knowledge, and mathematical techniques to solve problems. The best way to prepare for the exam is to do as many tutorial problems/exercises as possible.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 hours +10 mins reading time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The final exam aims to assess students’ understanding of important concepts and the ability to apply these concepts to model and solve practical problems to meet specific requirements.</Data></Cell>
