   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42891</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Infrastructure for Cloud Computing</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assignment is an individual written assignment based lecture contents, e.g. virtualisation technologies and the use of cloud within businesses.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1: Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">27/08/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10.00am Tuesday 27 August 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To allow students to demonstrate their knowledge of the concepts learnt in the subject, research skills and self-assess their progress in the subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment is based on group work. Students are required to specify, design, architect, develop and implement a major infrastructure based project. This project is divided into the following deliverables: (1) A design and architecture report (2) Implement/Build this infrastructure stack, noting issues of this deployment (3) A presentation/demo on the implementation will be during the lab in week 11. This includes peer marking and critical review.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 2: Group Major Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">08/10/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10.00am Tuesday 8 October 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Whilst designing a cloud computing infrastructure and implementing a prototype for a small size organisation, students are expected to analyse stakeholder needs, implement and test solutions, and demonstrate their subject knowledge and communication/presentation skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This examination is an open book assessment consisting of multiple-choice, single-answer questions, short-answer questions and an essay.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Written Exam - Theory Exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam Period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam Period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To allow students to demonstrate their knowledge of cloud computing infrastructure, e.g. cloud solutions, cloud core architectures, cloud platforms, cloud computing technologies, technical limitations, and so on.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Student participations will be recorded for randomly selected five lectures and/or labs during the semester. Up to 5 marks can be earned if you attend all the lectures and labs. In week 5, participating in discussion and presentation in class can have oppertunities to earn up to 5 marks.</Data></Cell>
