   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41022</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Innovation and Entrepreneurship Studio 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students working in teams of three will discuss with their mentors the product/service they are developing. The product may be, for example, a system, multimedia product etc to be designed, developed and tested by the team. Students shall write a report (maximum 2000 words) and submit it to justify the rationale and need for the product/service together with a short description of how they will execute it in their Assessment Project Stage 2. Students are required to come to a written agreement with their mentors by the end of Week 2 as to what their precise deliverables will be. They should make this in writing on a sheet of paper to be signed by all parties. Both students and mentors should keep a copy of the agreement in case of dispute. It should be clear that the innovative ideas expanded on the work is no less than that normally required to pass coursework of the same number of credit points. Individual mark will be assessed by the mentor depending on the individual contribution and the report will be marked as a whole. As a result, the members of the same group may end up having different marks.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Stage 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Maximum 2000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">14/12/2017</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Thursday 14 December 2017</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this task is to assess student’s competence in the following aspects:  Demonstrated understanding of the principles of Design Thinking Identifying customer needs – Empathy Critically investigate and analyse stakeholders views Demonstrate technical knowledge and skills, appropriate tools and resources to solve the problem Reflect critically on theory and professional practice on the problem identified</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will collaborate with stakeholders/industry partners to gather additional information to further identify needs that will contribute to the design and presentation of the prototype. This will include a solution proposal.  It should be clear that the innovative ideas expanded on the work is no less than that normally required to pass coursework of the same number of credit points. Individual mark will be assessed by the mentor depending on the individual contribution and the report will be marked as a whole. As a result, the members of the same group may end up having different marks.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Stage 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">60</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15minute presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">13/02/2018</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Tuesday 13 February 2018</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this task is to assess student's competence in the following areas:  Apply design thinking to identify and define a problem Collaborate with stakeholders to identify their needs Apply basic systems engineering principles Work effectively in a team to identify and define a problem and propose solutions Communicate effectively to propel team cohesion and articulate ideas Manage own time, tasks and learning issues to ensure project delivery on time and within scope Demonstrate critical self-reflection in documentation to improve ongoing personal performance</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
