   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41033</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Integrated Electronic Systems Design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task will examine students’ understanding of the material and provide both teaching staff and students feedback along the session. Online quizzes will be set at Week 2, 4, 6, and 9. Each quiz will contain questions in relation to the previous two weeks material. Feedback of the quizzes will be immediate online and discussion of the feedback during tutorial sessions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quizzes are held in the first 15 minutes of lab classes in the weeks indicated in the weekly program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quizzes are held in the first 15 minutes of lab classes in the weeks indicated in the weekly program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examine students’ knowledge and skills in relation to topics on circuits and systems.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assignment project brings the students into a practical world and provides them with the opportunity to create the circuit by innovation and analyse the performance of a potential commercial on-chip integrated filter for 5G communications. The students are required to acquire the basic knowledge on filter characteristics and design principles. It is required to understand the basic types and operational mechanism of radio frequency filters through lecture notes and laboratory exercises. A project report and a presentation are essential for assessment of the project and is expected to be due by 9am Monday 27/08/2018. The breakdown tasks are summarised below:  Understanding of the principle of radio frequency filter configurations and get familiar with the computer-aided design environment. Calculation of the values of the components required for on-chip filter designs. Configuration of a commercial on-chip filter based on the knowledge gained from the lecture notes and laboratory exercise. Observation of the input/output signal from the monitoring tools in the design environment. Displaying of the signal filter effect by evaluation of the frequency response shape, passband etc. Note down the performance of the designed filter. Compare the obtained results with a commercial product from the technical manual (datasheet). Explain the reason why if there is a discrepancy.  A technical project report covers:  A short literature of commercial filters and their key parameters related to circuit performance. A comparison table is expected. Reports on the design procedures, analysis, simulations, observation and conclusions. The report should contain the circuit diagram, circuit principles, analytical presentation, diagrams, data tables, pictures of observed input and output signals.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">On-Chip Integrated Filter Design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The document is online. The documents should not be longer than an equivalent 10 page A4 size.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">02/09/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">09:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">9.00am Monday 2 September 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Learn how to describe a signal filtering theory through a practical basic circuitry configuration. Obtain the basic computer-aided experience creating circuits for 5G applications. Learn how to use the advanced software predominantly used in the electronic and defence industry. Reaching out the most cutting-edge technologies through these essential tools of the electronics components and system designs.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Detailed information about the task can be found in the Project 2 documentation on UTSOnline in the subject folder. In summary, the tasks are as follows:  Pick up a project topic provided in the Project 2 Introduction to a commercial design project. Further understanding of industrial standards and protocols required following the design procedures. Practise system level layout and packaging skills Practise system integration skills Manipulate electronics simulation and measurement skills Verification of system performance and reliability Team work and group presentation based on the design project Reports on the above findings and simulation and/or experimental observations Reports in terms of functional blocks including both components level and system levels Delivery of conclusive findings and understanding from an end user point of view</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">System Level Design Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The document is online. It should not be longer than an equivalent 30 page printed document.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11/10/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.00pm Friday 11 October 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Learn how to design a daily used electronics system according to the practical requirements, gaining the knowledge in system schematics and design skills using advanced educational software tool kits.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This exam is a 'Restricted Open Book' exam and calculators will not be allowed. However each student is allowed to bring one A4 size paper sheet with them. The students can write whatever they wish on the sheet, but they must be written by themselves. Printed sheets and sheets written by others are allowed. The exam will be a combination of 'written answer' and multiple/single choice questions and be of 2 hours duration with 10 minutes reading time. All questions are compulsory.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
