   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48033</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Internet of Things</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will be involved in the design and development of a medium complexity IoT application. The main project assignment involves all key phases of system development. Its focus is on the understanding of the problem space, key requirements (application drivers), system architecture, system design and implementation; this also includes builds/scripts/code, how resources can be used and critical risks/mitigation applied. For all project-related items, excluding the labs, quizzes and final exam, you will be working in teams of about 3-4 people. For Assessment task 1 it is recommended that you structure your groups from the beginning to ensure timely delivery and a high-quality project presentation. The final project report should include a light version of Project Plan, System Requirements Specification (SRS), Models and Architecture Documentation (ADD) and System Design Documentation (SDD).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project presentation is due in your allocated lab class in Week 12; Project documentation is due by Saturday 26 October 2019 at 23:59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project presentation is due in your allocated lab class in Week 12; Project documentation is due by Saturday 26 October 2019 at 23:59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Through this task, students will demonstrate their understanding and learn skills required for the design and implementation of an IoT based solution.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The lab work will allow students to become familiar with IoT technologies. During labs, the students will be learning how to use IoT application programming tools, as well as, how to use the IOT hardware, microcomputers, sensors and actuators and other electronic/ electromechanical devices.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Labs</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab work will be due in weekly classes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab work will be due in weekly classes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are expected to complete weekly lab activities and demonstrate the completed lab work/working programs to the lab tutor.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The short quizzes will be in the form of multiple choice questions. There will be 2-3 quiz questions to be completed within 5 minutes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Short Quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Not applicable</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Not applicable              Weekly, online quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Short 5 minute quizzes aim to assess student understanding of topics covered during the preceding lectures.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Weekly, online quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This will occur at scheduled sessions (in IoT lab, Room 11.08.409) few days after project presentations and the project package delivery. All IOT students must participate. Q/A session per individual student with questions including: degree of project tailoring, &quot;agile&quot;/just in time technologies employed/understood, individual aims, amount of effort, individual contribution, deliveries, project complexity, collaboration issues and self assessment.  Open book exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The final exam aims to assess student understanding of topics covered during the entire session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual presentation on an agreed on topic realted IoT from the list of topics/acse studies posted on UTSOnline for the subject by Week 4 and schedule arranged by Week 7. The principal rule is that the topic and its presentation must value add to the development of the project and/or theory presented in the formal plenary sessions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
