   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42721</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Introduction to Biomedical Engineering</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Generally students will be given a variety of case biomedical problems that require modelling using Matlab. As part of this assessment, students will need to analyse the computational results and write a report of maximum 1500 words explaining the process of modelling, results, plots etc., any comparisons if appropriate as well as the biomedical implications of the model results.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Basic Computational Modelling for Design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Maximum 1500 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">28/08/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10.00pm Friday 28 August 2020              Week 5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Accuracy of the results Mathematical basis and assumptions made in the model Efficiency of Matlab coding Analysis of results Report with results</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assess understanding and familiarity of basic computational and mathematical aspects that underpin all biomedical engineering systems. It seeks to equip students with abilities to develop simplified and basic mathematical and computational models of the biomedical systems and processes that may be used to simulate their behaviour which will help in the design of biomedical devices and systems. This assignment is mainly focused around develoment of MATLAB skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will be asked to formulate the mathematical problem and develop a set of MATLAB-based computational models for biomedical engineering systems. These include development of algorithmd to solve and develop Pseudo codes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Computational Modelling of Realistic Biomedical Systems and Processes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Maximum 3500 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">09/10/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10.00pm Friday 9 October 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Knowledge of mathematical modelling and problem formulation Development of algorithm and Pseudocode Accurate analysis using MATLAB Accuracy of results and presentation of report Brief literature survey highlighting the biomedical engineering context</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task introduces skills of computational modelling of some of the biomedical systems and processes for the simulation and design of devices. The models must be developed using MATLAB.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will make measurements on ECG, EMG and EEG signals using sensors to be provided in the Labs (CHT/SIGNALS Lab) to collect the data which needs to processed and analysed using MATLAB.</Data></Cell>
