   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42082</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Introduction to Complex Systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Consider a complex system in an area of application. Analyse a problem in the context of this system and identify possible interventions to redress the situation. Analyse the implications of your suggested interventions on stakeholders and on other systems. In doing so, identify the trade-offs that are associated with picking one suggestion over another. Based upon your analyses, make a group recommendation of your preferred intervention.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Ten (10) pages maximum.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Allow students to collaboratively engage with complex systems and develop and demonstrate their understanding of such systems.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students make weekly contributions to their portfolio, demonstrating the development of their thinking in this area and their engagement with the issues discussed in class. Students develop their learning in the area of complex systems and demonstrate this through evidence of inquiry and reflection. Through peer communication and reflection students synthesize their learning throughout the session to build a holistic picture of the subject matter.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflective portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">N/A</Data></Cell>
