    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 10              Quiz to be completed on Canvas in students' own time.  Quiz opens 9am Monday 5th Oct. Quiz closes 11:59pm Friday 9th Oct</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz to be completed on Canvas in students' own time.  Quiz opens 9am Monday 5th Oct. Quiz closes 11:59pm Friday 9th Oct</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will be graded individually and marks are allocated per question as will be specified in the quiz.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment requires students to apply what they have learned to recreate a classic 2D game. Students will be able to choose form a small list of games to create, drawn from the early eras of the games industry. At this stage, the project will need to have the scene for a single level set up, visual assets and animations created, and basic player movement functionality implemented. Students will also need to provide a design for a new twist on the game that is to be delivered upon in Assessment 4. Additional assessment details and marking rubric will provided on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Classic Game Recreation - Getting Started</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">21/09/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Monday 21 September 2020              Submission through Git - commit and push to new branch called &quot;Assess3&quot;. Further instructions on submission procedure in the specifications provided on Canvas.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will be graded on their ability to apply the knowledge from the lectures, labs, and self-directed study to establish the foundations for recreating a classic 2D game.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submission through Git - commit and push to new branch called &quot;Assess3&quot;. Further instructions on submission procedure in the specifications provided on Canvas.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment extends upon Assessment 3 by requiring students to produce two scenes in their recreated game. The first is to as faithful of a recreation of a level from the classic game as possible, demonstrating the students ability to interpret an existing game experience and develop it. The second scene is to contain the student's own innovative twist (as promised in Assessment 3) to the core game mechanics and player experience, which exposes students to a design and development cycle of original content. Students are encouraged to push the boundaries of their skill in this second scene and seek new knowledge in order to implement their novel gameplay design. Additional assessment details and marking rubric will provided on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Classic Game Recreation - Enhancing and Innovating</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">35</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">23/10/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 23 October 2020              Submission through Git - commit and push to new branch called &quot;Assess4&quot;. Further instructions on submission procedure in the specifications provided on Canvas.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submission through Git - commit and push to new branch called &quot;Assess4&quot;. Further instructions on submission procedure in the specifications provided on Canvas.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will be graded on their ability to faithfully recreate a classic 2D game as well as deliver upon an innovative design twist to the game.</Data></Cell>
