   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41082</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Introduction to Data Engineering</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The textbook has embedded quizzes and tasks. These form the basis of this assessment, and will be used to obtain your mark. There is a program of chapters, with their tasks to complete week by week. This is published in the UTS:Online folder.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Learning Matlab for modeling engineering systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">22/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12.00am Friday 22 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Central to the subject is the ability to model complex systems. In particular, to use Matlab to do this. You will learn Matlab by using the interactive online textbook from zyBooks.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The problem chosen is the Terminal Assignment Problem 2 This is a classic “benchmark” used in many network planning courses. The task is to formulate the problem in a Matlab program, and demonstrate its workings.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Model and Optimization of a complex system using Matlab</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">22/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12.00am Friday 22 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A very important element of Data Engineering is the ability to optimize things. Very often this is done through Machine Learning. The motivation for this task is to introduce Machine Learning / Stochastic Optimization using: · A simple to learn algorithm, on · A simple well know “benchmark” problem, using · A programming language that is already familiar (Matlab)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Create one of the following Products Option 1: Collecting Data from the EIF system Option 2: PBIL Optimization System Option 3: Collecting Data from your Smartphone</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Create an App using MatLab Appdesigner</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12.00am Friday 5 June 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Create an App using Matlab Appdesigner that provides a GUI for one of the tasks done earlier in the session.</Data></Cell>
