   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48510</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Introduction to Electrical and Electronic Engineering</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There are 10 labs where students learn and practice laboratory hands-on skills. Students need to buy and bring the Lab Kit or Project Kit to each lab activity and design, construct, test and troubleshoot circuits as indicated in the Lab Notes. Students will also be exposed to surface-mount and through-hole soldering.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory Assessments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each lab is 3 hours in duration.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In the timetabled activities from Week 1 to Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In the timetabled activities from Week 1 to Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To help students acquire basic hands-on electrical laboratory skills, competence to work with electrical measurement equipment and to understand the underlying concepts taught in classes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students attend two 90-minute lab tests to demonstrate their competence in designing circuits, measuring circuit parameters, modelling circuit behaviour, plotting results and tying experimental results to theory.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory Tests</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each lab test is 90 minutes in duration.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7 and Week 10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7 and Week 10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To ensure electrical laboratory skills are acquired, and to ensure competence in the use of electrical test and measurement equipment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Weekly submission of solutions to unique problems related to selected topics.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">WebTutor Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Due dates for each Topic are listed on the Main Menu page of WebTutor.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To spread the learning load evenly throughout the session, to ensure understanding of basic mathematical and circuit analysis concepts, and to provide immediate feedback.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Due dates for each Topic are listed on the Main Menu page of WebTutor.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Solve problems related to the subject’s topics. This is a &quot;restricted open book&quot; examination. Students are allowed to bring one A4 size double-sided page of handwritten notes only. Both programmable and non-programmable calculators are permitted.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 hours plus 10 minutes reading time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This Centrally Conducted Formal Exam will be scheduled by the University during the final 2 assessment weeks of the session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This Centrally Conducted Formal Exam will be scheduled by the University during the final 2 assessment weeks of the session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The final exam aims to test students' understanding on the use of concepts learned throughout the session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory work plays a very important role in your learning in this subject. It is used to develop practical skills and to reinforce theory studied in lectures and tutorials. The attendance at laboratories is compulsory and students who are more than 15 minutes late at the start of a laboratory session will be considered absent for that particular lab for assessment purposes. Your attendance will be monitored throughout the semester and must be verified by a lab supervisor’s signature in your Laboratory Notes at the end of each laboratory. A roll call will be conducted taken after the first 15 minutes of each lab session. Be sure to bring the component kit and Laboratory and Essential Notes to each laboratory session. You are expected to complete all parts of the experiment within the allocated lab time and enter all the experimental data into the Laboratory and Essential Notes to get full credit for that particular lab. Entering data into loose sheets will not be assesed. Partially completed labs within allocated lab time will attract only partial marks. Labs completed outside the allocated lab time do not attract any formal credit. If you are absent for a laboratory due to illness or misadventure and has a valid evidence such as a medical certificate, you need to securely fasten (glue or tape) the certificate to the first page of the missed lab in your Laboratory Notes. You should complete the lab in your own time and present the results as well as the medical certificate in the following week at the lab for verification by a lab supervisor. After completing each laboratory task within laboratory time and demonstrating an acceptable level of competency and knowledge to the lab tutors, a mark will be awarded for each lab session. The laboratory attendance is compulsory and to pass the subject each student must attend and complete at least 4 labs out of total 6 labs.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each lab session is 3 hours long.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week range</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 4 to Week 11</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To help students acquire the knowledge and skills of using laboratory instrumentation and demonstrate the use of basic electronics and measurement apparatus to display, measure, and record results of simple laboratory experiments.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
