   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48610</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Introduction to Mechanical and Mechatronic Engineering</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Complete hand drawn engineering drawings of several objects. Students will have opportunity to practice on several sample tasks in class. Refer to detailed assessment criteria provided in the assessment task document available from UTSOnline - Assessment tasks</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Drawing Assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design/drawing/plan/sketch</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A set of engineering drawings/sketches including: parallel oblique projection, isometric, orthogonal and section views.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 5 - Electronic submission via UTSOnline anytime before Friday 14:00</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 5 - Electronic submission via UTSOnline anytime before Friday 14:00</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students to develop and demonstrate their competence in engineering drawing and sketching.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Using SolidWorks CAD software, generate part models, one assembly model, sets of engineering detail drawings of parts and one assembly drawing with a parts list for a simple mechanical assembly. Refer to detailed assessment criteria provided in the assessment task document available from UTSOnline - Assessment tasks</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Computer Aided Design (CAD) assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design/drawing/plan/sketch</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7 - Electronic submission via UTSOnline anytime before Friday 14:00</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7 - Electronic submission via UTSOnline anytime before Friday 14:00</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students to develop and demonstrate their competence in CAD solid modelling.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A set of sample engineering mechanics problems with solutions are available via UTSOnline. Students are expected to use these problems to help them learn engineering mechanics. The quiz will be one question very similar to problems in set 1 or 2 in the sample engineering mechanics problems provided. Time allowed is 40 minutes. The quiz will commence promptly at 5 minutes past the scheduled class starting time. The quiz will be closed book. Refer to detailed assessment criteria available from UTSOnline - Assessment Tasks</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Mechanics Quiz 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">One engineering mechanics problem.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Cancelled - conducted as self-paced practice quiz as homework</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students to demonstrate mastery of basic engineering mechanics.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Cancelled - conducted as self-paced practice quiz as homework</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A set of sample engineering mechanics problems with solutions are available via UTSOnline. Students are expected to use these problems to help them learn engineering mechanics. The quiz will be one question very similar to problems in set 3 or 4 in the sample engineering mechanics problems provided. Time allowed is 30 minutes. The quiz will commence promptly at 5 minutes past the scheduled class starting time. The quiz will be closed book. Refer to detailed assessment criteria available from UTSOnline - Assessment Tasks</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Mechanics Quiz 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">One engineering mechanics problem.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 10 - Electronic submission via UTSOnline anytime before Friday 14:00</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 10 - Electronic submission via UTSOnline anytime before Friday 14:00</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students to demonstrate mastery of basic engineering mechanics.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Follow engineering drawings to fabricate a motion and power transmission and energy conversion device. Design, manufacture, test, evaluate and improve a defined mechanical device. Implement a mechatronics system to acquire vehicle performance data. Produce engineering documentation including detail drawings, CAD models, calculations, performance data and charts, evaluations etc. This is a groupwork project. All group members are required to contribute to building the mechanical device and preparing engineering documentation.  There is a mix of individual and group assessment tasks. Refer to detailed assessment criteria provided in the assessment task document available from UTSOnline - Assessment tasks</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering Functional Prototyping Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">55</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">*** Week 8: Individual workplan and initial drawings (20%), submitted via UTSOnline before 14:00pm Monday in Week 8. Students need to book a timeslot with a lab tutor for grading and feedback on their submitted documents.    *** Week 12: Submission of WPV SolidWorks models, technical shop drawings and project documentation, including bill of materials and simulation results, submitted online via UTSOnline anytime before 14:00pm Friday in Week 12 (35%).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">*** Week 8: Individual workplan and initial drawings (20%), submitted via UTSOnline before 14:00pm Monday in Week 8. Students need to book a timeslot with a lab tutor for grading and feedback on their submitted documents.    *** Week 12: Submission of WPV SolidWorks models, technical shop drawings and project documentation, including bill of materials and simulation results, submitted online via UTSOnline anytime before 14:00pm Friday in Week 12 (35%).</Data></Cell>
