   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41170</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Introduction to Quantum Computing</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Complete weekly online multiple-choice quiz covering the content studied in the prior week. Two attempts will be permitted.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Weekly quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Varying between 10 and 20 questions</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">For students to benchmark their understanding of concepts presented within the weekly subject sessions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examine and critique quantum protocols, algorithms, and proofs. During each lab session, the students will be tasked with orally critiquing presented quantum protocols and proofs. Within groups, the students will develop an argument and elect a representative to deliver the argument to the class. Students will be assigned to self-assess their contribution as well as that of other group members via feedback survey.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In-Lab critiquing</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5-minute presentations within each designated lab session</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment task contributes to the development of quantum computing knowledge and its appropriate application, as well as contextualising professional and communication skills within the quantum computing discipline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In teams, the students will explain specific quantum algorithms and concepts to the rest of the class. Emphasis is placed on effectively communicating new ideas using a variety of teaching and learning tools. Students will critique themselves and each other via feedback survey. A portion of the grade will reflect the quality of the feedback given.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In-Lab presentations</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5-minute presentations within each designated lab session</Data></Cell>
