   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42090</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Introduction to Sustainable Microgrids</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will solve numerical problems to model and analyse performance of microgrid components including PV units, wind turbines and energy storage systems.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Problem Solving</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1 hour</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">n/a</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class in       Test 1-18/03/2020 and Test 2: 22/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Test 1-18/03/2020 and Test 2: 22/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To demonstrate students’ knowledge of modelling microgrid components and analyse their performance.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students need to create a written proposal for their project, and have it agreed to by their mentor(s). The project is group work, but the proposal will be assessed individually. It must include background, technical challenges, targets, agreed deliverables and a timeline for the work to be carried out. A template with suggested section headings will be provided.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Proposal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The length of the proposal should be sufficient to fully describe the proposed product, deliverables and timeline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">21/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Tuesday 21 April 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To create a project proposal, define a scope for design project, and negotiate the scope and outcomes with the academic mentor(s).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students present their project progress and outcomes to demonstrate their presentation skills and details of their design.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10-minute presentation, followed by 5-minute question/answer session</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">n/a</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class in       Presentation 1 (Preliminary): 21/04/2020 and Presentation 2 (Final): 9/6/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To communicate students’ design project progress and their understanding of microgrid basics, such as basic components, energy storage, control, operation, protection.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation 1 (Preliminary): 21/04/2020 and Presentation 2 (Final): 9/6/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students must demonstrate their product/prototype in a laboratory setting, and show that it meets the design criteria, targets and deliverables from the project proposal.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Team Product/Prototype Delivery</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstration</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A 10-minute demonstration will be required, followed by question/answer sessions</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">n/a</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class in       10/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To demonstrate students’ ability to deliver a product or prototype. Students must demonstrate their capacity to solve problems, create solutions, work in teams, communicate professionally, and manage the timelines.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to conduct their own independent research and prepare an individual written report. Each student must research and prepare a written report to show how the project issues were addressed, and the relevant background, analysis, methodology, results, etc. Students are encouraged to discuss their draft with lecturers to seek for early feedback. The report will follow IEEE article format (two columns).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">8 to 10 pages</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10/06/2020</Data></Cell>
