   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48441</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Introductory Digital Systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will complete three practical assessments in scheduled laboratory classes to demonstrate their understanding of FPGAs, microcontrollers, peripheral and systems integration. In these laboratory assessments, students will apply skills developed in previous lab activities by modifying and integrating hardware and software building blocks to meet provided specifications.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment task 1: In-class laboratory assessments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In your allocated laboratory class in weeks 6, 11 and 12.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In your allocated laboratory class in weeks 6, 11 and 12.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students demonstrate the ability to integrate pre-developed hardware and software component modules in a hands-on laboratory setting.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will complete in-class individual online quizzes to demonstrate their knowledge of concepts and applications of combinational and sequential logic circuits and microcontrollers. These include design and analysis of digital circuits and associated software.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment task 2: Quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
