    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The quiz will assess the student’s knowledge about the theoretical and some practical aspects of the subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will be allocated to groups to do their projects together. There will be 3-5 students in a group, and they will cooperate and collaborate to complete their assigned projects. The projects will be performed based on knowledge and skills the students learn in the lectures and labs. The projects will be carried out in studios. The students will submit the reports to the lecturer by the end of Week 11, and they are required to present their achieved results in the studio in Week 12. The score for the project (including achieved results, reports for research projects, social collaboration skill and presentation in the studio) will account for 40% of the total score of the students - 30% for report (group work) and 10% for presentation (individual).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Projects</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The technical report will be less than 10 pages. The presentation will last for 30 minutes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The last day of Week 11 for the report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will work on projects, where they will apply skills learnt in class, labs, as well as their own research in IoT Security. Furthermore, the project presentation will assess students' presentation and report skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The last day of Week 11 for the report.</Data></Cell>
