   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32553</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Leadership and People Management</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Research the following question and document your response in the form of an essay: Over a four-week period conduct a critical scrutiny of your everyday practices in your work role. This involves keeping a daily journal in which you reflect on your actions each day and identify flaws in your practices around relationship management, openness to learning, and readiness to transform your behaviour when appropriate. The reading of select articles on self-reflexive practice should be conducted concurrently with the keeping of the daily journal. Ensure that your response shows evidence of consultation of: · the literature on self-reflexive practices and leadership · deep reflection on your behaviour at work, and orientation to others, over the four-week period of active self-reflexivity.  Submissions should be made via email to Ken.Dovey@uts.edu.au.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Essay</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Essay</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Maximum length: 2 000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30/04/2017</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:45 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.45pm Sunday 30 April 2017</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Self-analysis of your leadership behaviour in your current role</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment task requires you to execute a six-week action plan (based on feedback to assignment 1) that addresses one of the leadership flaws indentified in the first assessment task. You are required to monitor and evaluate your progress via a specific workplace project wherein you attempt to improve that aspect of your leadership practice identified in Assignment One. Keep a learning journal wherein you show evidence of critical self-reflection, learning from experience, and the capacity to use that learning to develop more effective leadership practices in the area designated for improvement. Note that the assessment grade will be allocated entirely on the quality of evidence provided: evidence that demonstrates your ability to learn from experience (especially mistakes) and to embed that learning in improved workplace leadership practices. The strategic action of the project should be conducted over an six-week period and the report should provide:  An executive summary of your learning journal; an evaluation of the achievement/non-achievement of your learning objectives; an analysis of the reasons why the self-transformational objective was/was not achieved (i.e. analyse the accuracy of your critical assessment; the effectiveness of the various strategies through which you attempted to transform your behaviour; inhibitors to, and/or defences against, learning that you experienced; the role of others in your success/failure; etc.); the listing of up to five key leadership principles that resulted from the learning gained from this project. These principles should have an appropriate slogan, and be explicated using the concepts introduced in this subject. Links back to the experience that sparked the insight that led to the principle, should be made clear. [Note: throughout the process of the implementation of the project, the key insights/learning gained should be documented in your learning journal (that you have utilised since the beggining of the subject). This tacitly acquired learning, within a specific work context, should form the basis of the five leadership principles that you identify and explicate].  The report should follow the following format:  executive summary of the learning journal (1 page) evaluation of outcome of project action (5 lines) analysis of the reasons for failure/success of the action project (1 page) explication (using the concepts introduced by the class sessions) of up to five leadership principles developed from the key learning gained from the project (2-3 pages).  Submissions should be made to Ken.Dovey@uts.edu.au.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Self-transformation Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">60</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Maximum length: 6 pages</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11/06/2017</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:45 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.45pm Sunday 11 June 2017</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Learning through action. Accessing the knowledge of self embedded in contexts of your life</Data></Cell>
