   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49069</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Leadership and Responsibility</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will be required to join one of 6 groups each of which is divided into 5 teams of 5-6 students each. The aim of the groups is to come up with a sustainability initiative and high-level execution plan for UTS to implement within a 1 to 2-year period. The details of the project, group dynamics, conditions, requirements and constraints can be found in the detailed project description available through Canvas. The project is made up of the following deliverables: Part A - Initial pitches and selection – each student will pitch to their own team the initiative they want their team to work on. Teams will choose a winning pitch. The winning pitch author will become the team leader through the process of crafting a vision and strategy to underpin the initiative (SLOs 1, 4) Part B - Weekly research and artefact production – students will take turns in leading/managing the weekly work required to adequately perform all the necessary research and produce the necessary artefacts to ensure that their team’s initiative is the one chosen by the group they belong to (SLOs 1, 2, 3 4) Part C - Presentations (SLO 1, 4)  Initially, to their own group for selection Then, to the rest of the groups for final selection Finally, to the UTS Sustainability Engagement Manager  Presentation in the form of pre-recorded videos.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group activities and project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week range</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 2 to Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each week students will be given a short video or text dealing with some aspect of leadership and responsibility. During the tutorial time, each team will analyse the material provided and answer a set of questions. On alternate weeks, each team will be required to either report to the rest of the cohort in a class discussion or to the teaching team in the form of a one-page written report due by the end of the day.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study analysis</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week range</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 3 to Week 10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each student will be required to identify 2 persons they consider leaders from their own perspective - at least one of the chosen leaders must be a person that all the rest of the class either already knows or has the possibility of knowing about, e.g. Gandhi, while the other one can be a person in that student’s life, only known to them. The task is to analyse the leadership of those persons from the perspective of each of the weekly topics discussed during the lectures and tutorials. The deliverable for this assessment is a weekly online posting of maximum 250 words on the discussion board of each team, which will be discussed and peer marked.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Weekly reflection and posting on discussion board</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week range</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 6 to Week 9</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will be required to peruse reputable media coverage of issues/problems affecting either domestic or international contexts and find an example of ‘good’ leadership and an example of ‘bad’ leadership. Students must explain what makes each case either ‘good’ or ‘bad’ leadership. The deliverable for this assessment is two submissions, each with 3 weekly 1-page (maximum) reports which will be peer marked and discussed during tutorials.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Weekly journal</Data></Cell>
