   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32561</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Leading Organisational Change</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">An individual submission (500 words + Elements of organisations ‘pyramid’ incl. SIPOC + timeline) is required to describe the context for a proposed change. Locate where in the ‘pyramid’ the change is targeted and explain why. Formulate key metrics for measuring a successful change (current state versus future state). Propose feasible timeline and resources suitable within the framework of assessment 3. Ensure that this case study is disclosable for a group work assignment and presentation. If the student is currently not employed, the case has to be derived from a past experience. The word document should be submitted to UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual case submissions</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">31/03/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10.00pm Sunday 31 March 2019              Submit slide deck on UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit slide deck on UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The individual case presents an opportunity for participants to:  Analyse the change challenge within a lived organisation. Formulate context for change and objectives. Propose practical actions and success criteria that are context relevant to implement the change.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A succinct individual presentation (maximum 12 powerpoint slides) is required per assigned pre-reading. The pre-reading will be individually assigned prior to the upcoming session. A 20-minute presentation should cover:  main assumptions in this theory/study key insights and learning a critique (what does it add, miss, contradict, …) in relation to other session pre-reading, in-class material, and today's socio-economical-environmental context how it relates to own experience how does it inform the change plan proposed in assignment 1.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual pre-reading presentations</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The slide deck should be submitted to UTSOnline before 9:00am on the day before the relevant class session. Presentation will be given during the relevant class session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The slide deck should be submitted to UTSOnline before 9:00am on the day before the relevant class session. Presentation will be given during the relevant class session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The presentations give an opportunity for participants to practice:  Identifying, understanding and synthetising core concepts relevant to organisational change. Linking concepts to other theories and empirical studies. Translating concepts into their own context.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In session 2, participants will be assigned to groups of not more than 5 people, within which they have to complete this group assignment. Each group should select one of the companies represented in the group within which to address the following tasks (without breaching the policies of the company or introducing risk to the participant’s employment in the company!): Based on the work done for the selected assignment 1, the group workshop in session 2 will be dedicated to:  analyse the context for the change process that is being undertaken (including a description of the way in which the company understands the challenge in terms of its strategic and competitive environment, the main stakeholders, the current routines, past change initiatives…) analyse the nature (scale, depth, …) of change produce a list of 2 to 5 of the most important issues that should be addressed to enhance the company’s anticipated response to the challenge. Choose an issue that you are able to address (and that will have an optimal positive impact) design an intervention to drive the change you desire.  In between sessions, the group will implement the proposed change; test the impact of the intervention; document the progress for presentation to the class (assignment 3). During sessions 3 and 4, group workshops will be dedicated to applying the material of the day; integrate practical learning from the field; evaluate the progress made or not made; re-assess if necessary and propose a modified plan that would be ideal for further implementation; reflect on assumptions. In session 5, the group will present a narrative of the change journey (from first proposal in assignment 1 till end). This should highlight the conceptualisation and implementation process; provide a critical view of the process itself; propose a view into the future. Length for presentation in session 5 The final presentation should be no more than 12 slides in length. The group assignment provides an opportunity to reinforce learning relating to all subject objectives, extending the learning into a specific, real organisation, into the domain of implementation, and within a team context. A 20-minute presentation should be made to the class, followed by discussion. Slides for the presentation should be submitted to UTSOline. Assessment will be based on the presentation and associated discussion.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Length for presentation in session 5 The final presentation should be no more than 12 slides in length. The group assignment provides an opportunity to reinforce learning relating to all subject objectives, extending the learning into a specific, real organisation, into the domain of implementation, and within a team context. A 20-minute presentation should be made to the class, followed by discussion. Slides for the presentation should be submitted to UTSOline. Assessment will be based on the presentation and associated discussion.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">29/05/2019</Data></Cell>
