   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42903</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">MPLS and Services Architecture</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 1 consists of three multiple-choice supervised on-line quizzes, to be taken via UTSonline. The quizzes test your ability to solve theoretical problems in different parts of the course: Quiz 1 covers topics from Modules 1 and 2, Quiz 2 covers topics from Modules 3-5.1 and Quiz 3 covers topics from Modules 5.2-6.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Three in-class quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">60</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The first quiz (worth 10%) will be held at the start of the first block and will have a duration of 30 minutes; it is intended to ensure that students have read the lecture material and watched the videos for Modules 1 and 2 prior to attending the first block, and provides feedback to students on their performance prior to the census date. The remaining quizzes (each worth 25%) will be held at the start of the second day of blocks two and three and will have a duration of one hour.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The first quiz (worth 10%) will be held at the start of the first block and will have a duration of 30 minutes; it is intended to ensure that students have read the lecture material and watched the videos for Modules 1 and 2 prior to attending the first block, and provides feedback to students on their performance prior to the census date. The remaining quizzes (each worth 25%) will be held at the start of the second day of blocks two and three and will have a duration of one hour.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The quizzes will be supervised (in-lab) on-line multiple-choice tests, modelled after the style of official industry-based Nokia (Alcatel-Lucent) Prometric examinations. Students will need to demonstrate their problem-solving and analytic skills in each of the topics covered in the course, with a particular focus on traffic engineering and resiliancy. The first quiz, covering introductory material and MPLS fundamentals, will be held at the start of the first laboratory session to ensure that students are provided with timely feedback on the depth of their theoretical problem-solving capabilities prior to starting the labs; remaining quizzes, which have a higher weight, will be held on the second day of the second and third two-day blocks. General feedback will be provided to the class following the quiz; students are welcome to individually go through their specific quiz results with the lecturer.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The first quiz (at the start of the first two-day block), covering introductory materials (Modules 1 and 2) will provide early feedback for students to evaluate their capabilities and depth of understanding at an early stage in the course. The second and third quizzes are more challenging and will evaluate students' knowledge and problem-solving abilities in greater depth, covering Modules 3, 4 and 5.1 for Quiz 2 and Modules 5 (5.2+) and 6 for Quiz 3.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 2 evaluates your ability to troubleshoot a misconfigured network, and implement and test MPLS-based network services on top of an IP network inside a Nokia (Alcatel-Lucent) Service Router network.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">One laboratory exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The laboratory exam runs for a period of one hour</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory exams will be individually scheduled for each student in the week following the completion of Block 3. Students will be advised as to the schedule (which may be negotiable, at the discretion of the subject coordinator) during their Block 3 class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory exams will be individually scheduled for each student in the week following the completion of Block 3. Students will be advised as to the schedule (which may be negotiable, at the discretion of the subject coordinator) during their Block 3 class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will be assessed on the basis of their ability to diagnose and correct any unexpected network faults, correctly implement a specific network configuration on Alcatel-Lucent routers, and demonstrate that the network performs according to the requested specifications. The assessment is similar to that required for the MPLS component of the Nokia (Alcatel-Lucent) NRS-II certification laboratory exam. Individual feedback will be provided following the test on request. Several examples of typical configuration errors and appropriate troubleshooting strategies will be discussed in class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The laboratory exam evaluates the ability of students to correct configuration errors in a given network, then deploy a range of specified MPLS configurations including traffic-engineering and resilliancy features, subject to strict time constraints, as would be the case in an emergency situation in a live network.</Data></Cell>
