   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49002</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Managing Projects</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is an individual, research-based assignment in two parts. Students are expected to conduct research and present findings on the topic on a provided template. Students are expected to undertake a rigorous literature search of discovery on a chosen topic. Part 1 (25 marks) will include a minimum of five (5) recent and relevant academic refereed publications (which is a mandatory component of the output). Part 2 (20 marks) will be a reflection and insight on material presented in part 1.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Research and Reflections</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">45</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Up to 25 pages for part 1, and up to 10 pages for part 2 (both following templates provided)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 6              Part 1 of assignment 1 is due in Week 6; Part 2 of assignment 1 is due in Week 12.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Part 1 of assignment 1 is due in Week 6; Part 2 of assignment 1 is due in Week 12.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Please note: The weighting of Assessment Criteria is approximate; for detailed information, please see your Marking Guide.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">You will work in groups of up to six people to develop a detailed project management plan for the construction of an engineering project. Your plan should include (but not limited to):  Activities Network diagram Resource plan Microsoft Project generated project program (or equivalent) Detailed financial estimates, etc  The deliverables of this assignment are:  Six weekly deliverables due between weeks 3 and 10 as illustrated in the assignment brief (2 marks per week, 12 marks in total) A Project Plan Report due in week 12 (18 marks) An Electronic Presentation due in week 12 (10 marks).  More details will be available in the project handout brief to be made available by week 2.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Project Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2,000 and 3,000 words, excluding appendices</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The weighting of Assessment Criteria is approximate; for detailed information, please see your Marking Guide.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each student will submit an individual diary in weeks 4, 8 and 12 (5 marks each). The diary will include students’ reflections on their activities relating to their performance in assignment 1, assignment 2 as well as their learning activities in the subject.</Data></Cell>
