    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Please see the Marking Criteria for Project Reports of 48621 Manufacturing Engineering in the folder of “Lab1-Projects” at UTSOnline. * The Marking Criteria for Project Reports of 48621 must be used with this Subject Outline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To help students understand the relevance of manufacturing to all engineering, identify various manufacturing processes and give reasons for the manufacturer's choice of the processes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each student is asked to organise an individual written report based on the investigations on the processes of fabrication and assembly of a relatively complex industrial product discussed in the lab classes. Typical examples include Automotive differential, Gear Pump and Workshop Crane etc.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Major Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">23:59, Saturday of Week 11</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">23:59, Saturday of Week 11</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Please see the Marking Criteria for Project Reports of 48621 Manufacturing Engineering in the folder of “Lab1-Projects” at UTSOnline. * The Marking Criteria for Project Reports of 48621 must be used with this Subject Outline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To familiarize students with the manufacture and assembly of a complex engineering modern metal sub-system involving volume production. To enable students to present their findings in a significant engineering report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to form teams to fabricate a simple product (typical examples include T-Puzzle and Water Pump) using the raw materials supplied. A team leader should be nominated to be responsible for managing the project and delegating tasks to individual members. Basic hand tools, drills, lathes and cut off saws in the laboratory are accessible. The assessment of this task consists of two components, i.e. fabrication and written report. The weight of each component is 10%. The fabrication will be marked based on the performance of the product tested in the laboratory. Each student is asked to organise an individual written report to detail the research on the hand tools project and the fabrication process. The written report will be marked according to the Marking Criteria for Project Reports of 48621 Manufacturing Engineering available in the folder of “Lab1-Projects” at UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Practical Handwork Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
