   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42905</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Marketing Technology</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Format: Individual assignment leading a class discussion on a contemporary marketing case or topic. You will be provided with a brief reading, along with specific questions that must be answered. The assignment requirements differ depending on whether the workshop is a case study or a marketing topic. Marketing case study: Research of the relevant industry and product class is required. In addition to the specific questions asked in the reading, you are expected to use relevant analytical tools that have been covered in the subject, and also consider the contextual circumstance of the case such as:  What market is the product/company in? Who are its competitors and what are the competitor/substitute products? What are the competitive advantages and weaknesses of the product or company? Where is the product within the Product Life Cycle? What is the value proposition? How is the market changing? What options are available? What actions should be taken?  Marketing topic: The marketing topics form an extension to material covered in lectures and focus on a particular contemporary marketing issue. A brief introduction or reading will be provided, along with a number of questions. You are expected to research the topic widely, choose a point of view and argue your position in your presentation. Further information: Wide reading is expected to support your argument. This is a marketing course and you are expected to:  Make your presentation exciting and engaging.   Display an understanding of the specific case/problem or circumstance in the source readings. Show how it relates to the underlying theory relevant to the workshop. Argue the case presented in the question. Provide an insightful, entertaining and thought provoking presentation to promote class discussion. Many of the workshops focus on technology products, you are required to consider  the marketing implications, do not get caught up in the technology except to the extent it frames the marketing context. A suggested format for the presentation is:  State your core argument Briefly summarise the reading provided (create the context) Discussion on the specific questions and general questions of the case. Conclusion</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case Study presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20 minute presentation (plus 5 minutes for answering questions)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">On day allocated</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Workshop Marking Guide  Answering the question &amp; insight 10 Application of marketing concepts or depth of research 10 Quality of presentation 10 Creativity and promotion of discussion 10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment gives you the opportunity to consider a marketing topic or case in depth. You will be provided with a 1-5 page reading, along with specific questions that must be answered.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Format: Individual assignment. Development of a marketing plan for a new product. Requirement: Development of a marketing plan for a new product. See marketingplan.doc for the information to be included in the marketing plan. There are 3 interrelated parts to this assignment: 1. Develop a new product. 2. Pitch the product to the class in pitching week 3. Create a marketing plan to launch that product or service 1. Develop a new product The new product or service must be original and realistic. There are no set requirements on what product you propose however one that is realistic and that means something to you personally will be easier to develop. A product can include a physical good, a service or an idea. The following scenarios are suggested to help you identify a potential new product, choose one only: • Your company has come to a crossroads, a new product, service or opportunity is needed to ensure future growth. Your challenge is to identify a new product and develop a marketing plan. • Develop a product that your organisation has a need for and would likely purchase and use in its operations. • You have been contemplating leaving your existing employment to start up a new business and develop the product and marketing plan for that business. 2. Pitch your new product in a class presentation This is a chance to test you product idea in front of the class. Presenting your pitch during pitching week (17th September) is mandatory. The pitch is a 5 minute maximum presentation (including discussion/feedback) to pitch the essentials of your idea to the class. It is recommended that the presentation be a maximum of 3 slides and focus on: what the product is (the offering), who would use it (target segments), why they would use it and why they would choose it over alternatives (value proposition). 3. Create the marketing plan for your chosen product Develop a comprehensive marketing plan based on the template provided in the first lecture (marketingplan.docx). The template lists the key information to be included in your marketing plan, additional sections may be added if appropriate to your product. Note: You may use the product pitched during pitching week, a modified version of it, or a wholly new product (the whole purpose of pitching week is for you to test your product idea and incorporate any changes you deem necessary into the marketing plan). You are expected to use the market analysis tools covered during this semester and apply them appropriately to your product and marketing plan. Independent research is also expected to complete this assignment: a) Research is required into the particular industry, competitors and markets associated with the product, this research should be reflected in your marketing plan b) Research the typical/unique marketing requirements for the particular class of product that you have developed. For example if your product is a luxury good research the marketing literature on luxury goods, if it is a web based product research the marketing literature on marketing a web based product. The results of your research should be reflected in your marketing plan.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Workplace Marketing Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">60</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Written assignment. No set length</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11/10/2016</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6.00pm Tuesday 11 October 2016</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">• Is the product feasible, realistic and easily understood? • Is the differentiation of the product, the value proposition, target market and market positioning clearly stated and logical • Has the organisational and industry context for the marketing plan including identification of any constraints or structural industry opportunities been clearly defined. • Have the marketing concepts covered during the course been applied in the marketing plan • Is the marketing plan appropriate for the particular class of product that is proposed (eg: the marketing requirements for a luxury good will differ from that of industrial software) • Is the marketing plan well structured and easy to understand, do the conclusions follow logically throughout the plan</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment gives you the opportunity to apply marketing concepts through the development of a comprehensive marketing plan for a new service or product.</Data></Cell>
