   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48601</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Mechanical Vibration and Measurement</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are given a series of questions in UTSOnline. These questions are based on preparation week materials. Students are expected to complete all questions within a fixed timeframe.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 1 online assessment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30 minutes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">16/03/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday 16 March 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To confirm student knowledge and understanding of prerequisite/revision material.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">After attending practical laboratory sessions or completing tasks using remote labs, students will be given a number of questions that they must complete using UTSOnline. This will include a number of multiple choice problems, calculations, and short answer questions that directly relate to the laboratory and theory taught during lectures related to these lab tasks. Students are encouraged to complete lab worksheets, finalise results and then undertake online assessments. Multiple tests will be held throughout the session, due dates are below.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Practical and remote laboratory sessions (two assessments)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30 minutes per quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 1: 6 Apr;  Quiz 2: 15 Jun;</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 1: 6 Apr;  Quiz 2: 15 Jun;</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To establish student comprehension of fundamental knowledge of practical session activities and content.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are given one problem to solve within a given time frame. They are required to solve this problem and provide full details of the solutions including free body diagrams, equation of motion derivation, matrix model, and solution where appropriate.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In-class tests (two tests)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">45 minutes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Class Test 1: In Class on 13 Apr;  Class Test 2: In Class on 18 May</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To confirm student ability to model simplified dynamical systems and solve for governing equations and parameters.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Class Test 1: In Class on 13 Apr;  Class Test 2: In Class on 18 May</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are given a project sheet containing a description of a real world mechanical system (with high level complexity and technical challenge) and reports. They are required to develop the system model and obtain the system's dynamic characteristics, then perform the vibration tests, and validate the results. They are required to submit a report including descriptions of test setup, method used, data processing and result interpreting, etc. Students are encouraged to form groups (up to 4 people) to work on the project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project 1: Modelling and experimental testing of half car test rig</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">27/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday 27 April 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To determine student ability to numerically model and experimentally validate a simplified dynamical system. To confirm ability to prepare a technical document and thereby demonstrate ability to work in a team.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are given a project sheet containing a description of a real-world mechanical system (with high-level complexity and technical challenge) and reports. They are required to develop the system model and obtain the system's dynamic characteristics, then perform the vibration tests, and validate the results. They are required to submit a report including descriptions of the test setup, method used, data processing and result interpreting, etc.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project 2: Modelling and experimental validation of multi-storey tower</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">01/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday 1 June 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To confirm student ability to numerically model and experimentally validate a complex dynamical system. To confirm ability to extend model to synthesise advanced configuration and use to make an engineering decision. To confirm ability to prepare a technical document.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are given an exam sheet containing up to 10 questions; comprising of vibration theory (60%), measurement and sensors (20%) and condition monitoring (20%). They are required to solve all of these questions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 hours + 10 minutes reading time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are given an exam sheet containing 7 questions; comprising three covering vibration theory (60%), two in the area of measurement (25%) and one in condition monitoring (15%). They are required to solve all of these questions.</Data></Cell>
