   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48623</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Mechatronics 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to answer a series of questions relating to the C programming language and general programming methodologies. The quiz will be administered through UTSOnline during allocated class time under UTS examination conditions. Each question may include (but is not limited to): multiple choice, fill in the blanks, numerical calculation or description matching and are based on the Lynda course, “Up and Running with C”. A detailed assessment brief will be included in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">C Programming Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">23/03/2020, 6pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">23/03/2020, 6pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The aim of this assessment is to evaluate the C language skills which are essential to progress in the subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to familiarize with embedded C language and you will create functions to control a stepper motor with different operating modes including continuous rotation and discrete step counting. Students are acquired to calibrate distance readings from an IR sensor, display them use them as input in the control of a stepper motor. Students will control a motor to undertake a prescribed set of motions, interface with an infra-red (IR) distance measuring sensor and LCD display. A detailed assessment brief will be included in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Actuation and Sensing</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstration</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06/04/2020, 6pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06/04/2020, 6pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The aim of this assessment is to evaluate the students’ skills on interfacing and integration of exteroceptive sensors and actuators.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students in groups are required to integrate all the modules created in Assessment 2 with a robot to carry out basic tasks. This tasks include (but not limited to) measuring and displaying an IR reading, moving a robot with a button press, directing the IR sensor to a certain orientation and wall follow. A detailed assessment brief will be included in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">System Integration</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstration</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">04/05/2020, 6pm for the Monday group 08/05/2020, 6pm for the Friday group</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The aim of this assessment is to evaluate the students’ skills on system integration.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">04/05/2020, 6pm for the Monday group 08/05/2020, 6pm for the Friday group</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students in groups are required to develop solutions to a robotic challenge. The specifications are designed to allow multiple solutions and the students are encouraged to develop new and innovative methods. The students will need to develop suitable solutions and demonstrate it in a real scenario. A detailed assessment brief will be included in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstration and Competition</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstration</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">22</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25/05/2020, 6pm for the Monday group 29/05/2020, 6pm for the Friday group</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25/05/2020, 6pm for the Monday group 29/05/2020, 6pm for the Friday group</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The aim of this assessment is to evaluate the students’ skills on designing and implementing solutions to a given robotic problem.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The students in groups are required to write a detailed report on their solution to the robotic challenge given in the Assessment 4. The report should include block diagrams, flow charts, rationale for making certain decision, etc. The students in groups are also required to do presentations explaining design decisions, failures and rationale, etc. The groups are required to include an edited video of their maze run. A detailed assessment brief will be included in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report and Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">13</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">01/06/2020, 6pm for the Monday group 05/06/2020, 9am for the Friday group</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">01/06/2020, 6pm for the Monday group 05/06/2020, 9am for the Friday group</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The aim of this assessment is to evaluate the students’ technical and communication skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The students will revise all the materials and project work and sit for a formal open book exam. The students are required to answer all the questions (including mechatronic design question(s))</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Formal Exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The aim of the formal exam is to assess the students’ deeper knowledge gained through lectures, lab classes and projects.</Data></Cell>
