   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41076</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Methods in Quantum Computing</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There will be three assignments each involving mathematical analysis of quantum protocols. Each assignment will be staged across 3-week periods and will require analysis of 3-5 known quantum protocols. The first assignment will allow you to receive formative feedback and will be marked collaboratively, during class. The remaining two assignments will be assigned 20% each.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quantum Protocol Assignements</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">As required to show working and correct answer.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30/08/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 30 August 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To practise and hone skills in analysis of quantum protocols</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Choose a topic in quantum computing that excites you. Research, using relevant scholarly and/or popular resources, and/or imagine the application a future quantum technology might bring us. Speculate on how the technology might serve or change society/business/personal lives/economy/health, engineering etc. Prepare and record a 5-10-minute presentation that discusses the technology and its application. Upload your video to YouTube and send your link to our UTSOnline discussion board. Provide feedback to at least 5 other videos and include a ‘star rating’ in UTSOnline. More information about providing peer feedback will be provided during class and on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Out of the (Quantum) Box Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5-10 minute video</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20/09/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 20 September 2019              Feedback will be given 1 week later.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Feedback will be given 1 week later.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To articulate and brainstorm the known and possible applications of quantum technologies.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each group (ideally pairs), will be given known quantum computing protocols. Groups will need to explain why the protocols are more advantageous than classical counterparts. In order to determine this, students will need to research the classical and quantum literature in the appropriate protocol. Findings will be documented in a report. A template with headings will be provided on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quantum Protocol Group Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">3000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">18/10/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 18 October 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To collaborate to evaluate and justify the advantages of quantum over classical computing</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
