   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32118</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Mobile Communications and Computing</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment is designed to test students on various concepts that have been presented in previous weeks. Note: Closed book - no internet access for the in-class exercises.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Two quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">n/a</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class in       Week 4 and Week 6</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 4 and Week 6</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To provide students with feedback to gauge their performance up to this stage in the subject, identify any specific areas which need more work and give an indication of the level of difficulty of questions in the final test.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The essay will have four main components: (1) a description of the mobile application that they will develop in the Lab, (2) an analysis that clearly identifies the needs and justification for the selected application, (3) a review of the technologies selected and (4) a discussion why these technologies are selected and deployed. This is a group exercise and the essay is strictly limited to 6 pages (single space, single column, font size 11, excluding diagrams and references). Component 1 is group-assessed. Components 2, 3, an 4 are individual-assessed.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">One written essay</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Essay</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">8</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 8              Online submission. 5pm Monday of Week 8</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Online submission. 5pm Monday of Week 8</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment is designed to test students' knowledge in selecting and deploying appropriate technologies for their mobile application project. The assessment is also designed to address students’ writing and presentation skills in the form of a project proposal. The purpose is also to allow students to initiate their own innovative solution, analyse stakeholder needs and decide and select the best solution.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The written test covers the topics addressed in the weeks 1-7. The test will be 1 hour and 20 minutes duration, and will be held in the normal lecture theatre for this subject during the scheduled session time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Test covering the topics presented in the subject</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">8</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 8              In-class, Week 8</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assess the knowledge, level of understanding and problem-solving abilities of each student across the entire range of subject matter.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In-class, Week 8</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A small design project. This is a group-of-three assignment. In this assignment you design and create screenshots of a mobile application. You will present the application in week 11 or 12. The presentations will be peer assessed. The design is reported in a small report. Note: due to peer assessment, attendance to all presentations in week 11 and week 12 is mandatory. For the group assignment students will be assessed as a team, which means each group member will normally receive the same mark. If you have trouble with the operation of your group, ask your tutor for advice (preferably ask as a group). If some of the group feel that other members are not contributing the tutor should be informed and a group meeting held to produce a solution. In extreme cases a group member may be asked by the tutor to withdraw from the Subject, do extra work or accept a lower mark. No complaints about group operation will be considered after week 4.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Small design project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Not applicable</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Not applicable; see Further information</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To develop design skills in collaboration and to convincingly communicate the outcome of the design to stakeholders.</Data></Cell>
