   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32011</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Multilayer Switched Networks</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Online tests will be completed through Cisco Academy on-line exam server in each week. Students are expected to do these to assist their learning of this subject. The feedback of results will be immediate and automatic, with guidance as to which subject areas the student needs to study further. Completion of online tests after due date will not be marked.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Weekly Chapter Online tests</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to Program section in this subject outline about the detailed tasks and due time in each week.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to Program section in this subject outline about the detailed tasks and due time in each week.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment provides an opportunity to students for self-reflection, self-preview and self-review.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment task is a closed-book, paper-based quiz. It is a short written test to be completed in class. The questions will be based on the contents between week 1 and week 5.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Maximum 45 mins</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 6 during the lecture time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 6 during the lecture time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This early session assessment is designed to give students feedback in terms of what they learn by the middle of semester so that students can adjust their learning strategy and improve their learning efficiency.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is a practical assessment conducted on real equipment in class hours. Given network specifications and detailed tasks, each group will be given limited time to build a network on real equipment allocated by instructors. Students are to apply their knowledge and skills to completed assigned tasks including network design, installation, deployment, and troubleshooting related to multilayer switching technologies in this subject. Students' hand-written Engineering Journals/notes may be allowed to use subject to instructors' inspection.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Skill Based Assessment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Approximately 1.5-2.5 hours, subject to numnber of students in the group.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 11 and 12 in Class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">As a final practical assessment, this assessment task evaluates students' competency on their hands-on skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 11 and 12 in Class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This in-class test is a closed-book individual assessment. Each student will be given limited time to complete the short-answer questions in writing. The questions will test theoretical and design aspects of the curriculum covered during the whole session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Written Test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Maximum 1 hour 45 mins</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12 during the lecture time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12 during the lecture time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment is to evaluate students' overall performance of achieving the subject learning objectives. It focuses on knowledge and conceptual understanding.</Data></Cell>
