   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41043</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Natural Language Processing</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is an individual assessment where each student needs to search current job advertisements related to NLP, and analyse the skills needed for the jobs. The report needs to describe the identified jobs, the required skills and experience, and what business domains the jobs are needed for. The report will also need to have discussions outlining the student’s current skills and experiences, and the skill gaps the student needs to fill to meet the job requirements.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Career Understanding and Analysis</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A report of 6 pages, in an 11 point font.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">03/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5.00pm Friday 3 April 2020              Submission at UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submission at UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To identify the skill sets needed in a related industry and produce a report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will need to group themselves according to common career and business domain interests identified in Assessment 1. In the Assessment 2, each group will need to identify a problem in NLP, and review the current state-of-the-art technologies that address the problem. The report will need to detail what NLP problem is identified, how the current state-of-the-art technologies addressed the problem, what are the drawbacks of the current technologies, and what are the remaining open questions for the problem.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Research Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A report of 10 pages, in an 11 point font.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">01/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5.00pm Friday 1 May 2020              Submission at UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submission at UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To identify a research problem and produce a report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Based on the drawbacks of the current technologies and the remaining questions identified in Assessment 2, in Assessment 3 each group needs to propose an idea to improve the state-of-the-art. A project on this idea needs to be developed, where both theoretical and empirical analysis what shows the advantages of the proposed idea are needed. The report needs to include theoretical justifications on why the proposed idea is expected to improve the state-of-the-art. It will also need to include the workflow of the code and empirical analysis of project results on sample NLP data.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Development</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A report of 12 pages, in an 11 point font, plus a 15 minute oral defence.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">22/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5.00pm Friday 22 May 2020              The reports are submitted at UTSOnline by the above due date. The presentations will be in class as per the schedule.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To develop a project report and a presentation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The reports are submitted at UTSOnline by the above due date. The presentations will be in class as per the schedule.</Data></Cell>
