   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49275</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Neural Networks and Fuzzy Logic</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each student is required to answer all questions. Clearly provide the explanation, reasoning, working and source code if appropriate for each question.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1: Basic Neural Networks and Fuzzy Systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Approximately 10-15 pages including source code (if appropriate)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">23/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5.00pm Thursday 23 April 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Provide an understanding of neural network theory and fuzzy logic theory and applications.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each student is required to answer all questions. Clearly provide the explanation, reasoning, working and source code if appropriate for each question.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 2: Advanced Neural Networks and Fuzzy Systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Approximately 10-15 pages including source code (if appropriate)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5.00pm Thursday 11 June 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Provides an advanced understanding of neural network theory and applications.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each student works on a single project for the whole session. Each project requires the use of either neural network or fuzzy logic techniques for solving practical problems. The equipment is based upon experience gained with authentic control applications or computer applications and is suitably modified for student use. There will be two project seminars detailing progress to date, and an Individual Research Paper Submission. Seminar 1: In the first seminar, students in each group are required to present the specification of their project (approximately 10 minutes). It is expected that they will have finalised the functional block diagram and demonstrated the feasibility of the system or software. Seminar 2: In the second seminar, students in each group are required to present the methodology, testing and results of their project (approximately 10 minutes). Finally, they will be required to give a demonstration of their work. Individual Research Paper Submission: Each student is required to write and submit his/her own research article. This article must follow IEEE format (template available in Canvas). A typical research article would have the following format: Abstract I. Introduction (including background of the research, literature reviews, motivations, contributions/ objective, etc) II. Methods (including system design using neural network/deep learning or/and fuzzy logic system, design implementation, etc) III. Experiments and Results IV. Discussions V. Conclusion and Future directions References</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Major Group Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Research article: 6-8 pages, double column (IEEE format)  Introduction: Aims, literature survey, project specifications (10/100) Methods: modules, methodology, analysis, novel ideas (40/100) Results: Design modules tested, results against specifications, optimisation, quality of hardware/software, photograph (40/100) Conclusion (10/100)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30th April 2020 (Seminar 1: 10%), 11th June 2020 (Seminar 2: 10%), 5:00pm 25th June 2020 (Research article (individual task) 30%)See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50% (Seminar 1: 10%; Seminar 2/Demo: 10%; Individual Research Paper: 30%)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Develop and implement a basic trainable neural network or a fuzzy logic system for a typical control, computing application or biomedical application.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30th April 2020 (Seminar 1: 10%), 11th June 2020 (Seminar 2: 10%), 5:00pm 25th June 2020 (Research article (individual task) 30%)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
