   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42009</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Parallel and Multicore Computing</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Written assignment on visualisation technologies and the use of Parallel and Multicore Computing system within businesses.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This project is divided into the following deliverables (1) A project specification, learning contract and assessment criteria will be negotiated with the subject coordinator and their tutor by week 6. (2) A design and architecture report for viable Parallel and Multicore Computing systems infrastructure (using Open Source or commercial product) will be delivered by week 10 (3) Implement/Build this infrastructure stack, noting issues of this deployment by week 13. (4) A presentation on the implementation will be during the lecture in week 13. This includes peer marking and critical review.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Major Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The scale and scope of the implementation will be negotiated on the basis of the size of the group.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will negotiate a learning contract which will include the project assessment criteria.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A group from 2 to 4 students will complete a Project and deliver a solution that involves: specification, architecture, design, development and implementation of a major Parallel and Multicore Computing system based application.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This exam will cover a broad theory behind Parallel and Multicore Computing system technologies. This may include standards, security, architecture design, selection of Parallel and Multicore Computing models, multicore characteristics , types of balancing protocol(s), choice of topologies or what to look for in a typical Parallel and Multicore Computing based user application , etc.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Theory Exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
