   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49258</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Pavement Analysis and Design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will solve two sets of assignments. Each assignment will involve mathematical computation of given technical problems. Solutions will be presented as short written reports.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59PM, Sunday 19 April 2020 (ASSIGNMENT Set 1) 11:59PM, Sunday 17 May 2020 (ASSIGNMENT Set 2)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59PM, Sunday 19 April 2020 (ASSIGNMENT Set 1) 11:59PM, Sunday 17 May 2020 (ASSIGNMENT Set 2)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Strengthen design skills and problem solving techniques; identify students’ issues in analysis and design, apply corrective measures and give students appropriate feedback. Students will classify, formulate, and solve various problems, and differentiate the different types of solutions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The description of the group project will be provided to all students (See UTSOnline). Each team should carry out a research project including assembling of information, evaluating data, demonstrating design procedures, describing at least a relevant case history, summarising the results and providing practical recommendations on a specific topic. Students should work as a team, to collect current articles, integrate the related information, compare existing methods, recommend approaches based on their suitability and find at least one appropriate case study associated with their topic. It will be an opportunity for students to practice real world engineering problems and promote their critical thinking and research skills. Different research projects are allocated to each group of students to practice disciplinary research skills. Students will form themselves in small groups, providing a collaborative learning experience. Students can directly connect the defined research projects to one or some of the subject topics; hence, they will be able to understand deeply the issues involved in the subject through research based learning.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Research Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59PM, Sunday 31 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59PM, Sunday 31 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To engage with research and to encourage students to critique findings in literature and become research oriented lifelong learners. To develop research and team work skills. The main aim of the research project is to develop research skills associated with pavement design.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">One open book quiz and one closed book quiz will be held during the session. The aims of these quizzes are to keep students up to date with the concepts and methods covered in lectures, practice problem, solving techniques, provide convenient means for students to assess their understanding of fundamental rules and ability to deal with small design and practical problems.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59PM, Sunday 5 April 2020 (Online QUIZ 1) 11:59PM, Sunday 10 May 2020 (Online QUIZ 2)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Strengthen design skills and problem solving techniques; identify students’ issues in analysis and design, apply corrective measure and give students appropriate feedback.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59PM, Sunday 5 April 2020 (Online QUIZ 1) 11:59PM, Sunday 10 May 2020 (Online QUIZ 2)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This examination lasts for 2 hours and will consist of 5 to 7 questions on different topics. The final exam is open book and students can bring any written material in the examination venue. The questions will comprise of technical problems and students will apply analytical skills to propose correct solution based on given input data.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To validate learning on the fundamental concepts, problem solving skills, analysis and design procedures in design of geotechnical structures and their application to realistic problems. To assess student's capabilities in development of the required objectives of the subject and gain sound knowledge of in this area and also to encourage students to review the main concepts of the topics and integrate the knowledge gained throughout the session.</Data></Cell>
