    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this assessment is to allow students to learn by combining prior research, analysis and through active collaboration with their peers in class. This assessment task evaluates the performance of individual preparation and also the group learning that takes place in the class room. There will also be specific formal quiz to provide feedback about student learning.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The objective of this task is for you to familiarize with the current situation of pollution control &amp; waste management scenario both at local and global level. You are required to prepare 2 formal research reports (1 and 2) of no more than 2 pages chosen from a list of topics provided. Ensure that your report does not just contain the information you have sourced, but also reflects your critical questioning and thinking. These two reports are to be submitted via Turnitin.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Research reports</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">No longer than 2 pages each. Reference list can be an extra page.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">17 April 2020 by 11:59 pm through Turnitin</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">17 April 2020 by 11:59 pm through Turnitin</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To undertake research on varied topics. Throughout the session, students will be prompted to undertake research on specific topics. It is expected that students post their findings on UTSOnline. Two specific research reports will also need to be submitted via Turnitin. Details of the topics and due dates will be communicated via UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to develop a good understanding of aspects related to different design components of a waste management system and use these skills to develop and design a waste management system for a chosen suburb. Students are also required to visit a landfill and/or another type of waste management facility to gain an understanding of the real practice of waste management. Students are required to contact the operators of the faciltiy, organise and attend a field trip, discuss what is observed in comparison to what they learnt about design and operation of these systems, critically evaluate the system, and use this information in designing the waste management system. This is a group activity designed to use effective team work. It is the responsibility of every student to ensure they belong to a Group. It is mandatory that all students participate in a field visit, submit a report, participate in the presentation, and be part of assessing another groups' work. Your final report will be a technical presentation with different sections. The length of the report should not be more than 20 pages. Duration of the presentation: 15-20 minutes (Maximum). You are also required to provide peer assessment of other group's report and presentation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Major project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">No longer than 20 pages, including reference list.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report due on: 22 May 2020 by 11:59 pm through Turnitin</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The aim of this is for students to demonstrate their learning while designing a waste management system for a chosen suburb. As part of this acitivity, students are also required to critically examine a real case scenario of a landfill or a waste management treatment facility.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report due on: 22 May 2020 by 11:59 pm through Turnitin</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The Final Exam will be an open book exam held during the formal exams period. This is an individual summative assessment and will assess students' ability and learning in all the objectives of the subject. Successful completion of this task is underpinned by participating in pre-reading/research and face-to-face sessions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">45</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
