    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment 3 due (Team Product/Prototype proposal) – Friday 5pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students must demonstrate that they have reached a number of key milestones towards the final outcome of the product/prototype. As part of this, students must demonstrate their ability to identify and solve problems, create solutions, work in teams, communicate professionally, and manage the timelines. The deliverables will consist of a group presentation and laboratory demonstration. Group work will be assessed according to the delivered product/prototype including the presentation and demonstration. Individual work will be assessed according to the individual learning contract and the recorded journal activities.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Team Product/Prototype Delivery 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A 10-15 minute demonstration will be required, followed by question/answer sessions</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              Assessment 4 due (Team  Product/Prototype Delivery 1) – in the lecture</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment 4 due (Team  Product/Prototype Delivery 1) – in the lecture</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To demonstrate students’ ability to make significant progress towards the delivery of the product/prototype.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students must demonstrate that they have completed the prototype. As part of this, they must demonstrate their capacity to identify and solve problems, create solutions, work in teams, communicate professionally, and manage the timelines. The deliverables include a written report submitted online via Turnitin. Students are required to submit an individual project report to show background, individual design objectives, technical challenges, approaches and methods, results and analyses. The report should focus on the student’s personal targets, contributions and understandings. The report will be submitted via Turnitin. The report should include figures, tables and references as appropriate.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Team  Product/Prototype Delivery 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Minimum 10,000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              Assessment 5 due (Team  Product/Prototype Delivery 2) – Friday 5pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment 5 due (Team  Product/Prototype Delivery 2) – Friday 5pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To demonstrate students’ ability to deliver the final prototype and summarise what has been achieved during the studio design process.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment is to carry out exercise problems related to transmission line compensation, power system stability, load frequency control, and automatic voltage regulator.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Due dates for the assessment tasks and assessment criteria will be indicated along with the particular assessment task sheets.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Test knowledge of the use of the concepts learnt in the theory for practical applications.</Data></Cell>
