   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49150</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Prestressed Concrete Design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task includes an assignment and a quiz. The assignment involves design calculations that require problem solving and numerical analysis for determinate structures. The quiz assesses prerequisite knowledge to allow students to self-assess. The quiz involves design calculations that require problem solving and numerical analysis for determinate structures.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment and Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Pre-assessment Quiz due 22/03/2020, in class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Pre-assessment Quiz due 22/03/2020, in class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Before census day to allow students to demonstrate and examine their knowledge of the prerequisite subjects and receive timely feedback on their progress.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A group of 3 to 4 students will work on a computer modelling and design project. A different drawing will be given to each group. Students are required to implement RAM Concept sotware to model the prestressed concrete structure and design the required tendons. Students then write a report with the following details:  aims of the project modelling dimensions and geometry a summary of the materials properties and extra assumptions used calculation steps outputs of the Ram Concept software discussion of results list of references</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 5 June 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">After mid-break to allow students to demonstrate their knowledge of the concepts learnt in the subject, apply their skills to solve problems and self-assess their progress in the subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">All assignments are quantitative – design calculations and subsequent design decisions will be required. Students will analyse and design to Limit State Design philosophy of the current Australian Standard AS3600-2009 in accordance with current accepted design practice. Topics for each assignment include Tension Members, Indeterminate Beams and Indeterminate Slabs. Assignment questions will be uploaded to UTSOnline. Students should solve the question and provide the detailed calculations for the design. Every step of the calculation and utilised formulations with proper reference to notes should be provided.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1 due 27/04/2020, 11:59pm; Assignment 2 due 08/05/2020, 11:59pm; Assignment 3 due 05/06/2020, 11:59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There will be three assignments to allow students to apply their skills to identify problems and apply appropriate approaches, make decisions to solve the problem and design components and systems for prestressed concrete structures to satisfy Australian standards and international guidelines.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1 due 27/04/2020, 11:59pm; Assignment 2 due 08/05/2020, 11:59pm; Assignment 3 due 05/06/2020, 11:59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The restricted open-book final exam covers the following topics:  Design of Tension Members Design of Continuous Beams Design of Continuous slabs  In the Final and Pre-assessment exams, students are allowed to use their lecture notes, class handouts, AS 3600-2009 and AS/NZ 1170. Strictly, “Textbooks” &amp; “Solved Problems” are not allowed. The exam will comprise one (1) theoretical question and three (3) design questions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">45</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
