   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48821</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Principles of Environmental Engineering</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS based online Quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Knowledge quiz (Formative)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz is available in week 1 and can be done throughout the semester on an as needs basis. The quizzes can be attempted multiple times.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz is available in week 1 and can be done throughout the semester on an as needs basis. The quizzes can be attempted multiple times.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The quizzes are designed for students to develop and self test their understanding of key concepts, and their application to environmental engineering.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 hours</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">16/09/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10.00am Monday 16 September 2019              Refer to in-class announcements for any changes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to in-class announcements for any changes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment will enable students to receive feedback on their learning during lectures and in-class activities. The feedback is provided via in-class quizzes or doing group discussions/tasks that encourage collaborative learning.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Develop a conceptual design and evaluation strategy for the treatment of a contaminated material (eg. wastewater, soil, air). This will involve developing an investigation plan for the waste to be treated.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Waste treatment design project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">3,000-4,000 words excluding references. Please use provided exemplars and assessment weighting as a guide.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">07/10/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Monday 7 October 2019              Please submit to Task 3 dropbox in UTSOnline. Each group will only submit one file.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assessment framework is based around the structural complexity of the approach used to analyse and solve the problem. This framework and examination of student exemplars will form an in-class activity.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task is designed to get students to engage with the knowledge from fundamental concepts on reactors, reaction kinetics and chemical transformations and integrate this with their laboratory experiences to create a conceptual design and evaluation program for a waste treatment system.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Please submit to Task 3 dropbox in UTSOnline. Each group will only submit one file.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task requires students to develop a multimedia presentation of the task 3 project. The target audience is the client. See UTSOnline for further information on the design brief and report format</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Communication</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Multimedia presentation is limited to 5 minutes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20/10/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 20 October 2019              The presentation must be uploaded to the students UTS YouTube account. A file with the URL should be uploaded to the Task 4 dropbox in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The presentation must be uploaded to the students UTS YouTube account. A file with the URL should be uploaded to the Task 4 dropbox in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Discussion of this assessment framework and examination of student exemplars will form an in-class activity.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task is designed to get students to communicate key knowledge from their project to an end user. It uses multi-media and therefore complements the written report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Formal exam, open-book.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 hours + 10 minutes reading time</Data></Cell>
