   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41183</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Privacy Preserving</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In this assessment task, student teams will investigate a real‐world privacy breach involving a corporate environment. They will evaluate the levels of privacy in terms of data breach. They are required to write a report to summarise those breaches. Group assessment 20% Individual assessment 30%</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report on privacy attacks</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is a group task, the planning report should be approximately 2000‐2500 words.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7, 11:59 pm 11/09/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7, 11:59 pm 11/09/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In this task students will demonstrate the application of the standard practice of attacking, develop teamwork skills in evaluating and planning testing, and develop awareness of ethical codes of conduct whilst working in the corporate environment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In this assesment task students will Implement and/or compare a set of existing privacy/security algorithms on a specific problem domain to defend the attack in the first assignment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Privacy preserving project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is an individual assessment task. Students are required to submit a report of approximately 2000‐2500 words along with exhibits to support findings.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12, 11:59 pm 23/10/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12, 11:59 pm 23/10/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In this task students will demonstrate their ability and competence in using appropriate privacy preserving technologies to defend against proposed attacks, and critically analyse experimental testing results before making well‐informed conclusions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
