   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49119</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Problematic Soils and Ground Improvement Techniques</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will classify, formulate and solve various problems, and differentiate the types of solutions. A number of assignments for each topic are prepared. Assignment questions will be uploaded to UTSOnline and students should solve the question and provide the detailed calculations for the design. Every step of the calculation and utilised formulations with proper reference to notes and available literature should be provided.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments (Summative)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to subject timetable on UTSOnline for due dates</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to subject timetable on UTSOnline for due dates</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To give students the opportunity to practice problem solving. The assessment task gives students the opportunity to practice various approaches related to problematic soils and ground improvement and to evaluate them. Students will classify, formulate, and solve various problems, and differentiate the different types of solutions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A group of 4 to 6 students will work on a major research project with case studies. A different topic will be given to each group. Students will write a report with details including; executive summary, introduction/background, aims of the project , modelling dimensions and geometry, summary of the materials properties and extra assumptions used , calculation steps, outputs , discussion of results, and list of references. Students should refer to UTSOnline for further instructions for major project report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group research project report (Summative)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to subject timetable on UTSOnline for due dates</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to subject timetable on UTSOnline for due dates</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To engage with research and to encourage students to be research oriented and life long learners. To develope research skills.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students solve these quizzes available on UTSOnline and submit the detailed solutions and the answers online. These are individual quizzes to support student preparation for the main assignments and tasks.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Online Quiz (Formative)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to subject timetable on UTSOnline for due dates</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To allow students to demonstrate what they have learnt, to establish what more they should learn and give them the opportunity to have formative and feed forward assessment of their performance.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to subject timetable on UTSOnline for due dates</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The final exam is open book and students can bring any notes or books they need. Students can use a programmable calculator. The exam will cover all topics.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Examination (Summative)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exam is held during UTS exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exam is held during UTS exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To validate learning on the fundamental concepts, problem solving skills, analysis and design procedures in ground improvement and construction challanges in real life. To assess student's abilities to develop the required objectives of the subject and gain sound knowledge of problematic soils and improvement techniques. To encourage students to review the main concepts of the topics and integrate the knowledge gained throughout the session.</Data></Cell>
