   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41089</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Professional Studio B</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students create an Individual Learning Contract (ILC), and then to have it agreed to by their academic mentor(s). The ILC will be created as a UTSOnline Portfolio, with a structured format and length requirements as noted in the template that will be provided. The ILC should describe the following:  Activities that will enable the student to gain the knowledge and skills that will enhance the student’s contribution to the Team and Product/Prototype. Activities that will enable the student to gain extra knowledge and skills that they nominate, and do not necessarily address the Product/Prototype. The knowledge and/or skill that they have chosen to teach to their peers.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual Learning Agreement</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">4</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 4              In class in week 4 One-on-One meeting with lecturer</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class in week 4 One-on-One meeting with lecturer</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Creation of an Individual Learning Contract allows students to identify and document their learning direction, and set goals for the session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are expected to submit evidence of their individual work completed throughout the session that demonstrates how they have met the goals articulated in the Individual Learning Contract (ILC). Students' work will be assessed against what was agreed in the ILC. The length and format of the submission will depend upon what activities were chosen in the ILC. Part of this includes teaching the class activity that was agreed in the Individual Learning Contract.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual Learning Contract Completion</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Strictly limited to 8 physical pages of assessable text, supporting diagrams and tables (typical range: 3000 word min - 6000 word maximum).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period              One-on-One meeting with the teaching staff. To be scheduled nearer the end of the session (week 13)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">One-on-One meeting with the teaching staff. To be scheduled nearer the end of the session (week 13)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">On completion of the Individual Learning Contract, students demonstrate that they have achieved the goals set near the start of the session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Teams create a written requirement specification document for their Product/Prototype, develop a project plan for development activities and timelines, and have these agreed to by their Product Owner(s) and academic mentor(s). The requirement specifications should include agreed functional and quality requirements and product deliverables for the work to be carried out. A template with suggested section headings will be provided as guidance. Teams set up a WiKi on UTSOnline that they will use throughout the session for delivery of the Product outcomes. This assessment task forms the first item to be posted on the WiKi.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Team Project Plan and Product/Prototype Requirement Specifications</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class in Week 7. Team meeting with the Product Owner and lecturer.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Negotiate the scope and outcomes with the Product Owner(s) and academic mentor(s), develop a Product/Prototype Requirement Specifications Document, and a project plan for development activities.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class in Week 7. Team meeting with the Product Owner and lecturer.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There are three parts to this task:  The design specifications and the working Product or Prototype, which must be demonstrated in class. A presentation delivered in class that describes what was produced, including a Product / Prototype demonstration. The length of the presentation will typically be between 20-30 minutes depending upon the number of students in the team. A set of WiKi pages that document the design specifications and the working Product/Prototype implemented. The number of WiKi pages will depend upon the complexity of the Product/Prototype and the number of students in the team. There must be a history of regular contributions from the planning stage to delivery stage that shows the team's progress over time.  All students must be present in class for the final presentation/demonstration, and all students must have contributed to the WiKi throughout the session. The WiKi should document the process followed, and contributions by individual team members.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Team Product/Prototype Delivery</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Last week of the session (week 12). Team demonstration to Product Owner and Lecturer.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Last week of the session (week 12). Team demonstration to Product Owner and Lecturer.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students demonstrate their ability to deliver a Product or Prototype to an agreed scope. In doing so, students also demonstrate their capacity to solve problems, create solutions, develop design specifications, implement the Product/Prototype, work in teams, communicate professionally, and manage time and tasks.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
