   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41039</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Programming 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Building on the material presented in the preparation lectures, exercise and workshop exercises, the student will attempt a programming challenge.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab Assessments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              Weekly, last task due by 5/6/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Weekly, last task due by 5/6/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task provides a mixture of formative and summative assessment to allow students to gauge their progress towards the subject objectives in a low-stakes, controlled environment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The student will be presented with a large program codebase, from which they will select a portion of approximately 50 lines of code, which they will then read and comment. The comments should explain the purposes and key structural elements of the reviewed code correctly and concisely, and relate that code back to the overall codebase.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Code Comprehension</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50-100 lines of code, commented.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 10              Final due date will be the end of Week 10 (22/5/2020), though students may submit work for assessment earlier.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final due date will be the end of Week 10 (22/5/2020), though students may submit work for assessment earlier.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The ability to understand code at a higher level than simple line-by-line translation is a key skill in developing strong mental models supporting program design and development skills. Being able to read, comprehend and explain code is a fundamental step in developing deeper understanding.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Building on the material presented throughout the subject, students will progressively build components of a single, substantial piece of software, meeting a design objective.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Approximately 500 lines of code.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              End of Week 12 (5/6/2020).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">While understanding of the elements of a computer program is foundational, without comprehending how they function in a larger whole the core goal of programming is lost. This task combines the individual elements learnt throughout the subject into a single, functioning whole.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">End of Week 12 (5/6/2020).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Answer questions posed by the examiner in an interview format.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Oral Exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5 minutes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Programming is skillset that exists independently of the keyboard and screen. Developing as a competent programmer requires to the ability to understand computational problems, build suitable mental models and develop conceptual solutions effectively, before the computer is even approached. The oral exam is an opportunity for students to demonstrate their comprehension of the mental disciplines required as a programmer.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The student will develop program(s) to solve a (series of) challenging free-form problem(s), requiring research into techniques that may be outside the scope of the subject, and thus at least some independent study.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Extension</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              End of Week 12 (5/6/2020)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">End of Week 12 (5/6/2020)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Knowledge and skill can be demonstrated in many ways. In programming subjects in particular, more sustained and free-form development than that allowed by normal assessment tasks can reveal a deeper understanding than otherwise apparent. This task offers the opportunity for students to demonstrate a higher degree of knowledge and skill through work on more difficult computational and programming problems that extend beyond the immediate material of the subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
