   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48023</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Programming Fundamentals</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Complete sections of a program by inserting programming statements that achieve the required purpose.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Pass / fail mastery tests</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">One or more hours each week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week range</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 2 to Week 12              To pass the subject, students must pass all the pass/fail tests satisfactorily by the end of week 12 (i.e. 11:59pm Friday October 23, 2020). However, to be eligible to receive a mark for the assignment, a student must have completed all the pass/fail AND additional lab tests by the end of week 11 (i.e. 11:59pm Friday October 16, 2020).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To pass the subject, students must pass all the pass/fail tests satisfactorily by the end of week 12 (i.e. 11:59pm Friday October 23, 2020). However, to be eligible to receive a mark for the assignment, a student must have completed all the pass/fail AND additional lab tests by the end of week 11 (i.e. 11:59pm Friday October 16, 2020).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of these tests is to establish that a student has acquired the minimum knowledge and programming skills required to pass this subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In this assignment, students will build and/or extend a basic class structure. Students will submit their assignment for marking to the online test system. More details about the assignment will be provided in the assignment specification. This assignment is an individual work.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assignment is due at 11:59pm Friday October 23, 2020. However, to be eligible to receive a mark for the assignment, a student must have completed all the pass/fail AND additional lab tests by the last lab session of week 11 (i.e. 11:59pm Friday, October 16, 2020). Students may submit the assignment as many times as they like, without loss of marks, prior to the submission date/time. For feedback, students are encouraged to submit their partly completed assignments to the online test system regularly, prior to the deadline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assignment is due at 11:59pm Friday October 23, 2020. However, to be eligible to receive a mark for the assignment, a student must have completed all the pass/fail AND additional lab tests by the last lab session of week 11 (i.e. 11:59pm Friday, October 16, 2020). Students may submit the assignment as many times as they like, without loss of marks, prior to the submission date/time. For feedback, students are encouraged to submit their partly completed assignments to the online test system regularly, prior to the deadline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this assessment task is to provide students with the opportunity to show they can apply the basic skills and knowledge of programming in a context where it is not made explicit exactly which basic skills and knowledge need to be used.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In this assessment task students will build and/or extend existing code to implement specified requirements. This assessment task is individual.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Additional lab exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">One or more hours each week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week range</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 2 to Week 12              Students may attempt the lab exercises only after they have completed all of the pass/fail lab tests. The final opportunity to do these lab exercises is the end of week 12 (i.e. 11:59pm Friday October 23, 2020). However, note that to be eligible to receive a mark for the assignment, a student must have completed all the pass/fail AND additional lab tests by the last lab session of week 11 (i.e. 11:59pm Friday October 16, 2020).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of these tests is to (1) deepen the minimum knowledge and programming skills required to pass this subject and (2) broaden the students grasp of those skills and concepts by presenting further case studies.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students may attempt the lab exercises only after they have completed all of the pass/fail lab tests. The final opportunity to do these lab exercises is the end of week 12 (i.e. 11:59pm Friday October 23, 2020). However, note that to be eligible to receive a mark for the assignment, a student must have completed all the pass/fail AND additional lab tests by the last lab session of week 11 (i.e. 11:59pm Friday October 16, 2020).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will complete quiz questions announced via email and in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
