   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48001</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project BEngSc</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual task requiring students to do preliminary research on one facet of the project being investigated. Students are required to use at least three suitable sources of information to investigate the context of the project, detail their findings and highlight any further information they think will be valuable to the project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Information seeking</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 page summary of a chosen topic.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">3</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 3</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is an introductory activity, requiring students to investigate and report on information that will form the basis of their ongoing project work.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to submit structured, documented components which will be used to develop the final feasibility report. Each submission will be followed by peer and/or instructor feedback and regular Spark self and peer reviews will be included. In undertaking the work, students are expected to plan, record, monitor and collaborate on their work using project management tools.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report Development Tasks</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Part 1 (requirements) due 5pm Friday week 4. Part 2 (proposal)  due 5pm Friday week 5. Part 3 (milestone 1) due 5pm Friday week 8. Part 4 (milestone 2) due 5pm Friday week 10.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Part 1 (requirements) due 5pm Friday week 4. Part 2 (proposal)  due 5pm Friday week 5. Part 3 (milestone 1) due 5pm Friday week 8. Part 4 (milestone 2) due 5pm Friday week 10.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To develop and improve the skills needed to develop, describe and communicate facets of an engineering project, including the justification for decisions made in the context of a complex problem.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Professionally presented final feasibility report including an individual statement of contribution from team members.  The report is a synthesis of the developed report components. Groups are expected to show they have made use of formative feedback and that they have used sound judgement in deciding on the information to be presented. All decisions made must be clearly justified and the final feasibility recommendation must be clearly communicated based on the value of the proposal.  In undertaking the work, students are expected to plan, record, monitor and collaborate on their work using project management tools and to report on its use.  In addition, Spark self and peer assessment will be done as part of this submission.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Feasability Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">60</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To deliver a feasibility report that is built on the development tasks requiring students to make use of feedback, and to exercise judgement in selecting the information to present and deciding on the feasibility of the project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Professionally presented final project proposal presented in an oral presentation with slides. Every team member is required to speak in the presentation. The content presented must indicate an understanding of the project in the context, make clear and well justified recommendations as to feasibility and be suitable for the audience.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 11</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Appropriate structure and presentation of the information with regard to purpose and audience.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Hand written reflection journal kept during the session; SPARK evaluations. A hand-written learning journal is required. SPARK self and peer assessment will be used throughout the session to aid student learning outcomes. Learning Journal: The purpose of this document is to ‘journal’ in chronological order the each individual student’s contribution. The journal is to be a ruled (or grid paper) fixed-page lecture book – suggest 196 or 240 pages. Students will record all of their own pertinent activities and tasks associated with the subject in a learning journal. As a guide, this would include: what work was undertaken (eg. a summary from readings, calculations, analysis, etc.); the time involved (eg. dates, start and finish times, cumulative hours to date, etc); notes, observations and reflections of individual performance as well as that of other team members. In addition, the journal should record group/team activities, meetings, decisions, planning, timing, responsibilities etc. The journal must be brought to every class. It will be periodically ‘signed-off’ by the subject coordinator at the ‘last entry’ in order to indicate work completed to-date. The journal will be submitted at the same time as the final project report or as advised by the subject coordinator. The subject coordinator will advise on how reports will be returned to students. SPARKPLUS Self and Peer Assessment: This online application will be used periodically throughout this subject to facilitate student learning, reflection, feedback and evaluation. The application will also be used as a mechanism to facilitate fairness when evaluating student’s individual performance in team based assignments.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">On-going, final submission the day of class during Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">On-going, final submission the day of class during Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Compulsory, achieve a 'satisfactory' level</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Journals tasks and evaluation activities undertaken in relation to the subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
