   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Prototyping Physical Interaction</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Develop a tutorial for an element of an interactive system, directed at your fellow students. Provide a clear description of how to use the element, and the types of contexts in which it may be deployed. Implement your example and demonstrate it. Provide working code and a working example of the element (which will be made available to all students in the subject). Submit this as a new thread on the discussion board. The example should either be highly original or the tutorial highly effective, as the aim is for you to provide your fellow students with resources from which to rapidly learn.  eg. Displaying system state as a colour produced by an RGB LED.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Develop a technology tutorial</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1 proof of a working example (video and example code/implementation and diagrams) 1 tutorial (approx. 1 page) and description of design context.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">14/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Tuesday 14 April 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To develop familiarity with implementing sensor and display technologies.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Form a group, and choose a design problem to address. Develop an individual approach to the problem, and design a physical, interactive solution. Develop a system diagram and describe in detail all the code and hardware needed to implement the system. Pay particular attention to the input and output data the components of the system will need to function, and the way that this data is passed around the system and is processed. Provide simplified pseudo-code for all software elements, and detailed information about each sensor and how it will connect to the system. Make an implementation plan, and provide a complete backlog of tasks for the implementation of the system.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Model an Implementation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1 individual report per student with: 1 system diagram. 3 pages on software. 3 pages describing sensors and feedback hardware 1-2 pages on plan and backlog.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">28/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Tuesday 28 April 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To accurately model the sensor, display, hardware and software elements within the prototype.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Build the complete interactive prototype and run a user study with the system to test your implementation and design. Your prototype implementation is not being specifically assessed at this stage. Instead, we focus on your capability to design and run a user study. Additionally, your analysis of the user feedback you provide will also be assessed.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Study Prototype with Users</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">35</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">As a group: a) 1 user study design and protocol (1500 words) and b) User study feedback as appendix (raw transcripts/data) As individuals:  1 analysis report (3000 words) covering c) Description of perceived user needs based on user study analysis d) Design alterations and refinements planned and their basis in user feedback</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 5 June 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To obtain user study feedback on your prototype system.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Incorporate the user feedback into the next iteration of the system, and present the final system. Create a video demonstration of the system and submit the system, alongside a rationale explaining your changes, and an individual reflection on your learning experience.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Prototype</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">As a group: 1 3-10 min video presenting system, carefully and thoroughly explaining the prototype design, and the basis of the design features within user feedback. 1 2000-word group rationale and summary of implemented improvements based on user feedback. As individuals: 1 1000-word Individual reflection on design process.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">16/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Tuesday 16 June 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To re-design and refine the fully-realized prototype system.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
