   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49309</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quality Planning and Analysis</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This subject has a major group assignment which has been designed with the aim of providing you a practical case where you are required to apply the various quality tools and techniques covered in this subject. The assignment consists of a number of tasks (parts) which involve various learning activities and sources including researching, creative and innovative thinking, analytical and problem solving skills, as well as system thinking and report writing. Assignment requirements including the specific tasks descriptions, examples of marking and turnitin assessment, date and format of submission will be made available at the start of the semester on the subject webpage at UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment (all exercises)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Page size requirements are specified in each task (part) of the actual assignment document. Page size difference i.e. slightly under or over is acceptable.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">9</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 9              A soft-copy must be submitted as per described instructions above and in the assignment instruction via Turnitin link on Canvas under assignment submission webpage.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A soft-copy must be submitted as per described instructions above and in the assignment instruction via Turnitin link on Canvas under assignment submission webpage.</Data></Cell>
