    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will learn how to tackle challenging mathematical problems in quantum information theory while collaborating in a group environment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Oral presentation. Each student will prepare a 10-minute oral presentation on a research paper of key relevance to the subject to be presented at the end of semester. Mid-semester, each student will select their paper to present from a collection prepared by the lecturer. Prior to the end of semester each will get a chance to present their paper in a tutorial and receive feedback on that presentation. The final presentation will take place within the last two weeks of semester and is structured as follows:  10 min: Student presentation of the research paper, uninterrupted, on whiteboard. 5 min: Questions on the presentation and the research topic it covers (where it overlaps with the material covered in the lecture).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation of research paper</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15 minutes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Learn how to summarise and present research papers and discuss technical aspects of quantum information theory.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Oral examination. Each student will have an oral examination at the end of semester. General questions will be asked about all the topics covered in the subject, with a specific focus on the assignments that students have completed in their group. The student will be asked to solve a problem on the whiteboard (with limited collaborative assistance provided). Students can refer to paper course material or notes in the exam.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Oral examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10-20 minutes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assess proficiency in the techniques of quantum information theory.</Data></Cell>
