   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41173</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quantum Software and Programming</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students choose a quantum algorithm from a list (Shor’s, HHL, etc) to investigate. Students should prepare a comprehensive report in a form of their choice and as agreed with the subject coordinator.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Research report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1500 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students formalise the problem that the algorithm aims to solve, understand how the algorithm works, and the time/space/query complexity of the algorithm.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students form different groups according to the quantum algorithms they chose in the first assessment, and for each group, use one of the high-level quantum programming languages to implement the algorithm, and successfully run a simulation on the respective platform.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group algorithm programming project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students should submit a code project of approximately 1000 lines of code for the group, where their individual contribution to the project is proportional and clearly highlighted.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To help students gain hands-on experience implementing quantum algorithms using high-level quantum programming languages.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students form different groups of their choice, and for each group, they will be required to implement the algorithm of decomposing arbitrary quantum gates to basic gates from a chosen universal set.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group compiler programming project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students should submit a code project of approximately 2000 lines of code for the group, where their individual contribution to the project is proportional and clearly highlighted.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To gain hands-on experience implementing a key component of compilers for a quantum programming language.</Data></Cell>
