   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48450</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Real-time Operating Systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The quiz/test will check what the students have learned.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quizzes/Tests</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">n/a</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class in       weeks from 2 to 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">weeks from 2 to 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To allow students to gain feedback on their understanding of key topics taught in this subject and examine their learning of the subject fundamentals.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment consists of a programming task and a simple report. The assignment provides a list of programming problems for you to complete followed by a written report based on your investigation. The assignment report needs to be submitted online through UTSOnline. A brief investigation report is expected to support the results obtained during your experiments. An introductory session for this assignment is planned (Q/A) in week 4.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Programming assignment and concept study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7              The assignment report is due at 23.59 PM, 29/04/2020See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assignment report is due at 23.59 PM, 29/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To provide students with an opportunity to demonstrate an enhanced level of practical skills in systems programming and simple report writing. In brief, students are required to write a program, and exceute their program on an instructor's PC to verifiy the program is functional, in order to meet the learning requriements defined in this subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assignment consists of a programming task and an investigation report. The assignment provides a list of programming problems for you to complete followed by a written report based on your investigation. The assignment report needs to be submitted online through UTSOnline. A comprehensive investigation report is expected to support the results obtained through your experiments. An introductory session for this assignment is planned (Q/A) in week 7.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Programming assignment and experimental analysis report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 10              The assignment report is due at 23.59 PM 20/05/2020See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To provide students with an opportunity to demonstrate an enhanced level of practical skills in systems programming, experiment analysis and report writing. In brief, students are required to wirte a program, and exceute their program on an instructor's PC to verifiy the program is functional, in order to meet the learning requriements defined in this subject. An analysis report is required after the program and experiments.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assignment report is due at 23.59 PM 20/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A restricted open book, written examination that contains questions directed at all material presented which was not the focus of the mid-session examination.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 hours, plus 10 minutes reading time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To obtain a measure of each student's mastery of the knowledge component of the curriculum across the whole session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
