   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32572</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflective Practice in Information Technology</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">SELF-DIRECTED PROFESSIONAL LEARNING IN INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY  This assessment is a self-directed learning contract for each student to research and develop understandings, knowledge and skills that they have identified as strategically important for their professional future. Each student negotiates their learning topic, objectives, activities, deliverables and assessment criteria with their mentor and the subject co-ordinator. The agreed learning contract is signed by the student, mentor and subject co-ordinator. Normally each contract will include a learning plan (10%), a background report (15%) and final deliverables (25%) that are evidence of successful completion of the learning plan. These final deliverables is usually a report, but other deliverables relevant to your Learning Contract can be negotiated with your mentor and the subject coordinator.  The default task is a 4000 word academic paper on some scholarly research that is of relevance to the IT profession.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment 1: LEARNING CONTRACT</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Learning Plan due in Week 4, Background Report in Week 7 and Final Deliverables due in Week 14</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">RESEARCHING, PRESENTING AND GROUPWORK Students in teams of three or four will research and then present in the lecture their findings about an attribute required for professional practice in Information Technology. The presentation is to include the findings of a short original research inquiry that investigates a question about the professional attribute. The presentation allows seven minutes per group member, plus time for questions and answers. Groups will indicate their preferred professional attribute for presentation (no guarantee of first-choice topic) and then will be allocated the week of their presentation. 50% of the mark will be from the subject coordinator and 50% will be from the peer assessment of other students. Professional attributes in IT include: Change Management Communication Originality &amp; Creativity Critical Thinking Ethics &amp; Professionalism Global &amp; Local Perspectives Information &amp; Knowledge Management Initiative &amp; Enterprise Innovation Leadership Life-Long Learning Multi-media Literacy Multi-modal and Trans-Literacy Planning &amp; Organising Problem Solving Research Self-Management Teamwork Technology Literacy Other ???</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment 2: GROUP PRESENTATION</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Weeks 6 to 13 in the lecture time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">SELF-AND-PEER EVALUATION &amp; REFLECTING ON RPIT ACTIVITIES This assessment aims to encourage professional self-evaluation, peer-evaluation, meta-cognition and life-long learning. Each student will peer evaluate the Group Presentations as they are given in class and collect personal reflections about their learning from RPIT’s activities.Peer evaluations will be worth about 16% of the 25% for this assessment. The portfolio will be worth the rest of the marks for this assessment.  The portfolio will include a minimum of 1500 words of fortnightly reflection about the learning contract, progress and deliverables and IT professional attributes, and final comments about their learning in RPIT. The reflective portfolio can be paper-based eg. a diary, or can be digital eg. a blog, google docs or similar. Each student discusses their reflective portfolio throughout the semester with their mentor.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment 3: REFLECTIVE PORTFOLIO</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Peer evaluations for each Group Presentation are due at the completion of each session of Presentations. Short reflections are to be discussed every fortnight with the Mentor and the final Portfolio submission is in Week 15.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
