   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48561</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Renewable Energy Systems Studio A</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students must keep an engineering journal to record observations, ideas/thoughts, results and discussions throughout the duration of the subject with particular focus on lab exercises and project. The journal will be assessed through checkpoints and discussions which include design, development and project management.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design and reflection journal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Journal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1-2 hours per week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Logbook/journal of each student will be discussed and assessed 2-3 times for the entire session during the LAB sessions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Logbook/journal of each student will be discussed and assessed 2-3 times for the entire session during the LAB sessions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To develop a practical engineering work habit of journaling ideas, discussions and results to organise students' thoughts and information in detail.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students work in teams to create a written proposal, and have it agreed to by their academic mentor(s). Teams define the scope and feasibility for their studio work, and negotiate the scope and outcomes with the academic mentor(s). Each team will choose from a pool of suggested applications, or may propose their own application, to develop and demonstrate a downsized working hardware prototype. It must include background, technical challenges, targets, agreed deliverables and a timeline for the work to be carried out. A template with suggested section headings will be provided.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Team prototype proposal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">4,000 to 7,000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 6              Team prototype presentation, report and PCB design (ready for fabrication)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Team prototype presentation, report and PCB design (ready for fabrication)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To design and plan the development of a selected application of power electronics and drive systems.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students must demonstrate that they have reached a number of key milestones towards the final outcome of the prototype. As part of this, students must demonstrate their ability to identify and solve problems, create solutions, work in teams, communicate professionally, and manage the timelines. The deliverables will consist of a written report submitted online via Turnitin, a presentation and laboratory demonstration.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Team prototype delivery 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A 10-15 minute demonstration will be required, followed by question/answer sessions</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">9</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 9              Team prototype presentation and Q&amp;A. The team should demonstrate how they have achieved the key milestones of the project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To demonstrate students’ ability to make significant progress towards the delivery of the prototype.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Team prototype presentation and Q&amp;A. The team should demonstrate how they have achieved the key milestones of the project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students must demonstrate that they have completed the prototype. As part of this, they must demonstrate their capacity to identify and solve problems, create solutions, work in teams, communicate professionally, and manage the timelines. The deliverables include a group presentation and laboratory demonstration of the working prototype. Students are also required to submit an individual project report to show background, individual design objectives, technical challenges, approaches and methods, results and analyses. The report should focus on the student’s personal targets, contributions and understandings. The report will be submitted via Turnitin. The report should include figures, tables and references as appropriate.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Team prototype delivery 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">35</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">4,000 to 7,000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              Project demonstration and report (to submit via Turnitin on UTSOnline)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project demonstration and report (to submit via Turnitin on UTSOnline)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To demonstrate students’ ability to deliver the final prototype and summarise what has been achieved during the studio design process.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
