   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48550</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Renewable Energy Systems Studio B</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The objective of these activities is for students to develop an appreciation of system design principles and of applications of electrical energy conversion devices. For this group project, you are required to (a) Form a group up to three students, (b) Select a suitable algorithm to optimize the energy efficiency of a renewable energy system, and (c) Develop a hardware prototype to verify the study of the system. Each group will present the work as a project demonstration and submit a complete project report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design/drawing/plan/sketch</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Not applicable</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Not applicable              Blended Labs and Group project approach. Lab reports in multiple weeks and Group demonstration and report submission in final week. Submissions via UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Blended Labs and Group project approach. Lab reports in multiple weeks and Group demonstration and report submission in final week. Submissions via UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The aim is to design a system for a reneweable energy or energy utilization system application. Students will work in groups of two or three and work through research, design, simulation, hardware implementation and testing, and final reporting stages. Students will work together and present their work in three presentations given to the subject coordinator and producea final group report to complement the presentation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In this 2-hour restricted open book exam, students are expected to apply the knowledge learned through online lectures, tutorials, lab exercises and projects to answer both close-ended and open-ended questions on renewable energy systems.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assess students' understanding of renewable and clean energy concepts and to test their capacity to analyse and solve problems. The students are assessed on all material covered throught the session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment involves the system design of one or a combination of renewable energy source(s). The tasks include select a potential site for the selected energy source(s), develop a system specification for the system, identify and design the building blocks for the system, and evaluate the system through mathematical analysis and/or simulation. The key assessment component is a 4-page (excluding appendices and references) IEEE style technical paper.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual assignments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 10              Individual assignment submission via UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To conduct a case study into a specific aspect of renewable energy and for each student to use any raw data and develop their own interpretation of the data to write a report that can be in the form of a technical paper, a book chapter, or whatever format is specified. The Assignments will vary considerably from year to year.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual assignment submission via UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
