   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49006</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Risk Management in Engineering</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering failures are categorised depending on the level and size of impact:  Large and localised Medium and localised Small and localised Large and widespread Medium and widespread Small and widespread  Students identify and describe two engineering failures from different categories that occurred previously. For each failure, students set the boundaries, identify stakeholders, define the inherent risk, describe in detail the causal chain, and explore if the case studies affected or were affected by Indigenous communities.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case Study Description</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2500 to 3000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Thursday 20 Aug @ 11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Thursday 20 Aug @ 11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">For students to predict and avoid failures due to human factors, design flaws, materials failure and extreme conditions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students conduct a risk assessment to quantitatively verify the magnitude of the risk exposure in terms of deaths/injuries/damages/costs using recognised methods in one of the case studies prepared in the assessment task 1. Then, they explore different risk reduction options and select the best option(s) considering the time, cost, quality and scope constraints that have significant Impacts on the decision-making. All of these are presented through a scientific paper following a template and documentation style similar to that used in engineering journals.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case Study Risk Assessment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Essay</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6 to 8 pages in IEEE format</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Thursday 24 Sep @ 11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Thursday 24 Sep @ 11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">For students to apply different risk assessment techniques and explore and select risk treatment options.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students prepare a risk management plan in accordance with AS/NZS ISO 31000 for one of the case studies investigated in previous assessment tasks. Students need to:  Define the system boundaries carefully; Establish the context clearly in accordance with the standard; Clearly state the risk tolerability criteria employed; Show evidence of consideration of alternatives for risk management; Include a discussion; and Consider aspects beyond the texts and lecture material (i.e. value-added discussion).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case Study Risk Management Plan</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5500 to 6000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Sunday 25 Oct @ 11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">For students to apply risk management principles and processes conforming with AS/NZS ISO 31000 in an engineering environment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Sunday 25 Oct @ 11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students prepare a risk management plan in accordance with AS/NZS ISO 31000.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Risk Management Plan</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">3500 to 4000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">18/08/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 18 August 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are to demonstrate their capabilities to apply the risk management principles and process conforming with AS/NZS ISO 31000 in an engineering environment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The examination consists of a mix of questions requiring, for example, narrative, numerical or diagrammatic responses.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Risk Exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 hours</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">04/10/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday 4 October 2019              Mid-semester exam during the lecture time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Mid-semester exam during the lecture time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The exam assesses students’ level of attainment of the subject objectives in the risk assessment and risk management areas.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to prepare a journal paper based on the topics that will be provided. A template and documentation style similar to that used in engineering journals will be given.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Risk Paper</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Essay</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5000 to 6000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20/10/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 20 October 2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are to demonstrate their knowledge and understanding in the risk management area while communicating their outcomes by preparing a scientific paper in accordance with the standard required for publication in an academic journal. The purpose is to encourage students to have critical thinking, identify research questions, develop a research methodology applying risk management principles, implement the research methodology in an engineering system, analyse results, develop risk measures, and come up with new ideas behind the subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
   </Row>
   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49106</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Road Engineering Practice</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to complete a small road design problem by using Australian road design standard. The student is required to assess the extent of the task and determine a workable geometric design for a proposed rural or urban road. Appropriate Australian Standards are to be complied with, as well as well established road industry practices. Feedback of this assignment will be provided to students three weeks after the submission deadline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1: Geometric Design of Roads</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design/drawing/plan/sketch</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">03/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12.59pm Sunday 3 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to complete a small road pavement design problem by applying Australian design standards. The student is required to determine the extent of the task and design a sustainable ‘pavement section’ for either a rural or urban zone. Appropriate Australian Standards are to be complied with, as well as well established industry practices. Feedback of this assignment will be provided to students three weeks after the submission deadline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 2: Structural Design of Roads</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design/drawing/plan/sketch</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
