   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42043</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Robotics Studio 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quizzes set out to test the student’s knowledge of fundamentals of programming, sensing and control in an incremental manner and provide feedback to students throughout the session. In each quiz, students are provided with a programming stub (code base) that is designed to perform a set task. Students are required to rectify / further develop this code base to accomplish the set task. Submission of student code for assessment is via a GIT code repository. Further information, including guidance on how to obtain the code base, is available on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Review Quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Due Date Sunday 23:59 in the respective weeks Quiz 1: Week 3; Quiz 2: Week 4; Quiz 3: Week 5; Quiz 4: Week 6</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Due Date Sunday 23:59 in the respective weeks Quiz 1: Week 3; Quiz 2: Week 4; Quiz 3: Week 5; Quiz 4: Week 6</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Test the student’s knowledge of programming, sensing and control in an incremental manner. Provide feedback to students throughout the session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students create an Individual Learning Contract (ILC) and then have it agreed to by their academic mentor(s). The ILC will be created as a Portfolio, with a structured format and length requirements as noted in the template that will be provided. The ILC should describe the following: 1. Activities that will enable the student to gain the knowledge and skills that will enhance the student’s contribution to the Project/Prototype. 2. Activities that will enable the student to gain extra knowledge and skills that they nominate, and do not necessarily address the Project/Prototype. 3. The knowledge and/or skill that they have chosen to teach to their peers. Further information, including submission mechanism is available on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual Learning Contract Agreement</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">03/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Sunday 3 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Creation of an Individual Learning Contract allows students to identify and document their learning direction, and set goals for the session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students must submit evidence of their individual work completed throughout the session that demonstrates how they have met the goals articulated in the Individual Learning Contract (ILC). Students' work will be assessed against what was agreed in the ILC. The progress will be evaluated as a technical sprint (demonstration of development). This development is part of agreed activities in ILC and contributes to developing final project. Part of this includes teaching the class activity that was agreed in the Individual Learning Contract, delivered in Week 11 as per schedule on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual Learning Contract Finalisation</Data></Cell>
