    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Creation of an Individual Learning Contract allows students to identify and document their learning direction, and set goals for the session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Mid-Project Sprint: Week 8; Peer Teaching: Week 10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There are three parts to this task: 1. The working project must be demonstrated in class. 2. A presentation delivered in class that describes what was produced, including a demonstration. The length of the presentation will be typically 10 minutes. 3. A report on document wiki with timeline and activities, and a git history that documents the process mapped to capabilities produced. There must be a history of regular contributions from the proposal stage to delivery, that shows the progress over time. All students must be present in class for the final presentation/demonstration, and all students will provide an assessment of other students in class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Demonstration / Delivery</Data></Cell>
