    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">n/a</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class in       Practical Test 1: Week 3; Practical Test 2: Week 4; Practical Test 3: Week 6; Practical Test 4: Week 7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Practical Test 1: Week 3; Practical Test 2: Week 4; Practical Test 3: Week 6; Practical Test 4: Week 7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Test the student’s knowledge of programming, perception and planning in an incremental manner. Provide feedback to students throughout the session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students create an Individual Learning Contract (ILC) and then have it agreed to by their academic mentor(s). The ILC will be created as a Portfolio, with a structured format and length requirements as noted in the template that will be provided. The ILC should describe the following:  Activities that will enable the student to gain the knowledge and skills that will enhance the student’s contribution to the Project/Prototype. Activities that will enable the student to gain extra knowledge and skills that they nominate, and do not necessarily address the Project/Prototype. The knowledge and/or skill that they have chosen to teach to their peers. Further information, including submission mechanism is available on Canvas. Part of this includes teaching the class activity that was agreed in the Individual Learning Contract, delivered in Week 10 as per schedule on Canvas.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual Learning Contract</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
