    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Creation of an Individual Learning Contract allows students to identify and document their learning direction, and set goals for the session.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There are four parts to this task:  The project sprint: Students will do a short presentation in the class that shows the progress of the project as agreed in ILC. The working project must be demonstrated in class. A presentation delivered in class that describes what was produced, including a demonstration. The length of the presentation will be typically 15 minutes. A report on document wiki with timeline and activities, and a git history that documents the process mapped to capabilities produced. There must be a history of regular contributions from the proposal stage to delivery, that shows the progress over time.  All students must be present in class for the final presentation/demonstration, and all students will provide an assessment of other students in class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Sprint, Demonstration and Delivery</Data></Cell>
