   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">31277</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Routing and Switching Essentials</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This examination is an open-book assessment. Each student will be given two hours (plus 10 minutes reading time) to complete up to ten questions in writing. Some questions may contain sub-questions. All questions are based on the CISCO Netacad and lab material, and at least 50% of questions will be about the key concepts from each week. Students are permitted to bring any written or printed material, including textbooks. However, access to any digital resources including accessing the internet and calculators are not permitted.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Written Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment is to evaluate students' overall performance on concept understanding of achieving the subject learning objectives for this subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment consists of two components. The first component is Packet Tracer modelling and Troubleshooting. This includes building a Packet Tracer model according to given requirements and troubleshooting a given Packet Tracer model and identifying the problems. This part will be individually assessed. The second component, Implementation, is based on group work. Each group will be given a maximum of 40 minutes to implement according to given network specifications. Students are to build and troubleshoot the network, and demonstrate that their network meets all requirements. Students need to discuss internally to solve the whole task collaboratively. 80 percent of marks are awarded to items on which each student in a group is assessed individually.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Skills-based Assessment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">45</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The component 1: Packet Tracer Modelling and Troubleshooting will be assessed in class in Week 11. The component 2: Implementation will be assessed in class in Week 12.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The component 1: Packet Tracer Modelling and Troubleshooting will be assessed in class in Week 11. The component 2: Implementation will be assessed in class in Week 12.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment task evaluates students' hands-on skills using the overall technologies in this subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There are quizzes in class. Quiz 1 is about VLSM exercise and is weighted 5%. No alternative subnetting assessments will be scheduled for students who miss the class when this assessment is scheduled. You must be on time for this assessment. Quiz 2 is weighted 10% and will have a maximum of 20 minutes, and consist of questions from the relevant chapter(s).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 1: Week 4 in class; Quiz 2: Week 10 in class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This early session assessment is designed to give students early feedback so that they can adjust their learning strategy and improve their learning efficiency.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 1: Week 4 in class; Quiz 2: Week 10 in class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There are three (3) quiz tests scheduled near the end of the classes in weeks 3, 5, &amp; 7. These quiz tests are based on the chapter(s) for the week in which they are held and will be completed in the last 20 minutes of the tutorial class. Each quiz will have a duration of 10 minutes and consist of one or two questions from the relevant chapter(s).</Data></Cell>
