   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48541</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Signal Theory</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The lab is ether pass/fail which means you either receive the full allocation mark or 0%. If you have made a serious attempt of the assignment but it is unsatisfactory, you will be offered feedback and an opportunity for re-submission without penalty. Labs are carried out in groups of three; however, each person must submit their own report. There is pre-work associated with labs 2 and 3. Pre-work must be completed prior to attending a lab session in order to be able to understand the lab and complete it successfully. If the pre-work is not completed before the lab session begins, you will be asked to leave and complete the lab in your own time. All lab reports are to contain the following three components:  The pre-work for the lab (except lab 1); Results obtained during the lab; Answers to the questions in the lab.  Please refer to the additional general information regarding the labs and submissions requirements on UTSOnline (please note you can lose marks if these are not followed.)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
