   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48433</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Software Architecture</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Watch the lecture, complete the quiz. Lectures and related material are provided online so that students can study the material at a time that suits them. A quiz is provided for each topic to enable students to check their progress toward mastering the topic.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Required topics quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each quiz is due before the start of the tutorial for its topic.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each quiz is due before the start of the tutorial for its topic.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstrate comprehension of the topic.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment task encourages students to engage and learn the subject progressively. To engage in tutorial discussions effectively students need to demonstrate their understanding of the topic by answering a quiz on the relevant topic.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There are four specialised software architectures suited to particular problems. Choose any two of them, study them, then answer their respective quizzes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Elective topic quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              The chosen quizzes must be completed by 6 PM on Friday the 30 October 2020.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The chosen quizzes must be completed by 6 PM on Friday the 30 October 2020.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Knowledge and understanding of the selected topic</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment task encourages students to study, understand and apply the means of developing specialised software architectures.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The project is a group assignment to be completed in small teams. You are expected to develop a software architecture for a non-trivial system using the techniques learned in this subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Team project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">35</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              The final report must be submitted by Friday the 30 October 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The architectural context reflects an understanding of the problem and its stakeholders. The developed architecture provides the required functionality and meets its quality objectives. Rationales for architectural decisions and preferred alternatives are credible. An individual reflective journal provides the weekly entries throughout the assignment to record your reflection on the learning journey.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Work in a team to develop an architecture for a specific system in a given context.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The final report must be submitted by Friday the 30 October 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each group will present their work in progress to another group for their review and critique. Reviews are completed using a review form (currently Google forms) and submitted on completion. Peer reviews are conducted in the tutorial room.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Peer review</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Peer reviews will be completed during the tutorial for each week of the major project. Reviews must be completed on the same day of the presentation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Peer reviews will be completed during the tutorial for each week of the major project. Reviews must be completed on the same day of the presentation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Observations and suggestions are well informed and impartial. Observations and suggestions are intended to improve the work.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Develop and practice the professional skill of reviewing and critiquing the work of peers.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstrate your knowledge of software and ability to apply it to a range of problems in both general and specialised domains. The final exam will contain both multiple-choice questions and subjective scenario-based descriptive questions. No supplementary exam will be given in this subject. If you miss any assessment through documented illness or misadventure, you should consult the subject coordinator.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period              This will be an open book exam.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This will be an open book exam.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstrate adequate knowledge of software architecture. Solve a given software architecture problem. Evaluate a given architecture in its context. Apply software architecture principles in a specialised domain.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assess a student's knowledge of software architecture and to apply that knowledge to a given problem.</Data></Cell>
