   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41113</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Software Development Studio 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The task for students is to demonstrate communication and collaboration skills as assessed by their peers via SparkPLUS , the ability to give feedback to other team members via SparkPLUS and to reflect on teamwork over the semester, notably how they think they have improved their communication and collaboration with examples, written in their journal. Note: There is a separate assessment document (available at the beginning of each semester) which gives fuller details for each assessment task.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Teamwork assessment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">08/11/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:55 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.55pm Sunday 8 November 2020              NB there are 3 different deliverables for Assessment Task 1; the first deliverable is optional:      • 1. SparkPLUS teamwork, formative evaluation - opens Mon 7th September 2020 (due Sun 13th September 2020, 11:55pm);  • 2. SparkPLUS teamwork, final evaluation - opens Mon 2nd November 2020 (due Sun 8th November 2020, 11:55pm); and  • 3. Overall reflection on teamwork - submit as final entry in reflection journal on Confluence  (due Sun 8th November 2020, 11:55pm).See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">NB there are 3 different deliverables for Assessment Task 1; the first deliverable is optional:      • 1. SparkPLUS teamwork, formative evaluation - opens Mon 7th September 2020 (due Sun 13th September 2020, 11:55pm);  • 2. SparkPLUS teamwork, final evaluation - opens Mon 2nd November 2020 (due Sun 8th November 2020, 11:55pm); and  • 3. Overall reflection on teamwork - submit as final entry in reflection journal on Confluence  (due Sun 8th November 2020, 11:55pm).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this task is for students to understand how well they are operating in a team.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The task for students is: to demonstrate critical reflection expressed as high level competence in their personal reflection journal, and, to demonstrate building design reflection capability in their weekly design reflection journals.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflective ability assessment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25/10/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:55 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.55pm Sunday 25 October 2020              NB there are 3 different deliverables for Assessment Task 2; the first deliverable is optional:      • 1.  Personal reflections, formative evaluation (due Sun 13th September 2020, 11:55pm;     • 2.  Personal reflections (due Sun 25th October 2020, 11:55pm); and      • 3.  Design Journal (due Sun 25th October 2020, 11:55pm).      Personal reflections are submitted as entries in student’s Reflection Journal on Confluence, and Design reflections are submitted as entries in student’s Design Journal on Confluence.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">NB there are 3 different deliverables for Assessment Task 2; the first deliverable is optional:      • 1.  Personal reflections, formative evaluation (due Sun 13th September 2020, 11:55pm;     • 2.  Personal reflections (due Sun 25th October 2020, 11:55pm); and      • 3.  Design Journal (due Sun 25th October 2020, 11:55pm).      Personal reflections are submitted as entries in student’s Reflection Journal on Confluence, and Design reflections are submitted as entries in student’s Design Journal on Confluence.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this task is to evaluate how well students are learning to reflect.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The task for students is to demonstrate:  how they are learning about process and what they are learning about process, and by showing their contributions to process.   This will be done by recording decisions and actions using the tools Jira and Confluence on a weekly basis.  Note: There is a separate Assessment document (available at the beginning of each semester) which gives fuller details for each assessment task.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Process assessment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11/11/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:55 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.55pm Wednesday 11 November 2020              Submission is the collection of the team's weekly project management and process entries in the online Jira and Confluence tools, and  the team's MS-Teams channel.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this task is to learn to make and record process decisions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submission is the collection of the team's weekly project management and process entries in the online Jira and Confluence tools, and  the team's MS-Teams channel.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The task for students is to demonstrate that the client is satisfied, the outcomes specified for the project description have been achieved, and the product performs as expected. This will be done via team demonstration of their product at the end of the semester.  Note: There is a separate Assessment document (available at the beginning of each semester) which gives fuller details for each assessment task.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Product assessment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">04/11/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Wednesday 4 November 2020              Demonstration of product will be during usual Wednesday SDS sessions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstration of product will be during usual Wednesday SDS sessions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this task is to learn how to build requirements and assess against those requirements.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
