    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25/10/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:55 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.55pm Sunday 25 October 2020              NB there are 3 different deliverables for  Assessment Task 2; the first deliverable is optional:      • 1.  Personal reflections, formative evaluation (due Sun 13th September 2020, 11:55pm;     • 2.  Personal reflections (due Sun 25th October 2020, 11:55pm); and      • 3.  Design Journal (due Sun 25th October 2020, 11:55pm).       Personal reflections are submitted as entries in student’s Reflection Journal on Confluence, and Design reflections are submitted as entries in student’s Design  Journal on ConfluenceSee also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">NB there are 3 different deliverables for  Assessment Task 2; the first deliverable is optional:      • 1.  Personal reflections, formative evaluation (due Sun 13th September 2020, 11:55pm;     • 2.  Personal reflections (due Sun 25th October 2020, 11:55pm); and      • 3.  Design Journal (due Sun 25th October 2020, 11:55pm).       Personal reflections are submitted as entries in student’s Reflection Journal on Confluence, and Design reflections are submitted as entries in student’s Design  Journal on Confluence</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The purpose of this task is to evaluate how well students are learning to reflect.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The task for students is to demonstrate how they are learning about process and what they are learning about process, and by showing their contributions to process. This will be done by recording decisions and actions using the tools Jira and Confluence on a weekly basis. In addition, students are required to write a critical evaluation of some aspect of process, based on a literature review and governed by a learning contract.  Note: There is a separate Assignment document (available at the beginning of each semester) which gives fuller details for each assessment task.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Process assessment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
