   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48440</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Software Engineering Practice</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment task will require a team of 4-6 students to analyse the assigned Agile Project Case Study problem; and produce, submit and present a group report containing  agile plan; software requirements specifications; and agile architecture (description and software prototype)  The deliverables of this assessment task also includes an oral/visual group report and prototype presentation (no PowerPoint slides), and individual contribution logbooks - as per Subject Weekly Schedule. Students may choose to work in a lab or from home. The additional information about the Agile Project Case Study and assessment tasks will be provided in the project brief. To pass this subject, the students must complete and submit this assessment task. To pass this task, the individual must earn &gt;= net 50% marks for the task.   SEP is a project-based subject to be completed in small teams or groups. Each student group will work as a small startup company. This is a practical subject and students should have familiarity with programming. In this subject, students will be dealing with all phases of a software intensive agile project life cycle. To make the Major Assignment:    Assessment Item 1 is the agile planning, analysis and architecture deliverable with individual contribution logbook; and Assessment Item 2 is the agile design, implementation and testing deliverable with individual contribution logbook.   There are two (2) compulsory agile project showcases or review sessions for Assessment Items 1-2 (see Subject Weekly Schedule):  Assessment Item 1 Review; and Assessment Item 2 Review.   Any individual student who failed to appear in these compulsory assignment assessment and review sessions (Showcase) will receive zero (0) as a final individual mark. See UTSOnline for additional guidelines.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project - Agile Planning, Analysis and Architecture</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There is no word limit.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 6              The submission deadline for Assignment 1 is due by 6 PM on Monday the 27th August 2018.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The submission deadline for Assignment 1 is due by 6 PM on Monday the 27th August 2018.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A more detailed marking scheme will be issued with the assignment guidelines.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment task will require a team of 4-6 students to produce, submit and present a group report, working software and individual contribution logbooks. Based on the agile plan, requirements and architecture (submitted for Assessment Items 1), each group shall  develop the software system design; implement the software system design; and prepare, submit and present a report that includes the description of major software system features, non-functional aspects, and software testing results with executed tests and defect log.  The deliverables of this assessment task also includes updated agile plan, an oral/visual presentation (no PowerPoint slides) of the implemented working system, individual contribution logbooks and working software code implemented - as per Subject Weekly Schedule. Each group shall explore different ways of ensuring quality outcomes through the agile development and testing approach. This can be supported through a set of software development and testing tools. To pass this subject, the students must complete and submit this assessment task. To pass this task, the individual must earn &gt;= net 50% marks for the task. Each student in a team is required to participate in all the roles (e.g. business analyst, developer, tester) and tasks associated with the required deliverables (e.g. agile requirements anlysis, planning, architecture, design, implementation and testing). See UTS Online for further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project - Agile Design, Implementation and Testing</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">60</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There is no word limit.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              The submission deadline for Assignment 2 is due by 6 PM on Monday the 15 October 2018See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The submission deadline for Assignment 2 is due by 6 PM on Monday the 15 October 2018</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">It includes 2 pre-workshop quizzes/tests (complete before the scheduled workshop session) and 2 in-workshop individual quizzes (of about maximum 20 minutes each, held as the first part of the workshop session). The quizzes shall measure the degree that the theory, as taught by the subject and practised by the individual in each of the phases of the project, is understood by each individual. No quiz submissions are allowed after the deadline. No makeup quizzes are allowed. Attendance at all workshop sessions is required. To pass this task, the individual must earn &gt;= net 50% marks for the task.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Short Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There is no word limit.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Not applicable</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Not applicable; see Further information</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment item will be marked according to how well the students demonstrate their critical and reflective thinking skills, in quizzes in the context of the discipline, established theory and project work.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment task will require a team of 4-6 students to produce, submit and present a group report and individual contribution logbooks. Base on an assigned problem statement, agile project software requirements specifications and a software development plan as per Assessment Item 1, each group shall prepare, submit and present a report that includes  agile software solution architecture and design; and updated agile software requirements specifications and software development plan.  The deliverables of this assessment task also includes an oral/visual group report presentation (no PowerPoint slides) and individual contribution logbooks - as per Subject Weekly Schedule. To pass this subject, the students must complete and submit this assessment task. To pass this task, the individual must earn &gt;= net 50% marks for the task.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There is no word limit.</Data></Cell>
