   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49133</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Steel and Composite Design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In this task, you will work together as a group in the form of a seminar discussion, but this task will be submitted and marked individually. The first submission of the major design project relates to topics covered in weeks 1-4. For this submission, students complete the following tasks:  Determine required dead loads (for the floors and walls), live loads (AS 1170.1-2002) and wind loads parameters (AS 1170.2-2011); Create a 3D model of the building in SAP2000; Apply all the determined loads (actions) to the 3D model; Run the structural analysis in SAP2000; Check the validity of the structural model using hand calculation methods (disused in the first lecture); Carry out steel design and design optimisation in SAP2000; Check the inter-story drifts for the moment resisting frame based on Clause 2.3.2 of AS3600-2009.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Major Design Project - First Submission</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">31/08/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12.00am Monday 31 August 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In this task, you will work together as a group in the form of a seminar discussion, but this task will be submitted and marked individually. The second submission of the major design project relates to topics covered in weeks 5-9. For this submission, students are supposed to design all the steel connections including beam-column connections, bracing connections and baseplates for the steel building that they designed using SAP2000 software and present the hand calculations in an organised design report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Major Design Project - Second Submission</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">28/09/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12.00am Monday 28 September 2020              Refer to class schedule posted on UTSOnline under Subject Information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Refer to class schedule posted on UTSOnline under Subject Information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The third submission of the major design project relates to topics covered in weeks 5-11. For this submission, students complete the following tasks:  Design the composite floors; Prepare a comprehensive design report covering the entire building design; Produce construction detail drawings for all the structural components; and Orally present design outcomes to professional and non-professional clients.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Major Design Project - Third Submission</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12/10/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12:00 AM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12.00am Monday 12 October 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Open book. Each student is responsible for ensuring that s/he has a calculator and the relevant codes, Steel Section Handbook relevant excerpts, as well as whatever reference material s/he chooses to bring in. Topics: Design of simple (web side plate and flexible end plate) and rigid (bolted moment end plate to column) connections and design of steel composite slabs and beams.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Three (3) hours.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Centrally conducted Exam: Date tba when Exams Branch publishes the Exam schedule.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Centrally conducted Exam: Date tba when Exams Branch publishes the Exam schedule.</Data></Cell>
