   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32562</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Strategic Business Management</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Inquisitive and critical questioning of the lecture contents/issues, and contribute work-based experience on the same issue.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Class contributions</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">01/11/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday 1 November 2019              At the end of the course</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">At the end of the course</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The research assignment Part 1 report consists of a critical strategic gap analysis of your company/organization. The report must be produced in a professional manner (including a table of contents with page number, a coherent executive summary, with a coherently organized and appropriately titled sections, and a compelling conclusion section. Word count on cover page. Arial 11 font with1.5 spacing.) Part 1 Objective(s): The student is to document a critical case-study analysis of their organization’s current business strategy and current strategic management processes and practices and current business model from the perspective of customer value creation. The student is required to engage and interview their organization's executive leaders to make this a practice-based assignment. Interview data should be documented in an appendix of the assignment report (not included in the word-count limits). Part 1 Task: The documentation (3000 words) required for assignment part 1 includes the following: 1. Analyze your organization’s business: vision/mission/values, industry, markets and customers. 2. Define what the term “value creation” means from the perspectives of customers, and the organization’s vision/mission and strategy. 3. Analyze and define your company’s current strategies (position, resource, knowledge &amp; capabilities) and strategic management process – assess its effectiveness in monitoring, tracking of value creation and alignment with the market and technological dynamics:  External competitive environments analysis Internal (resource/capabilities-based) analysis • Analysis of current strategy – does it match the above analyses? Analysis of organizational performance (financial and non-financial) – does it meet the strategic objectives? Analysis of your firm’s innovation capabilities (dynamic capabilities &amp; absorptive capacity)  4. Analyze your firm’s current business model using business model canvas – how distinctive (and integrative) it is and what are its weaknesses in light of the changing market and technological environments? 5. What strategic issues (gaps) have you identified – why do they exist and what are their implications? 6. Document company executives interview data in an appendix as evidence of practice-based analysis (outside word-count limits).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Part 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Part 1 soft copy due by email on 13 September at 11pm.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Part 1 soft copy due by email on 13 September at 11pm.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The report must be produced in a professional manner (including a table of contents with page number, a coherent executive summary, with a coherently organized and appropriately titled sections, and a compelling conclusion section. Word count on cover page. Arial 11 font with1.5 spacing.) Task: Part 2 Objective(s): From the insightful strategic analysis of Part 1, the student is required in Part 2 to: (a) recommend strategic options to resolve the strategic issues and close the strategic gaps identified in Part 1; (b) propose an enhanced, innovation-based strategy and the associated new business model(s) to sustain the firm’s competitive advantage; and (c) propose the requisite (new) strategic leadership capabilities and organizational practices to execute the innovation-based strategy. The student is required to engage and interview their organization's executive leaders to gain critical feedback on their proposed new strategy and business model for the case-study company/organization. Interview data should be documented in an appendix of the assignment report (not included in the word-count limits). Part 2 Tasks: The documentation (4500 words) required for assignment part 2 includes the following:  Explore and recommend strategic options to resolve the strategic issues (gaps) identified in Part 1; Propose an enhanced, innovation-oriented strategy and the associated NEW business model (justify and highlight its distinctiveness and how its constituent parts are integrated) to sustain your firm’s competitive advantage – clearly articulate/justify their alignment and the resultant sustainable advantage; Explore and propose ways, with justifications by citing the relevant literature, by which your firm could be transformed into an appropriate ambidextrous organization capable of pursuing both exploitative and exploratory innovations simultaneously:   Organizational designs, Choice – differentiation vs. integration vs. contextual? Why? Strategic leadership capabilities and practices, including managing conflicting tensions / risks, governance and incentive systems, organizational culture transformation, organizational capabilities growth  4. Document company executives interview data in an appendix as evidence of practice-based analysis (not included in the word-count limits).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Part 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">45</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Part 2 soft copy of Part 2 assignment report due by email on November 1 at 9am.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Part 2 soft copy of Part 2 assignment report due by email on November 1 at 9am.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation Task: Each student is required to present their organization’s strategic analysis of current state (per Part 1 outcomes) and the proposed new strategies, new business model, the requisite new organizational designs and leadership practices in order to effectively execute the new innovation-oriented business strategy (per Part 2 outcomes). Each presentation must finish within the allotted time (to be advised). Presentation PPT softcopy is due on Oct 27 at 7pm and hardcopy on Oct 28 at 9am.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual Project Presentation</Data></Cell>
