   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42016</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Strategic Finance</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Format: Presentation and Executive Summary Submission   The aim of the assignment is for the participants to apply their learning and insight from the first 3 weeks of the course in evaluating the performance of relevant ASX listed Technology Company based on the information contained in their annual financial statements.   You are then required to make recommendations as to whether you feel it would be advisable to invest in the company that you have evaluated and make recommendations for improving the performance of the company to their management team.   During the first session your groups will be allocated and you will be given a specific company or group of companies to evaluate.   Use ratios and any other relevant evaluation tools to perform an in-depth evaluation on the performance of the company in the most recent financial year. In order to make your evaluation meaningful you will need to compare the performance in the current year to the prior year performance or the performance of competitors   Your analysis should attempt to highlight the strengths and weaknesses of the company’s financial performance and position.   Make recommendations to management for improving the performance of the company and also conclude on whether this company would be a suitable investment for shareholders.   The deliverables will be a 10 minute PowerPoint presentation and a one page executive summary of ratios and recommendations, due in class on Monday 10 April.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Assignment 1 - Financial Analysis of ASX Listed Companies</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10-minute presentaion and one-page report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10/04/2017</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6.00pm Monday 10 April 2017              In Class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In Class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Marking Guide  Financial calculations and analysis Application of financial concepts Answering the question Quality of the report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Financial Analysis of ASX Listed Companies</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Format: Group Report   You will be provided with a case study on Flash Memory, a small technology business that specializes in the design and manufacture of solid state drives (SSDs) and memory modules for the computer and electronics industries.   You will be assisting the executives of Flash Memory in preparing the company's investing and financing plans for the next three years. The company invests aggressively in research and development of new products to stay ahead of the competition. Increased working capital requirements are forcing the CFO to consider alternatives for additional financing. In addition, you must also consider an investment opportunity in a new product line that has the potential to be extremely profitable.   You will need to prepare financial forecasts, calculate the weighted average cost of capital (WACC), estimate cash flows, and evaluate financing alternatives.   You will be required to hand in a brief report of a maximum of 5 pages with your recommendations. You may include an appendix with any financial information.   The report will be due in class on Tuesday 31 May.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Assignment 2 - Flash Memory Case Study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Maximum 5 page report. An appendix with any financial information may be included.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">29/05/2017</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6.00pm Monday 29 May 2017              In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Preparation of Financial Forecasts Calculation of Weighted Average Cost of Capital Net Present Value and New Product Line Analysis Modifying the Financial Forecasts for the New Product Line Selecting the Financial Plan Presentation of the Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment requires your group to apply all the concepts covered in the course in an integrated, real life case study. Your group will be assisting the executives of Flash Memory in preparing the company's investing and financing plans for the next three years. The intent of the assignment is to allow you to apply the concepts of working capital management, forecasting, cost of capital, investment analysis, valuation and decision making in a technology business.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Format:  Report   The final assignment is an individual submission of a short report covering the practical application of concepts covered during the course.   Select a company of interest to you (your employer, your own business, a company you are interested in working for or investing in). Make sure you have access to their financial statements and are able to gain insight into their strategy (for private businesses it will need to be a business where you have access to the directors, ie your employer and for public companies you can utilise the annual report).   Review the historic financial statements (3 years) and calculate any financial ratios necessary to diagnose the performance and position of the business.   What are the value drivers for this business?   How do the financial ratios compare to the strategy and industry positioning of the business?   Does the business manage its working capital well?   Benchmark ratios against industry peers and comment on your findings   How is the business funded? What is the capital structure of the business and do you think it is appropriate? What do you estimate as the cost of capital for this business?   What has been the historic revenue growth levels of the business? How does this compare to the sustainable growth rate? What insights does this provide?   Based on your historic financial analysis, document a SWOT analysis of your chosen company.   Perform a high level 3 year forecast of an abbreviated income statement and balance sheet. What assumptions are you using and why? What does your forecast reveal about the future funding needs of the business?   Perform a high level valuation of the business. State your assumptions used to forecast free cash flow for next 3 to 5 years. What are your assumptions about long term growth and the terminal value?   Finally, provide a brief set of strategic recommendations to increase the long term value of this business.   Your report should be no longer than 8 typed pages with any financial calculations in an appendix.   Your assignment must be emailed to andrewabdo@gmail.com by no later than 15 June 2016.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 3 - Practical Application</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">60</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Maximum 8 page report (with financial calculations appended)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11/06/2017</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:45 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.45pm Sunday 11 June 2017</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Financial statement and ratio analysis Identification of value drivers Analysis of funding and cost of capital Forecasting Valuation Recommendations</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment requires students to apply the strategic finance tools covered in the course to their current business (employer, client or entrepreneurial business).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Format: Individual assignment report A complete financial analysis of your company</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5 to 10 pages</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Post week 10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Post week 10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment of your company strategy and competitive position Complete financial analysis of your company’s performance Competitive benchmarking Recommendations to enhance value</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment gives you the opportunity to apply financial concepts to your organisation. It will test your ability to apply strategic finance to a technology business by assessing the financial performance of your company against its peers.</Data></Cell>
