    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment consists of 3 parts: Part A - Requirements Analysis and Individual SWOT (Individual). Each member of the group is to provide a requirements analysis document in relation to the provided case study and an individual SWOT analysis. Part B - Group SWOT Analysis and Final Report Allocations (Group). Specific details regarding the assignment may be found in the assignment sheet for Assignment 1 on UTS Online. Templates for parts A and B can be found on UTS Online. Submissions not using the relevant template will not be accepted.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1 (Individual and Group) - Research and Requirements Gathering</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Part A - 2 to 3 pages for Requirements Analysis and 1 page for SWOT (Individual) Part B - 5 pages for the completed templates for the team SWOT and report allocations (Group)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">18/08/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6.00pm Tuesday 18 August 2020              A DRAFT soft copy of the individual Part A (Requirements Analysis) should be ready for your meeting with your tutor and your other team members to reviewin Week 3. The final submission of all parts (Parts A and B) are to be submitted soft copy to your tutor by the set time and date in Week 4. The submission should be as attachments in one email to your tutor's UTS email account and cc'd to the subject coordinator (rene.leveaux@uts.edu.au)See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A DRAFT soft copy of the individual Part A (Requirements Analysis) should be ready for your meeting with your tutor and your other team members to reviewin Week 3. The final submission of all parts (Parts A and B) are to be submitted soft copy to your tutor by the set time and date in Week 4. The submission should be as attachments in one email to your tutor's UTS email account and cc'd to the subject coordinator (rene.leveaux@uts.edu.au)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each team will be required to provide a conceptual design document outlining the team's initial thoughts and ideas on their proposed design of an innovative solution in relation to a case study for consideration by the client. The submission would be supported with appropriate diagrams, which may include Entity Relationship Diagrams, Data Flow Diagrams, UML, etc. A template for this task may be found on UTS Online.Submissions not using the relevant template will not be accepted.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 2 (Group) - Initial Design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">8 to 10 pages as per assignment sheet (team total)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">01/09/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6.00pm Tuesday 1 September 2020              The submission is to be soft copy to your tutor by the set time and date in Week 6. The submission should be as an attachment in one email to your tutor's UTS email account and cc'd to the subject coordinator (rene.leveaux@uts.edu.au)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The submission is to be soft copy to your tutor by the set time and date in Week 6. The submission should be as an attachment in one email to your tutor's UTS email account and cc'd to the subject coordinator (rene.leveaux@uts.edu.au)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each team will be allocated a tutor who will also act as the client’s representative, and as such, will be the team’s contact point with the client organization. The tutor will also monitor the team's progress and will supply any additional relevant data or opinions on the operation or needs of the user community. The tutor will also act as a 'sounding board' on problems and provide relevant advice as needed. Your tutor will, where appropriate, give feedback and guidance to the group during the meetings; however, the the selection of various components, etc, for the solution will be the responsibility of the group, as the group will, in essence, be acting as a team of specialist IT solutions providers. Students will work in a project group in the role of a team of consultants engaged to develop an information systems strategy in response to a proposal request. Based on the given materials and additional research, the group will be required to work as a project team to develop a proposal for the design and delivery of a medium to large scale state-of-the-art IT / IS solution to a (hypothetical) current day situation. The submission in the form a of a final report and an industry level presentations/pitch. 1. Presentation / Pitch -Your presentation / pitch will be during set times established as per the assignment sheet. The soft copy of your presentation slides and materials will also be due at the same time. Submission is via an email attachment to the subject coordinator at rene.leveaux@uts.edu.au 2. Final Report -The report should be to the level of an industry based response to the request for a proposal, with approximately 35 to 50 pages of content in the body of the report. Accordingly, it is expected that the document will be concised but yet be of sufficient depth and address both the relevant IT / IS components and including the provision of the management processes for the delivery of the solution to the client, including Gantt charts, etc. The document should present what yout team is offering the client in the solution rather than a collections of definitions, etc. The relevant components of the report will be allocated amongst the team members by the members of the team. The assessment of both the report and presentation / pitch will be of similar standard to that of industry. Assessment will besolely on the contents of the submitted report and the presentation / pitch. A template for the report is provided on UTS Online and must be used. Reports submitted, not using the provided template, will not be accepted. Submission is to be in both hard copy and soft copy. Any hard copy submission submitted in loose leaf form will NOT be accepted. 3. Peer Assessment - Each individual member of the team will be required to assess each member of the their team (including themselves) as per the assignment sheet. 4. Final report allocations - Each team must additonally also provide an updated team allocations for the final report. Assessment for this assignment is both Individual and group. A breakdown of the marks is indicated on the assignment sheet.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 3 (Individual and Group) - Final Report and Presentation/Pitch</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">65</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report: The length of the body of the final report would be approximately 35 to 50 pages. Presentation / Pitch: 10 minute industry pitch followed by a 10 to 15 minutes Q &amp; A period.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week range</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 11 to Week 12              NOTE: The report submission (week 11 - 6pm Tuesday 13 October 2020) is in soft copy ONLY - no hard copy submission is required. The following week the second component of the submission is due (week 12 - 6pm 20 October 2020) - video or poster. Each team elects to submit either an industry level video or poster. A milestone submission of the draft of your teams report is due in week 8 - details of this submission can be found in the assignment sheet. The soft copy submission should be submitted as an email attachment to the subject coordinator at rene.leveaux@uts.edu.au and cc'd to your tutor at your tutor's UTS email address. Full details may be found in the assignment sheet.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">NOTE: The report submission (week 11 - 6pm Tuesday 13 October 2020) is in soft copy ONLY - no hard copy submission is required. The following week the second component of the submission is due (week 12 - 6pm 20 October 2020) - video or poster. Each team elects to submit either an industry level video or poster. A milestone submission of the draft of your teams report is due in week 8 - details of this submission can be found in the assignment sheet. The soft copy submission should be submitted as an email attachment to the subject coordinator at rene.leveaux@uts.edu.au and cc'd to your tutor at your tutor's UTS email address. Full details may be found in the assignment sheet.</Data></Cell>
