   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41150</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Summer Studio A</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A portfolio depicts an individual learning journey within the studio. Each student will develop a portfolio. It can be in the format of your choice. You can build on an existing portfolio if you have one or develop a new one. You can use the UTSOnline portfolio tool or develop you own (E.g. Weebly, WordPress site). Begin with an introduction to yourself, a photo and a description of what motivated you to take the studio subject and what you hope to get out of it. For each of the subject’s 5 learning objectives, provide artefacts and a reflective statement or justification that demonstrates (or proves) your achievement. Artefacts can include (but are not restricted to) documents and presentations; interview questions, records of discussions, sketches, plans, prototypes (or photos of), commentary on research articles. Each artefact needs to be accompanied by an explanation and a reflection of what learning you achieved. Achievement of each learning objective must be substantiated with a minimum of 2 artefacts, each with a reflective statement. A summative reflective statement is also included as a way for you to summarise what you have learnt and how these skills might transfer to career opportunities.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">100</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Gateway Sprint 1 Thursday 01/02/2018 in class 2.00pm Gateway Sprint 2 Thursday 15/02/2018 in class 2.00pm Gateway Sprint 3 complete submission Thursday 01/03/2018, 10.00am</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Gateway Sprint 1 Thursday 01/02/2018 in class 2.00pm Gateway Sprint 2 Thursday 15/02/2018 in class 2.00pm Gateway Sprint 3 complete submission Thursday 01/03/2018, 10.00am</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Performance statement/Criteria - Pass • Introduction is included with photo and statement of motivation to take studio subject. • Online or ePortfolio articulates achievement of each of the subject’s five learning objectives. • Each objective is substantiated by relevant, quality artefacts (such as project documentation, prototypes, records of discussions etc.) • Each objective is accompanied by a reflective statement indicating the ways in which the learning was achieved. The reflective statements are each clearly articulated, demonstrate high degrees of engagement in studio learning. • Portfolio is presented professionally, with no or few errors, is complete and comprehensive. Performance statement/Criteria - Not yet pass (Fail) • Introduction is not included, incomplete or lacks coherence. • Online or ePortfolio does not address all five of the subject learning objectives. • Some or all artefacts are not included, incomplete or irrelevant. • Reflective statements are either not included, incomplete or lack coherence.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">For students to demonstrate their achievement of each of the subject learning objectives using a collection of artefacts together with reflection.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
