   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41151</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Summer Studio B</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A Design Portfolio depicts a curated individual learning journey within the Summer Studio. Each student will develop a Design Portfolio. The Design Portfolio may be an electronic portfolio or ePortfolio in the format of student’s own choice. Students can build on an existing portfolio if they have one or develop a new one. Students can use the UTSOnline ePortfolio tool or develop their own using other platforms (e.g. Weebly, WordPress). The Design Portfolio should begin with an introduction to yourself, a photo and a description of what motivated you to take the studio subject and what you hope to get out of it (e.g. your objectives). In the first week, this should be expanded into your learning contract: what do you intend to achieve through the project, including learning goals and tasks to be completed. The Design Portfolio should end with a final reflection that synthesises your development and achievement of the subject learning outcomes throughout the Summer Studio journey. The Design Portfolio will be assessed at the end of each sprint.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design Portfolio (4 submissions)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">100</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submission 1 (Sprint 1): Sunday 10/02/2019, 11:00 pm; Submission 2 (Sprint 2): Sunday 17/02/2019, 11:00 pm; Submission 3 (Sprint 3): Sunday 24/02/2019, 11:00 pm; Submission 4 (Sprint 4): Monday 04/03/2019, 9:00 am</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submission 1 (Sprint 1): Sunday 10/02/2019, 11:00 pm; Submission 2 (Sprint 2): Sunday 17/02/2019, 11:00 pm; Submission 3 (Sprint 3): Sunday 24/02/2019, 11:00 pm; Submission 4 (Sprint 4): Monday 04/03/2019, 9:00 am</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Performance standard to Pass The Design Portfolio must include sufficient evidence to demonstrate development and (final) achievement of the SLOs. The Design Portfolio must be a professional presentation, with no or few errors (e.g. spelling, grammar, formatting, accessibility). It must be complete and comprehensive.   Submission 1 must contain:   An introduction with photo and statement of motivation to take the studio subject and objectives in taking the subject.   Your learning contract: what do you intend to achieve through the project, including learning goals and tasks to be completed. What will be your contribution to the group effort? What will you learn in that process? What will you produce? You may revise this in subsequent submissions.     Submissions 1 through 4 of the Design Portfolio must contain:   Curated artefacts (at least 2 per submission) which illustrates your engagement and development at each sprint and across the subject’s five Subject Learning Objectives.   Reflective statements which clearly articulate and demonstrate engagement with all studio teaching and learning activities (including evaluation and/or incorporation of expert, facilitator, and peer feedback, and provision of thoughtful, informed feedback to peers, including systematic group progress review each week).     By Submission 4 the Design Portfolio must contain:   A conclusion articulating how your learning journey has enabled you to meet or redefine your objectives.   A final reflective statement that synthesises your learning journey. Each subject learning objective is addressed in the final reflective statement indicating the ways in which the learning was achieved.   Reflectively curated, relevant artefacts that form a coherent and cumulative substantiation of claims of achievement of the subject’s five Subject Learning Objectives.     Performance statement/Criteria – Not yet pass (Fail)   Introduction is not included, incomplete or lacks coherence.   Design Portfolio does not address all five of the Subject Learning Objectives.   Artefacts are missing. Some artefacts are not included, incomplete or irrelevant.   A collection of artefacts is presented but lacks coherence or a compelling illustration of engagement across the Subject Learning Objectives.   Reflective statements are either not included, incomplete, lack coherence or are not substantiated by artefacts.   Reflective statements indicate little or no engagement with formative and/or other feedback provided.   Peer review is not demonstrated at the end of each sprint.   Self-evaluation is not demonstrated at the end of each sprint.   Submissions during sprints 1 through 4 of the Design Portfolio do not contain: Evidence of development of the design process and how learning has evolved at each stage.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">For students to demonstrate their achievement of each of the Subject Learning Objectives using a collection of artefacts together with reflections that meet the pass performance criteria.</Data></Cell>
