    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are encouraged to proactively engage with the subject material, class discussions, and activities. Regular attendance, punctuality, and a considered and respectful approach and constructive contributions to ideas proposed are essential. Students will also be allocated a topic to present on to coincide with a particular lecture.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Class Participation (Individual)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Not applicable</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Not applicable</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Regular and punctual attendance Active class participation Constrictive contribution to class discussions Effective and engaging presentations</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The students will be individually required to carry out a literature search and review to identify a contemporary sustainability issue. The student needs to identify the sustainability challenges, the stakeholders involved, along with a review of academic and professional literature relating to these challenges.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case Study Analysis Report (Individual)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Between 1800 and 2500 Words.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">01/09/2014</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">06:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6.00pm Monday 1 September 2014</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Relevant research undertaken Identify and articulate substantial sustainability challenge(s) Identify stakeholders and their needs Demonstrate a multidimensional perspective to sustainability</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A group of students will evaluate the individual case studies submitted by the group members in item 2 above, select a single case, and formulate broad-based recommendations to comprehensive address sustainability challenges presented from a multidimensional perspective. A report of such recommendations must be rigorously supported by evidence from evolving practise and academic and professional literature (30% - Group mark). The student groups will also present and defend their case studies and recommendations in class and respond to questions raised by their lecturer and peers (10% - Individually allocated mark).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case Study Recommendation Report and Presentation (Group/Individual)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Between 3000 and 4000 words.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week range</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12 to Week 13              Report Due (Hardcopy &amp; Online) 20th of October 2014 at 6:00pm; Presentations scheduled for 27th of October 2014 at 6:00pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Effective evaluation of alternatives Formulate comprehensive sustainability recommendations Support sustainability decisions by evidence from the literature Innovative integration of Information Systems enabled solution Present and defend sustainability recommendations/solution</Data></Cell>
