   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41190</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Sustainability and Information Systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students grasp the historical and cultural origins of current complex sustainability challenges and the need for collaboration, as an essential prerequisite to dealing with complex sustainability challenges and the pivotal role IT plays in enabling such collaboration. Students also identify intra-organizational and community-wide stakeholders and their role in sustainability dilemmas as well as evolving Green IT/ IS practices that assist in addressing sustainability challenges. Students will do this by individually carrying out a literature search and review to identify a contemporary sustainability issue and the role that IS might play in resolving that issue. They will need to identify the sustainability challenges, the stakeholders involved, some IS tools, along with a review of academic and professional literature relating to these challenges.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study analysis report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Literature review</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Maximum 2500 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students review, to understand, a particular aspect of sustainability in a particular context, and identify a problem of interest to investigate in more detail.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To analyse the ethical, social, technological, and economic issues relating to sustainability and the evolving Green IT/ IS practices that assist in addressing sustainability challenges. Three students will form a group in which they will develop capability in formulating comprehensive recommendations for addressing the selected sustainability challenge from a multidimensional perspective. This task will assess how students, (through collaboration, coordination) are able to evaluate their individual case studies submitted as Assignment 1 and will select a single case to pursue as Assignment 2. The group will formulate broad-based recommendations to comprehensively address a sustainability challenge, presented from a multidimensional perspective, including the role of IS tools in addressing this challenge. A report of such recommendations must be rigorously supported by evidence from evolving practice and academic and professional literature. The student groups will also present and defend their case studies and recommendations in class and respond to questions raised by their lecturer and peers.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Case study recommendation report and presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Maximum 3000 words; Presentation for 15 mins (5 mins/person)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To recommend courses of action to address the “identified”, and “analysed” issues.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The groups (formed for Assignment 2), will be given two weeks’ notice for a debate on a defined topic. Two groups will participate at a time with an opponent and proponent stand on the topic. They will be given 10 minutes time (each group 5 minutes) to convince opposition of their opinion. The most convincing group will be identified by the class vote. Each group member will be marked individually based on their performance on the debate against a co-designed criteria sheet.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Debate on socially sensitive sustainability challenges</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Debate on socially sensitive sustainability challenges to deepen social responsibility and improve communication skills and ability to coordinate.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Provide a solution for a computational problem.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Technical proficiency (computational tool)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design/drawing/plan/sketch</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">a short report (with an enclosed simulation file) explaining the results (max 1000 words)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Motivate students to exercise computational tools (for modelling skills) taught in the class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
