   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42912</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Sustainable Energy Resources</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In-class quiz will be given during one of the classes (Block 2B) which combines theory questions and calculations to assess the student’s learning. Group activities/discussions relating to the topic will be given on each block class that will be marked as a group. Additional materials for group discussions and quiz will be made available at UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In-class activities</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Variable.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Sunday 5 April 2020              Variable (Group discussions on each block; In-class Quiz on Block 2B (Week 6)).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Variable (Group discussions on each block; In-class Quiz on Block 2B (Week 6)).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment will enable students to receive feedback on their learning during lectures and in-class activities. The feedback is provided via in-class quizzes or doing group discussions/tasks that encourage collaborative learning.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A specific topic related to sustainable energy options will be assigned to each group of around 4-6 students. The students will become the class experts on the particular topic assigned. Each group will investigate and do a detailed research and in-depth understanding of the assigned topic and submit a written report and give an oral presentation to the class. The total mark for this assessment is 20% which will be divided into 10% for oral presentation and 10% for written report. This exercise will enable collaborative learning, develop teamwork, and research and communication skills. Guide questions and other details will be provided separately on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Oral presentation and report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10-15 pages.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">22/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">08:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">8.00pm Friday 22 May 2020              Week 10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will learn more in-depth knowledge and evaluation of specific sustainable energy options, and identify the pros and cons of such options. This will provide collaborative learning, and improve their research and communication skills, as they will work as a group. However, individual learning is assesed through their reporting.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is an individual written report. An energy scenario will be given wherein students will need to plan some strategies on how to approach the problem and provide solutions. This will include conducting literature reviews, interviews, calculations, and own analysis of how the energy portfolio should be designed in the future. A professional technical report is the expected outcome of this task. Additional assignment brief will be made available at UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Energy portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10-15 pages.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">07/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">08:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">8.00pm Sunday 7 June 2020              Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This will assess the student's understanding of the different available energy sources and technologies and their effects to environment and society, and to develop recommendations of appropriate sustainable energy technologies for the future.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Open book exam. All topics covered in the lectures and assignments are assessed.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 h + 10 min reading time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To assess the competency of students in undertstanding the concepts and principles of sustainable energy, socio-technical and environmental effects, and the evaluation of different energy sources and technologies.</Data></Cell>
