   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32520</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Systems Administration</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The skills test will provide the opportunity for students to demonstrate their system administration skills and record keeping techniques.  This is a &quot;restricted open book&quot; test. Students are only allowed to refer to their Learning Journal, and can use the Linux 'man' and 'info' commands on their virtual Linux servers, and can use their Windows servers help commands.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Networking Skills Test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">6</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 6              This Networking Skills Test will be completed in the lab class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This Networking Skills Test will be completed in the lab class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The use of a learning journal (also called an Engineering journal) will encourage students to keep good logbooks for systems under their control and to foster reflective learning. This should be developed over the entire semester and will be used in the final skills test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Learning Journal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Journal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Learning journals will be checked twice. Once in week 6 during the Networking Skills Test, and once in week 12 during the Final Skills Test. Students must have their journals available in class for marking at the start of the lab weeks mentioned.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Learning journals will be checked twice. Once in week 6 during the Networking Skills Test, and once in week 12 during the Final Skills Test. Students must have their journals available in class for marking at the start of the lab weeks mentioned.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The skills test will provide the opportunity for students to demonstrate their system administration skills and record keeping techniques. This is a &quot;restricted open book&quot; test. Students are allowed to refer to their Learning Journal, and can use the Linux &quot;man&quot; and &quot;info&quot; commands on their virtual Linux servers, and can use their Windows servers help commands.  Assessment would include: implementation of topics not covered in class - e.g. extra LPIC topics, depth of research, originality and resourcefulness. That means, students are encouraged to study more by themselves outside the class content.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Skills Test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              The Final Skills Test will be completed in the lab class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The Final Skills Test will be completed in the lab class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The final exam is a restricted open book exam and will test theoretical &amp; design aspects of the curriculum.</Data></Cell>
