   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">31281</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Systems Development Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Weekly review and tutorial</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">0</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There are no formal assessment criteria for this item. Advice and guidance provided by the tutor depends on their professional judgment about the problems faced by the team that need to be addressed and suggestions about how the team might address them. As the team develops project deliverables, the tutor will assess their progress using the criteria that will be used after formal delivery. This provides the team with formative feedback of work in progress.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The weekly project review and tutorial provides an opportunity for the team to discuss their progress and problems, and to develop plans for work that advances the project. Insofar as possible, these meetings are run in the same way as industry agile software projects are run. The meetings also provide an opportunity for the tutor to use their knowledge and experience to help the teams learn sound software engineering practices and the reasons for them.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Requirements peer review</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstrate that the business problem has been understood and clearly expressed in the business requirements. Review comments and suggestions are helpful and will improve the business requirements. [no content]</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The team presents their understanding of the problem and the requirements for its software solution for review by another team.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design peer review</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Show how the system's design will provide the required functionality and meet the required objectives. Clearly communicate the system's design to the audience. [no content]</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Present the design of the system to another team to review whether the design will deliver its required functionality and meet its objectives</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Determine whether or not the team has understood the problem and is making progress implementing a solution to it.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Mid project deliverables</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There is no predetermined length for any one deliverable.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7              Mid semester deliverables must be submitted by the end of Week 7. 11:59pm Friday 7 September</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Mid semester deliverables must be submitted by the end of Week 7. 11:59pm Friday 7 September</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The system development has been planned and managed. Teamwork has been managed. The business requirements have been elicited and understood. A system architecture will provide the required functionality and meet its non-functional objectives. A database design will provide the necessary data management. A user interface design will help and facilitate users to perform their tasks. [no content]</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assess how well the team has elicited and understood the business requirements and have designed a system to achieve those functional and non-functional requirements.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each group will present the readiness for delivery of their software system for their review and critique by another group. Reviews are completed using a review form (currently Google forms) and submitted on completion. Peer reviews are conducted in the tutorial room.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Delivery readiness peer review</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">There is no predetermined length for any of the deliverables.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 11              Reviews must be completed on the same day of the presentation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reviews must be completed on the same day of the presentation.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The coded programs are understandable and maintainable. The system has been adequately tested. Sufficient and appropriate information will support the system's implementation, use and maintenance. [no content]</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Each team presents the software system's readiness for delivery for critique by another team.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Make the completed software development and related artefacts available for assessment. The form of deliverables can be quite varied. The work in progress may be contained in a tool (e.g. project management such as Trello or Jira). The group's tutor must be provided with access to the work so that it can be assessed in situ. Some work may be a written report that can be submitted to the subject and assessment related Turnitin repository. Some assessment may be of behaviour (for example, team collaboration, sprint meetings) that will be observed by the group's tutor. Assessment is conducted in industry realistic conditions. In general work is submitted or made available for assessment as appropriate for the work itself.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">End of project deliverables</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">35</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              The final deliverables must be submitted by 11:59 PM, Friday 19th October</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The final deliverables must be submitted by 11:59 PM, Friday 19th October</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The implementation has been planned and managed. Teamwork has been managed. The system design has been implemented into understandable, maintanable programs. The system has been adequately tested. There is sufficient and suitable documentation to support the system's deployment, use and maintenance.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assess the implementation of the system's design into a working, deliverable and supportable system.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstrate the completed executable software system. The software system will be evaluated by a tutor in the tutorial room.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Developed software</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstration</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12              Students are expected to attend and demonstrate at the allocated time of their tutorial.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are expected to attend and demonstrate at the allocated time of their tutorial.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Provides the required functionality Achieves the required non-functional objectives..</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Evaluate the finished working system.</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49004</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Systems Engineering for Managers</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will be required to join ‘engineering consulting firms’ which have been approached by a client to assess and enhance the sustainability of a particular aspect of project that deals with the built environment, energy, water or waste management, or a combination of two or more of these. The details of the project, group dynamics, conditions, requirements and constraints can be found in the detailed project description available through Canvas. The project is made up of the following deliverables:  Part A - Final written report - students, applying systems thinking and broad research, will analyse the problem and propose an engineered solution which will be contained in a comprehensive written report (SLOs 1, 2, 3, 4) Part B - Weekly research reports – students will produce reports on the research that their team has conducted as their contribution to their group effort (SLOs 1, 2) Part C - Presentations – Initially, to peers, so that the cohort can assess all the different proposals and craft, with a combination of the best, a comprehensive proposal for the client, then to the client (SLOs 3, 4) Part D - Peer assessment – students will provide a peer assessment with SparkPlus which will be used to evaluate individual contributions to team delivery (SLO 3)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">70</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 10 and Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 10 and Week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will be required to peruse reputable media coverage of issues/problems affecting either domestic or international contexts and explain how they believe a systems thinking approach is helping or would help address the complexity of one of those contemporary issues/problems. The deliverable for this assessment is a weekly 1-page (maximum) report which will be peer marked and discussed during tutorials.</Data></Cell>
