   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32603</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Systems Quality Management</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Provide answers for the questions provided. Questions can be a combination of multiple choice/ fill-in-the blank/short response type questions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Class test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">8</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 8</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A set of questions to assess how well the student understands and applies the main concepts.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Identify and briefly describe an industry practice that implements one of ISO 9001's quality management principles. A scenario will be given on which the student describes how the industry practice implements the principle and how widespread it is in industry. Describe how the student will investigate the circumstances that favour the practice, how the practice is commonly implemented, the expected costs and benefits of this practice.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">45</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Approximately 2000 to 3000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Relevant: The proposal addresses the project objectives, constraints and risks. Complete: The proposal reasonably identifies all of the relevant objectives, constraints and risks. Informed: The identified objectives, constraints and risks inform the project strategy and plan. Justified: The proposed strategy and plan is shown to be the best alternative in the project circumstances.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstrate that the student understands the objectives, scope, constraints and risks of the proposed project and to align industry, academic and student expectations for the project.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Describe a principle of quality management that can be used by organizations for project or development teams and to guide decision making about practices in order to achieve quality requirements. The principle should provide a context for decision making and, most importantly, a clear and succinct rationale why the longer term benefits justify the short term costs and inconveniences of adopting the principle. Each group will present their project in class and submit project report on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Approximately 1500 to 2000 words</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project report due Week 9. Presentations will be held during Weeks 9-12 in class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Description: Clear description of the principle for software quality management.  Benefits: Benefits arising from the principle for the organization.  Applicability: Applicability of the principle with clear and succinct rationale.  Evidence: Evidence supporting the principle in achieving quality management.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will carry out a project to investigate and document a principle of software quality management. The principle should guide industry decision making about achieving software quality objectives in a given context.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project report due Week 9. Presentations will be held during Weeks 9-12 in class.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
