   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">42030</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Technology Disruptors Studio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students develop a problem statement, which summarises a key challenge in their workplace or articulates a future desired career direction, and design a prototype learning plan. The plan incorporates an introduction, professional context statement, learning profile, professional learning network and goals in an e-portfolio.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Professional Learning Plan</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1000 words or equivalent</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To identify knowledge and skills to be developed and reflectively design a learning plan by incorporating a range of perspectives, information and feedback.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students communicate and collaborate with each other by giving, receiving and responding to insights, provocations and critical feedback in the studio and via online discussions and interactions. Students submit a short online reflective commentary on their own synthesis of critical feedback and provide documented evidence of their group’s effective collaboration with each other and the design and learning processes in the studio and online.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group Activity and Commentary</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Journal</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual commentary and group’s communication (4x 500 words equivalent)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To develop collaborative practitioners who give, receive and evaluate critical feedback, foster peer learning, generate ideas and reflect on learning processes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Drawing on ideas generated by studio and online discussions, studio activities and scholarly readings, students write a summative evaluation for their e-Portfolio. The summative reflection evaluates their learning and justifies future actions in terms of learning about professional learning and identifies refinement or modifications of the professional learning plan and integrates a minimum of 4 scholarly sources.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection on Professional Learning</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Reflection</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">500 words or equivalent and e-Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To develop reflective practitioners who evaluate information and their own learning to identify and justify future actions.</Data></Cell>
