   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32931</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Technology Research Methods</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Part A: Individual Plan (10%) With your research supervisor, prepare a plan for your learning in this subject. You will need to detail the readings you commit to undertake, the workshops you will attend and short, online courses you will complete. State the goals you aim for and explain how the activity will enable you to achieve them. Length: 1500 words maximum Part B: Reflective Portfolio (40%) Collect the evidence of your engagement in your plan and write reflections on the extent to which you met your goals. The portfolio is a compilation of evidence of how you met your planned intended learning goals. Artefacts might include evidence of attendance or enrolment in workshops and courses, notes taken from readings and video viewings. Length: approximately 3000 words; other modes of presentation may be acceptable, such as video reflection.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual plan and reflective portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1A: 17 August 2020 (Week 4) at 11:59pm Assignment 1B: 23 October 2020 (Week 12) at 11:59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1A: 17 August 2020 (Week 4) at 11:59pm Assignment 1B: 23 October 2020 (Week 12) at 11:59pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Write your research proposal complete with the following sections. It should be comprehensively referenced using Harvard referencing and be free from spelling and grammatical errors.  Literature Review (from TRP) Aims Research Questions Methods Planned timeline Progress to date</Data></Cell>
