   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48651</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Thermodynamics</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will conduct one experiment and work on two laboratory reports using the data acquired in the laboratory. Task 1 is for the first laboratory report with a focus on the application of the first law of thermodynamics. Students should refer to all the documents in the folder of 'Laboratory' for 48651 on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory report 1 - Air Compressors</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">No more than 10 pages including Appendices.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">17/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 17 April 2020              Laboratory report in pdf format should be submitted electronically to UTSOnline. Each team will be required to submit one report.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory report in pdf format should be submitted electronically to UTSOnline. Each team will be required to submit one report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will apply the first and second laws of thermodynamics to analysing the System A (air compressor) using the same data for the first laboratory report. The detailed requirements are specified in the Instruction to Laboratory published on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory report 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">No more thean 6 pages.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 15 May 2020              Laboratory report in pdf format should be submitted electronically to UTSOnline. Each team will be required to submit one report.See also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory report in pdf format should be submitted electronically to UTSOnline. Each team will be required to submit one report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In Quiz 1, students will solve one question related to thermodynamic properties and work transfer. Students will have 30 minutes to complete the task</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 1 (Thermodynamic properties, work transfer)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">01/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">02:30 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2.30pm Wednesday 1 April 2020              All the quizzes are open book.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">All the quizzes are open book.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In Quiz 2, students will be required to complete one question for the application of the first law of thermodynamics. Students will have 30 minutes to complete the quiz.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 2 (The first law of thermodynamics)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">29/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">02:30 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2.30pm Wednesday 29 April 2020              All the quizzes are open book.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">All the quizzes are open book.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In Quiz 3, students will be required to complete one question for the application of the second law of thermodynamicsincluding entropy. Students will have 30 minutes to complete the quiz.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 3 (The second law of thermodynamics, entropy)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
