   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49102</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Traffic and Transportation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students must apply fundamental aspects of traffic flow theory to understand estimate key system performance variables for a series of case study examples. The assignment will involve developing the fundamental traffic flow relationships, completing regression analysis and shockwave analysis to quantify and alleviate the impacts of changes to a transport system.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Traffic Engineering Assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30/08/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 30 August 2019              via UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">via UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assignment will be assessed based on the correctness of the application in traffic flow theory and the justification used in defining potential solutions.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment is to test students' capability of applying traffic engineering principles/standards.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will complete a series of numerical problem solving exercises to appraise the performance of transport infrastructure and determine any mitigation strategies necessary to alleviate any identified issues. The work must be presented in a report format justifying the approach developed and any assumptions made.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Data collection, analysis and performance measurement Assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11/10/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:59 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.59pm Friday 11 October 2019              via UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">via UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assignment will be assessed based on problem identification and definition, methodological approach and correctness of the assessment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to complete an assignment that focuses on data collection and analysis procedures normally undertaken by practicing Traffic Engineers and Transport Planners.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">It is an open-book exam with formula sheet provided. The Final Examination will cover all material presented during the subject. It will comprise questions from both the Transport Planning and Traffic Operations strands of the course. The Final Examination is presented in a format that is 'practical' and requires written responses and calculations. It embraces the type of questions/problems that are faced daily in the civil engineering workplace, specific to the transport domain.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to demonstrate their ability to undertake necessary calculations and interpret models and designs related to the traffic and transport discipline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
