   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49328</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Turbomachines</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Four individual assignments on different aspects of turbomachines analysis and design. Students are expected to solve problems and answer questions posed in the assignments satisfactorily. All problems in an assignment are of equal value. Assignment briefs are posted on UTSOnline at least 3 weeks before their due date. Assignments are to be submitted electronically. Marked assignments are returned 2 weeks after their due date. Solutions and feedback are given upon the return of the assignments.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignments</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">32</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1: Week 4 (23:59 Friday 03/04/2020); Assignment 2: Week 7 (23:59 Friday 01/05); Assignment 3: Week 9 (23:59 Friday 15/05); Assignment 4: Week 11 (23:59 Friday 29/05)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment 1: Week 4 (23:59 Friday 03/04/2020); Assignment 2: Week 7 (23:59 Friday 01/05); Assignment 3: Week 9 (23:59 Friday 15/05); Assignment 4: Week 11 (23:59 Friday 29/05)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To gain experience in the analysis and design of a variety of turbomachines.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will be required to do research about a turbomachine device (which will be assigned via UTSOnline) and will then be required to write a technical report on the findings of the investigations. Students will be expected to investigate and show their results, qualitative and quantitative, as well as any key conclusions drawn. Students will need to state the current knowledge using literature, as well as consider using more than one case study. Students are encouraged to use various materials to aid their investigation (photos, diagrams etc). All sources need to be fully cited in a reference list. Further information (including a brief and further information on how to write a technical report) can be found on UTSOnline. This task is done in a team of 3-5 students only.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Projects</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">18</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">23:59 Fri Week 8 (08/05/2020)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">23:59 Fri Week 8 (08/05/2020)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To gain experience researching important Turbomachines, and working in a team.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The final examination will cover the contents in the whole subject.  Duration: 2 hrs + 10 mins reading time Open-book (any materials of print, typed, or written type can be used) There will be four questions of equal value  Programmable calculators are allowed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Exam (open-book, 2 hours plus 10 minutes reading time)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 hours plus 10 minutes reading time</Data></Cell>
