    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UNIX Systems Programming</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are asked to address programming exercises in the Unix shell. Detailed instructions will be provided by the tutors on the date of the test and a preparation example will be run in week 4. This test is open book (students are allowed to use all their study materials).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Programming Test - Unix</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 6, in the tutorial class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 6, in the tutorial class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Test students’ ability to develop scripts of simple and medium complexity in the Unix shell.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to take a multiple-answer test about the Unix shell with 15 questions on Canvas. Detailed instructions will be provided by the tutors on the date of the test and a preparation example is available on Canvas. This test is open book (students are allowed to use all their study materials).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Multiple Choice - Unix</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7, in the tutorial class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7, in the tutorial class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assess students’ understanding of Unix concepts and their ability to solve problems such as the computation of regular expressions, filename globbing, maximum file sizes, and others.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are asked to address programming exercises in Python. Detailed instructions will be provided by the tutors on the date of the test. This test is open book (students are allowed to use all their study materials).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Programming Test - Python</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
