    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 11, in the tutorial class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Test students’ ability to develop scripts of simple and medium complexity in Python.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 11, in the tutorial class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students are required to take a multiple-answer test about Perl with 15 questions on Canvas. Detailed instructions will be provided by the tutors on the date of the test. This test is open book (students are allowed to use all their study materials).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Multiple Choice - Python</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12, in the tutorial class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 12, in the tutorial class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assess students’ understanding of Python concepts and their ability to solve problems such as the evaluation of regular expressions, elements of lists and dictionaries, numerical expressions and others.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This take-home assessment task requires each student to develop a Python program based on a set of given specifications. It has to strictly be completed individually, i.e. the student should not receive any help from other students or externally. The assignment specifications will be handed out on Canvas on the lecture's day of week 8.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday 05/06/2020, 5pm. The assignment must be submitted via the Assignment menu on Canvas.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday 05/06/2020, 5pm. The assignment must be submitted via the Assignment menu on Canvas.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment is a take-home, individual programming assignment using Python. It reflects authentic professional practice by being presented as a set of functional specifications that can be tested individually using test patterns. It resembles a typical programming task assigned to a professional programmer, scaled to the scope and extent of this subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The students are asked to address programming exercises in the Unix shell. Detailed instructions will be provided by the tutors on the date of the test. This test is open book.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">17/08/2015</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Monday 17 August 2015</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assessment task requires the students to complete a realistic sample of Perl programming.</Data></Cell>
