   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49680</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Value Chain Engineering Systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Use data analysis with Excel to define the problem. This is a scenario-based task where you are provided with company customer complaints data to define the problem, analyse and propose solutions to. Your deliverables include spreadsheet (excel) analysis and a report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Supply Chain Analytics</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1500 words and Data Analysis with Excel</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 5              30 Aug 2020, 11pmSee also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30 Aug 2020, 11pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The detailed requirements and any support material for this Assignment are set out on Canvas. This is a Group Assignment. Assessment feedback - Report returned with marks (summative). In groups of three, students apply value chain analysis to a top Australian organisation. You will research the organisation and the value chain options, benefits and risks. You would prepare a managerial report based on the extensive analysis conducted on the case study provided. An additional 5-minute video-clip is to be submitted by each group member highlighting problem, solution methodology and findings to the company managers (this will be individually assessed). Duration of video-clip must be between 4 to 6 minutes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Engineering the Value Chain</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">It is expected that your group report shall be about 12 to 15 pages, although this will vary depending upon your apporach to the problem and issues. Video - duration of video-clip must be between 4 to 6 minutes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 11              18 Oct 2020, 11 pmSee also Further information.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">18 Oct 2020, 11 pm</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Two online quizzes will be conducted based on the subject content covered at the time (in week 6 and in week 12). These quizzes will be available for 2 days online and then they will be closed for students to participate.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Online quiz (Canvas based)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Mid-term quiz - in week 6 End-term quiz - in week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Mid-term quiz - in week 6 End-term quiz - in week 12</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A two hour exam with short written answers covering all material presented in the Subject. It is closed book and you need a non-programmable calculator. Any tables or formulae required will be given in the exam. You must achieve a minimum of 45% in the Final Exam and a minimum of 50% overall in order to pass the subject. This assessment is linked to the Subject Learning Objectives: 1,2,3,4,5,6,7.</Data></Cell>
