   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49123</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Waste and Pollution Management</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Summative Assessment Part A: Wastewater management and water reuse- Processes, rational description and calculations Part B: Develop knowledge of real world water reuse schemes Questions will be posted on UTSOnline under ‘Course Instruction and Assignments’ under the section of ‘Subject Information’.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Waste Management and Recycling</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">07/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12.00pm Tuesday 7 April 2020              Submit to UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit to UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Criteria: Single answers (Quantitative and qualitative) and methodology/approach to problem-solving. Design of water reuse scheme is a group activity.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment tests students' understanding of wastewater and bio-solids management principles, and ability to undertake basic design calculations and develop pollution abatement management practices. This will expose them to the design process of wastewater treatment plants.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Summative Assessment. Industrial waste minimisation - Process design, rational description and calculations on solid and waste management examples.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Waste minimisation methodologies and practices</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12:00 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">12.00pm Tuesday 5 May 2020              Submit to UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit to UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Criteria: Single answers (Quantitative and qualitative) and methodology/approach to problem-solving.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment will help students carry out processes in industrial waste minimisation which lead to the current practice of waste reduction and cleaner technology.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Summative Assignment Rainwater and stormwater management - calculation and essay questions</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Alternative water sources</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">17/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Sunday 17 May 2020              Submit to UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual assignment on best management strategies. Short qualitative and quantitative questions to illustrate the above principles.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment will help in the choice of alternative water sources for industries through case studies and design calculations.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit to UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This will be an open book exam, and as such you can bring your lecture notes and books for your reference during the exam. The exam will consist of a number of short-answer questions both quantitative and qualitative.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The duration of the examination is 2 hours and 10 minutes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam Period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam Period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Marks for each exam question are stated in the exam sheets.</Data></Cell>
