   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48840</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Water Supply and Wastewater Engineering</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Wastewater Treatment and management. Process design, rational description and calculations. Only short answer are expected on the calculations in the first part. The last question will discuss the case study of a waste water treatment plant. For the last question the students are asked to form a group of 3-4. Questions will be posted on UTSOnline under ‘Course Instruction and Assignments’ under the section of ‘Subject Information’.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Wastewater treatment and management</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Short-answer questions both quantitative and qualitative. Single answers and methodology/approach to problem-solving, provision of detailed and relevant discussions in case studies.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">16/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Thursday 16 April 2020              Submit to UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit to UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To test students’ knowledge of waste water treatment and management</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Water Treatment and management, water reticulation Process design, rational description and calculations and case studies examples Questions will be posted on UTSOnline under ‘Course Instruction and Assignments’ under the section of ‘Subject Information’.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Drinking water treatment and management</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Single answers and methodology/approach to problem-solving, provision of detailed and relevant discussions. 10 pages (maximum)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/06/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday 5 June 2020              Submit to UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit to UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Process description and design of water treatment processes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory 1 – Design of Sedimentation based on settling column test, case studies Laboratory 2 – On flocculation. In laboratory 1 the students will conduct sedimentation experiments and will collect the sample at different times. The water characteristics will be provided by the laboraty supervisor and students are expected to write a report. In laboratory 2 the students will conduct Jar test on flocculation and will collect the sample at different times. The water characteristics will be provided by the laboraty supervisor and students are expected to write a report. This task will be conducted in a group and group composition will be announced by the laboratory supervisor.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/ Practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A laboratory report should be submitted for each laboratory.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">22/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday 22 May 2020              Submit to UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Undertake experiments to investigate and validate key theory and principles taught in lectures.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Submit to UTSOnline</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This will be a closed book quiz. The quiz will consist of a number of short-answer questions both quantitative and qualitative. The coverage will be on based on waste water treatment and sewerage modeling.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Mid Session Quiz</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">2 hours</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">01/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Friday 1 May 2020              The quiz will be held in class on 1 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The quiz will be held in class on 1 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">-Close book quiz on concepts, principles, basic design wastewater treatment processes; -General principles of sewerage system. (short qualitative question and calculations on the principles of water and waste water management)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment of knowledge gained in lectures and laboratories</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The exam will consist of a number of short-answer questions both quantitative and qualitative.</Data></Cell>
