   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">48881</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Water and Environmental Design</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task involves preparing cultural impact assessment (CIA) report of a proposed land development project (hypothetical) based on the framework discussed in the class. The stand-alone report must include rationale of the CIA, background introduction to the proposed development site and the development scope, background research analysis of the development site to describe its significance to the cultural and heritage connections, assess the existing conditions and the how the proposed development alters the conditions, identifying potential impacts of development on cultural heritage attributes, suggest alternative mitigation and conservation strategies. The report must also include recommendations for integrating the CIA findings with the project planning and decision making process to mitigate adverse impacts of the project and including conservation strategies to avoid impacts, plans and approaches of stakeholder identification and the consultation processes.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Cultural and heritage impact assessment of a proposed land development project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">No length is specified however typically it is 10-20 pages.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25/08/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:45 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.45pm Sunday 25 August 2019              Document submitted in UTSOnline Task 1 dropbox.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Document submitted in UTSOnline Task 1 dropbox.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assessment framework is based around structural complexity of the approach used to design the cultural impact assessment report using the given framework as guide.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To produce a professional style written report on the cultural impact assessment of a proposed project that meets the needs of the client.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task involves undertaking the detailed land based effluent irrigation design. This report should integrate various aspects of the project proposal along with the detailed design calculations and discussion of design outcomes. A final stand-alone design report based on the design brief will be produced with the client as an end user.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Technical Design Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">50</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">No length is specified however typically it is 10-20 pages.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">29/09/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:45 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.45pm Sunday 29 September 2019              Document should be upload to UTSOnline Task 2 dropbox.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Document should be upload to UTSOnline Task 2 dropbox.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assessment framework is based around structural complexity of the approach used to analyse and solve the problem.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To produce a professional style written design report that meets the needs of the client.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task will involve creating a multimedia presentation of the Task 1 and 2 projects. The target audience is the supervisor of the writer.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Communication (Reflection)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Multimedia presentation is limited to 5 minutes total for each both Tasks 1 and 2.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25/10/2019</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:45 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.45pm Friday 25 October 2019              Task 3 video should be uploaded to the students UTS Youtube account. A document with the Youtube URL should be uploaded to the task 3 dropbox in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The assessment framework is based around structural complexity of the approach used to analyse and solve the problem.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To determine skills in effectively preparing and presenting a reflection upon the professional engineering experience undertaken in Assessment Tasks 1 and 2.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 3 video should be uploaded to the students UTS Youtube account. A document with the Youtube URL should be uploaded to the task 3 dropbox in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This task involves reflecting and then writing how the various Stage 1 competencies (where relevant) were addressed while undertaking Tasks 2, 3 and 4. Use the provided exemplar as a guide for report formatting and analysis. please also comment on how the design tasks and brief could be changed to better cover the Stage 1 competencies.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Typically the length is 2-4 pages however no page limit is specified.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date/Time</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10/10/2017</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11:45 PM</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11.45pm Tuesday 10 October 2017              Document must be submitted to UTSOnline Task 5 dropbox</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Document must be submitted to UTSOnline Task 5 dropbox</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">A holistic assessment framework is used. Examination of exemplards forms an inclass activities.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Professional engineers need to be able to reflect upon their experiences and identify what they have learnt. This task uses a reflective framework from Engineers Australia Stage 1 competencies which addresses the major competencies required for applying established engineering methods to complex engineering problem solving.</Data></Cell>
