   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">31268</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Web Systems</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">You will develop practical UNIX skills using a problem-based approach using an online Computer Based Training software package. This will develop your Problem Solving (B1) and Implement/Test solutions( B5) graduate attributes. You will be expected to complete the training exercises during the tutorial.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Linux Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Exercises</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Generally each Linux exercise will be due at 5pm Friday of the week after the scheduled Linux lab.  Due dates are listed in the Program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Generally each Linux exercise will be due at 5pm Friday of the week after the scheduled Linux lab.  Due dates are listed in the Program</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This closed book online quiz will test your knowledge of the basic computing theory developed in the lecture and tutorial materials in from week 1 to week 6. (C1 Apply Abstraction graduate attribute). You must sit for this quiz in your allocated tutorial.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class in Week 7              in your scheduled lab</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">in your scheduled lab</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This quiz is a &quot;low stakes&quot; test of the concepts covered in the early stage of this subject. Each question includes instant formative feedback to enable you do understand the intended result.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This closed book online quiz will test your knowledge of the basic computing theory developed in the lecture and tutorial materials in from week 7 to week 10. (C1 Apply Abstraction graduate attribute). You must sit for this quiz in your allocated tutorial.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">11</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In class in Week 11              In your scheduled lab</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This quiz is a &quot;low stakes&quot; test of the concepts covered in the middle stage of this subject. Each question includes instant formative feedback to enable you do understand the intended result.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">In your scheduled lab</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">You will develop a website for a given specification by applying stakeholder analysis (A1, F3) and critical reflection (C1, E1) and will construct the site using HTML, CSS and UNIX commands (B5). You will also consider accessibility issues (F3) in your design. You will provide constructive feedback (E1) to other websites given your research (B6) This website will be  a student website using unix commands to set up the appropriate directory structure with correct security access permissions; developed by hand using HTML and CSS and not using any other tool  You will then peer-assess 2 other student websites. You will critique website quality aspects such as aesthetics and accessibility and will write 1 paragraph justifying your assessment.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assignment</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">5 web pages and 1 CSS file. 1 paragraph on feedback per website.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">7</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Week 7              Website (20%): Due 5pm on Friday Week 7    &amp;   Peer Marking (5%): Due 5pm Friday Week 8</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Website (20%): Due 5pm on Friday Week 7    &amp;   Peer Marking (5%): Due 5pm Friday Week 8</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The skills test will consist of a set of hands-on problem solving (B1), Implementation and testing (B5) UNIX exercises based on the lab Linux exercises. You must sit for this quiz in your allocated tutorial. This test is restricted open book - you can bring a double-sided A4 page of notes into the test.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Skills Test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
