    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Please note that the weightings are approximate and they may vary from year to year and from one term exam to another.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To allow students to demonstrate their knowledge of the concepts learnt in the subject, apply their skills to solve problems and self-assess their progress in the subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The practical tasks requires students to work together in groups to set up and measure the performance of a Wi-Fi network. This work will be done by students outside class hours and involves setting up and performing measurements on Wi-Fi networks and modelling the behaviour of the network and wireless propagation. More information is available on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Labs</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab Test is on the weekly schedule given in the Program.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Lab Test is on the weekly schedule given in the Program.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Please note that the weightings are approximate, and may vary from year to year.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">It is designed to provide students with an overview of Wi-Fi operation and performance measurements. Students will use Excel and Matlab to analyse the measurements recorded from a live Wi-Fi network.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The exam is an open-book individual assessment taken on the UTSOnline Server. The two hour exam includes for example multiple choice single, multiple answer, fill in the blanks questions, essay questions. This examination will be held in exam period under supervision. The questions will be based on the key concepts presented during the weekly lectures. More information on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">40</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period              This is a centrally conducted exam and the date will be given on the exam timetable.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The intent of the final exam is to allow students to demonstrate their knowledge of wireless networks operation, standards and problem solving which they have learnt in the subject.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This is a centrally conducted exam and the date will be given on the exam timetable.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Research Topic - Students can work individually or in group of two on an allocated wireless research topic. The task involves researching, preparing a PowerPoint presentation with detailed slide notes, delivering the presentation in class and answering questions from audience related to topic. The deliverables of the project are proposal, draft presentation and class presentation, and report. The details of each deliverable and marking scheme are given on UTSOnline. Assessment of the task will involve the following criteria: depth and complexity of research, accurate acknowledgement of sources, consistency of referencing style, credibility and relevance of the source, ability to express key ideas, completeness of information; and quality &amp; clarity of expression, quality of visual graphic communication, successful delivery of ideas and audience engagement, etc. Peer feedback will be provided immediately after the presentation and instructor (or facilitator) feedback will be provided during consultation hours.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Assessment Report</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">20</Data></Cell>
