   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">49227</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Wireless Sensor Networks</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Provide an individual perspective on the project's scope, initial requirement (light version), usage scenarios and preliminary WSN model/architecture. Discuss and provide the rationale your for your individual choice of sensing/actuation technology for the WSN-based solution in context of the problem. Provide a light version of the project plan in context of the scope, the team organisation, schedule/milestones and final deliverables. The first assignment is of an introductory nature to the implementation phases of your project. Its focus is on the understanding of the problem space, key/driver requirements, the choice of WSN technology and what would be the initial model of the architecture of proposed solution. How they are related, implementation issues, how resources can be critically applied, how the budget can be spent, critical risks/mitigation strategies, commitment to deliverables for main Assignment 2 and the development of a Project Systems Engineering Document/Report. Its ultimate aim is to explore, compare and integrate individual ideas related to development of the final solutions/options.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Scoping the Project</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Maximum 7 pages, minimum 4 pages including diagrams and pictures</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">05/04/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Sunday 5 April 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">This assignment will help to determine the selection of the preferred option(s) for the final WSN system solution that you will decide on when working in teams of about 3-4 people for assessments 2 and 3.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The second assignment is the main project development package that includes a design documentation providing final architecture/high level and low level designs; and test/integration plans; and any documentation related to implementation for the assigned project .The assignment should be completed by cooperating small teams of approximately 3-4 students and integrated by the Team as a seamless Team deliverable. You will be assessed individually and as a Team. You are required to identify each team member’s contribution in your written report.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Design, Implementation and Documentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Maximum 30 pages</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Date</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10/05/2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Sunday 10 May 2020</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Teams should provide WSN Architecture/Design and possibly a mock-up UI. Consideration should be given to use of Open Source hardware/software and COTS components (hardware toolkits, IDEs, Frameworks, DBMS, libraries, and middleware, etc.)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The third assignment is a Team presentation and demonstration which includes a discussion on the deliverable plus its conformance to the major functional abstractions/components identified. The assignment should be completed by cooperating small Teams of approximately 3-4 students and integrated by the Team as a seamless Team deliverable. You will be assessed individually and as a team.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Project Presentation, Demonstration</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Laboratory/practical</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">25</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Slides (including demos) should be prepared to deliver 10-15 minute oral presentations</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final teaching week in Class and Lab</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Group, group and individually assessed</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Demonstration of the prototype WSN application. Delivery of the project's artefacts and the final report. Each team has a total of 10-15 minutes to present the project and all team members should participate, we will then dedicate 5 minutes for questions and answers. Students are encouraged to conduct real environmental experiments (e.g. measuring the soil moisture content using sensors, generate and analyze data). To demonstrate your measurement, students could select one of the following options which suits you best:  Bring your laptop, sensors,... and run measurements Record a short movie of measurement and present in the class Prepare some snapshots of results to be included in the slides</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final teaching week in Class and Lab</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">4 short quizzes are designed for individual students. Students are required to answer different types of questions. There will be no negative marks for incorrect answers. Quizzes are paper-based and will be held in class, during the lecture time.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quizzes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Quiz/test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">15 to 30 minutes</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Weeks 5,6,9,10 in Class or Lab</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Weeks 5,6,9,10 in Class or Lab</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">For individual students to evaluate their learning and understanding of the key concepts based on the given materials (lecture notes and handbook).</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">The final exam is a computer-based theoretical exam based on the given materials (lecture notes and hand books). Students will be required to answer different types of questions (e.g. Fill in the Blank, Matching Questions, Multiple Choice, Multiple Response, Open Response, and True/False questions). There will be NO negative marks for wrong answers. The final exam will occur at a scheduled time during the formal examination session. This is a restricted open-book exam and students can bring one A4-size double-sided page of handwritten notes into the final exam.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Final Exam</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Examination</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1 hour (excluding 10 minutes reading time)</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">UTS Exam period</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">For individual students to test their gained knowledge, learning and understanding of the key concepts and technologies required for them to effectively participate in various phases of the WSN system development.</Data></Cell>
