   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41037</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Work Integrated Learning 1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">All students should attempt to complete Module C1.1b Mentoring early in their internship. Module C1.1a Reviewing Engineering is only to be completed by students who cannot satisfactorily complete Module C1.1b. C1.1b Mentoring - To be completed by students during WIL1 as early in their internship as possible. In this module, students are provided with resources to help them find a professional mentor, either within or outside their workplace. Students provide their mentor with some brief induction materials and ask them to commit to 3 x 45 minute meetings over the course of the 6 month internship. At the first meeting (to be conducted early in the internship), students discuss with their mentor their goals for the first internship, including which WIL elective modules to undertake (if any). Students then devise an action plan for their learning goals. The second meeting (to be held about halfway through the internship) is for a progress check and to revise the plan if needed. The final meeting (to be done towards the end of the internship) is to reflect on goals achieved and to briefly look ahead towards the second internship. C1.1a Reviewing Engineering – Only to be completed by students who are unable to complete C1.1b. This module provides an opportunity for students to learn about one aspect of their chosen field of engineering in some depth so that they can hold an intelligent conversation with an experienced practitioner about that area. Students determine a topic that is relevant to their specific major of engineering that is of interest to them personally. They then research the topic by reading information from the UTS library and/or internet, watching videos and/or documentaries, and/or interviews. Next, they create a 'story' that covers, but is not limited to, a history/context for your topic, details about the topic including both technical details as well as general details, an impact analysis of how that technology/practice/person changed the everyday practice of engineering, and finally, what they think the future holds in regards to the topic. Students then create a 3 minute original video comprising a mixture of still images, video snippets, and narration that conveys your story. The video must be fast-paced, insightful and interesting, with a high standard of video and audio quality.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Module C1.1-EITHER C1.1b Mentoring OR C1.1a Reviewing Engineering</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Presentation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">30</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Module C1.1b Mentoring should be completed early in your internship (ideally within the first 6 weeks). Students should refer to the task schedule provided in the &quot;assessment&quot; folder of the module in UTSOnline. Module C1.1a is only to be completed by students who cannot satisfactorily complete module C1.1b. Students who do need to undertake module C1.1a should refer to the task schedule provided in the &quot;assessment&quot; folder of the module in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Module C1.1b Mentoring should be completed early in your internship (ideally within the first 6 weeks). Students should refer to the task schedule provided in the &quot;assessment&quot; folder of the module in UTSOnline. Module C1.1a is only to be completed by students who cannot satisfactorily complete module C1.1b. Students who do need to undertake module C1.1a should refer to the task schedule provided in the &quot;assessment&quot; folder of the module in UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">To establish a mentoring relationship with an experienced practitioner, to plan objectives for your workplace internship experience and to plan objectives for 41037 WIL1.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Establish a UTSOnline ePortfolio with an embedded Reflective Learning Journal for yourself if you haven't already done so (details are on UTSOnline).   Update your Reflective Learning Journal and ePortfolio throughout your internship period as per the requirements on UTSOnline.   Submit your ePortfolio for assessment and feedback at different points during your internship, as per the requirements on UTSOnline.</Data></Cell>
