   <Row>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">41047</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Work Integrated Learning 2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Students will use an online portfolio to document and maintain evidence of their professional learning and development. Students will also post their entries to a discussion board to share experiences with other interns and to provide and receive feedback. Students should attach evidence for their learning and development. Evidence will be required for at least some claims in WIL2 and will also be required for the EPR2 final report. Evidence may include photographs, screenshots, emails, technical drawings, documentation, awards, performance review, congratulatory emails, completed work, etc. Detailed instructions are on UTS Online WIL2. TASK 1.1 Internship Details:  Update your portfolio’s About Me page with details of your internship  TASK 1.2 Internship Goals:  Find a mentor at your workplace and review your internship learning plan (from EPP2). Update your plan and attach it to the GOALS section of your portfolio. Add your mentor’s details to the About Me page of your portfolio. Write a reflection on the process and results of your planning.  TASK 1.3 Performance Review:  Arrange a face to face meeting with your supervisor to have an initial performance review. Write a reflection about this process and result of the review. You should focus on one competency or attribute that needs to be developed. Read one of your peer’s posted work and provide feedback based on your experiences.  TASK 1.4 Reflection:  Write a reflection on an experience at your internship that didn’t work out as well as you expected. What did you learn from it and how can you use that experience to be a more effective professional. Read one of your peer’s posted work and provide feedback based on your experiences.  TASK 1.5 Development:  Review your initial performance review, and the reflection you wrote about it, with your mentor or supervisor. Did you succeed in developing the area that you wanted to work on? Consider the effectiveness (or otherwise) of the plan you wrote in stage 4 of your reflection. If it worked,use the experience to write a Developing Competency Claim, or Developing Attribute Claim (as appropriate), If the plan didn’t work, why didn’t it work? Research a new method or tool you can use to develop this area, and write a new Stage 4 plan.  TASK 1.6 Final Reflection:  Reflect on your development as an engineer over the course of your internship. Consider a significant event, or sequence of events, that had a profound effect on you. What was it? What did you learn from it? How did it change you? How will you use this in the future?</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Compulsory Module C2.3 - Reflect on Learnings and Development</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Portfolio</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">80</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Custom</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 1.1 due Friday of week 1; Task 1.2 due Friday of week 2; Task 1.3 due Friday of week 4; Task 1.4 due Friday of week 7; Task 1.5 due Friday of week 10; Task 1.6 due Friday of week 12;</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Task 1.1 due Friday of week 1; Task 1.2 due Friday of week 2; Task 1.3 due Friday of week 4; Task 1.4 due Friday of week 7; Task 1.5 due Friday of week 10; Task 1.6 due Friday of week 12;</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Individual</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Completeness; Quality; Presentation; Originality</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Record evidence of professional development; learn from experience more effectively by analysing previous episodes; learn from others by peer-review; broaden learning by learning from others' professional development.. This portfolio will serve as a record of achievement as well as evidence of having met various levels of UTS:FEIT graduate attributes and/or Engineers Australia Stage 2 competencies.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Choose a module from the list of options that best aligns with your internship, goals, and timing. Each module is designed to further your development while completing your internship.</Data></Cell>
